# Snapshots of the register pages and entries this archive has read.
#
# One row per find. A snapshot is a photograph of the page as the viewer showed it when it was read:
# `entry` is a close crop of the entry, `page` the whole page (either may be blank), both under
# site/public/snaps/. Nothing here is a transcription — the transcription is in readings.psv,
# found.psv and the note — but every reading that has a snapshot says so, on /snapshots/, on the
# person's page and on the /found/ page, and the snapshot names the film, the image number and the
# link to the viewer so anyone with the right sign-in can check it against the original.
#
# Fields: id|entry|page|title|film|where|view|says|slugs|captured|note
#   slugs   comma list of people.json / ancestors.json / found.json slugs this snapshot supports (may be blank)
#   view    the link to the image in the viewer (FamilySearch images need a free sign-in)
# tools/snapshots.py checks every file, slug and note exists and refuses a row that does not.
karlobag-marriage-1774|karlobag-marriage-1774-entry.jpg|karlobag-marriage-1774-page.jpg|Karlobag, 2 May 1774 — Vincentius Smojver «Vukich» and Oliva, daughter of the late Caetanus Bacchi|Karlobag marriages 1736–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 306, right-hand page: headed 1773, then «Anno Dni 1774»; the entry is the one with «Maij» in the left margin, the second under the 1774 heading|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-G3FD|«Praemissis praemittendis et habito mutuo consensu Vincentii filii Josephi Smojver, vulgo nuncupati Vukich, ac Olivae filiae defti Caetani Bacchi, eos per verba de praesenti solemniter matrimonio conjunxi, praesentibus Dno Nicolao Jurich et Francisco [Lukulich?]». The year is read from the heading above; the witnesses at one zoom.|vicentius-fabiano-smojver-vukic,oliva-andreana-bacchi,josiph-smojver-vukic,caetano-bacchi|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-marriage-1760|karlobag-marriage-1760-entry.jpg|karlobag-marriage-1760-page.jpg|Karlobag, 20 October 1760 — Paulus Perpich marries Anna, widow of Caetanus Bachi|Karlobag marriages 1736–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 293, left-hand page, headed «Anno Domini 1760»; the entry is the second of 20 October, the one beginning «Idem eadem die»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-G77|«Idem eadem die matrimonialiter copulavi Paulum Perpich et Annam viduam Caetani Bachi. Praesentibus testibus Joanno Mat[hosich] ac Petro Bevandich». Shows a Caetanus Bacchi dead by October 1760; probably the elder Caetanus (ahnentafel 214) — not proved.|caetano-bacchi,anna-widow-of-caetanus-bacchi-married-paulus-perpich|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-marriage-1753|karlobag-marriage-1753-entry.jpg|karlobag-marriage-1753-page.jpg|Karlobag, 4 February 1753 — Caetanus Bachi marries Anna, daughter of the late Alexius Lukatelli|Karlobag marriages 1736–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 287, right-hand page: «Anno Domini 1752», then «Anno Domini 1753»; the entry is the last on the page, «Idem eadem die» after the 4 February entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-GCS|«Idem eadem die matrimonialiter copulavi ad faciem Ecclesiae Cajetanum Bachi et Annam filiam defuncti Alexij Lukatelli. Praesentibus Wolffgango Suvich ac Joanne Radkovich». The father's surname is read from the full page.|caetano-bacchi,anna-daughter-of-the-late-alexius-lukatelli-wife-of-caetanus-bacchi|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-marriage-1747||karlobag-marriage-1747-page.jpg|Karlobag, 22 November 1747 — Jakov Pilepich marries Katta, daughter of the late Vicko Luckinich|Karlobag marriages 1736–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 283, right-hand page, headed «Letta 1747»: the entry dated «Dan 22: Novembra», second from the foot of the 1747 block (Croatian text)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-GHR|Croatian entry of the priest Andrij Kollekar joining «Jakova Lillepicha» (Pilepich) and «Kattu», the daughter «heer pokoif Vicka fucki[nicha]» — read as «daughter of the late Vicko Luckinich». The surnames are read at about 4x and are the least certain words.|jacob-pilipic,catherina-catta-luckinic,vicentius-vicko-luckinic|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1747-pilepich-luckinic.md
karlobag-marriage-1785||karlobag-marriage-1785-page.jpg|Karlobag, 2 November 1785 — Michael Gerkacs and Lucia, daughter of Paul Tomljanovic of Montani Stanize|Karlobag marriages 1736–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 324, right-hand page, headed «Anno Dni 1785»: the third entry, in the left margin «2 Novemb»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-G3Z4|«… matrimonio conjunxi ego Joes Antonius Ivankovich Parochus … Michaelis filij defti Nicolai Gergacs et Luciae Pauli Tomljenovich Loci Mostani [Montani] Stanize». Gives the groom's late father (ahnentafel 220) and the bride's father (222).|michaeli-michaele-gerkacs-gergacs,lucia-maja-tomljanovic,nicolaus-gerkacs,pauli-tomljanovic|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1785-gerkacs-tomljanovic.md
karlobag-marriage-1798||karlobag-marriage-1798-page.jpg|Karlobag, 14 February 1798 — Josephus Pilepich (widower) and Maria, daughter of Vincentius (probable)|Karlobag marriages 1736–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 343, right-hand page, headed «Anno Dni 1798»: the second entry, in the left margin «14 Febr[uarij]»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-G35T|«… Josephi viduei [Pilepich?] et Mariae filiae Vincenti [Smojver?] …». Date, both first names and the father's given name fit; both surnames are faint, so the identification as ahnentafel 52 and 53 is probable, not proved.|josephus-josip-pilipic,oliva-maria-smojver,vicentius-fabiano-smojver-vukic|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1798-pilepich-smojver.md
karlobag-marriage-1755-uroda||karlobag-marriage-1755-uroda-page.jpg|Karlobag, 5 February 1755 — Matthias Kriskovich marries Magdalena, daughter of Dominicus Uroda|Karlobag marriages 1736–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 289, right-hand page: «Anno Domini 1754», then «1755»; the entry is the last on the page, «Die 5ta Febr»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-GFZ|«Matthiam Kriskovich et Magdalenam filiam Dominici Uroda. Praesentibus Nicolao Perpich ac Josepho Venerando». A Dominicus Uroda with a daughter marrying in 1755; not shown to be related to Georgius Uroda (ahnentafel 108).|magdalena-daughter-of-dominicus-uroda-wife-of-matthias-kriskovich|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-marriage-1767-uroda|karlobag-marriage-1767-uroda-entry.jpg|karlobag-marriage-1767-uroda-page.jpg|Karlobag, 13 November 1767 — a man of Senj marries Maria, daughter of the late Dominicus Uroda|Karlobag marriages 1736–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 300, right-hand page, headed «Anno Dni 1767»: the second entry, in the left margin «13 9bris»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-G36T|«… conjunxi Joannem [? underlined word] Senicensem et Mariam filiam defuncti Dominici Uroda, praesentibus testibus …». The groom's given name is read as Joannes (an earlier note of this archive said Josephus; the page reads Joannem, with an underlined word after it). Shows Dominicus Uroda dead by November 1767.|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-marriages-1748-uroda-witness||karlobag-marriages-1748-dominicus-uroda-page.jpg|Karlobag, 1748 — «Dominico Uroda» a witness at marriages (3, 5 October and 17 November)|Karlobag marriages 1736–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 284, left-hand page, headed «Anno Domini 1748»: the entries of 3 and 5 October and 17 November each end «… et Dominico Uroda»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-G72|Dominicus «Dume» Uroda appears as witness about ten times between 1744 and 1749; this page shows three. He was an adult Karlobag man by 1744 and dead by 1767. He may be the father of Georgius Uroda (ahnentafel 108); nothing read says so.|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-births-1725-ana-luckinic||karlobag-births-1725-ana-luckinic-page.jpg|Karlobag, 13 April 1725 — Ana, daughter of Vicko Luckinich and his wife Mare|Karlobag births 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 47, left-hand page, in the viewer's numbering (about book page 31): the entries of April 1725 are written near the foot, out of date order|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L99G-1|«Na 13 Aprilya 1725 Ja Pop Andrij Kollekar karstih [k]… Vicka Luckinicha, nyegove xene mare imen[om] Anu koy bi kum Sg. Karlo Slayner …». Read as a daughter Ana to Vicko and Mare; the index and the tree make «Mare» the child. The same page carries the godfather entry of 1724.|ana-daughter-of-vicko-luckinich-and-mare-read-anu,vicko-lukcinich-godfather,mare-luckinic|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-1727-no-luckinic-baptism.md
karlobag-births-1753-bacchi-sponsor||karlobag-births-1753-bacchi-sponsor-page.jpg|Karlobag, 18 March 1753 — «Caietan Bachi» and his wife Anna as sponsors|Karlobag births 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 117, right-hand page, in the viewer's numbering (book page 211), headed «Letta 1753»: the entry «Dan 18: Marca» near the foot|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L9SN-V|A baptism of a child of Petar Tomljenovich «Bihu kumi Caietan Bachi, svojom xenom Annom» — Caetanus with his wife Anna, six weeks after their wedding. Read at about 4x.|caetano-bacchi|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-births-1754-silvester-bacchi||karlobag-births-1754-silvester-bacchi-page.jpg|Karlobag, early January 1754 — Silvester, son of Gaetanus and Anne Bachi|Karlobag births 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 119, right-hand page, in the viewer's numbering (book page 215), headed «Letta 1754»: the second entry under «Dan 1 Genvara» (dated 2 or 3 January)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L994-1|«… krstih Antola [Antonu?] Sylvestra sina Gajetana y Anne Bachi. Bihu kumi Jose y Venera Dur[…]ch». The first name is read at one zoom.|silvester-son-of-gaetanus-and-anna-bachi,caetano-bacchi|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
selce-marriage-1798||selce-marriage-1798-antic-loncaric-page.jpg|Selce, 18 October 1798 — Joannes Antić and Martha Lončarić|Selce marriages 1790–1815 (DGS 5482267, FamilySearch waypoint 9R2M-BZF)|image 248, left-hand page, headed «Anno 1798»: the second entry, numbered 27 in the margin|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-59DG-Z|Latin entry of the chaplain Michael Kombol: «… Joannem filium defuncti Antonii et Ursulae Antich cum Martha filia Pauli et Annae Lonchasich», witnesses Mathia Jellichich and Georgio Antich. Names both sets of parents (ahnentafel 96–99).|joannis-antic,margarita-martha-loncaric,joannis-antic-2,ursula,pauli-loncaric,anna-papic|11 October 2026|notes/selce-marriage-1798-antic-loncaric.md
selce-marriage-1800||selce-marriage-1800-jellicic-drozovic-page.jpg|Selce, 14 October 1800 — Georgius Jelličić and Margaretha Drozović|Selce marriages 1790–1815 (DGS 5482267, FamilySearch waypoint 9R2M-BZF)|image 251, left-hand page, «Die 14 8bris Ao 1800»: the fourth entry, numbered 96 in the margin|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-5963-H|«… Georgium filium Mathiae et Margaritae Jellichich cum Margareta filia Joannis et Catharinae Drozovich, praesentibus Laurentio Allegri? et Joanne Drozovich». The bride's surname reads DROZOVICH, not the tree's Brozović. Names both sets of parents (ahnentafel 100–103).|georgi-juraj-jellicic,margarita-brozovic,mathia-jellicic,margarita,joanni-brozovic,catharina-2|11 October 2026|notes/selce-marriage-1800-jellicic-drozovic.md
kranj-baptism-1775||kranj-baptism-1775-franz-kosina-page.jpg|Kranj–Šmartin, 3 December 1775 — Franciscus Xaverius Kosina, son of Lucas and Helena (probably Franz Kosinar)|Krstna knjiga Kranj–Šmartin 1747–1779 (Nadškofijski arhiv Ljubljana, Matricula sig. 00883)|page 330, right-hand page: the second row, day «3», baptiser «Zeller», locus «S. Thomae» with the number 10|https://data.matricula-online.eu/sl/slovenia/ljubljana/kranj-smartin/00883/?pg=330|Infans «Koskina Franciscus Xaverius», parents «Lucas et Helena Kosarsa [Kosina]», «Domus Paroch. Local», S. Thomae 10. The year is read from the heading «1776 Januarij» two pages on. Probable, not proved, to be the Franz Kosinar who died 1849.|franciscus-xaverius-kosina-son-of-lucas-and-helena|11 October 2026|notes/the-kozina-of-zgornje-bitnje.md
karlobag-death-1778-pilepich||karlobag-death-1778-pilepich-page.jpg|Karlobag, 10 April 1778 — Jacobus Pilepich, captain of the port, buried in his own crypt|Karlobag deaths 1774–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 364, right-hand page (folio 17), headed «Anno Dni 1778»: the entry in the margin «10 Aprilis»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-GSBG|«D. Jacobus Pilepich Capitaneus portûs, munitus omnibus Sacramentis per M.R. D. Andream Pintor Capellanum Loci, spiritum Deo reddidit … in propria Crypta in Parochiali Ecclesia existente … tumulatus est». Ahnentafel 104's death.|jacob-pilipic|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-1778-jacobus-pilepich.md
karlobag-death-1776-smojver||karlobag-death-1776-smojver-page.jpg|Karlobag, 16 May 1776 — Josephus Smojver, called Vukcich, aged 45|Karlobag deaths 1774–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 361, right-hand page (folio 11), headed «Anno Dni 1776»: the second entry under «Maij»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-G3WG|«Josephus Smojver dictus Vukcich, annorum 45, munitus omnibus Sacramentis obiit in Domino atque die 17 … tumulatus est». Ahnentafel 212's death; the age puts his birth about 1731.|josiph-smojver-vukic|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-1778-jacobus-pilepich.md
karlobag-death-1783-gerkacs||karlobag-death-1783-gerkacs-page.jpg|Karlobag, 30 October 1783 — Nicolaus Gergacs, aged 66, died in his son Antonius's house|Karlobag deaths 1774–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 376, right-hand page (folio 39), headed «Anno Dni 1783»: the entry «30 8bris»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-GSBH|«Nicolaus Gergacs annorum 66, munitus omnibus sacramentis obiit in domo filij sui Antonij, et die 31 ejusdem sepultus est in Cemeterio laterali». Ahnentafel 220's death.|nicolaus-gerkacs|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-1778-jacobus-pilepich.md
karlobag-death-1790-luckinic||karlobag-death-1790-luckinic-page.jpg|Karlobag, 29 May 1790 — Catharina, aged 70, widow of the late Jacob Pilepich|Karlobag deaths 1774–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 388, right-hand page (folio 63), headed «Anno Domini 1790»: the entry «29 ejusdem [Maij]», the last but one on the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-G3QY|«Catharina annorum 70 vidua defti Dni Capitanei Jacobi Pilepich obiit in Domino munita omnibus sacramentis, atque die 30 sepulta est». Ahnentafel 105's death; the age 70 puts her birth about 1720, which no baptism of 1717–1732 supports.|catherina-catta-luckinic|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-1778-jacobus-pilepich.md
karlobag-death-1791-uroda||karlobag-death-1791-uroda-page.jpg|Karlobag, 10 September 1791 — Dominus Georgius Uroda, buried in his own crypt (no age given)|Karlobag deaths 1774–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 390, right-hand page (folio 67), headed «Anno Domini 1791»: the entry «10 ejusdem» under September, near the foot|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-GSY8|«Dñus Georgius Uroda, munitus omnibus Sacramentis, in domo sua obiit, atque die 12 sepultus est in propria sua Cripta ante fores Ecclesiae Parochialis existente». NO AGE is given, and no occupation. Ahnentafel 108's death.|georgi-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/uroda-1791.md
karlobag-death-1809-lucia-maja||karlobag-death-1809-lucia-maja-page.jpg|Karlobag, 19 September 1809 — Lucia, called Maja, wife of Michael Gergacs, aged 34|Karlobag deaths 1804–1861 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 125, left-hand page (page 12), headed «Annus Domini 1809»: the entry «19 [Sept]», fourth from the foot|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-G99J|«Lucia, vulgo Maja, uxor Michaelis Gergacs, annorum 34, provisa omnibus sacramentis obiit in Domino, atque in propria crypta … humata est». Ahnentafel 111's death; an age of 34 cannot fit a marriage of 1785 and a daughter of 1789, so her age stays unresolved.|lucia-maja-tomljanovic|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-deaths-1809-1828.md
karlobag-death-1828-pilepich||karlobag-death-1828-pilepich-page.jpg|Karlobag, 28 June 1828 — Josephus Pilepich, aged 61|Karlobag deaths 1804–1861 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 138, right-hand page (page 35), headed «Anno Domini 1828»: the entry of 28 June (margin «Junii»), about the fifth from the top|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-G9HP|«… Josephus Pilepich Carlobagensis annorum 61 in communione S. Matris Ecclesiae animam Deo reddidit, cujus corpus die 29 h. sepultum est in coemeterio S. Caroli». Ahnentafel 52's death, found through the book's index (KAZALO). The page is dense Latin and read at about 3x.|josephus-josip-pilipic|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-deaths-1809-1828.md
karlobag-death-1834-maria-uroda||karlobag-death-1834-maria-uroda-page.jpg|Karlobag, 6 August 1834 — Maria, wife of the fisherman Georgius Uroda, aged 45|Karlobag deaths 1804–1861 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 149, right-hand page (folio 52), headed «Anno Domini 1834»: an entry in the upper half of the page, among those of July–August|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-G991|«Maria uxor piscatoris Georgii Uroda annorum 45 …», died 6 August 1834 and buried the 7th. Ahnentafel 55's death (née Gerkacs, married 1807); it names her husband, ahnentafel 54, as a fisherman, still alive. The entry is small and was read at about 4x; find it by the word «piscatoris».|mariam-gerkacs-gergacs,joannis-georgius-georgio-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-deaths-uroda.md
karlobag-baptism-1781-oliva-smojver||karlobag-baptism-1781-oliva-smojver-page.jpg|Karlobag, March 1781 — Oliva Maria, daughter of Vincentius Smojver «Vukich» and Oliva|Karlobag births 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 217, right-hand page (book page 65), headed «Anno Domini 1781»: the seventh entry, margin «Ejusdem» under March|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L998-5|«Ego Joes Antonius Ivankovich Parochus Loci baptizavi infantem natam ex Vincentio et Oliva Smoyver, vulgo Vukich, Conjugibus hujus Civitatis, cui impositum est nomen Oliva Maria». Ahnentafel 53's baptism; the parents are 106 and 107, married 7 years earlier (see the 1774 marriage).|oliva-maria-smojver,vicentius-fabiano-smojver-vukic,oliva-andreana-bacchi|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-1781-oliva-smojver.md
karlobag-baptism-1777-uroda||karlobag-baptism-1777-uroda-page.jpg|Karlobag, 21–22 April 1777 — Joannes Georgius, son of Georgius Uroda and Maria|Karlobag births 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 202, right-hand page (book page 37), headed «Anno Dni 1777»: the entry under the margin «Aprilis», second from the foot («Ego Joes Antius … ex Georgio et Maria Uroda … Joannis Georgij»)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L991-3|«Ego Joes Antius Ivankovich Parochus Loci baptizavi Infantem … ex Georgio et Maria Uroda Conjugibus hujus Loci, cui impositum est nomen Joannis Georgij». Ahnentafel 54's baptism, naming his parents (108 and 109); the godfather is a colonel. Read at about 3x.|joannis-georgius-georgio-uroda,georgi-uroda,maria-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/uroda-generation-found.md
selce-death-1793-antonius-antic||selce-death-1793-antonius-antic-page.jpg|Selce, 27 February 1793 — Antonius Antich Martini, aged about 54 (the given name is Antonius, not the tree's Joannes)|Selce deaths 1790–1815 (DGS 5482267, FamilySearch waypoint 9R2M-BZF)|image 81, left-hand page, headed «Anno 1793»: the fourth entry, house number 34 in the margin|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-59DD-H|«Die 27a Februarii 793 Antonius Antich Martini annorum circiter 54 in communione S. Matris Ecclesiae … animam Deo creatori suo reddidit». The day, month and age are the tree's for ahnentafel 96; the first word is Antonius, underlined, where the tree has Joannes — recorded as evidence of an Antonius Antich, not as a settled reading of 96.|joannis-antic-2|11 October 2026|notes/selce-deaths-1793-1807-1811.md
selce-death-1807-anna-papic||selce-death-1807-anna-papic-page.jpg|Selce, 24 August 1807 — Anna, wife of Paulus Lončarich Papich, aged about 65|Selce deaths 1790–1815 (DGS 5482267, FamilySearch waypoint 9R2M-BZF)|image 110, left-hand page: the first entry at the top, house number 134 in the margin; the page ends with the note that the parish of Selce was founded in November or December 1807|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-5962-V|«Die 24a Mensis Augusti anno ut supra 1807. Anna uxor Pauli Lončarich Papich annorum circiter 65 in communione S. M. Ecclesiae … animam Deo creatori suo reddidit». Ahnentafel 99's death, entered with the by-name Papich.|anna-papic|11 October 2026|notes/selce-deaths-1793-1807-1811.md
selce-death-1811-pauli-loncaric||selce-death-1811-pauli-loncaric-page.jpg|Selce, 29 September 1811 — Paulus Lončarich, widower, aged about 70|Selce deaths 1790–1815 (DGS 5482267, FamilySearch waypoint 9R2M-BZF)|image 120, RIGHT-hand page (printed page 111; the working note says left): the first entry at the top, «Die 29 7bis Ao 1811»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-596R-H|«Die 29 7bis Ao 1811. Paulus Lončarich viduus annorum circiter 70 in communione S. M. Ecclesiae … animam Deo creatori suo reddidit». Ahnentafel 98's death; viduus fits the 1807 death of his wife; the house, 134, is read from the neighbouring left page's margin.|pauli-loncaric|11 October 2026|notes/selce-deaths-1793-1807-1811.md
krivi-put-baptism-1859-antonija-perpic||krivi-put-baptism-1859-antonija-perpic-page.jpg|Krivi Put, 12/15 May 1859 — Antonija Perpić, daughter of Joannes and Lucia Perpić, house 136|Krivi Put births 1847–1884 (DGS 5494757, FamilySearch waypoint 9R28-DP8)|image 64, left-hand page (printed page 110): entry 51, the fourth row of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-RNXT|Born «12 Maji 1859», baptised «15 Maji 1859», Antonia Perpić, legit., parents «Joannis et Lucia Perpić», «Krivi put No 136», godparents Lucas and Anna Tomljanović. Ahnentafel 7's baptism, now read from the page (it had been index only).|antonija-tonka-perpic-prpic|11 October 2026|notes/krivi-put-antonija-perpic-1859-read-from-the-image.md
krivi-put-baptism-1861-stephanus-perpic||krivi-put-baptism-1861-stephanus-perpic-page.jpg|Krivi Put, 13/16 December 1861 — Stephanus Perpić, son of Joannes and Lucia Perpić, house 136|Krivi Put births 1847–1884 (DGS 5494757, FamilySearch waypoint 9R28-DP8)|image 78, left-hand page (printed page 134): entry 109, the fifth row, «10bris 1861» (December)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-RNXH|«13. 10bris 1861 [born], 16. 10bris 1861 [baptised], Stephanus Perpić, Joannes Perpić & Lucia Perpić, Krivi put No 136». 10bris is December: the entries on the page run 30 November, 1, 7, 13, 13, 26 and 29 December, then «Annus 1862». Names ahnentafel 14 and 15 and the house; the tree's 13 October is wrong.|joannis-perpic,lucia|11 October 2026|notes/stephanus-perpic-was-born-in-december-1861.md
senj-marriage-1885-papic-perpic|senj-marriage-1885-papic-perpic-right.jpg|senj-marriage-1885-papic-perpic-left.jpg|Senj, 3 May 1885 — Josip Papić and Antonia Perpić (parents: Juraj Papa & Matia Pilipić; Ivan Perpić & Luca rođena Perpić)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1859–1920 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-N3F)|image 196, a two-page spread: the LEFT page (printed 191) has the couple, places and ages, the RIGHT page (printed p. 192) the parents, witnesses and priest; the entry is no. 5, the middle row of both|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-17PK|Left: «5. 1885 dne 3 Svibnja · Josip Papić, bremenar, Senj, 27, neoženjen · Antonia Perpić, Krivi put / Senj, 25 [?]». Right: parents «Juraj Papa težak i Matia rođena Pilipić» and «Ivan Perpić seljak i Luca rođena Perpić», witnesses Franjo Perpić and Tomo Perpić, priest Mirko Babić kapelan. Names ahnentafel 12, 13, 14 and 15 and gives Lucia's maiden name as Perpić; the bride's age figure is blotted and read at one zoom.|josip-anton-papic,antonija-tonka-perpic-prpic,georgius-juraj-joannis-papa-antic-papic,matia-matthea-pilipic,joannis-perpic,lucia|11 October 2026|notes/reading-2026-09-13-familysearch.md
senj-marriage-1888-kozina-boras|senj-marriage-1888-kozina-boras-right.jpg|senj-marriage-1888-kozina-boras-left.jpg|Senj, 12 January 1888 — Martin Kozina of Kranj and Angjelika Boras|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1859–1920 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-N3F)|image 214, a two-page spread: the LEFT page (printed 210) has the couple, origin, domicile and ages, the RIGHT page (printed p. 209) the parents, witnesses and priest; the entry is no. 1, the top row of both|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-1WMS|Left: «1. 1888 dne 12 Siječnja · Martin Kozina, trgovac · Kranjska župa sv. Martina kod Kranjburg [Kranj] · Senj · rim. kat. · 47 · neoženjen — Angjelika Boras, šivačica · Senj · 30 · neudata». Right: parents «Gertruda Kozina, posjednica» (property-owner, with a dash where the father would be) and «Josip Boras, gradski stražar, i Maria rođena Kabalin»; witnesses Mile Crnković, trgovac, and Ivan Boras; priest Mirko Babić, kapelan; banns dispensed (read on 7 January 1888). The page that names Martin Kozina's origin as the parish of Kranj–Šmartin.|martin-martinus-kosina,angelika-boras|11 October 2026|notes/martin-kozina-came-from-carniola.md
senj-marriage-1913-nagoda-blazevic|senj-marriage-1913-nagoda-blazevic-left.jpg|senj-marriage-1913-nagoda-blazevic-right.jpg|Senj, 5 October 1913 — Josip Nagoda and Tereza Blažević, born 23 October 1888, of Krmpote|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1859–1920 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-N3F)|image 331, a two-page spread: the LEFT page (printed p. 326) has the couple, origin, domicile and birth dates, the RIGHT page the parents, witnesses and priest; the entry is no. 23, the last row of both|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-178S|Left: «23. 1913 listopada 5 · Nagoda Josip, [occupation] · Blažević Tereza, radnica u tvornici duhana u Senju · Krmpote · born 1888 23/10, unmarried». Right: the bride's parents «Pavao Blažević i Marija rođ. Tomljanović, poljodjelci iz župe sv. Jakov Krmpote». Confirms the tree's birth date for Tereza (23 October 1888) and names her parents; Pavao and Marija are ahnentafel 4's brother and sister-in-law, not direct ancestors.|terezija-tereza-blazevic|11 October 2026|notes/reading-2026-09-10.md
senj-marriage-1918-potocnjak-blazevic|senj-marriage-1918-potocnjak-blazevic-left.jpg|senj-marriage-1918-potocnjak-blazevic-right.jpg|Senj, 1 April 1918 — Vinko Potočnjak and Antonija Blažević, born 12 May 1884|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1859–1920 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-N3F)|image 353, a two-page spread: the LEFT page (printed p. 348) has the couple, the RIGHT page the parents, witnesses and priest; the entry is no. 5, the bottom row of both|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-1QBL|Left: «5. 1918 travnja 1 · Potočnjak Vinko [occupation], widower [read at one zoom], b. 1888 4/4 · Blažević Antonija, nadglednica u tvornici duhana, Senj, b. 1884 12/5, unmarried». Right: parents «Blažević Pavao i Marija rođ. Tomljanović, poljodjelci iz župe Krmpote», witnesses Josip Nagoda and Franjo Blažević, priest Josip Benac; banns read three times. The birth «1884 12/5» is the register's, where the tree says 17 May.|antonija-blazevic|11 October 2026|notes/reading-2026-09-10.md
senj-marriage-1919-matijevic-blazevic|senj-marriage-1919-matijevic-blazevic-left.jpg|senj-marriage-1919-matijevic-blazevic-right.jpg|Senj, 12 May 1919 — Viktor Matijević and Katica Blažević, of Krmpote|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1859–1920 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-N3F)|image 360, a two-page spread: the LEFT page (printed p. 355) has the couple, the RIGHT page the parents, witnesses and priest; the entry is no. 18, the fourth row from the foot of the left page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-176N|Left: «18. 1919 12 svibnja · Viktor Matijević [occupation], Senj · Katica Blažević, radnica u tvornici duhana, Krmpote / Senj, b. 1885 19/10». Right: the bride's parents «Pavao Blažević i Marija rođ. Tomljanović» and the groom's «Mate Matijević i Lucija rođ. Tomljanović». Confirms the tree's birth date for Katica.|katica-blazevic|11 October 2026|notes/reading-2026-09-10.md
senj-marriage-1919-kosina-blazevic|senj-marriage-1919-kosina-blazevic-left.jpg|senj-marriage-1919-kosina-blazevic-right.jpg|Senj, 20 November 1919 — Pavao Kosina and Anka Blažević (and, on 24 November, Antun Kosina)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1859–1920 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-N3F)|image 364, a two-page spread: the LEFT page (printed p. 359) has the couples, the RIGHT page the parents, witnesses and priest; the entries are no. 44 (the top row) and no. 46 (the third row)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-174V|Left: «44. 1919 studenoga 20 · Pavao Kosina, trgovac, Senj, b. 1894 [day] · Anka Blažević, radnica u tvornici duhana, Otočac [?]/Senj, b. 1893» and «46. studenoga 24 · Antun Kosina, trgovac · Anka Kasnić? …». Right: both grooms' parents «+ Martin Kozina i Anđelika r. Boras»; Anka's «Juraj Blažević i Tereza r. Žubrinić» (ahnentafel 4 and 5). Names the same widow Anđelika Boras on two entries of one page.|anka-blazevic,pavao-kosina,angelika-boras|11 October 2026|notes/martin-kozina-came-from-carniola.md
senj-death-1886-matija-pilipic||senj-death-1886-matija-pilipic-page.jpg|Senj, 9 February 1886 — Matija Pilepić, wife of Vicko Pilepić, aged 78|Senj deaths (Umrli) 1859–1907 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-K6D)|image 370, left-hand page: entry no. 13, the sixth row (the page is headed by the year 1886; entries of 29 January to 9 February)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-1HVP|«13. 1886 dne 9 veljače · Matija Pilepić, žena · Vicko Pilepić, fin. stražar u miru, njezin muž · Karlobag [birthplace] · Senj · rim. kat. · 78». Ahnentafel 27's death, naming her husband (ahnentafel 26) with his occupation. A printed Latin-and-Croatian table, read at about 3x.|matia-mathiam-georgiam-uroda,vicentius-andreas-vincent-pilipic|11 October 2026|notes/senj-1886-matia-uroda.md
senj-death-1897-vicko-pilipic||senj-death-1897-vicko-pilipic-page.jpg|Senj, 14 November 1897 — Vicko Pilepić, retired financial guard, widower, «navodno 93»|Senj deaths (Umrli) 1859–1907 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-K6D)|image 513, left-hand page (printed p. 98): entry no. 70, the eighth row, «1897 studenoga 14»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-14RR|«70. 1897 studenoga 14 · Vicko Pilepić, finanse nadmernar [finan. nadzornik?] u miru · Udovac · Karlobag · Senj · rim. kat. · navodno 93 god.». Ahnentafel 26's death; the clerk marks the age as hearsay («navodno»), and the page gives no cause in this crop.|vicentius-andreas-vincent-pilipic|11 October 2026|notes/senj-1886-matia-uroda.md
senj-death-1907-toma-blazevic||senj-death-1907-toma-blazevic-page.jpg|Senj, 26 July 1907 — Toma Blažević, day-labourer, widower of the late Tereza, aged 69|Senj deaths (Umrli) 1859–1907 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-K6D)|image 640, left-hand page (printed p. 225): entry no. 60, the fifth row, «1907 srpnja 26»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-14XR|«60. 1907 srpnja 26 · Blažević Toma, nadničar · Udovac iza pok. Tereze · [born] sv. Jakov Krmpote · Senj · Rk. · 69 god.». Ahnentafel 8's death: the register names his late wife Tereza (ahnentafel 9), putting her death before 1907. The cause column is on the right-hand page, which was not captured.|toma-tomislav-blazevic,tereza-pecanic|11 October 2026|notes/senj-1886-matia-uroda.md
otocac-baptism-1835-maria-oreskovic||otocac-baptism-1835-maria-oreskovic-page.jpg|Otočac, 8 September 1835 — Maria Catharina Orešković, daughter of Marcus Oreskovich «adoptatus Sekula» and Lucia née Sekula, Dubrava 29|Otočac births 1834–1846 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-N3B; printed Latin table)|image 13, right-hand half of the image (printed page number 10): entry no. 41, the second row, «1835 Septembris die 8va»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-GRSC|«Maria Catharina, filia legitima, Confiniarius ex Pago Dubrava N° D.29, Marcus Oreskovich, adoptatus [Sekula], et Lucia uxor ejus nata Sekula, Catholici», sponsors and the baptising chaplain Matthaeus Mattasich in the next columns; protocol no. 41. Ahnentafel 21's baptism, naming her parents (ahnentafel 42 and 43) and the house.|maria-catharina-oreskovic-oreskovic,marcus-oreskovic-oreskovic,lucia-sekula|11 October 2026|notes/eight-readings-that-named-nobody.md
otocac-death-1838-toma-zubrinic||otocac-death-1838-toma-zubrinic-page.jpg|Otočac, 4 January 1838 — Thomas Xubrinich, border-guardsman, of Šumećica No. 2, aged 70|Otočac births 1846–1858 and deaths 1834–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-Y4C)|image 117, right-hand half (printed page 45): entry no. 3 of «Anno Domini 1838», the third row below the year heading|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-PVR4|«1838 Januarii die 4ta · Thomas Xubrinich, Incola Otočanus Centuriae Confiniariae, ex Pago Shumechiza N° 2 · aet. 70 · Senectutis debilitas · … Matthaeus Mattasich, Administrator [priest]; protocol no. 3». Ahnentafel 40's death; the house, Šumećica 2, is the house of his son's and grandson's later baptisms.|toma-zubrinic|11 October 2026|notes/otocac-toma-zubrinic-1838.md
otocac-death-1849-marija-findric||otocac-death-1849-marija-findric-page.jpg|Otočac, 29 July 1849 — Maria Žubrinić, widow, aged 69, buried in the parish vault|Otočac births 1846–1858 and deaths 1834–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-Y4C)|image 167, left-hand half (printed page 153): entry no. 53, the third row, «Leta 1849 dne 29 Srpnja»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-PVHR|«Leta 1849 dne 29 Srpnja preminula je · Maria Žubrinić, udovica · 69 · slaboća starosti po dokazu liečnika · sa svetimi otajstvi umirućih providjena · u župničkoj grobnici»; protocol no. 53. Ahnentafel 41's death, entered under her married name; the register does not give her maiden name (Findrić), which comes from other documents. Read at about 3x in a Croatian-language table.|marija-findric|11 October 2026|notes/otocac-marija-findric-1849.md
otocac-baptism-1856-stephanus-zubrinic||otocac-baptism-1856-stephanus-zubrinic-page.jpg|Otočac, 3 July 1856 — Stephanus, son of Nicolaus Xubrinich and Anna «nata Štrumbulko», Šumećica No. 2|Otočac births 1846–1858 and deaths 1834–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-Y4C)|image 76, right-hand half (the page after 18 June 1856, printed number 137): entry no. 49, the seventh row, «Anno Domini 1856 die 3 Julii»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-PK2C|«Stephanus, filius legitimus, Romano-Catholicus · Confiniarius ex Pago Shumechiza N° 2 · [father] Nicolaus Xubrinich et [mother] Anna uxor ejus nata Štrumbulko [Strumbulko], Romano-Catholici», baptised by Josephus Mazuranić, parish priest; protocol no. 49. Names ahnentafel 10 and 11 and the house; the mother is entered here with the by-name Štrumbulko and in 1858 as Marić. The surnames are read at one zoom from a dense Latin table; the entry was found by the date and house number.|nicolaus-zubrinic-xubrinic,ana-shambul-maric,stephanus-zubrinic-1856|11 October 2026|notes/ana-maric-plan.md
kranj-baptism-1841-martin-kosina|kranj-baptism-1841-martin-kosina-right.jpg|kranj-baptism-1841-martin-kosina-left.jpg|Kranj–Šmartin, 16 November 1841 — Martin, born at Oberfeichting (Zgornje Bitnje) No. 9, to Gertraud Kosina, no father named|Krstna knjiga Kranj–Šmartin 1832–1870 (Nadškofijski arhiv Ljubljana, Matricula sig. 00886)|book page 64 (viewer pg=65, a spread): the LEFT page is headed «Jahr 1841» with the month «November»; the entry is its ninth row (Oberfeichting, house 9, name Martin); the RIGHT page carries the same row's parents, godparents and priest|https://data.matricula-online.eu/sl/slovenia/ljubljana/kranj-smartin/00886/?pg=65|Left: «Jahr 1841 · November · born and baptised 16 November · Oberfeichting · 9 · Martin · katholisch · Knaben»; right, the same row: the Vater cell is empty and the Mutter cell reads «Gertraud Kosina». The tick in the Unehelich column is read in the working note, not re-checked in this reduced image. The two photographs are the viewer's own, reduced; row counting (ninth on each page) is how the two halves are matched.|martin-martinus-kosina|11 October 2026|notes/martin-kozina-was-born-at-zgornje-bitnje.md
kranj-marriage-1833-kosinar-labornik|kranj-marriage-1833-kosinar-labornik-right.jpg|kranj-marriage-1833-kosinar-labornik-left.jpg|Kranj–Šmartin, 6 January 1833 — Johann Kosinar, Häusler of Oberfeichting 9, and Luzia Labornik|Poročna knjiga / Trauungsbuch Kranj–Šmartin 1816–1855 (Nadškofijski arhiv Ljubljana, Matricula sig. 00899)|viewer pg=37, a spread (book page 35): the first row of the table, headed 1833; the LEFT page has the groom, the bride and their ages, the RIGHT page the parents of each, the witnesses and the priest|https://data.matricula-online.eu/sl/slovenia/ljubljana/kranj-smartin/00899/?pg=37|Left: «1833 · 6. Jänner · Obern feichting · 9 · Johann Kosinar, Häusler · katholisch · 30 · ledig» and the bride «Obern feichting · 3 · Luzia Labornik · 38 · ledig». Right: the groom's parents «Franz Kosinar, Häusler» and «Mina Tomshan, Häuslerin» (read at one zoom), the bride's parents «Mathes Labornik, Häusler» and «Gertraud Magnishan, Häuslerin». The groom's father's name is the evidence that ties this household to the 1814 baptism of a Franz Kosinar. The occupation word (Häusler / Hüblar) and the parents' names are as read in the working note from the page at higher zoom; in these reduced images the occupation word is ambiguous and the page is cropped, not transcribed.|martin-martinus-kosina|11 October 2026|notes/martin-kozina-was-born-at-zgornje-bitnje.md
kranj-marriage-1800-kosinar-dortschen|kranj-marriage-1800-kosinar-dortschen-right.jpg|kranj-marriage-1800-kosinar-dortschen-left.jpg|Kranj–Šmartin, 27 October 1800 — Franz Kosinar of Feichting (house 10), aged 24, and Maria Dortschen, aged 20|Poročna knjiga / Trauungsbuch Kranj–Šmartin 1780–1815 (Nadškofijski arhiv Ljubljana, Matricula sig. 00901)|viewer pg=33, a spread: the LEFT page is headed 1800 and runs June–November; the entry is its eighth row («Den 27ten» under October, Feichting, house 10, groom's age 24); the RIGHT page carries the same row's bride (age 20), her parents and the witnesses|https://data.matricula-online.eu/sl/slovenia/ljubljana/kranj-smartin/00901/?pg=33|Left: «1800 · October · den 27ten · Feichting b. St. Joh. · 10 · Franz Kosinar · katholisch · 24 · ledig». Right, the eighth row: the bride «Maria Dortschen · katholisch · 20 · ledig», her parents, the witnesses (one is Matthäus Kosinar per the working note) and the priest. The two halves are matched by counting ten rows on each page. German Kurrent at the viewer's default size; the names beyond the groom's and the ages are read in the working note at higher zoom, not from these reduced images.|franz-kosinar,maria-mina-dortschen,matthaeus-kosinar|11 October 2026|notes/martin-kozina-was-born-at-zgornje-bitnje.md
kranj-baptism-1814-gertraud-kosinar|kranj-baptism-1814-gertraud-kosinar-right.jpg|kranj-baptism-1814-gertraud-kosinar-left.jpg|Kranj–Šmartin, 18 March 1814 — Gertraud, daughter of Franz Kosinar (Hüblar) and Maria Dortschen, house 10|Krstna knjiga / Taufbuch Kranj–Šmartin 1812–1831 (Nadškofijski arhiv Ljubljana, Matricula sig. 00885)|viewer pg=15, a spread (book page about 28): the LEFT page is headed «1814» with the dates March–April; the entry is its third row («Den 18 März», house 10, Gertraud); the RIGHT page is the facing half (godparents, priest and place columns), whose rows are not individually matched here|https://data.matricula-online.eu/sl/slovenia/ljubljana/kranj-smartin/00885/?pg=15|Left: «1814 · Den 18 März · 10 · Gertraud · ehelich · Vater: Franz Kosinar, Hüblar · Mutter: Maria Dortschen». The right-hand page has the godparent and priest columns; it is kept for completeness, is hard to read at this size, and its rows are not matched to the left-hand rows. Gertraud was Martin Kozina's mother (she bore him in 1841 at 27). Reduced viewer images; the transcription is in the found-person row.|gertraud-gertruda-kosina,franz-kosinar,maria-mina-dortschen|11 October 2026|notes/martin-kozina-was-born-at-zgornje-bitnje.md
selce-death-1829-joannes-antic||selce-death-1829-joannes-antic-page.jpg|Selce, 13 March 1829 — Joannes Antich «Papa», aged 64, house 51|Selce deaths (Umrli) 1816–1886 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-N32)|image 18 (a single page, headed «Liber Defunctorum», months of 1829): the third entry, «Dis 13 Martii 1829», house number 51|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-1QQL|«Dis 13 Martii 1829 · 51 · Joannes Antich Papa obiit Annorum 64, omnibus morientium SS. provisus, et statuto tempore in loco consueto per me Vincentium Kombel Parochum loci sepultus est». Ahnentafel 48's death; the house, 51, is the house of his son's baptism (1838) and marriage (1835).|joannis-antic|11 October 2026|notes/selce-antic-1829-papa.md
selce-death-1850-osip-antic||selce-death-1850-osip-antic-page.jpg|Selce, 21 October 1850 — Osip Antić, labourer, aged 44, of cholera|Selce deaths (Umrli) 1816–1886 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-N32)|image 54, right-hand page (printed page 99), headed «Mens. 8bris 1850»: the entry «Letta 850 na 21. 8bra», in the lower third of the list, with the cause column «Od kolere»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-13PY|«Letta 850 na 21. 8bra · Preminu Osip Antić težak i Mare kćer · 44 · Od kolere». The page is a cholera casualty list: 156 deaths in the year, entered one a line. Ahnentafel 24's death; the row is found by the date and by the name Antić; the house number is crowded and not re-read in this image.|josephum-antic|11 October 2026|notes/selce-cholera-1850.md
selce-death-1882-maria-antic||selce-death-1882-maria-antic-page.jpg|Selce, 6 July 1882 — Maria Antić, widow of the late Josip, daughter of Juraj and Mara Jeličić, aged 73|Selce deaths (Umrli) 1816–1886 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-N32)|image 111, left-hand page (printed page 144), headed «Mens. Februarii 1882» running to July: entry no. 21, «dne 6 Srpnja», house 29|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-1357|«21 · dne 6 Srpnja 1882 · 29 · Udova Maria Antić, supruga pok. Josipa, kći Jurja i Mare Jeličić · R. Katolikinja»; buried 7 July. Ahnentafel 25's death, naming her parents (Juraj and Mara, who would be ahnentafel 50 and 51) and her husband. Printed Croatian table, read at about 2x.|maria-jellicic|11 October 2026|notes/selce-deaths.md
selce-baptism-1806-josephus-antic||selce-baptism-1806-josephus-antic-page.jpg|Selce, 14 March 1806 — Josephus, son of Joannes and Martha Antich «Papa», house 44|Selce births (Rođeni) 1778–1861 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2M-BZF)|image 47, left-hand page, headed «Anno Dni 1806»: the fifth entry, «Die 14 Martii Aº 1806», house number 44 in the margin (the right-hand page carries a Latin note labelled VRBNIK)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-596J-2|«Die 14 Martii Aº 1806 baptizavi ego Michael Kombol C.L. infantem lege natam patre Joanne, Matre Martha Antich Papa, nomine Josephum, susceptoribus conjugibus Judice Mathia Jellichich et ejus consorte Margarita». Ahnentafel 24's baptism, with the by-name Papa underlined. The page header reads 1806; the priest signs C.L. (Capellanus Loci).|josephum-antic|11 October 2026|notes/vrbnik-or-selce.md
selce-baptism-1809-maria-jellicic||selce-baptism-1809-maria-jellicic-page.jpg|Selce, 22 March 1809 — Maria, daughter of Georgius and Margarita Jellichich «dictis Jurešina»|Selce births (Rođeni) 1778–1861 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2M-BZF)|image 57, left-hand page, headed «1809»: entry no. 70, the first on the page, house number 110 in the margin|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-5961-L|«70 · Die 22 Martii Aº 1809 baptizavi ego Michaël Kombol Parochus Loci infantem lege natam patre Georgio, Matre Margarita Jellichich dictis Jurešina, nomine Mariam, susceptoribus adolescente Leopoldo Jellichich et Agnete consorte Vincentii Lonzarich Hel dicti». Ahnentafel 25's baptism; the by-name is underlined. The first entry on the page, so unmistakable.|maria-jellicic|11 October 2026|notes/selce-1809-baptism.md
selce-baptism-1838-gregorius-antic||selce-baptism-1838-gregorius-antic-page.jpg|Selce, 11 March 1838 — Gregorius (read; the son of ahnentafel 24 and 25), house 51|Selce births (Rođeni) 1778–1861 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2M-BZF)|image 186, right-hand page (printed 53), «Annus 1838»: the first entry, «Die 11a Martii 1838», house number 51|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-5963-L|«Die 11a Martii 1838 · 51 · Ego Vincentius Rombal Parochus Loci Baptizavi Gregorium … conjugum Josephi Antich Papa, filii Denati Joannis et [Lon]csarich, et Mariae, filiae Denatorum Georgii et Margarittae». Ahnentafel 12's baptism; the name reads Gregorium here, Georgius elsewhere.|georgius-juraj-joannis-papa-antic-papic|11 October 2026|notes/selce-1838-baptism.md
selce-marriage-1835-antic-jellicic|selce-marriage-1835-antic-jellicic-right.jpg|selce-marriage-1835-antic-jellicic-left.jpg|Selce, 22 November 1835 — Josephus Antich «Papa» and Maria Jellichich, house 51 (entry 81)|Selce marriages (Vjenčani) 1815–1878 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-N35)|image 26, a two-page spread (kept as two images): the LEFT image is the left-hand page, headed «Annus 1835» and running from 22 July; the RIGHT image is the right-hand page (printed 21–22, with the archivist's tab SMEARED INK / RAZLIVENA TINTA), where entry 81, the second numbered entry below the loose slip, is the 22 November marriage of house 51|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-1Q7H|Right-hand page, entry 81 (domus 51), «[Die 22 9bris 1835] · 81 · … Ego Vincentius Rombal Parochus Loci Copulavi Josephum Antich Papa, filium Denati Joannis et Margarittae, cum virgine Maria Jellicich, filia Denatorum Georgii et Margarittae», witnesses beside. The by-name Papa is underlined. Ahnentafel 24 × 25, naming 48, 49, 50 and 51. A loose slip of paper lies over the top left of the right-hand page. The prose is dense Latin, read at about 2x; entry 81 is the one the working note transcribes.|josephum-antic,maria-jellicic,joannis-antic|11 October 2026|notes/selce-1835-marriage.md
senj-baptism-1857-josip-papic||senj-baptism-1857-josip-papic-page.jpg|Senj, 1 November 1857 — Josephus, son of Joannes Papa and Mathia Pilipić (godparents Michael and Catharina Stipančić)|Senj births (Rođeni) 1756–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2M-L27)|image 571, right-hand page (printed 31), the second entry from the foot of the visible part, numbered 117: «Anno Domini 1857 die 1 Novembris»; the entry before it (116) is the baptism of Aloysia Anna on the same date|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-5TBF|«Anno Domini 1857 die [1] Novembris. Ego Joannes Pašić cooperator loci baptizavi Josephum filium legitimum Romano-Catholicum Joannis Papa et ejus uxoris Mathiae Pilipić. Levantibus patrinis: + Michael Stipančić, + Catharina [..]». Ahnentafel 6's baptism, naming his parents (ahnentafel 12 and 13). Read at about 2x; the surname «Papa» is underlined as in Selce.|josip-anton-papic,georgius-juraj-joannis-papa-antic-papic,matia-matthea-pilipic|11 October 2026|notes/reading-2026-09-10.md
karlobag-baptism-1810-matia-uroda||karlobag-baptism-1810-matia-uroda-page.jpg|Karlobag, 23 April 1810 — Mathia Georgia, daughter of Georgius and Maria Uroda (godparents Jacobus Blazevich and Maria, wife of Joannes Uroda)|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1804–1861 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 19, right-hand page, headed «Anno Domini 1810» (book page 10): the entry in the margin «23. [April]», the row directly below the 15 April entry (the one beginning «Vincentiam Mariam…») and directly above the «24» entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-G9V8|«Mathiam Georgiam hodie natam a Georgio et Maria Uroda conjugibus hujus Parochiae baptizavi. Patrini fuerunt Jacobus Blazevich et Maria conjux Joannis Uroda». Ahnentafel 27's baptism: parents ahnentafel 54 and 55. The godfather is a Blazevich of Karlobag. Latin cursive read at about 1.5x; the left page of this image is headed 1809.|matia-mathiam-georgiam-uroda,georgius-juraj-joannis-papa-antic-papic,mariam-gerkacs-gergacs|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-1810-uroda.md
karlobag-baptism-1838-matia-pilipic||karlobag-baptism-1838-matia-pilipic-page.jpg|Karlobag, 18 September 1838 — Matthea, daughter of the chamber shipmaster Vincentius Pilipich and Mathea Uroda|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1804–1861 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 58, left-hand page (book page 88), headed «Anno Domini 1838»: the second entry from the foot, margin «Die 18 Septemb.», just above «Die 20 Septemb.»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-G9BN|«Cooperator Carolus Perzevich baptizavit Mattheam filiam legitimam cammeralis nautae Vincentii Pilipich et Matheae Uroda conjugum hujus civitatis. Patrini fuerunt Antonius Kuchulian … et Oliva filia dicti Josephi Pilipich mercatoris». Ahnentafel 13's baptism, naming her parents (ahnentafel 26 and 27). The line is dense Latin at about 1.5x; the title cammeralis nauta (chamber seaman) is read here from the left-page line the working note transcribes.|matia-matthea-pilipic,vicentius-andreas-vincent-pilipic,matia-mathiam-georgiam-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-1838-pilipic.md
karlobag-baptism-1763-smojver-uroda-godparents||karlobag-baptism-1763-smojver-uroda-godparents-page.jpg|Karlobag, 2 November 1763 — Georgius and his wife Maria Uroda stand godparents to Carolus, son of Paulus and Ursula Smojver|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 149, left-hand page (book page 266), headed «Anno Domini 1763»: the first entry on the page, «Die 2da Novembris»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L99V-6|«Die 2da Novembris. Josephus Suvich Parochus baptizavi Carolum filium Pauli et Ursulae Smoivar, levantibus e sacro Fonte patrinis Georgio ac ejus conjuge Maria Uroda». The first time this archive has seen Georgius and Maria Uroda together as a couple in a register, six months before the baptism of their first known child; the godchild's family name is written «Smoivar», read as Smojver (the surname of ahnentafel 212 and 106) but not proved to be the same family. The husband's surname is not written, only the wife's, and the page does not say these are ahnentafel 108 and 109.|georgius-uroda,maria-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1764-dominicus-uroda||karlobag-baptism-1764-dominicus-uroda-page.jpg|Karlobag, 6 May 1764 — Joannes Dominicus, son of Georgius and Maria Uroda (godparents Antonio Barach of Šibenik and Vincentia, wife of Joannes Margvart)|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 151, left-hand page (book page 270), headed «Anno Domini 1764»: the second entry, «Die 6ta May»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L998-Y|«Die 6ta May. Jose: Suvich Parochus baptizavi Joannem Dominicum filium Georgij et Maria Uroda, levantibus a sacro Fonte patrinis Antonio Barach e [Šibenik] ac Vincentia conjuge Joannis Margvart». The child's name is JOANNES DOMINICUS, where the index has «Dominicum». The first known child of ahnentafel 108 and 109; one godfather is from Šibenik. Read at about 1.5x.|dominicus-uroda,georgius-uroda,maria-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1750-04-jerolima-uroda||karlobag-baptism-1750-jerolima-uroda-line.png|Karlobag, 23 April 1750 — Jerolima, widow (udova) Uroda, godmother|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 112, left-hand page (book page 200, «Lěto 1750»): the entry of «Dan 23 Apla», a crop of three lines|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L99N-1|Croatian-language baptism entry; the godparents are «Tadia Kovacevich i Jerolima udova Uroda» (read at about 2x). The first appearance of Jerolima, a widow named Uroda, in these pages.|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1751-04-jerolima-uroda||karlobag-baptism-1751-jerolima-uroda-line.png|Karlobag, 25 April 1751 — Jerolima, widow Uroda, godmother|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 114, right-hand page (book page 205 head, «Dan 25 Aprila 1751»): the first entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L9SN-C|«… kumi Pop Miko Martin … i udova Jerolima Uroda»: the priest's own kin stand with her. Read at about 2x.|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1752-03-12-jure-uroda||karlobag-baptism-1752-03-12-jure-uroda-line.png|Karlobag, 12 March 1752 — «Jure Uroda» and Jerolima, widow of Dume Uroda, godparents|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 116, left-hand page (book page 208, «Lěta 1752»): the entry of «Dan 12 Marca», fourth from the top|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L9SP-G|«… Martina i … Maxuran. Bihu kumi Jure Uroda i Gjerolima udova [Sokoić] Dume Uroda». A man called JURE URODA (Georgius) is godfather with the widow of a Dume (Dominicus) Uroda. The word between «udova» and «Dume» is read as Sokoić and is uncertain.|dume-uroda,georgius-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1752-03-21-dume-uroda||karlobag-baptism-1752-03-21-dume-uroda-line.png|Karlobag, 21 March 1752 — Jerolina, widow [Sokoić] «Dume Uroda», godmother|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 116, left-hand page (book page 208), the entry of «Dan 21 Detto» (21 March) at the foot|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L9SP-G|«… Ivana … bihu kumi Lorenco Curtellini [od Sibenika?] i Gjerolina udova Sokoić Dume Uroda». The widow is named with her husband's name Dume Uroda.|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1752-04-03-jure-uroda||karlobag-baptism-1752-04-03-jure-uroda-line.png|Karlobag, 3 April 1752 — «Jure» and Jerolina, widow [Sokoić] Dume Uroda, godparents|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 116, right-hand page (book page 209, «Dan 2 Aprila 1752»): the second entry, «Dan 3 Aprila»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L9SP-G|«Dan 3 Aprila … sina Pavla i Franice Bevandich. Bihu kumi Jure i Gjerolina udova [Sokoić] Dume Uroda». Here the godfather is written only «Jure»; a word «Uroda» appears to be written over the line above it, and I read this as the same Jure Uroda as on 12 March; not certain.|dume-uroda,georgius-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1745-08-marta-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1745-08-marta-uroda-line.png||Karlobag, 11 August 1745 — a daughter (Marta Franceskina, as read) of Dume Uroda and Jerolina|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 100, left-hand page (book page 178): the entry «Na 11 Agusta 1745», about two-thirds of the way down.|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L9SG-2|«Na 11 Agusta 1745. Ja Pop Osip Xurich kersti cher Dume urode i xene Jerolime imenom Marta Franceskina [read at one zoom]. Bi kum Don Josep iz Kontra a kuma Lucia xena Uvje Xurica». The only baptism found of a child of Dume Uroda; it names his wife as Jerolina. Croatian text, read at about 3x; the child's second name is uncertain.|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1744-05-son-of-dume-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1744-05-son-of-dume-uroda-line.png||Karlobag, 10 May 1744 — a son of Dume Uroda and Jerolime (name read as «Gratiova», uncertain)|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 96, left-hand page (book page 170): the entry «Na 10 Maia 1744», at the foot of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L9S6-W|«Na 10 Maia 1744. Korstih sina Dume urode i njegove [že]ne Jerolime imenom [Gratiova?]. Bi kum Dno Antonio Alfier [?] Johetoni [?] Gnor … a kuma Gospodjena Mi[…] Agnerin neputa …». Baptism of a SON of Dume Uroda and Jerolima; the child's name is not read with confidence. Croatian text, about 3x; the godparents' names are a poor reading. THE FAMILYSEARCH INDEX READS THIS CHILD AS «GIAKOVA» (JAKOV, JACOBUS) — a son named Jakov, so not Georgius; found 11 October 2026 under the spelling «Urode».|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1742-son-of-dume-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1742-son-of-dume-uroda-line.png|karlobag-baptism-1742-son-of-dume-uroda-name.png|Karlobag, mid-1742 — a son of Dume Uroda and his wife, the name read as «… Juria» (possibly Jurja/Georgius; not secure)|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 91, right-hand page (book page 161, «Na … Maja 1742» at its head): the last entry on the page, «Na 4 [month, read Ajmilo/Aprila?] 1742»; the month word is unclear, and it follows the entries of 3 and 4 June 1742, so it is probably a later 4th (July?)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L9S5-D|«Na 4: [month?] 1742. Korstih sina Dume urode i njegove xene [Jerolime?] imenom [Cvidora?] Juria. Bi kum Milo Bulinc(?) a kuma Marija xena Martina Vorbanovića». The child is a SON of Dume Uroda; the given name is two words, the second read as «Juria»/«Furia». Read at the page's full resolution; the first word of the name and the month are not read with confidence. RE-READ AT HIGHER MAGNIFICATION (second image): «Na 4: [Ajmila/Apmila, month not read] 1742 · [K]orstih sina Dume urode i njegove xene … imenom [Gvidora/Evidora] Juria [Furia], bi kum Milo Bulinc … a kuma Marija xena Martina …». «Sina Dume urode» (son of Dume Uroda) is clear; the child's name is two words, the first read as Gvidora/Evidora and the second as Juria/Furia; the month word is not Aprila (the entry follows 3 and 4 June) and is not read.|dume-uroda,georgius-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1739-12-franica-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1739-12-franica-uroda-line.png||Karlobag, mid-December 1739 — Franica (as read), daughter of Dume Uroda and his wife EVA|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 82, right-hand page (book page 147, headed «Na 11 Xbra 1739»): the entry «Na 12 [or 17] Stoga», about a third of the way down|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L9SZ-B|«Na 12 Stoga: Korstih ja Andrij Kolekar Plovan cher Dume urode i njegove xene Eve imenom Franica. Bi kum Mathio Milkovich a kuma [..] xena Pave Samonicha». A daughter named Franica to Dume Uroda and a wife named EVA — three years before Jerolina is Dume's wife in the same book. Read at about 3x; the month word is read as «Stoga» (December).|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1734-03-dume-uroda-horaca-eva-line|karlobag-baptism-1734-03-dume-uroda-horaca-eva-line.png||Karlobag, 8 March 1734 — a child (name read as Dominico) of Dume Uroda, «alias Horaca» (as read), and his wife EVA|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 61, left-hand page (book page 106, headed «Na 14 Febora 1734»): the entry «Na 8 Marca 1734», about two-thirds of the way down|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L9SF-W|«Na 8 Marca 1734: Krstih sina Dume Urode alliti Kovaca [first read as Horaca] i njegove xene Eve imenom Dominico [?]. Bi kum Gior. Angelo Bakj[..] a kuma Marica xena Jane Mega [?]». A baptism to Dume Uroda and a wife named EVA five years before the Franica of December 1739 — the earliest child of this couple seen. The by-name after «alliti» was first read as Horaca; re-read at 3x on 11 October 2026 it is «kovaca» — a smith's by-name (kovač), which would tie Dume to the many Kovačević of Karlobag. Read at about 3x; child's name and godparents' surnames are not firm.|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1733-01-antona-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1733-01-antona-uroda-line.png||Karlobag, 16 January 1733 — Antona, daughter of «Sime» (index) or Dume (?) Uroda and his wife EVA|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 57, left-hand page (book page 100, headed «Na 1 Genvara 1733»): the third entry, «Na 16 Genvara 1733»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L937-1|«Na 16 Genvara 1733: Ja Pop Andrij Kolekar Plovan krstih sina [Sime / Dume?] urode i njegove xene Eve imenom Antona. Bi kum Andro Kum[anovich?] soldat od Tortice … a kuma …». The FamilySearch index reads this father as SIME Uroda (baptism 16 January 1733, parents Sime Uroda and Eva). The first letter of the father's name is not firm: it may be a Dume with the capital misread. If it is Dume, Dume and Eva had Antona in January 1733, a child in March 1734 and Franica in December 1739. The same page is repeated on image 56 (duplicate frame).|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1737-01-eva-kuma-wife-of-dume-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1737-01-eva-kuma-wife-of-dume-uroda-line.png||Karlobag, 12 January 1737 — «kuma Eva xena Dume urode» (godmother, wife of Dume Uroda)|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1770 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 70, right-hand page, lower half: the entry «Na 12 Jenora 1737», third from the foot|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L9SC-Z|«Na 12 Jenora 1737: Krstih cher Jve Berondicha [?] njegove xene Eve … ime Gasparina. Bi kum Mato Mato[vich?] a kuma Eva xena Dume urode.» Not a baptism of the Urodas' child: it shows Eva as Dume Uroda's wife in January 1737, between the 1734 baptism and the Franica of December 1739, so the Eva of 1733–39 is one woman. Read at about 3x.|dume-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-marriage-1739-06-svjata-simona-uroda-sibenik|karlobag-marriage-1739-06-svjata-simona-uroda-sibenik-line.png||Karlobag, 7 June 1739 — marriage of Martin Svjata and Simona, daughter of the late DUME URODA «od Šibenika» (of Šibenik)|Karlobag marriages (Vjenčani) 1736–1804 (DGS 5481649, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-HZK)|image 279, left-hand page: the entry headed «Dan 7: Junija», after the year heading «Letta 1739» and the entry of 28 May|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-GHW|«Dan 7: Junija. Andrij Kollekar Plovan sakupih u S. Matrimonij Martina Svjata [Sviata?] y Simonu pokoi[nog] Dume urode od Sibenika. Biha svidoki Tavia Kovacevich y Bartul Misich.» The wording matches the book's formula for a bride «Heer pokoi X» (daughter of the late X), though the word «Heer» is not written here. So: a DUME URODA from Šibenik, dead by June 1739, with a daughter Simona. The living Dume Uroda of the Karlobag baptisms (wife Eva, daughter Franica baptised December 1739) cannot be this man, so this is a second Dume Uroda — possibly the living Dume's father or another relation, not established — and the first sight of the family as Dalmatian. Read at about 3x.|dume-uroda-of-sibenik|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
drnis-baptism-1770-josepha-uroda|drnis-baptism-1770-josepha-uroda-line.png||Drniš, 13 March 1770 — Josepha, daughter of PAMPAO Uroda and Mariana Bachi, both soldiers|Drniš baptisms, 1770 (FamilySearch Croatia, Church Books 1516–1994, reference 68; index record 1:1:QKMG-2TSF)|the left-hand page of the opening, the second entry from the top, headed «Die 13 Martii 1770»; the margin names her «Josepha Uroda»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-T9MF-4|«Ego Fr. Josephus Jakick Capuc. Baptizavi infantem natam sub die primae ejusdem [mensis], ex legitimis Conjugibus Pampao Uroda, et Mariana Bachi, Militum [Illustrissimi?] Domini Capi[tanei] Dulatti [?]. Cui nomen impositum Josepha. Patrinus fuit Stephanus Susszek et Catharina uxor Francisci Pasquali, omnes Militas.» A Franciscan baptises a girl born on the 1st of the month. The father is written PAMPAO (the index reads «Janpao»; 1778 reads «Pompio»), the mother's surname Bachi, and the household is a SOLDIER's, as are the godparents: a military family at Drniš, not a Karlobag one. The words after «Militum» (the captain's name) are not firm. Read at about 4x.|pompeo-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
drnis-baptism-1778-julia-magdalena-uroda|drnis-baptism-1778-julia-magdalena-uroda-line.png||Drniš, 26 August 1778 — Julia Magdalena, daughter of CAPORAL Pompeo Uroda and Maria Anna Bachi|Drniš baptisms, 1778 (FamilySearch Croatia, Church Books 1516–1994, reference 112; index record 1:1:QKMG-2VW7)|left-hand page of the opening, the entry headed «Die 26 Augusti 1778» that follows the first of two entries of that date|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-T93P-D|«Die 26 Augusti 1778. Ego Fr. Elias Soldich Parochus Darnisii baptizavi infantem natum sub die 23 ejusdem, ex legitimis Conjugibus Caporal Pompeo Uroda et Maria Anna Bachi. Cui nomen impositum Julia Magdalena. Patrini fuerunt Domina Magdalena et Dominus Serdar Antonius Nachich hujus Parochiae.» The father is called CAPORAL — a corporal — and the godfather a SERDAR, a Venetian-Dalmatian militia rank: the same soldier household as in 1770, now spelled POMPEO. Read at about 3x.|pompeo-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
drnis-baptism-1780-joseph-uroda|drnis-baptism-1780-joseph-uroda-line.png||Drniš, 23 October 1780 — Joseph, son of Domino CAPORAL POMPEO Uroda and Maria Anna Bauchi, all soldiers|Drniš baptisms, 1780 (FamilySearch Croatia, Church Books 1516–1994, reference 122; index record 1:1:QKMG-2D3D)|right-hand page of the opening, the entry at the top, headed «Die 23 Octobris 1780»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-T93K-L|«Die 23 Octobris 1780. Ego Fr. Elias Soldich Parochus Curae Darnisij baptizavi infantem natum sub die 13 hujus, ex legitimis Conjugibus Domino Caporal Pompeo Uroda et Domina Maria Anna Bauchi. Cui nomen impositum Joseph. Patrinus fuit Dominus Angelus Sarich et Anna Maria …chin, omnes Milites.» THE INDEX READS THE FATHER AS «TOMASO»; THE PAGE READS POMPEO — so the Drniš baptisms of 1770, 1778 and 1780 are one man, Corporal Pompeo (Pampao) Uroda, and his wife Maria Anna Bachi/Bauchi, a soldier's household. Read at about 3x.|pompeo-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1767-petrus-jacobus-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1767-petrus-jacobus-uroda-line.png||Karlobag, 2 July 1767 — Petrus Jacobus, son of Georgius and Maria Uroda; godparents the criminal judge Antonius Dorliga and the wife of Antonius Iurich|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 161, left-hand page (book page 290, headed «Anno Dni 1767»): the first entry, «2 July»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L99P-F|«Ego Joannes Antonius Ivancovich Parochi Administrator baptizavi [Petrum] Jacobum filium legitimum jugalium Georgii et Mariae Uroda natum die 29 [Junii]. Levantibus e sacro fonte Dno Antonio Dorliga, Judice Criminali ac Dna [..]cica conjuge Dni Antonii Iurich.» The line is clipped at the right by the page curvature, so the child's first name and the godmother's own surname are not firm. The father's neighbours are officials, not kin that can be named.|georgius-uroda,maria-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1769-heva-joanna-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1769-heva-joanna-uroda-line.jpg||Karlobag, 28 December 1769 — Heva Joanna, daughter of Georgius and Maria Uroda; godparents the Chancellor Josephus Kumanović and Sancina, wife of Antonius Dorliga|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 173, right-hand page (book page 313, headed «Anno Dni 1769»): the entry «25 Xbris», above the heading «Anno Domini 1770»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L9SQ-F|«Ego Jacobus Mallinarich Capellanus baptizavi Filiam die 28 hujus Mensis natam ex Georgio et Maria Uroda Conjugibus hujus Parochiae, cui impositum est nomen Heva Joanna. Patrini fuerunt Dnus Cancellarius Josephus Kumanovich et Dna Sancina Dorligo Antonij uxor.» (The margin says 25; the text says 28.)|georgius-uroda,maria-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1772-maria-catharina-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1772-maria-catharina-uroda-line.jpg||Karlobag, 29 April 1772 — Maria Catharina, daughter of Georgius and Maria Uroda; godparents the Chancellor Josephus Kumanović and his wife Joanna|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 187, left-hand page, headed «Anno Dni 1772»: the entry «29 ejusdem [Aprilis]», third on the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L99D-Q|«Rendus Dnus Jacobus Mallinarich Capellanus Cesaricensis baptizavit filiam heri natam ex Georgio et Maria Uroda Conjugibus hujus Parochiae cui impositum est Nomen Maria Catharina. Patrini fuere Dominus Josephus Kumarovich Cancellarius cum sua Dna Conjuge Joanna.» The same Chancellor as in 1769.|georgius-uroda,maria-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1773-maria-heva-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1773-maria-heva-uroda-line.jpg||Karlobag, September 1773 — Maria Heva, daughter of Georgius and Maria Uroda, «hujus loci Civibus»; godparents Antonius Pomsick and Aloysia, wife of Josephus Collini|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 191, right-hand page, headed «Anno Dni 1773»: the entry near the foot, before the first of October|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L99R-B|«Idem Admin[istrator] baptizavit Mariam Hevam filiam ante quinque dies natam ex Georgio et Maria Uroda hujus loci Civibus. Patrini de sacro fonte suscipientibus Dno Antonio Pomsick et Dna Aloysia conjuge Dni Josephi Collini.» The parents are called citizens (Cives) of the town.|georgius-uroda,maria-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1780-antonius-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1780-antonius-uroda-line.jpg||Karlobag, 13 June 1780 — Antonius, son of Dno Georgius and Maria Uroda; godparents the standard-bearer Antonius Klein and Catharina, wife of the pro-tribune Joannes Kallinich de Zirfeld|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 214, left-hand page, headed «Anno Dni 1780»: the last entry, «13 ejusdem» [June]|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L99M-9|«Idem qui supra Baptizavit Filium anteheri Natum ex Dno Georgio et Maria Uroda Conjugibus hujus Civitatis, cui impositum est nomen Antonius. Patrini fuerunt Dnus Vexillifer Antonius Klein, et Dna Catharina Conjux Dni pro Tribuni Joannis Kallinich de Zirfeld.» Both godparents are of the military garrison.|georgius-uroda,maria-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1784-dominicus-christianus-uroda|karlobag-baptism-1784-dominicus-christianus-uroda-line.png||Karlobag, 17 May 1784 — a son, Dominicus Christianus Joannes, of Dno Georgius and Dna Maria Uroda; godparents Nicolaus Samanich and Heva, wife of Joannes Butorović|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 229, left-hand page, headed «Anno Dni 1784»: the second entry after «2 Moÿ», «17 ejusdem»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L9SP-S|«Idem qui supra Capellanus loci baptizavi filium [heri] natum ex Dno Georgio et Dna Maria Uroda conjugibus hujus loci Parochiae. Cui impositum est nomen Dominici Cristiani Joannis. Levantibus e sacro fonte Dno Nicolao Samanich et Dna Heva uxore Dni Joannis Butorovic.» Georgius and Maria are Dominus and Domina here. The index lists this child as «Joannis».|georgius-uroda,maria-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
pag-baptism-1728-caietanus-bachi|pag-baptism-1728-caietanus-bachi-line.png||Pag, 14 March 1728 — Caietanus Antonius Gregorius, son of Dno ANGELO BACHI, patrician, and Dna Oliva — a candidate for the Caetanus Bachi who married at Karlobag in 1753|Pag baptisms, 1728 (FamilySearch Croatia, Church Books 1516–1994; index record 1:1:XQMM-RTYT)|right-hand page of the opening, the last entry, headed «Anno Dni 1728 die 14 Martii»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-FKZ2|«Anno Dni 1728 die 14 Martii. Ego Frater Gregorius … de licentia Rmi D. D. Joannis Franc. Mirovich Archiepi … baptizavi infantem natum die 12 eiusdem [mensis] de legitimo matrimonio procreatum ex Dno Angelo Bachi Patricio, et Dna Oliva Filia Dni Gasparo Lizavola [?] conjugibus. Cui imposui nomen Caietanus Antonius ac Gregorius. Patrini fuerunt Dns Laurentius Cassius [?] Strenuus Miles nomine Illmi ac Excmi Domini Antonij Zane dignissimi Comitis hujus civitatis Pagi, et Dna Lucia …» The father is a PATRICIAN of the island town of Pag, and the child is named CAIETANUS — the rare given name of the Caetanus Bachi who married Anna Lukatelli at Karlobag on 4 February 1753, aged 24 if this is he; a daughter of his at Karlobag is called OLIVA, like the mother here. (The tree's Angelo, ahnentafel 428, comes only from a DIFFERENT Karlobag baptism of 1779 — a Caetanus Antonius, son of Angelo and Catharina — so he is not evidence for this link; see the 1779 snapshot.) NOT PROVED: the Karlobag entries never name his father or birthplace, and the tree's mother is «Catharina». Pag lies a short crossing from Karlobag. The godfather's title and the mother's father's surname are not firm. Read at about 3x.|caetano-bacchi|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1780-05-vitus-smojver|karlobag-baptism-1780-05-vitus-smojver-line.jpg||Karlobag, 17 May 1780 — Vitus, son of Paulo and Barbara Smojver, «hujus Civitatis»; godparents Simon Matthievich and Margarita Damiani Budak|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 214, left-hand page, headed «Anno Dni 1780»: the entry «17 ejusdem», after the 15th and before the 22nd (the month, May, is by its place on the page)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L99M-9|«17 ejusdem. M.R.D. Michaël Martinjazi Baptizavit Filium hodie Natum ex Paulo & Barbara Smojver, Conjugibus hujus Civitatis, cui impositum est nomen Viti. Patrini fuerunt Simon Matthievich & Margarita Damiani Budak.» A Paulus Smojver again at Karlobag, now with a wife Barbara (1763: Ursula) and written without the by-name «Vukić». Read at about 3x.||11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1779-01-caetanus-antonius-bacchi|karlobag-baptism-1779-01-caetanus-antonius-bacchi-line.png||Karlobag, 12 January 1779 — Caetanus Antonius, son of Angelo and Catharina Bachi; godparents the Captain Joannes Jankovich and Maria, wife of Dno Georgius Uroda|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 210, left-hand page, headed «Anno Dni 1779»: the entry «12 Januarij», the third from the top|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L9SQ-C|«12 Januarij. M.R.D. Michael Martinaj Presbyter Curatus Loci Baptizavit infantem hodie natum ex Angelo & Catharina Bachi conjugibus hujatibus, cui impositum est nomen Caetani Antonij. Patrini fuerunt Dnus Capitaneus Joannes Jankovich et Dna Maria uxor Dni Georgij Uroda.» THIS IS THE BAPTISM THE TREE WRONGLY TAKES FOR THE ELDER CAETANUS BACCHI (ahnentafel 214, born 1779 «maybe»): a different, younger Caetanus Antonius, son of ANGELO and CATHARINA — a second Bacchi household at Karlobag in 1779 — and the godmother is MARIA, wife of Dominus Georgius Uroda (ahnentafel 109). Read at about 3x.|maria-uroda|11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
betina-baptism-1835-andrea-uroda|betina-baptism-1835-andrea-uroda-line.jpg||Betina, 28 November 1835 — Andrea, son of Simeone Uroda and Giovanna Barran, both «a Betina»|Betina baptisms, 1835 (FamilySearch Croatia, Church Books 1516–1994, reference 19; index record 1:1:QKMG-896Y; the printed Italian «Libro degli atti di nascita», Distretto di Sebenico, Circolo di Zara)|left half of the printed table, entry no. 24; the second entry (no. 23) is Andrea and Nicolò, children of Antonio Moikin|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-YCSL|Printed form, Italian: «Nato li 28 [ventotto] Novembre 1835 … Battezzato li 28 … Andrea» — masculine, legitimate; mother «Giovanna [Barran] a Betina»; father «Simeone Uroda a Betina»; the parents' marriage (25 February 1835, Betina) and the godfather «Andrea Barazic a Betina» in the columns to the right. The parents are Catholic and live at Betina, in the Šibenik district under Austrian Dalmatia, and nothing on the page says they came from anywhere. The 1829 baptism of Maria «Urodan» (image ref. 20) and the 1839 baptism of Antonio «Urada» (ref. 33) are the same printed form and were opened but add no origin. A resident Betina family of the 19th century, not a Karlobag one. Read at about 3x.||11 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1739-jakomo-pilipich|karlobag-baptism-1739-jakomo-pilipich-line.png||Karlobag, «30 [Oct or Nov] 1739» — Jakomo, son of a Jakov Pilipić; godparents Gn. Mik[ula] Zorović and Kate, wife of Gn. Antun Dorliga|Karlobag births (Rođeni) 1691–1804 (DGS 5481648, FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-3Y9)|image 82, left-hand page, the last entry on the page, headed «Na 30: [month] 1739»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L9SZ-B|«Na 30: [Ovra] 1739: Korstih ja Plovan Andrij Kollekar korstih [sina] Jakova Pilipicha imenom Jakomo … [word not read: a place, perhaps «u kaštel»] … bi kum Gn. Mik[ula] Zorović a kuma Kate [Blizi?] Gn. Antona Dorliga.» THE INDEX DATES IT 30 NOVEMBER; THE MONTH WORD (an abbreviation ending «-ovra») COULD BE OCTOBER OR NOVEMBER AND IS NOT FIRM. The child's father is named «Jakov Pilipić» and the godparents are the town's gentry (Zorović; the wife of Antun Dorliga, who in 1767 is the criminal judge) — a man of standing, which fits a captain of the port. NO MOTHER IS NAMED. Several words in the middle of the entry are not read at this resolution. Read at about 3x.|jacob-pilipic|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-marriage-1767-06-grubisich-witness-dominicus-uroda|sibenik-marriage-1767-06-grubisich-witness-dominicus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik, 3 June 1767 — marriage of Joannes Grubisich and Ariana, daughter of the late Michael Boydanovich alias Pancora; the witnesses include «Dno Dominico Uroda»|Šibenik cathedral parish marriages 1752–1787 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-W3R, 468 images)|image 373, left-hand page, the first entry, headed «Anno Domini 1767 die vero 3tia mensis Junii»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-29R2|«Ego Presbyter Josephus Caristo Rector Ecclesiae Parochialis S. Benedicti … Joannem filium Michaeli Grubisich ex Parochia Sanctae Mariae Vallis Viridis et Arianam [?] filiam relictae q. Michaelis Boydanovich alias Pancora, Parochiae S. Benedicti, in Ecclesia S. Francisci Fratrum Minorum Conventualium interrogavi … matrimonio conjunxi coram Testibus Matthaeo Xeravizza, et Dno Dominico Uroda, ac multis.» The witness's surname is read as Uroda (V-shaped initial, final «a»); the entry gives no father, place or age. The first Uroda seen in the Šibenik registers; NOT shown to be the Karlobag Dominicus or Dume. Read at about 3x.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1762-08-loccasovich-witness-dominicus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1762-08-loccasovich-witness-dominicus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 10 August 1762 — marriage of Antonius Loccasovich and Elera Dulitich; the witnesses include «Dno Dominico Uroda»|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images)|image 469, right-hand page (numbered 91), the first entry, headed «Die 10 Augusti 1762»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-5CMB|«Tribus denuntiationibus dispensatis … Ego Presbyter Thomas Jadovon Rector Ecclesiae S. Marci in Suburbio Maris in Ecclesia Cathedrali S. Jacobi interrogavi Antonium filium Francisci Loccasovich et Eleram filiam Petri Dulitich ambos supradictae Parochiae S. Marci … in matrimonium conjunxi, praesentibus testibus Illmo Domino Angelo Semonich alias Perova, et Dno Dominico Uroda aliisque multis.» Read at about 3x; the surname is written with a V-shaped initial and a final «a», the same hand and spelling as the 1767 witness at the cathedral parish. The entry gives him no father, place or age.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1759-09-meich-witness-magister-dominicus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1759-09-meich-witness-magister-dominicus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 11 September 1759 — marriage of Matthaeus Meich of Zlosela and Antonia, widow of the master Hieronymus Sigovec; the witnesses include «Magistro Dominico Uroda»|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images)|image 458, right-hand page (the page after p. 80), the second entry, headed «Die 11 Septemb. 1759»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-5CNW|«Duabus denuntiationibus … Ego Presbiter Thomas Jadovon Rector Eccl. S. Marci in Suburbio Maris interrogavi in supradicta ecclesia Matthaeum filium qd. Stephani Meich ex Villa Zloseba [Zlosela] Antoniamque relictam qd. magistri Hieronimi Sigoveo, eorumque mutuo consensu habito per verba de praesenti eos solemniter matrimonio conjunxi, praesentibus testibus Magistro Domico [Dominico] Uroda, et Antonio Lucenti aliisque multis.» Read at about 3x; «Domico» is a contracted «Dominico». The title here is «Magister» (a master of a trade), not «Dno» as in 1762 and 1767. No father, place or age is given.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1757-09-kvancich-witness-joannes-son-of-dominicus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1757-09-kvancich-witness-joannes-son-of-dominicus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 27 September 1757 — marriage of Matthaeus Kvancich and Lucia, widow of Andreas Segna; the witnesses include «Joanne filio Dominici Uroda»|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images)|image 450, right-hand page (numbered 75), the entry headed «Die 27 Septemb. 1757», which ends at the foot of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-5CK7|«Tribus denunciationibus dispensatis ab Reverendissimo Vicario Generali Nicolao Difnico … Ego Presbiter Thomas Jadovon Rector Ecclesiae S. Marci in Suburbio Maris, in Ecclesia S. Rochi, interrogavi Matheum filium qd. Joannis Kvancich et Luciam relictam qd. Andreae Segna, eorumque mutuo consensu habito per verba de praesenti eos matrimonio conjunxi, praesentibus testibus Joseph Fevetti, et Joanne filio Dominici Uroda, aliisque multis.» Read at about 3x. **A son of a Dominicus Uroda, Joannes, of an age to witness in 1757** (the first mention of a Uroda child in the Šibenik registers); the entry does not say who Joannes is, how old, or that the Dominicus is the Dominicus of 1759–1767. Names with doubtful letters: «Kvancich» and «Segna».|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1756-01-clavich-witness-dominicus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1756-01-clavich-witness-dominicus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 11 January 1756 — marriage of Silvester (or Saulus) Clavich and Dominica, daughter of the master Joannes Kinchela; the witnesses are «Dominico Uroda et Michaele Cigo»|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images)|image 446, right-hand page, the entry headed «Die 11 Januarii 1756» at the foot of the page (the page after the one numbered 69)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-5CWL|«Die 11 Januarii 1756. Tribus denuntiationibus praemissis … Ego Presbiter Thomas Jadovon Parochus Ecclesiae S. Marci in Suburbio Maris interrogavi in supradicta Ecclesia Silvestrum vel Saulum filium Stephani Clavich, et Dominicam filiam magistri Joannis Kinchela, eorumque mutuo consensu habito per verba de praesenti eos matrimonio conjunxi, praesentibus testibus Dominico Uroda et Michaele Cigo aliisque multis.» Read at about 3x; the first name of the groom is doubtful. The earliest of five sightings of a Dominicus Uroda at Šibenik (1756, 1757, 1759, 1762, 1767), here with no title.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1738-05-lucia-dragovich-godmother-wife-of-georgius-uroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1738-05-lucia-dragovich-godmother-wife-of-georgius-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 19 May 1738 — baptism of Lucia, daughter of Michael and Mathea Dragovich; the godmother is «Dna [Su]guetia, uxor Mri Georgij Vroda» (wife of the master Georgius Uroda)|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 117, left-hand page, an entry in the lower half, headed «Die 19 Maji 1738»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-L3MW|«Die 19 Maji 1738. Lucia filia Dni Michaelis et Mathee coniugum Dragovich ex hac P[arochi]a S. Marci, in lucem edita die 13 [Maji], Baptizata fuit in hoc Patri[s] Baptisterio per me Franciscum Can[onicu]m Parchych … cui impositum fuit [nomen Lucia]. Patrini fuerunt Philippus Defrateo, et Dna Guetia [the name is unclear, perhaps Suguetia] Uxor Mri Georgij Vroda.» Read at about 3x. **A Magister Georgius Uroda, already married, in Šibenik in May 1738**: the first mention of any Georgius Uroda at Šibenik, and 25 years before the Georgius of Karlobag has a first child. The wife's name is not read with certainty; she is not named Maria. Whether this is the Georgius of Karlobag (ahnentafel 108), his father, or a namesake is not shown.|georgius-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1738-10-maria-vidovich-godfather-magister-franciscus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1738-10-maria-vidovich-godfather-magister-franciscus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 12 October 1738 — baptism of Maria, daughter of Antonius and Margareta Vidovich; the godfather is «Magister Franciscus Vroda» (the master Franciscus Uroda)|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 118, left-hand page, the last entry on the page, headed «Die 12 Octobris 1738» (the margin reads «Maria Vidovich»)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-LSG4|«Die 12 Octobris 1738. Ego Presbiter Nicolaus Mijagostovich Vice Parochus S. Marci Baptizavi in Baptisterio dictae Parochiae infantem natam sub die 7 Septembris ex Conjugibus Antonii et Margerita Vidovich cui impositum fuit nomen Maria; Patrini fuerunt Magister Franciscus Vroda, et Marta [Marchiani?].» Read at about 3x; the first godparent is a Magister Franciscus Uroda (the surname with the same V-shaped initial as the Dominicus sightings), the godmother's surname is a guess. A second master of the name at Šibenik in 1738, five months after the Magister Georgius Uroda of 19 May.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1735-01-domica-godfather-magister-franciscus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1735-01-domica-godfather-magister-franciscus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 30 January 1735 — baptism of Domica, daughter of Joannes and Antonia [surname Maraglia?]; the godparents are «Franciscus Vroda» and Simona [Suraeovich?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 111, right-hand page (numbered 4), the second entry, headed «Die 30 Januarii 1735»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-LSFH|«Die 30 Januarii 1735. Domica filia Joannis et Antoniae coniugum Maraglia [?] ex hac Par[ochia] S. Marci, in lucem edita die 21 [Januarii], Bap[tizata] fuit in hoc Patri[s] Baptisterio per me … Parochi … Rectorem, cui praesentum nomen impositum fuit. Patrini fuerunt Franciscus Vroda, et Simona Suraeovich [?].» Read at about 3x; the child's surname and the godmother's are doubtful; **Franciscus Uroda**, here without «Magister», is the same name as the master of October 1738, three years earlier. The earliest sighting of any Uroda at Šibenik.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1733-04-maria-maraglia-godfather-magister-franciscus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1733-04-maria-maraglia-godfather-magister-franciscus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 25 April 1733 — baptism of Maria, daughter of Joannes and Anastasia [surname Maraglia?]; the godparents are «Mr Franciscus Vroda» (the master Franciscus Uroda) and Anastasia [Signorin?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 109, right-hand page, the third entry, headed «Die 25 Aprilis 1733» (the margin reads «Maria Maraglia»)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-LSPC|«Die 25 Aprilis 1733. Maria filia Joannis et Anastasiae coniugum Maraglia [?], in lucem edita die 20 [Aprilis], Baptizata fuit in hoc Patri Baptisterio per me Franciscum Parchych S. Marci Rectorem, cui praesentum nomen impositum fuit. Patrini fuerunt Mr Franciscus Vroda, et Anastasia Signoria [?].» Read at about 3x; «Mr» is a contraction of Magister; the child's and godmother's surnames are doubtful. **The earliest sighting of any Uroda at Šibenik (1733)**, the same Franciscus who stands godfather to Joannes and Antonia's Domica in January 1735 and, as «Magister», to Antonius and Margareta Vidovich's Maria in October 1738.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1741-01-joana-peresich-godfather-magister-dominicus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1741-01-joana-peresich-godfather-magister-dominicus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 1 January 1741 — baptism of Joana, daughter of Thomas and Lucia Peresich alias Bodulovich; the godparents are «Magister Dominicus Vroda» (the master Dominicus Uroda) and Dominica, daughter of Matthaeus Marchovich|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 123, right-hand page (numbered 17), the first entry, headed «Die 1ª Januarii 1741» (the margin reads «Joana Peresich alias Bodulovich»)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-LSDL|«Die [1] Januarii 1741. Joana filia Tomae et Luciae Conjugum Peresich alias Bodulovich ex hac Parochia S. Marci in lucem edita die 30 Decembris, Baptizata fuit in hoc Parochiali Baptisterio per me V[ice] Parochum Nicolaum Mijagostovich, cui praescriptum nomen impositum fuit. Patrini fuerunt Magister Dominicus Vroda, et Dominica filia Matthaei Marchovich.» Read at about 3x. **The earliest sighting of Dominicus Uroda (1741), already a «Magister»**, 15 years before he appears as a witness at Dolac marriages (1756–1762). The Dolac godfather of Šibenik's Uroda: Franciscus (1733, 1735, 1738), Georgius (1738 as a godmother's husband), Dominicus (1741).|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1742-05-georgius-biliznich-mother-antonia-daughter-of-franciscus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1742-05-georgius-biliznich-mother-antonia-daughter-of-franciscus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 6 May 1742 — baptism of Georgius, son of Joannes [Presrou?] de Flumine alias Biliznich and of Antonia, «filia q[uondam] Francisci Vrodda de hac Parochia S. Marci» (daughter of the late Franciscus Uroda)|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 126, left-hand page, the last entry on the page, headed «Anno Domini 1742 – Die 6 Maij» (the margin reads «Georgius Biliznich»)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-LS6J|«Anno Domini 1742 – Die 6 Maij. Georgius filius Joannis [Presrou?] de Flumine, alias Biliznich, et Antoniae filiae q[uondam] Francisci Vrodda de hac Parochia S. Marci, Coniugum, natus die 17 mensis Aprilis proxime elapsi. Baptizatus fuit in hac Parochiali Ecclesia S. Marci per me Angelum Trapileo; cui impositum fuit nomen Georgius, [ut supra]. Patrini fuere Viscardus Pini, et Dna Cecilia Vidovich q[uondam] Caroli.» Read at about 3x; the father's second name is doubtful. **Antonia is the daughter of the LATE Franciscus Uroda of Šibenik**: so Franciscus (godfather 1733, 1735, 1738) was dead by April 1742, and had at least this daughter, who married a Joannes Biliznich of the same parish. The child is a Georgius Biliznich, not a Georgius Uroda.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1741-04-domica-maraglia-godfather-magister-dominicus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1741-04-domica-maraglia-godfather-magister-dominicus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 23 April 1741 — baptism of Domica, daughter of Joannes and Antonia Maraglia [?]; the godparents are «Mr Dominicus Vroda» (the master Dominicus Uroda) and Maria Vergada [?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 125, left-hand page, the first entry, headed «Die 23 Aprilis 1741» (the margin reads «Domica Maraglia»)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-LSXW|«Die 23 Aprilis 1741. Domica filia Joannis et Antoniae coniugum Maraglia [?] ex hac Par[ochia] S. Marci, in lucem edita die prima supradicti [mensis], Baptizata fuit in hoc Patri[s] Baptisterio per me Franciscum Parchych … Rectorem, cui praesentum nomen impositum fuit. Patrini fuerunt Mr Dominicus Vroda, et Dna Maria Vergada [?].» Read at about 3x. **Magister Dominicus Uroda is godfather to a child of the same couple (Joannes and Antonia/Anastasia Maraglia) as Franciscus Uroda was in 1733 and 1735**: the families are bound together, perhaps by kinship, and so, perhaps, are the two Uroda men. The earlier Domica of 30 January 1735 (same parents) presumably died.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1703-01-paulus-son-of-joannes-uroda-and-ursula|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1703-01-paulus-son-of-joannes-uroda-and-ursula-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), January 1703 — baptism of Paulus, «procreatum ex Joanne Vroda, et Ursula eius conjugibus» (son of Joannes Uroda and Ursula); godparents the master Hieronymus [Magaznich?] and Jacobina, wife of the master Melchior [Bayrinich?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 12, left-hand page, an entry in the lower half, headed «Die 2[8] Januarii 1703» (the day is half hidden by an ink blot)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-2K1V|«Die 2[8] Januarii 1703. Ego Fr[ater] Paulus Nicolich Vice Parochus in Ecclesia S. Marci in suburbio Maris Baptizavi infantem, cui impositum est nomen Paulus, procreatum ex Joanne Vroda, et Ursula eius conjugibus: Patrini fuerunt [Mr] Hieronymus Magaznich [?] et Jacobina uxor [Mri] Melchioris Bayrinich [?].» Read at about 3x; the godparents' surnames are doubtful, the father's is clear (the same V-shaped initial and final «a» as the Dominicus sightings). **The earliest Uroda at Šibenik: a Joannes Uroda, married to Ursula, with a baptised son in 1703**, thirty years before the first Franciscus.|joannes-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1705-05-antonius-son-of-joannes-and-ursula-vrodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1705-05-antonius-son-of-joannes-and-ursula-vrodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 31 May 1705 — baptism of Antonius, son of Joannes and Ursula Vrodich [Urodić]; godparents Joannes Micheli and Magdalena, wife of [Dno] Beri [?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 19, right-hand page (numbered 15), the second entry, headed «Die 31 Maji 1705»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-2LWP|«Die 31 Maji 1705. Ego Fr. Andreas Rovich [Kovich?] Parochus S. Marci in Suburbio Maris Baptizavi infantem natum ex legitimis Conjugibus V[iris] Joanne et Ursa [Ursula] Vrodich, cui nomen impositum fuit Antonius. Patrini fuere Dnus Joannes Micheli et Dna Magdalena uxor Dni Beri Rifinici [?].» Read at about 3x; the surname is spelled «Vrodich» (Urodić), and the same couple, Joannes and Ursula, had Paulus in January 1703 (image 12). The godparents' names are doubtful.|joannes-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1705-10-simeon-son-of-lucas-vrodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1705-10-simeon-son-of-lucas-vrodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 27 October 1705 — baptism of Simeon, son of Lucas and [Ursula/Anna?] Vrodich [Urodić]; godfather Dominicus Condoguari of the city|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 20, right-hand page (numbered 16), the second entry, headed «Die 27 8bris 1705»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-2LX6|«Die 27 8bris 1705. Ego Fr. Andreas Rovich Parochus S. Marci in Suburbio Maris Baptizavi infantulum natum ex legitimis Conjugibus [Lucas et …] (Conj: Vrodich) cui nomen impositum fuit Simeon. Patrini fuere Dominicus Condoguari ex Civitate et Brigida uxor q. Gasparini Bra[…].» Read at about 3x; the surname «Vrodich» is clear, the parents' given names are partly lost in the page-edge shadow (Lucas and a woman's name). **A second Uroda couple at Šibenik in 1705**, unconnected on the page to Joannes and Ursula.|lucas-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1706-05-paulus-son-of-thomas-vrodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1706-05-paulus-son-of-thomas-vrodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 14 May 1706 — baptism of Paulus, son of Thomas and Anastasia Vrodich [Urodić]; godparents Marcus and Catarina, spouses [Liatich?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 22, left-hand page, the first entry, headed «Die 14 Maji 1706»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-2LHY|«Die 14 Maji 1706. Ego Fr. Andreas Rovich Parochus S. Marci in Suburbio Maris Baptizavi infantulum natum ex legitimis Conjugibus V[iris] Thoma et Anastasia Conjug[ibus] Vrodich, cui nomen impositum Paulus. Patrini fuerunt Marcus et Catarina Conjuges Liatich.» Read at about 3x; «Vrodich» is clear, the mother's name is read as Anastasia. **A third Uroda household at Šibenik 1703–1706 (Joannes and Ursula; Lucas; Thomas and Anastasia)**: the surname was common in the Dolac suburb in the first years of the book.|thomas-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1710-01-paulus-antonius-son-of-lucas-vrodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1710-01-paulus-antonius-son-of-lucas-vrodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 16 January 1710 — baptism of Paulus Antonius, son of Lucas [?] and [Joanna?] Vrodich [Urodić]; godparents Simon Jarich and [Eda/Lida] Urobich [Uroda?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 35, right-hand page (numbered 30), the last entry on the page, headed «Die 16 Januarii 1710»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-L3SZ|«Die 16 Januarii 1710. Paulus Antonius filius Lucae [?] et [Joannae?] Vrodich Conjugum Baptizatus fuit per me Fratrem Philippum Servovich Parochum eccl. S. Marci. Patrini fuerunt Simon Jarich, et [Eida/Lida] Urobich.» Read at about 3x; the father's given name looks like «Luce» (Lucas) and the mother's is unclear, the surname «Vrodich» is clear; the godmother's surname is written «Urobich» (probably Urodić too). **Lucas Vrodich, who had a son Simeon in 1705, has another son Paulus Antonius in 1710**; the parish priest is now Fr. Philippus Servovich.|lucas-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1710-10-paulus-son-of-franciscus-vrodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1710-10-paulus-son-of-franciscus-vrodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 23 October 1710 — baptism of Paulus, son of FRANCISCUS and Anna Vrodich [Urodić], «Conjugum Catholicorum»; godparents Dno Joannes Theodorovich and Jacoba Bonacich|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 38, left-hand page, the last entry (the margin before it is blank), headed «Die 23 8bris 1710»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-L386|«Die 23 8bris 1710. Paulus filius Francisci Vrodich et Annae Conjugum Catholicorum, Baptizatus fuit per me Fr. Philippum Servovich Parochum eccl. S. Marci. Patrini fuerunt Dnus Joannes Theodorovich et Jacoba Bonacich.» Read at about 3x. **The first appearance of the name Franciscus Uroda, with a wife Anna and a son Paulus, in 1710**; the Magister Franciscus of 1733–1738 (dead by 1742, daughter Antonia) is very probably this man, who by 1733 would be a father of grown children, or his son of the same name. Three Paulus Uroda are baptised in the first decade of the book (1703 son of Joannes, 1706 son of Thomas, 1710 son of Franciscus).|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1712-11-stanislava-daughter-of-franciscus-vrodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1712-11-stanislava-daughter-of-franciscus-vrodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 21 November 1712 — baptism of Stanislava [Stanislaha], daughter of Franciscus and Anna Vrodich [Urodić]; godparents Dno Franciscus Theodorus [?] and Dna Genovefa Maraschi|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 44, left-hand page, the first entry, headed «Die 21 Novembris 1712»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-L3QF|«Die 21 [Novembris] 1712. Stanislava filia Francisci et Annae Vrodich Conjugum Baptizata fuit per me Fr. Philippum Surovich Parochum eccl. S. Marci in eadem ecclesia. Patrini fuerunt Dnus Franciscus Theodorus [?] et Dna Genovefa Maraschi [?].» Read at about 3x; the day and the godfather's surname are partly uncertain. **Franciscus and Anna Vrodich's second child in two years** (Paulus, 23 October 1710).|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1715-10-simona-daughter-of-franciscus-vrodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1715-10-simona-daughter-of-franciscus-vrodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 28 October 1715 — baptism of SIMONA, daughter of Franciscus and [Lucia] Vrodich [Urodić], born 21 October; the godparents include «D. Georgius Vrodi[ch?] Gasparovich» (a Georgius, the surname partly under a pasted slip)|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 53, left-hand page, an entry near the top, headed «Die 28 8bris 1715»; a paper slip pasted on the page covers the right edge of the godparents' line|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-L344|«Die 28 8bris 1715. Ego Fr. Philippus Surcovich Parochus Vicarius S. Marci in Suburbio Maris Sibenicensis, in eadem Ecclesia Baptizavi infantulum procreatum ex legitimo matrimonio sub die 21 eiusdem mensis, ex Lucia [?] et Francisco Vrodich de eadem Parochia. Cui nomen impositum fuit Simona. Patrini [fuerunt] D. Georgius Vrodi[ch?] Gasparovich [?] …» Read at about 3x; the mother's name (Lucia?) and the godfather's second surname are doubtful. **A daughter SIMONA of a Franciscus Vrodich in 1715**, with a Georgius (a Vrodi-) as godfather; this Franciscus has a different wife's name from the Franciscus and Anna of 1710 and 1712 (a second marriage, or two Franciscus). The dead «Dume Uroda of Šibenik» of the 1739 Karlobag marriage had a daughter SIMONA who married then; the name is a coincidence at most.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1721-10-franciscus-antonius-son-of-franciscus-urode-and-anna|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1721-10-franciscus-antonius-son-of-franciscus-urode-and-anna-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 19 October [?] 1721 — baptism of FRANCISCUS ANTONIUS, son of Franciscus URODE and Anna, born 3 of the month; godparents D. Petrus Mioćević and his wife Dominica|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 75, left-hand page, a full entry near the middle, headed «Die 19 [8bris?] 1721» (the month is an abbreviation, read as October from the run of dates either side)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-LST3|«Die 19 [8bris] 1721. Franciscus Antonius filius Francisci Urode et Annae coniugum natus fuit 3. huius mensis et Baptizatus a me Fr. Joannem Annick Vice Parochum S. Marci in Suburbio Maris Sibenici in praefata Ecclesia S. Marci. Patrini fuerunt D. Petrus Miocevich, et D. Dominicha uxor eiusdem Petri ambo ex hac Curia». Read at about 4x; the surname is written plainly «Urode». **A son of a Franciscus Urode and Anna in 1721** — the wife's name of the Franciscus of 1710 (Paulus) and 1712 (Stanislava), who are therefore probably this man; the 1715 Simona's mother was read «Lucia?» (a second wife, or the reading is wrong).|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1721-12-thomasa-karmelich-godfather-georgius-urodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1721-12-thomasa-karmelich-godfather-georgius-urodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 27 December 1721 — baptism of Thomasa, daughter of Antonius Karmelić and Margarita; godparents GEORGIUS URODICH and Margarita, daughter of D. Simeon Venier|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 75, right-hand page, the first full entry below the middle, headed «Die 27 Xbris 1721»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-LST3|«Die 27 [Xbris] 1721. Thomasa filia Antonii Karmelich et Margaritae coniugum nata fuit 16. huius, et Baptizata a me Fr. Joannem Annick V.P. S. Marci in dicta Eccl. S. Marci. Patrini fuerunt Georgius Urodich, et Margarita filia D. Simeonis Venier, ambo ex hac Curia». Read at about 4x; «Urodich» is clear. A GEORGIUS URODICH who stands godfather; a Georgius of the same name stood godfather on 28 January 1720 and a «Georgius Vrodi[ch?]» on 28 October 1715.|georgius-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1720-01-paulus-son-of-stephanus-godfather-georgius-urodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1720-01-paulus-son-of-stephanus-godfather-georgius-urodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 28 January 1720 — baptism of Paulus, son of Stephanus and Magdalena Gajcević [?]; godparents GEORGIUS URODICH and Angela, wife of D. Georgius Vidović|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 69, right-hand page, bottom half, an entry headed «Die 28 Januarii 1720»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-LS1T|«Die 28 Januarii 1720. Paulus filius Stephani et Magdalenae Gajcevich natus fuit 27 huius. Baptizatusque a me fr. Joannem Annickem Vice Parochum S. Marci in eodem Ecclesia. Patrini fuerunt Giorgius Urodich [urobich?], et Angela uxor D. Giorgii Vidovich: ambo ex hac Curia». Read at about 4x; the third letter from the end of the surname is open and could be b or d — read as Urodich because the same hand writes it Urodich in December 1721. (A Georgius VIDOVIĆ, with a wife Stanislava, is also a godfather in these pages; he is not an Uroda.)|georgius-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1725-03-antonia-tintich-godfather-magister-franciscus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1725-03-antonia-tintich-godfather-magister-franciscus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 19 March 1725 — baptism of Antonia, daughter of Michael and Catharina Tintich; godparents MR. FRANCISCUS VRODA and Angela Julioli|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 88, left-hand page, an entry in the middle, headed «Die 19 Martij 1725»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-LSP9|«Die 19 Martij 1725. Antonia filia Michaelis, et Chatre [Catharinae] Coniugum Tintich, ex hac Parochia S. Marci, in lucem edita die dicto, Baptizata fuit in hoc Parti Baptio per me Presbirum Franciscum Canonicum Parchych D.ae Ecclesiae Rectorem. Patrini fuerunt M.r Francus Vroda, et Angela Julioli». Read at about 4x; «Mr» is the Magister (master) title. **The earliest sighting of a Magister Franciscus Vroda, eight years before the godfather of 1733.** Angela Julioli stands as godmother beside him again and again; she is a fixture of the font and not kin.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1726-01-paula-bratich-godfather-magister-dominicus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1726-01-paula-bratich-godfather-magister-dominicus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 27 January 1726 — baptism of Paula, daughter of Laurentius and Helena Bratich; godparents Anastasia, wife of Mr. Rochus Signoriza, and MR. DOMINICUS [?] VRODA|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 91, right-hand page, near the top, headed «Die 27 Janij 1726»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-LSR3|«Die 27 Janij 1726. Paula filia Laurentij et Helenae Coniugum Bratich, ex hac Parochia S. Marci, in lucem edita die 22 d.ti, Baptizata fuit in hoc Parti Baptio per me Presbirum Franciscum Canonicum Parchych D.ae Ecclesiae Rectorem. Patrini fuerunt Anastasia Uxor Mri Rochi Signoriza, et Mr. Domcus [Dominicus?] Vroda». Read at about 4x; the forename is abbreviated and may be Dominicus (the Magister Dominicus Vroda of 1741–1767) — **if so, he is a master by January 1726.**|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1728-07-matthaeus-son-of-joannes-godfather-franciscus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1728-07-matthaeus-son-of-joannes-godfather-franciscus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 6 July 1728 — baptism of Matthaeus, son of Joannes and Antonia Marcolia [?]; godparents D. FRANCISCUS VRODA and Palma Bonacich|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 98, left-hand page, upper middle, headed «Die 6 July 1728»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-LSLZ|«Die 6 Suly [July] 1728. Matheus filius Joannis, et Antonie Conjugum Margolia [?], ex hac Parochia S. Marci, in lucem editus die prima d.ti, Baptizatus fuit in hoc Parti Baptio per me Presb. Franciscum Canonicum Parchych D.ae Ecclesiae Rectorem. Patrini fuerunt Dñ Francus Vroda, et Dña Palma Bonacich». Read at about 3x.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1728-10-simeona-scalabrin-godfather-franciscus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1728-10-simeona-scalabrin-godfather-franciscus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 26 October 1728 — baptism of Simeona, daughter of Paulus and Joanna Scalabrin; godparents D. FRANCISCUS VRODA and Magdalena Vdragovich|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 98, right-hand page, near the top, headed «Die 26 8bris 1728»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-LSLZ|«Die 26 8bris 1728. Simeona filia Pauli, et Joanne Conjugum Scalabrin, ex hac Parochia S. Marci, in lucem edita die 20 d.ti, Baptizata fuit in hoc Parti Baptio per me Presb. Franciscum Canonicum Parchych D.ae Ecclesiae Rectorem. Patrini fuerunt Dñ. Francus Vroda, et Magd.a Vdragovich». Read at about 4x.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1729-01-stephanus-son-of-jacobus-godfather-franciscus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1729-01-stephanus-son-of-jacobus-godfather-franciscus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 7 January 1729 — baptism of Stephanus, son of Jacobus and Anastasia Gusinovich [?], born 26 December 1728; godparents D. FRANCISCUS VRODA and Angela Julioli|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 99, left-hand page, the first entry at the top, headed «Die 7 Januarij 1729»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-LSR4|«Die 7 Januarij 1729. Stephanus filius Jacobi, et Anastasie Conjugum Gusinovich, ex hac Parochia S. Marci, in lucem editus die 26 Xbris 1728, Baptizatus fuit in hoc Parti Baptio per me Presbirum Franciscum Canonicum Parchych D.ae Ecclesiae Rectorem. Patrini fuerunt Dñ. Francus Vroda, et Angela Julioli». Read at about 4x; the year is read 1729 from the run of dates either side. Angela Julioli stands as godmother beside him again and again; she is a fixture of the font and not kin.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1729-08-bartolomea-godfather-franciscus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1729-08-bartolomea-godfather-franciscus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 23 August 1729 — baptism of Bartolomea, daughter of Georgius and Bartolomea Arounovich [?], born 16 of the month; godparents MR. FRANCISCUS VRODA and a woman named Kinckelova [?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 102, left-hand page, lower half, headed «Die 23 Aug 1729» (an entry out of sequence: it stands between entries of December 1730 and April 1731)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-LSJK|«Die 23 Aug 1729. Bartolomea filia Georgij, et Bartolomea Conjugum Arounovich [?], in lucem edita die 16 d.ti, Baptizata fuit in hoc Parti Baptio per me Presb. Franciscum Canonicum Parchych D.ae Ecclesiae Rectorem. Patrini fuerunt Mr. Francus Vroda, et Aohn [?] Kinckelova». Read at about 4x; **again «Mr.», a master**; the page is out of order, so the year is as written.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1729-09-simeon-son-of-marcus-godfather-franciscus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1729-09-simeon-son-of-marcus-godfather-franciscus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 12 September [?] 1729 — baptism of Simeon, son of Marcus and Joanna Josatovich [?]; godparents D. FRANCISCUS VRODA and Angela Julioli|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 99, left-hand page, lower half, headed «Die 12 7bris 1729» (the month abbreviation is read as September from the next entry, 2 October 1729)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-LSR4|«Die 12 [7bris] 1729. Simeon filius Marci, et Joanne Conjugum Josatovich [?], ex hac Parochia S. Marci, in lucem editus die 5 d.ti, Baptizatus fuit in hoc Parti Baptio per me Presbirum Franciscum Canonicum Parchych D.ae Ecclesiae Rectorem. Patrini fuerunt Dñ. Francus Vroda, et Angela Julioli». Read at about 4x. Angela Julioli stands as godmother beside him again and again; she is a fixture of the font and not kin.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1730-02-twins-matthaeus-and-joanna-godfather-franciscus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1730-02-twins-matthaeus-and-joanna-godfather-franciscus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 12 February 1730 — baptism of the twins Matthaeus and Joanna, children of Marcus and Mathea Bodulovich; godparents D. FRANCISCUS VRODA and Angela Julioli|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 99, right-hand page, upper half, headed «Die 12 Febrij 1730»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-LSR4|«Die 12 Febrij 1730. Mattheus et Joanna Fratres Gemelli filij Marci, et Mathee Conjugum Bodulovich, ex hac Parochia S. Marci, in lucem editi die 3 d.ti, Baptizati fuerunt in hoc Parti Baptio per me Presbirum Franciscum Canonicum Parchych D.ae Ecclesiae Rectorem. Patrini fuerunt Dñ. Francus Vroda, et Angela Julioli». Read at about 4x. Angela Julioli stands as godmother beside him again and again; she is a fixture of the font and not kin.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1744-12-lucia-daughter-of-magister-dominicus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1744-12-lucia-daughter-of-magister-dominicus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 15 December 1744 — baptism of LUCIA, daughter of MAGISTER DOMINICUS and FLORIA VRODA, born 12 December; godparents D. Antonius Bellagamba and a Magister Dominicus|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 131, left-hand page, last full entry, margin «Lucia Vroda», headed «Anno Dni 1744 – Die 15 mensis Decembris»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-LS8H|«Anno Dni 1744 – Die 15 mensis Decembris. Ego Angelus Trapileo Parochus huius Ecclesiae S. Marci baptizavi in hoc Parochiali Baptisterio infantem natam die 12 mensis Xbris anni 1744, ex legitimo matrimonio magistri Dolcarij [Doleari?] Dominici, et Floriae Coniugum Vrodda ambo de hac Parochia, cui impositum fuit nomen Lucia. Patrini fuere D. Antonius Bellagamba locum tenens Libratorid [?], et magister Pellio [?] Dominicus». Read at about 4x; the word after «magistri» (Dolcarij / Doleari) may be a trade (a cooper) or a by-name, and the godfather's surname is doubtful. **A Magister Dominicus Vroda is a father, with a wife Floria, in December 1744.**|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1745-05-vittoria-daughter-of-dominicus-and-floria-vrodda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1745-05-vittoria-daughter-of-dominicus-and-floria-vrodda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 16 May 1745 — baptism of VITTORIA, daughter of DOMINICUS and FLORIA VRODDA, born 10 [May]; godparents Joannes Piaggio and Antonia Zanoli alias Bellagamba|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 132, left-hand page, the last entry, margin «Vittoria Vrodda», headed «Anno Dni 1745 – Die 16 Maij»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-LSJQ|«Anno Dni 1745 – Die 16 Maij. Ego Angelus Trapileo Parochus huius Ecclesiae S. Marci et Subcanonicus huius Cathedralis Ecclesiae, baptizavi in hoc Parochiali Baptisterio infantem natum die 10 [Maij?] prox. elapsi, ex legit.o matrimonio vid.t Dominico, et Floria Vrodda de hac Parochia, cui impositum fuit nomen Victoria. Patrini fuere Joannes Piaggio, et Antonia Zanoli alias Bellagamba ambo de hac Parochia». Read at about 4x; the same couple as the Lucia of December 1744 (Dominicus and Floria Vroda).|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1746-10-franceschina-mestrovich-mother-antonia-vrodda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1746-10-franceschina-mestrovich-mother-antonia-vrodda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 23 October 1746 — baptism of FRANCESCHINA, daughter of JOANNES MESTROVICH alias CALAFAT and ANTONIA VRODDA, born 1 October|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 135, right-hand page, second entry from the bottom, margin «Francesca Mestrouich alias Calafat», headed «Anno Dni 1746 – Die 23 mensis Octobris»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-LS8D|«Anno Dni 1746 – Die 23 mensis Octobris. Ego Angelus Trapileo Parochus huius Ecclesiae S. Marci baptizavi in hoc Parochiali Baptisterio infantem natam die prima mensis currentis, ex legit.o matrimonio vid.t ex Coniugibus Joannis Mestrouich alias Calafat et Antoniae Vrodda ambo de hac Parochia, cui impositum fuit nomen Franceschina. Patrini fuere Illmus D. Julius Viddouich nobilis Scardonen. et Illma D. Maria Bonacich similiter nob. Scardonen., ambo de hac Parochia». Read at about 4x. **An Uroda daughter, Antonia, married to a Joannes Mestrovich alias Calafat** (a Magister Joannes Mestrovich alias Calafat «de Villa Stobrec» stands godfather in 1747).|antonia-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1749-06-antonia-pagen-godfather-dominicus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1749-06-antonia-pagen-godfather-dominicus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 27 June 1749 — baptism of Antonia, daughter of Matthaeus and Helena Pagenovich; godparents DOMINICUS VRODA and Elisabeth Soldin|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 140, left-hand page, lower half, margin «Antonia Pagen», headed «Die 27 Junij 1749»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-LSVK|«Die 27 Junij 1749. Ego J. Bona Radnich [parochus] baptizavi in hoc Parti Bapt.o infantem natam die 15 huius ex Matheo et Helena Pagenovich leg. con. ex hac Cura. Patrini, Dominicus Vroda, et Elisabeth Soldin ex hac Parochia. Cui nomen impositum est Antonia». Read at about 4x; the parish priest of 1746–1752 is a different man from the Trapileo of 1744–45.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1752-03-joseph-bodulovich-godfather-dominicus-uroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1752-03-joseph-bodulovich-godfather-dominicus-uroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 20 March 1752 — baptism of Josephus, son of Thomas and Lucia Bodulovich, born 26 February; godparents DOMINICUS URODA and Justina Mlix [?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 143, right-hand page, near the bottom, headed «Die 20 Martij 1752»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-LSZM|«Die 20 Martij 1752. Ego J. Bonavent. Radnich baptizavi in hoc Parti Bapto infantem natum die 26 p.e. Februarij ex Thoma et Lucia Bodulovich leg. con. huius loci, cui nomen impos. est Josephus. Patrini Dominicus Uroda, et Justina Mlix [?] ex hac Cura». Read at about 4x; the surname is written «Uroda» here.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1755-07-vitus-antonius-pajanin-assistant-dominicus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1755-07-vitus-antonius-pajanin-assistant-dominicus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 6 July 1755 — baptism of Vitus Antonius, son of Aloysius and Mathea Pajanin, born 11 June; godfather Joannes Matheus Miocevich, and «assistens DOM. DOMINICUS VRODA»|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 153, left-hand page, the first entry, margin «Vitus Antonius Pajanin», headed «Die 6 July 1755»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-LSDX|«Die 6 July 1755. Ego Presbiter Thomas Jadovou Parochus Ecclesiae S. Marci in suburbio Marij, Baptizavi in Baptisterio supradictae Ecclesiae infantem natum die 11 Junij ex Coniugibus Aloysio et Mathea Pajanin, cui impositum fuit Nomen Vitus Antonius. Patrini fuerunt Dominus Joannes Matheus Miocevich, et assistens Dom. Dominicus Vroda». Read at about 4x; «assistens» is a second sponsor or a witness to the rite.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1757-02-lucia-pajanin-godfather-dominicus-son-of-late-georgius-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1757-02-lucia-pajanin-godfather-dominicus-son-of-late-georgius-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 13 February 1757 — baptism of Lucia, daughter of Matheus and Elena Pajanin, born 16 October 1756; godparents D. DOMINICUS, SON OF THE LATE GEORGIUS VRODA, and Bartholomea, wife of Nicolaus Save|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 159, right-hand page, the first entry, margin «Lucia Pajanin», headed «Die 13 Februarij 1757» (page 52)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-LSVT|«Die 13 Februarij 1757. Ego Presbiter Thomas Jadovou Parochus Eccl. S. Marci in Suburbio Marij, baptizavi in Baptisterio supradictae Ecclesiae infantem natam die 16 Octobris anni 1756 ex Coniugibus Matheo et Elena Pajanin, cui impositum fuit nomen Lucia, patrini fuerunt D. Dominicus filius qd. [quondam] Georgij Vroda, et Bartholomea Uxor Nicolai Save». Read at about 4x. **«Dominicus, son of the late Georgius Vroda»: the only entry of any register read that names a father of a Šibenik Uroda master, and it says the father was dead by February 1757.** Whether this Dominicus is the Magister of 1741, 1745–55 and 1756–67 is not stated; he is written «Dominicus» and no trade is given.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik,georgius-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1757-09-helena-raich-godfather-dominicus-vroda-pictor|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1757-09-helena-raich-godfather-dominicus-vroda-pictor-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 11 September 1757 — baptism of Helena, daughter of Matheus and Margarita Raich, born 10 August; godfather DOMINICUS VRODA, PICTOR (a painter), and Josephus Maverci|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1701–1784 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2C-L2Q, 434 images)|image 161, right-hand page, the last entry, margin «Helena Raich», headed «Die 11 Septe.r 1757»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-LS6D|«Die 11 Septe.r 1757. Ego Presbiter Thomas Jadovou Parochus Ecclesiae S. Marci in Suburbio Marij, Baptizavi in Baptisterio supradictae Ecclesiae Infantem natam die decima Augusti anni supradicti, ex coniugibus Matheo, et Margarita Raich, cui impositum fuit nomen Helena. Patrini fuerunt Dominicus Vroda Pictor, et Josephus Maverci». Read at about 4x; «Pictor» (painter) is a trade written beside the name. A Dominicus Vroda in a different trade from the «Magister» of the 1740s; whether one man or two is not shown.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1687-04-anastasia-godparents-dominicus-vroda-and-catarina-wife-of-thomas-vrodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1687-04-anastasia-godparents-dominicus-vroda-and-catarina-wife-of-thomas-vrodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), April 1687 — baptism of Anastasia, daughter of Laurentius and Lucia [Vlovich?]; godparents DOMINICUS VRODA and Catarina, wife of THOMAS VRODICH|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 9, the right-hand page, upper middle, an entry headed «Die 19 Aprilis» (the page is in the year 1687; the entries around it are not in strict date order)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-NWQ|«Die 19 Aprilis [1687]. Ego fr Andreas Reinich [?] à Corai Parochus S. Marci Suburbij Maris Baptizavi infantem natam die 13 [?] ex Laurentio et Lucia [Vlovich?] cui nomen impositum est Anastasia ex dicta Parochia. Patrini fuerunt Dominicus Vroda et Catarina uxor Thome Vrodich». Read at about 4x; the surname is spelled Vroda in the first and Vrodich in the second. **The earliest Uroda in any Šibenik register read: two men, a Dominicus and a Thomas, in April 1687, the second married to a Catarina.**|dominicus-vroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1689-01-joanna-sevelich-godparents-dominus-vrodich-and-ursula|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1689-01-joanna-sevelich-godparents-dominus-vrodich-and-ursula-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 8 [or 6] January 1689 — baptism of Joanna, daughter of Joannes Sevelich and Gliuba; godparents DOMINUS VRODICH and Ursula, his wife|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 11, the foot of the left-hand page, the last entry, headed «Die 8 Januarii 1689»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-N44|«Die 8 Januarii 1689. Ego fr Petrus Paropsidi de Cothor Vice Parochus huius Ecclesiae S. Marci Baptizavi infante natu ex Joanne Sevelich & Gliuba coniugibus eiusdem Parochiae cui nomen impositu e Joanna. Patrini fuerunt Dominus Vrodich & Vrsula eius coniunx ex eadem Parochia». Read at about 4x; the forename of «Dominus Vrodich» is not given (the Dominicus Vroda of 1687, 1692, 1693 is the likely man; his wife is Ursula in July 1692).|dominicus-vroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1691-12-catharina-sintich-godparents-anastasia-wife-of-paulus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1691-12-catharina-sintich-godparents-anastasia-wife-of-paulus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 2 December 1691 — baptism of Catharina, daughter of Stephanus Sintich and Lucia, born 25 November; godparents Joannes Rupcich and ANASTASIA, WIFE OF PAULUS VRODA|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 20, right-hand page, the first entry at the top, headed «Die 2 Decembris 1691»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-NDB|«Die 2 Decembris 1691. Ego fr Petrus Paropsidi de Cothor Parochus huius Ecclesiae Parochialis S. Marci Baptizavi infante nato sub die 25 Novembris ultimo elapsi ex Stephano Sintich & Lucia coniugibus: cui nomen impositum est Catharina. Patrini fuerunt Joannes Rupcich & Anastasia coniunx Pauli Vroda omnes ex hac Parochia Sancti Marci». Read at about 4x. **A Paulus Vroda, married to an Anastasia, in December 1691.**|paulus-vroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1692-07-lucia-daughter-of-dominicus-vrodi-and-ursula|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1692-07-lucia-daughter-of-dominicus-vrodi-and-ursula-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 31 July 1692 — baptism of LUCIA, daughter of DOMINICUS VRODI and URSULA, born 28 July; godparents Franciscus Amadeo alias Pepich of this city, and Margarita, wife of Franciscus Stanisich|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 23, left-hand page, near the foot, the entry headed «Die 31 Julij 1692»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-NWR|«Die 31 Julij 1692. Ego fr Petrus Paropsidi de Cothor Parochus huius Ecclesiae Parochialis S. Marci Baptizavi infante nata sub die 28 huius ex Dominico Vrodi, & Ursula coniugibus: Cui nomen impositum est Lucia. Patrini fuerunt Franciscus Amadeo alias Pepich ex hac Civitate, & Margarita uxor Francisci Stanisich ex hac Parochia Sancti Marci». Read at about 4x. **A Dominicus Vrodi with a wife Ursula and a daughter Lucia in 1692.**|dominicus-vroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1692-08-elias-boghcrich-godmother-justina-daughter-of-thomas-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1692-08-elias-boghcrich-godmother-justina-daughter-of-thomas-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 2 August 1692 — baptism of Elias, son of Andreas Boghcrich [Bogherich] and Joanna Vidovich, born 31 July; godparents Narcissus Crinelosi [Cimelosi] and JUSTINA, DAUGHTER OF THOMAS VRODA|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 23, left-hand page, the last entry, headed «Die 2 Augusti 1692»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-NWR|«Die 2 Augusti 1692. Ego fr Petrus Paropsidi de Cothor Parochus huius Ecclesiae Parochialis S. Marci Baptizavi infante nato sub die 31 Julij ex Andrea Bogherich filio q. Eliae Franich, & Joanna Vidovich coniugibus: Cui nomen impositum est Elias. Patrini fuerunt Narcisus Crinelosi, & Justina filia Thome Vroda omnes ex hac Parochia Sancti Marci». Read at about 4x. **A Thomas Vroda who has a daughter old enough to be a godmother in 1692** (so married by about 1675).|thomas-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1692-08-antonius-son-of-luca-vrodi|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1692-08-antonius-son-of-luca-vrodi-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 6 August 1692 — baptism of ANTONIUS, son of LUCA VRODI and MARIOTA, born 3 [August]; godparents Andreas Stanisich and Antonia, wife of Andreas Franini|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 24, left-hand page, the first entry, headed «Die 6 Augusti 1692»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-NWX|«Die 6 Augusti 1692. Ego fr Petrus Paropsidi de Cothor Parochus huius Ecclesiae Parochialis S. Marci Baptizavi infante nato sub die 3 huius ex Luca Vrodi, & Mariota coniugibus: cui nomen impositum est Antonius. Patrini fuerunt Andreas Stanisich, & Antonia uxor Andree Franini omnes ex hac Parochia». Read at about 4x. **A Lucas Vrodi with a wife Mariota in 1692** — the Lucas Vrodich of 1705 and 1710, or his father.|lucas-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1692-09-joannes-galiotovich-godmother-catharina-wife-of-thomas-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1692-09-joannes-galiotovich-godmother-catharina-wife-of-thomas-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 17 September 1692 — baptism of Joannes, son of Elias Galiotovich and Helena Stanisich, born 29 August; godparents Petrus Gechich and CATHARINA, WIFE OF THOMAS VRODA|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 24, left-hand page, the last entry, headed «Die 17 Septembris 1692»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-NWX|«Die 17 Septembris 1692. Ego fr Petrus Paropsidi de Cothor Parochus huius Ecclesiae S. Marci Baptizavi infante natum sub die 29 Augusti ex Elia Galiotovich, & Helena Stanisich coniugibus: Cui nomen impositum est Joannes. Patrini fuerunt Petrus Gechich, & Catharina uxor Thome Vrode. Omnes ex hac Parochia Sancti Marci». Read at about 4x. **Thomas Vroda's wife is Catharina** (as in April 1687).|thomas-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1693-02-catharina-croglienich-godfather-dominicus-vrodi|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1693-02-catharina-croglienich-godfather-dominicus-vrodi-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 22 February 1693 — baptism of Catharina, daughter of Joannes Croglienich and Hieronyma, born 19 [February]; godparents DOMINICUS VRODI and Ursula, wife of Hieronymus Trapilei|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 25, left-hand page, the first entry at the top, headed «Die 22 Februarii 1693»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-NX6|«Die 22 Februarii 1693. Ego fr Petrus Paropsidi de Cothor Parochus huius Ecclesiae Parochialis S. Marci Baptizavi infantem natam sub die 19 currentis ex Joanne Croglienich, & Hieronyma coniugibus: Cui nomen impositum est Catharina. Patrini fuerunt Dominicus Vrodi, & Ursula uxor Hieronymi Trapilei. Omnes ex hac Parochia Sancti Marci». Read at about 4x. The godmother Ursula is the wife of a Hieronymus Trapilei, so she is not Dominicus's wife (Ursula, July 1692) unless the entry runs two names together.|dominicus-vroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1693-08-paulina-miglianich-godparents-paulus-vroda-and-stanislava|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1693-08-paulina-miglianich-godparents-paulus-vroda-and-stanislava-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 24 August 1693 — baptism of Paulina, daughter of Stephanus and Lucia Miglianich; godparents PAULUS VRODA and Stanislava [?], his wife|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 25, right-hand page, the last entry, headed «Die 24 Agusti 1693»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-NX6|«1693. Die 24 Agusti. Paulina filia Stefani et Lucie Miglianich coniugum fuit bap[tizata] per me f. Bonaventura Bilogla[v] Parochum Sancti Marci de suburbio Marij. Patrini fuerunt Paulus Vroda et Stanislava [?] uxor eiusdem». Read at about 4x in a new hand (Fr. Bonaventura Bilogla[v], from August 1693); the wife's name is doubtful (Stanislava, Veonislava). **Paulus Vroda is married to an Anastasia in 1691 and to a «Stanislava» [?] in 1693** — a different wife, or one name misread.|paulus-vroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1693-09-aurelia-daughter-of-domini-and-silvia-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1693-09-aurelia-daughter-of-domini-and-silvia-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 17 September 1693 — baptism of AURELIA, daughter of «Domini» [Dominici?] and Silvia [?] VRODA; godparents Simeon Vidovich and Vicentia Vidovich|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 26, left-hand page, near the top, the entry headed «Die 17 Septembris 1693»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-NZX|«1693. Die 17 setembris. Aurelia filia Domini [Dominici?] et Salvi [Silvia?] Vroda coniugum fuit baptizata per me f. Bonaventura Bilogla[v] Parochum S. Marci de suburbio Marij. Patrini fuerunt Simeon Vidovich et Vicentia Vidovich». Read at about 4x; **doubtful in two places**: «Domini» may be a short form of Dominici (the Dominicus Vrodi of 1692, whose wife was Ursula, not Silvia) and the mother's name is not clear.|dominicus-vroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1695-07-joanna-godmother-stanca-vroda|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1695-07-joanna-godmother-stanca-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), July 1695 — baptism of Joanna, daughter of Stephanus [?] and Lucia Tintich [?]; godparents D. HIERONYMUS TRAPILEUS and STANCA VRODA|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 29, right-hand page, the first entry at the top (page 95), headed «Die 13 [?] July 1695»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-NHZ|«1695. Die 13 [?] July. Joanna filia Josefani [?] et Lucie Tintis [?] coniugum fuit bapti[zata] per me f. Bonaventura Bilogla[v] Parochum Sancti Marci de suburbio Marij. Patrini fuerunt D. Gerolimus Trapileus et Stanca Vroda». Read at about 4x; the date and the parents' names are doubtful, **the godmother «Stanca Vroda»** is clear. A Stanca [Stanislava?] Vroda may be the Stanislava, wife of Paulus Vroda (1693).|paulus-vroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1696-05-jacoba-godmother-lucia-vrodna-doubtful|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1696-05-jacoba-godmother-lucia-vrodna-doubtful-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 5 May 1696 — baptism of Jacoba, daughter of Franciscus [?] and Michaela Michel [?]; godparents D. Franciscus Stanisich and LUCIA VRODNA [Urodna?] (doubtful)|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 30, left-hand page, the entry headed «Die 5 Maij 1696», near the foot of the first strip|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-N78|«1696. Die 5 May. Jacoba filia Franjer [?] Michaeli [?] Michel coniugum fuit bap[tizata] per me fratrem Bonaventuram Bilogla[v] Parochum de suburbio Marij Sancti Marci. Patrini fuerunt D. Franc. Stanisich et Lucia Vrodna». Read at about 3x; the second surname may be Vrodna, Urodna or another word (**doubtful** and recorded only as such).||12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-baptism-1698-07-michael-son-of-lucas-and-marieta-vrodich|sibenik-dolac-baptism-1698-07-michael-son-of-lucas-and-marieta-vrodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 13 July 1698 — baptism of MICHAEL, son of LUCAS and MARIETA VRODICH; godparents Joannes Bratich and Juanippo [?] Anetich|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) births 1685–1700 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R24-1XW, 41 images; the first book, cover «Liber Baptizatorum 8 Oct 1685 – 1700»)|image 34, left-hand page, the entry headed «Die 13 Julij [1698]», margin «Michael Vrodich»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-N4R|«Die 13 Julij [1698]. Ego fr. Andreas Rezich [?] à Corai Parochus S. Marci Suburbij Maris Sibenici Baptizavi infante natum sub die 9 diti ex legitimis coniugibus: Dno Luca et Marietta Vrodich cui nomen impositum fuit Michael. Patrini fuerunt Joannes Bratich et Juanippo [?] Anetich ambo ex dicta Parochia». Read at about 4x; the margin note gives the child's name and surname «Michael Vrodich». **A Lucas Vrodich with a wife Marieta, a son Michael in 1698** (a Lucas Vrodi with a wife Mariota had a son Antonius in 1692).|lucas-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1701-11-lucas-son-of-the-late-antonius-vroda-and-francisca|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1701-11-lucas-son-of-the-late-antonius-vroda-and-francisca-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 13 November 1701 — marriage of LUCAS, SON OF THE LATE ANTONIUS VRODA, and Francisca, daughter of the late Joannes Loveta|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images; the book's cover reads «Šibenik, župa Dolac, vjenčani 6/2.1701–8/4.1764»)|image 372, right-hand page, the entry headed «Die 13 Novembris 1701» in the upper half|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-5ZDG|«Die 13 Novembris 1701. Lucas filius qm Antonij Vroda contraxit matrimonium per verba de presenti cum Francisca filia qm Joannis Loveta ex hac Parochia S. Marci, presente me fre Andrea Rinich [?] … et testis Dno Jacobo …». Read at about 4x; the first line's second word is written «Lucas» and the father's forename is a clear «Antonij». **A Lucas Vroda, son of the late ANTONIUS Vroda, marries a Francisca in 1701** — after the Mariota of 1692 and the Marieta of 1698, so a widower's second marriage (or two Lucases); the Simeon of 1705 and the Paulus Antonius of 1710 follow in the baptisms.|lucas-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1702-01-thomas-vrodich-and-anastasia-daughter-of-jacobus|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1702-01-thomas-vrodich-and-anastasia-daughter-of-jacobus-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 8 January 1702 — marriage of THOMAS VRODICH and Anastasia, daughter of Jacobus Vitich [?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images; the book's cover reads «Šibenik, župa Dolac, vjenčani 6/2.1701–8/4.1764»)|image 373, right-hand page, the entry headed «Die 8 Januarii 1702» (page edge worn)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-5ZDT|«Die 8 Januarii 1702. Thomas Vrodich ex hac Parochia S. Marci contraxit matrimonium per verba de presenti cum Anastasia filia qm Jacobi Vitich [?] ex Antiq[ua?] … post solitas tres denuntiationes, presente me fre Andrea Rupich …». Read at about 3x; the bride's father's name and place are partly lost to the worn edge. **Thomas Vrodich marries an ANASTASIA on 8 January 1702 — the Thomas and Anastasia whose son Paulus is baptised on 14 May 1706**; he had a wife Catarina in 1687 and 1692, so this is a second marriage (or a second Thomas).|thomas-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1710-10-antonius-son-of-the-late-paulus-vrodich-and-anna-widow|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1710-10-antonius-son-of-the-late-paulus-vrodich-and-anna-widow-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), [1 or 7] October 1710 — marriage of ANTONIUS, SON OF THE LATE PAULUS VRODICH, and Anna, widow of the late Antonius Ivanitich|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images; the book's cover reads «Šibenik, župa Dolac, vjenčani 6/2.1701–8/4.1764»)|image 382, left-hand page, the first entry at the top, headed «Die [1 or 7] octobris 1710»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-5Z7Y|«Die [7] octobris 1710. Contraxit sacrum matrimonium per verba de presenti Antonius filius qdm Pauli Vrodich cum Vidua Anna uxore qdm Antonij Ivanitich [?] pro tribus denuntiationibus in propria habitatione sui sponsi … presente me Fr. Andrea [?] … Parocho S. Marci …». Read at about 3x; the day number and the late husband's name are doubtful. **A son Antonius of a PAULUS Vrodich, dead by 1710** — the Paulus Vroda of 1691–95 (wife Anastasia/Stanislava), so his son is a groom in 1710.|paulus-vroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1717-02-witness-franciscus-vrodich|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1717-02-witness-franciscus-vrodich-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 7 February 1717 — marriage of Nicolaus Sesanovich and Thomizza, widow of the late Marcus; the witnesses include Christophorus Cornich and «Franc[iscus] Vrodich»|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images; the book's cover reads «Šibenik, župa Dolac, vjenčani 6/2.1701–8/4.1764»)|image 391, left-hand page, the entry headed «Die 7 februarii 1717» at the foot of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-5ZWY|«Die 7 februarii 1717. [Denuntiationibus] duobus omissis cum dispensatione … Nicolaus Sesanovich ad … Thomizza relicta qdm Marci … Presente me fr. Philippo Surcovich Parocho … et testibus … D. Christophoro Cornich, frane Vrodich [?], et omnibus aliis». Read at about 4x in a faint hand; the witness's forename is abbreviated and may be Franc[iscus] (the Franciscus Vrodich of the baptisms 1710–1721) — **doubtful**.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1718-10-antonius-son-of-lucas-vrodich-and-antonia|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1718-10-antonius-son-of-lucas-vrodich-and-antonia-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 30 October 1718 — marriage of ANTONIUS, SON OF LUCAS VRODICH, and Antonia, daughter of Matthaeus Merra [?]|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images; the book's cover reads «Šibenik, župa Dolac, vjenčani 6/2.1701–8/4.1764»)|image 395, left-hand page, the entry headed «Die 30 8bris 1718» at the foot of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-5CLY|«Die 30 8bris 1718. Antonius filius Luce Vrodich contraxit S. matrimonium cum Antonia filia Mathei Merra [?] ex hujus Parochie S. Marci sub Urbio Maris, denuntiationibus omissis et dispensatione Ill.mi et Rev.mi D.D. Episcopi Dominici Calegari. per verba de presenti cum mutuo consensu et nullo impedimento detecto in domo presente me fratre Georgii Selatouich Vice Parocho … testibus … D. Don Luca filius D. Michaeli … et D. Marcus fili[us] …». Read at about 4x. **A son Antonius of a Lucas Vrodich** — the Antonius baptised 6 August 1692 would be 26.|lucas-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1725-11-michael-lestanovich-and-matthea-kymcevich-witness-franciscus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1725-11-michael-lestanovich-and-matthea-kymcevich-witness-franciscus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 25 November 1725 — marriage of Michael Lestanovich and Matthea, daughter of Petrus Kymcevich; the witnesses are «Dno Anto Carisso, et Franco Vroda»|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images; the book's cover reads «Šibenik, župa Dolac, vjenčani 6/2.1701–8/4.1764»)|image 403, left-hand page, the entry headed «Die 25 Novembris 1725» at the top|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-5C1K|«Die 25 Novembris 1725. [Tribus] denuntiationibus premissis … Michaelem filium Jacobi Lestanovich et Matheam filiam Dni Petri Kymcevich ex hac Parochia S. Marci. Ego Pr. Franciscus Parchych Dre Ecclesie Rector, eorum mutuo consensu habito solemniter per verba de presenti matrimonio conjunxi. Presentibus testibus Dno Anto Carisso, et Franco Vroda». Read at about 4x. **The Franco Vroda who stands at the font from 1725 (the «Mr. Franciscus Vroda» of the baptisms) is a witness here the same month.**|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1739-01-joannes-buyas-and-franceschina-toglian-witness-dominicus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1739-01-joannes-buyas-and-franceschina-toglian-witness-dominicus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 13 January 1739 — marriage of Joannes Buyas [?] and Franceschina, daughter of Matthaeus Toglian; the witnesses are «Dno Georgio Bonacich, et Mro Domco Vroda»|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images; the book's cover reads «Šibenik, župa Dolac, vjenčani 6/2.1701–8/4.1764»)|image 420, left-hand page, the last lines at the top (the entry begins at the foot of image 419, right-hand page, headed «Die 13 Januarii 1739»)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-5CHV|«… Toglian ex da Pa. Ego Fr. Franciscus Parchych Dre Ecclesie Rector, eorum mutuo consensu habito solemnitr per verba de presenti matrimonio conjunxi in da Ecclesia. Presentibus testibus Dno Georgio Bonacich, et Mro Domco Vroda multisq. alys». Read at about 4x; the heading and the couple's names are on image 419. **A Magister Dominicus Vroda (the «Mr Domcus Vroda» abbreviation of 1726) is a witness in January 1739** — two years before the godfather of 1741.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-marriage-1746-08-matheus-darin-and-vincentia-pavicich-witness-dominicus-vrodda-son-of-magister-georgius|sibenik-dolac-marriage-1746-08-matheus-darin-and-vincentia-pavicich-witness-dominicus-vrodda-son-of-magister-georgius-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 4 August 1746 — marriage of Matheus Darin of Jasana and Vincentia Pavicich, servants of the noble Julius Viddovich; the witnesses include «DOMINICO VRODDA, FILIO MAGISTRI GEORGII DE HAC PAROCHIA»|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) marriages 1701–1764 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-RM9, 554 images; the book's cover reads «Šibenik, župa Dolac, vjenčani 6/2.1701–8/4.1764»)|image 433, left-hand page, the entry headed «Anno Dni 1746 – Die 4 Aug», margin «Matheus Darin cum Vincentia Pavicich»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-5CLB|«Anno Dni 1746 – Die 4 Aug. Omissis tribus denuntiationibus ex facultate mihi tradita … Ego Angelus Trapileo Paroc. Ecclesie S. Marci huius sub Urbii Maris … interrogavi Matheum Joannis filium Aloysii Darin de Jasana nunc servus Ill.mi D.Co. Julij Viddovich Nob. Scardon. et Vincentiam filiam qm Marci Pavicich de Villa Verbagna Diecesis Lesine … Presentibus testibus Ill.mo D. Georgio Viddovich Nob. Scardon., Ill.mo D. Aloysio Simeonech Nob. Sibenicen. et DOMINICO VRODDA FILIO MAGISTRI GEORGII DE HAC PAROCHIA, multisq…». Read at about 4x. **«Dominicus Vrodda, son of Magister Georgius» — the same Dominicus whose father is «the late Georgius Vroda» in February 1757. So Magister Georgius Uroda of Dolac was ALIVE on 4 August 1746 and dead by 13 February 1757.**|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik,georgius-uroda-of-sibenik|12 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-death-1740-10-magdalena-daughter-of-magister-georgius-vrode|sibenik-dolac-death-1740-10-magdalena-daughter-of-magister-georgius-vrode-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 29 October 1740 — burial of MAGDALENA, [infant] daughter of MAGISTER GEORGIUS VRODE, in the church of S. Dominic|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) deaths 1701–1783 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-C62, 523 images; the 1701–1783 deaths book)|image 222, right-hand page, the entry headed «Die 29 Octobris 1740», between the entries of 27 October and 2 November|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-P6S4|«Die 29 Octobris 1740. Magdalena Infans [?] filia Magistri Georgii Vrode, animam Deo reddidit, cuius corpus sepultum fuit in Ecclesia S. Dominici Fratrum Praedicatorum.» Read at about 4x; the second word after the forename is faint and may be «Infans». **A child of a Magister Georgius Vroda dies in October 1740** — and no baptism of a Magdalena (or any child of a Georgius Uroda) is in the Dolac baptism book of 1731–1744 (images 108–129, read), so she was baptised in another parish or not entered.|georgius-uroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-death-1742-01-marietta-daughter-of-magister-antonius-vroda|sibenik-dolac-death-1742-01-marietta-daughter-of-magister-antonius-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 18 January 1742 — death of MARIETTA, daughter of MAGISTER ANTONIUS VRODA, who had received the sacraments|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) deaths 1701–1783 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-C62, 523 images; the 1701–1783 deaths book)|image 231, right-hand page, the last entry at the foot, headed «Die 18 Januarii 1742»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-PDTB|«Die 18 Januarii 1742. Marietta [Marcetta?] filia Magistri Antonij Vroda, munita SS. Sacramentis per Rev.dum V. Parocum Nicolaum Miagostovich, animam Deo reddidit in Parochia S. Marci, cuius corpus sepult[um fuit …]». Read at about 4x; the forename is crowded against the margin. **A Magister ANTONIUS Vroda, alive [«Magistri», not «qm»] in January 1742** — the Antonius baptised 6 August 1692 (son of Lucas) who married Antonia on 30 October 1718.|antonius-uroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-death-1742-07-dominica-daughter-of-magister-antonius-and-antonia-vrodda|sibenik-dolac-death-1742-07-dominica-daughter-of-magister-antonius-and-antonia-vrodda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 19 July 1742 — death of DOMINICA, aged about 13, daughter of MAGISTER ANTONIUS and ANTONIA VRODDA; buried in the church of S. Dominic|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) deaths 1701–1783 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-C62, 523 images; the 1701–1783 deaths book)|image 233, right-hand page, the last entry on the page (margin «Dom. Vroda 29»), headed «Anno Dni 1742 – 19 Julii»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-PDJ7|«Anno Dni 1742 – 19 Julii. Dominica filia Magistri Antonij, et Antoniae Conjugum Vrodda, annorum circiter 13 agens, confessa, sanctissimoque olei unctione roborata a me Angelo Trapileo Parocho Ecclesiae S. Marci, cuius corpus sepultum est in Ecclesia S. Dominici Fratrum Praedicatorum.» Read at about 4x. **The wife is named: Antonia — as in the marriage of Antonius, son of Lucas Vrodich, and Antonia on 30 October 1718**; a daughter of about 13 is born about 1729.|antonius-uroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-death-1744-01-paulus-infant-son-of-magister-dominicus-and-floria-vrodda|sibenik-dolac-death-1744-01-paulus-infant-son-of-magister-dominicus-and-floria-vrodda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 7 January 1744 — burial of PAULUS, an infant son of MAGISTER DOMINICUS and FLORIA VRODDA, in the church of the nuns of S. Salvator|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) deaths 1701–1783 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-C62, 523 images; the 1701–1783 deaths book)|image 236, left-hand page, lower half (margin «Paulus Vrodda 48»), headed «Anno Dni 1744 – Die 7 Januarii»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-PD19|«Anno Dni 1744 – Die 7 Januarii. Paulus parvulus filius Magistri Dominici, et Floriae Vrodda, cuius corpus sepultum fuit in Ecclesia monialium S. Salvatoris huius Civitatis.» Read at about 4x. **A first child of Magister Dominicus Vroda and Floria, who then have Lucia (born 12 December 1744) and Vittoria (born 10 May 1745).**|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-death-1746-06-lucia-of-the-late-magister-dominicus-vrodda-aged-77|sibenik-dolac-death-1746-06-lucia-of-the-late-magister-dominicus-vrodda-aged-77-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 21 June 1746 — death of LUCIA, wife [widow?] of the late MAGISTER DOMINICUS VRODDA, aged about 77; buried in the church of S. Mark|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) deaths 1701–1783 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-C62, 523 images; the 1701–1783 deaths book)|image 241, left-hand page, the second entry (margin «Lucia Vrodda 88»), headed «Anno Dni 1746 Die 21 Junij»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-PDPS|«Anno Dni 1746 – Die 21 Junij. Lucia ux[or] q. Mag: Dominici Vrodda huius Parochiae S. Marci, munita SS. Sacramentis in Communione S.M.E. clausit diem extremum annorum 77 circiter, cuius corpus iacet in hac Parochiali Ecclesia S. Marci.» Read at about 4x; the abbreviation after «Lucia» is read «ux.» (wife), which would make her the widow of a **Magister Dominicus Vrodda dead by 21 June 1746** and born about 1669 — so the elder Dominicus Vroda of 1687–1693 (wife Ursula, before) or a master of the same name.|dominicus-vroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-death-1754-08-dominus-georgius-vroda-aged-60|sibenik-dolac-death-1754-08-dominus-georgius-vroda-aged-60-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 17 August 1754 — death of DOMINUS GEORGIUS VRODA, aged about 60, buried in the church of S. Dominic|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) deaths 1701–1783 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-C62, 523 images; the 1701–1783 deaths book)|image 254, left-hand page, near the top (margin «Georgius Vroda»), headed «Die 17 Augusti 1754»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-PDD9|«Die 17 Augusti 1754. Dominus Georgius Vroda aetatis annorum 60: Confessus et Sacra Unctione munitus, sed ob continuam phrenesim Sacra Communione orbatus obiit, cuius corpus sepultum fuit in Ecclesia S. Dominici Fratrum Praedicatorum.» Read at about 4x. **The only Georgius Vroda found dying between August 1746 and August 1754 in a read of images 241–254, and so very probably the Magister Georgius alive on 4 August 1746 and dead by 13 February 1757** (images 255–262 of the book, to February 1757, were not read). Aged about 60 → born about 1694.|georgius-uroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-cathedral-birth-1694-10-georgius-son-of-dominicus-and-lucietta-vroda|sibenik-cathedral-birth-1694-10-georgius-son-of-dominicus-and-lucietta-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik cathedral (S. Jacobi), baptised 10 October 1694 — GEORGIUS, born 6 October 1694, son of DOMINICUS and LUCIETTA VRODA; margin «Georgius Vroda»|Šibenik cathedral parish (S. Jacobi) births 1693–17.. (FamilySearch waypoint 9R28-SPJ, the «Liber Baptizatorum 1693–», cover at image 260; the baptisms of the Dolac suburb were also done in the cathedral baptistery)|image 272, right-hand page, last entry (margin «Georgius Vroda»), headed «Die 10 Octobris 1694»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-5Y4J|«Die 10 Octobris 1694. Ego Joannes Bapta Chiochius alias Monticelli Vicarius … Baptizavi infantem natum sub die 6 Octobris 1694 in Parochia Divi Jacobi, cui impositus nomen Georgius ex Coniugibus Dominico et Lucietta Vroda; Patrini fuerunt Illmus Dominus Hieronymus Sopra[?] et Domina Franceschina uxor Excellmi Domini Vicenty de Dominis.» Read at about 4x; the surname is written «Vroda» in the text and in the margin. **A Georgius Vroda aged «60» died at Dolac on 17 August 1754 (image 254); a boy born 6 October 1694 would have been 59 years 10 months old that day.** The parents' names, Dominicus and Lucietta, match the elder Magister Dominicus Vrodda and his widow Lucia, aged about 77 at death on 21 June 1746, of the Dolac parish.|georgius-uroda-of-sibenik,dominicus-vroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-cathedral-birth-1694-01-michaela-daughter-of-magister-lucas-and-maria-vroda|sibenik-cathedral-birth-1694-01-michaela-daughter-of-magister-lucas-and-maria-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik cathedral (S. Jacobi), January 1694 — MICHAELA, daughter of MAGISTER LUCAS and MARIA VRODA; margin «Michaela Vroda»|Šibenik cathedral parish (S. Jacobi) births 1693–17.. (FamilySearch waypoint 9R28-SPJ, the «Liber Baptizatorum 1693–», cover at image 260; the baptisms of the Dolac suburb were also done in the cathedral baptistery)|image 268, left-hand page, last entry (margin «Michaela Vroda»), below the heading «1694» and «Die 5 [?] Januarii 1694»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-R4N|«Ego D. Stephanus Martinelli … Baptizavi in Baptisterio S. Jacobi ex licentia Rev. Ordinarij infantem natam sub die … cui impositum fuit nomen Michaela filia Magistri Lucae et Mariae Vrodal. Patrini fuerunt Thomas … Joannes Ingurovich et Vitus uxor Hieronimi Trapilei [?].» Read at about 4x. A Dolac household baptised at the cathedral baptistery with the Ordinary's leave: the Lucas Vrodi × Mariota of the Dolac books (Antonius 6 August 1692, Michael 13 July 1698) is the likely couple, but the Dolac baptism books carry no Michaela — so a Dolac family's children may be missing from the Dolac books.|lucas-uroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-cathedral-birth-1696-10-simeon-son-of-magister-dominicus-and-lucia-vrodda|sibenik-cathedral-birth-1696-10-simeon-son-of-magister-dominicus-and-lucia-vrodda-line.jpg||Šibenik cathedral (S. Jacobi), 14 [October] 1696 — SIMEON, son of MAGISTER DOMINICUS and LUCIA VRODDA of the Dolac suburb parish (S. Marci); margin «Simeon Vroda»|Šibenik cathedral parish (S. Jacobi) births 1693–17.. (FamilySearch waypoint 9R28-SPJ, the «Liber Baptizatorum 1693–», cover at image 260; the baptisms of the Dolac suburb were also done in the cathedral baptistery)|image 286, left-hand page, last entry (margin «Simeon Vroda»), headed «Die 14 dicti 1696»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-5YCB|«Ego Abbas et Canonicus Joannes Vilcovich [?] … in Basilica Divi Jacobi ex Parochia Divi Marci Suburbii, a Reverendo Domino Bono Vicario, infantem natum die … ex Coningibus Magistro Domco ac Lucia Vrodda; cui impositum fuit nomen Simeon: Patrini fuerunt Lucas … Joannes Dugovich [?] Locumtenens Militum Lombardorum et Domina Maria uxor … Domini Gubernatoris.» Read at about 4x. **The same pair as Georgius's parents of 1694 — Dominicus (Magister) and Lucia — now written as of the parish of S. Marci, i.e. the Dolac household of the elder Magister Dominicus Vrodda, whose widow Lucia died aged about 77 on 21 June 1746.** The day-of-month and the month are partly lost; the page runs through October 1696.|dominicus-vroda-of-sibenik,georgius-uroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-dolac-death-1738-11-magister-franciscus-vroda|sibenik-dolac-death-1738-11-magister-franciscus-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik (Dolac parish, S. Marci), 15 November 1738 — death of MAGISTER FRANCISCUS VRODA, buried in the church of the Holy Trinity|Šibenik, Dolac parish (S. Marci in Suburbio Maris) deaths 1701–1783 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2Z-C62, 523 images; the 1701–1756 book)|image 216, right-hand page, the middle entry, headed «Die 15 Novembris 1738»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-P647|«Die 15 Novembris 1738. Magister Franciscus Vroda munitus Sanctissimis Sacramentis per Rev.dum Vicarium Parochum Nicolaum Miagostovich animam Deo reddidit, cuius corpus sepultum fuit in Ecclesia Parochiali Sanctissimae Trinitatis.» Read at about 4x; the day-of-month reads 15 (the entry after it is also dated the 15th). **The Magister Franciscus Vroda who stood godfather at Dolac on 12 October 1738 and was dead by 6 May 1742 (his daughter Antonia, wife of a Joannes Biliznich): he died a month after his last sighting.** The Magister Franciscus Vroda of 1725–1738 and the Franciscus Vrodich × Anna of 1710–1721 are very probably one man; not shown.|franciscus-uroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-cathedral-birth-1740-06-joseph-joannes-son-of-magister-dominicus-and-flora-vroda|sibenik-cathedral-birth-1740-06-joseph-joannes-son-of-magister-dominicus-and-flora-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik cathedral (S. Jacobi), 7 June 1740 — ceremonies supplied for JOSEPH JOANNES, born 16 December 1739, son of MAGISTER DOMINICUS and FLORA VRODA of the parish of S. Marci; margin «Joseph Joannes Vroda»|Šibenik cathedral parish (S. Jacobi) births 1737–1768 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-MNY, 691 images; cover at image 10); the baptisms of the Dolac suburb were also done in the cathedral baptistery|image 31, right-hand page, first full entry (margin «Joseph Joannes Vroda»), headed «Die 7 [?] Junii 1740»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-RHF5|«Ego Presbyter Antonius Gianovich [?] Sacrista huius Cathedralis Ecclesiae de licentia Rdi Parochi S. Marci in suburbio maris supplevi reliquas ceremonias in Baptisterio eiusdem Cathedralis infanti nato die 16 Decembris anni praeteriti 1739 ex coniugibus Magistro Dominico et Flora Vroda Parochiae S. Marci, cui impositum fuit nomen Joseph Joannes, qui infans ritu baptismi fuit domi a parentum ob imminentis mortis periculum a Reverendo Domino Nicolao Miagostonich … Parocho dictae Parochiae S. Marci; cui assistentes fuerunt Joseph Fontana … et Magister Dominicus Gersovich parochiae S. Spiritus.» Read at about 4x; a few words are uncertain. **A first child of Magister Dominicus and Flora (the Floria of the Dolac books, whose Paulus, Lucia and Vittoria follow in 1744–45), baptised at home for danger of death and the ceremonies supplied at the cathedral; he is very probably the «Joannes filius Dominici Uroda», old enough to witness a marriage on 27 September 1757.**|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
sibenik-cathedral-birth-1741-08-anna-daughter-of-magister-dominicus-and-flora-vroda|sibenik-cathedral-birth-1741-08-anna-daughter-of-magister-dominicus-and-flora-vroda-line.jpg||Šibenik cathedral (S. Jacobi), 6 August 1741 — ceremonies supplied for ANNA, born in May 1741, daughter of MAGISTER DOMINICUS and FLORA VRODA of the parish of S. Marci; margin «Anna Vroda»|Šibenik cathedral parish (S. Jacobi) births 1737–1768 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-MNY, 691 images; cover at image 10); the baptisms of the Dolac suburb were also done in the cathedral baptistery|image 41, left-hand page, last entry (margin «Anna Vroda»), headed «Die 6 Augusti 1741»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-RH2W|«Die 6 Augusti 1741. Anna filia Mri Dominici [et] Florae coniugum Vroda parochiae S. Marci suburbii maris, hanc infantem natam die 2? Maii proxime elapsi … fuit in [casa] … ab … baptizari ex licentia … S. Marci … ceremoniae supplerae … cui impositum nomen Anna; Patrini … Julia Vidovich et … Joannes Antonius [Scolini?].» Read at about 4x; the middle of the entry is hard to read and the day of birth is doubtful. A second child of Dominicus and Flora, in no Dolac book.|dominicus-uroda-of-sibenik|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
pag-death-1764-01-angelus-bacchi-aromatarius|pag-death-1764-01-angelus-bacchi-aromatarius-line.jpg||Pag, 19 January 1764 — death of DNUS ANGELUS BACCHI, apothecary («Aromatarius»), aged about 68|Pag deaths (FamilySearch Croatia, Church Books 1516–1994, DGS film 005494123 item 2; index record 1:1:XQM9-MT4W)|a spread of the register, right-hand page, near the foot, headed «Anno Dni 1764 die 19 Januarij»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-FJTY|«Anno Dni 1764 die 19 Januarij. Obijt Dnus Angelus Bacchi Aromatarius in Comunione S. Matris Ecclesiae, cuius corpus sepultum est in Ecclesia totius [?] Insignis Collegiatae … confessus … Dno Cancellario Joanni Mestrovich … Sacramento Eucharistiae … annorum circiter 68.» Read at about 4x; the place is Pag by the index and by the Collegiate church; the register does not name the town in this entry. **Born about 1696 — the age of the Dno Angelo Bachi, patrician, whose son Caietanus Antonius Gregorius was baptised at Pag on 14 March 1728; the trade, apothecary, is new.** No son is named. The Caetanus Bachi who married at Karlobag on 4 February 1753 was dead by October 1760, so this death says nothing about him.|angelus-bacchi-of-pag|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
nin-death-1768-10-dna-viena-bachi|nin-death-1768-10-dna-viena-bachi-line.jpg||Nin, 6 October 1768 [the index says 1767] — death of DNA VIENA BACHI, who died suddenly and was buried in the chapel of the B.V.M. delle Purine|Nin (Roman Catholic) births 1755–1797, 1825–1854, marriages and deaths (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2H-PYM, DGS film 005494105 item 7; index record 1:1:XQMM-LPL5)|a spread of the deaths register in Italian, right-hand page, near the foot (the entry before 14 ottobre 1769)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899X-KQSP|«Addì 6 ottobre 176[6/8]. Passò da questa a miglior vita Dna Viena Bachi la quale morì di morte improvvisa e fù sepolta in capella della B.V.M. delle Purine.» Read at about 5x; the last digit of the year is not firm (the entries around it run 1768–1769; the index says 6 October 1767). **A Bachi household at NIN in 1768–1787** — the index has two more Bachi burials in the same book, Elisabetta (12 May 1777) and Antonio (23 November 1787, with a Filippo Carleva) — Nin lies on the mainland across from Pag. Whether it is the Pag family of Angelo Bachi is not shown.|viena-bachi-of-nin|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
karlobag-baptism-1715-10-luca-son-of-mikule-bach|karlobag-baptism-1715-10-luca-son-of-mikule-bach-line.jpg||Karlobag, October 1715 — a son LUCA baptised to MIKULE BACH[…]; the index reads «Bachi??»|Karlobag births 1691–1804 (FamilySearch, DGS film 005481648; index record 1:1:QKMX-YL4S)|left-hand page, first entry, headed «Na 2? oktobra 1715» (a Croatian-language entry by the priest Anton Hreljanović)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L939-3|«Na [2]1 oktobra 1715. Ja pop Anton Hreljanović krstih sina Mikule [Babi — struck out] Bach[…], imenom Luca, komu bi kum Volfa Ivich, a kuma njegova mat Marija.» Read at about 5x; the surname is cut by the edge of the left page after «Bach» and the scribe struck out a first spelling, so **«Bachi» is the index's reading, not a firm one — it may be Bačić or another name**. The name Luca is a man's (Luka) here, though the index files it as a woman. If it is Bachi it is a Bachi at Karlobag 38 years before the marriage of 1753, and the Caetanus of 1753 need not have come from Pag.|luca-bach-of-karlobag|13 October 2026|notes/karlobag-marriage-1774-smojver-bacchi.md
senj-marriage-1736-12-matia-urolla-of-zastva|senj-marriage-1736-12-matia-urolla-of-zastva-line.jpg||Senj, 2 December 1736 — Matia Urolla of Zastva|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 13, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L458|«Na 2 xbra Ja plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Matia Urolla od Zastva shherom Jure R[...]ra od Klane imenom Jelena, polak nihovih Atestaciy [dopuschenjem] Gna Arkizakna d. Cholich.» Read at about 5x; the surname is written Urolla (or Vrolla); the place Zastva is not identified|matia-urolla-of-zastva|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1739-10-marko-tomicic-of-krmpote|senj-marriage-1739-10-marko-tomicic-of-krmpote-line.jpg||Senj, 13 October 1739 — Marko Tomičić of Krmpote|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 23, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4CZ|«Na 13 8bra Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Marka Tomicicha iz Kermpot shherom Sime Kerpula alit[i] …cicha imenom Lucia, kim bi ja svidoka Matesa Simich … Ja Calovich Mladi.» Read at about 6x; the groom's origin is Krmpote, a place this archive researches (row 33); the bride's father's surname is only partly legible|marko-tomicic-of-krmpote|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1745-10-mihu-soyata-lucia-bevandich|senj-marriage-1745-10-mihu-soyata-lucia-bevandich-line.jpg||Senj, 10 October 1745 — Mihu Šojat of Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 37, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4CX|«Na 10 8bra Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Mihu Soyata shherom Pokoinoga Luke Bevandicha imenom Lucia, kim bi ja svidoka Gergo Filipovich i Boze Soyat.» Read at about 6x; the year 1745 follows from the headings: image 34R carries «1745» before the January entries and image 38L opens with a 1 December entry then the heading «1746»|mihu-sojat-of-senj|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1747-10-juretic-bakar-katarina-papic|senj-marriage-1747-10-juretic-bakar-katarina-papic-line.jpg||Senj, 11 October [1747] — Katarina Papić daughter of Matia|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 43, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LWYT|«Na 11 8bra Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Antona Juretichia od Bakra shherom Matia Papicha od Prixan [?] imenom Katarinu, kim bi ja svidoka Jve Skukan i Matias Francetich.» Read at about 6x; the year is by the run (image 43R is the 1747 autumn: 1747 heading on 40R, 29 Oct entries follow)|katarina-papic-daughter-of-matia|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1765-pernich-of-krmpote-widow-of-vid-sojat|senj-marriage-1765-pernich-of-krmpote-widow-of-vid-sojat-line.jpg||Senj, 1765 (February–April; the day is «Na isti dan», the same as the entry above) — Pernich of Krmpote groom of 1765|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 74, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4MT|«Na isti dan Sn kanonik Luka de Vranjanin zdruzi u S. Matrimonij [name] Pernich iz Kermpot … za udovu P. Vide Sojata i … kim svidoki bihu Franciško Vikentić, i Matte Perqich.» Read at about 6x; the groom's forename and the bride's are not legible in the strip; the year is that of the January–April 1765 run on image 74L (the heading 1765 is on 73R). A Pernich [Prpić?] household of Krmpote marrying a Šojat widow — both surnames this archive researches|pernich-of-krmpote-groom-of-1765|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1768-03-anna-widow-of-mate-blazevic|senj-marriage-1768-03-anna-widow-of-mate-blazevic-line.jpg||Senj, March 1768 — Anna widow of Mate Blažević|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 82, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4Q2|«… Marca. Zn Pop Jandre Carich zdruzi u sveti Matrimony Udovicu pokoynoga Mate Blaxevicha imenom Annu s. Gergom Solakihen [?]; svidoci bihu Bartel Carich i Mate Skerich.» Read at about 6x; the page is the cramped 1768 hand, the day is lost at the left edge, the groom's surname is doubtful. A Blažević widow of Senj in 1768; her husband Mate is dead|anna-widow-of-mate-blazevic|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1769-01-mate-blazevic-marries-a-widow|senj-marriage-1769-01-mate-blazevic-marries-a-widow-line.jpg||Senj, 23 January 1769 — Mate Blažević of Senj groom of 1769|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 84, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LWRX|«Na 23. Sn Pop Jos Demelli zakupi u S. Matrimon udovicu […] s Matiom Blaxevich […] svidoki bihu […]» Read at about 6x from a cropped line; the bride's name and the place are not legible at this size and need a closer read. Image 84L is the January 1769 run (the heading «Jenvar 1769» above the entries of 8, 15, 19, 22, 22, 23, 23, 29 January)|mate-blazevic-of-senj-groom-of-1769|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1779-02-lorne-blazevic-franica-fobber|senj-marriage-1779-02-lorne-blazevic-franica-fobber-line.jpg||Senj, February 1779 (after 2 February; the day is on the page's left edge) — Lorne Blažević groom of 1779|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 104, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LW2C|«Sakupi u Sti Matrimoni Gdn Pop Giure Nicevich Lorne Blaxevich s Franicom Fobber, Svidoci Ivan Cerfich i Frane Rosich.» Read from a thin crop at about 6x; the groom's forename and the bride's surname are doubtful. A Blažević [Blaxevich] marrying at Senj in 1779|lorne-blazevic-groom-of-1779|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1783-06-juraj-oreskovic-adjutant-catharina-milanes|senj-marriage-1783-06-juraj-oreskovic-adjutant-catharina-milanes-line.jpg||Senj, 24 June 1783 — Juraj Orešković adjutant of the Otočac regiment|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 118, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LW63|«Na 24. Sakupih ja Juraj Milanes Can. i Plovan u Sveti Matrimonij Gna Jurja d' Oreskovich Ajuta Slavnoga Regimenta Otocskoga s Dojlon Catharinom Milanes [?] … pokojnoga Gna Obrist[…] Tranica [?], koj bihu naprojdani iedan za ova tri puta po dopushcenju Precert Gna Capitular Vikara …» Read from a thin crop at about 6x (the hand is a clear Croatian-language italic); the bride's surname and her father are only partly legible and the year 1783 is fixed by the headings: «1783 Jenvar» opens on image 115R and «Letto 1784 Januar» opens on image 121R after the December entries. An Orešković officer of the Otočac regiment — the surname of ahnentafel 21 — marrying at Senj|juraj-oreskovic-adjutant-of-the-otocac-regiment|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1786-02-dube-sojat-widow-antonia-bunich|senj-marriage-1786-02-dube-sojat-widow-antonia-bunich-line.jpg||Senj, February 1786 — Dube Šojat of Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 130, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LWXK|«Sakupi u S. Matrimonij Gn Pop Sime Ikovich Dube Sojata s Udovom Antoniom Bunich koji bihu naprojdani tri puta; svidoci bihu Osip Ikovich, Jerolim Dora [?]. Tvrdim ja Plovan Juraj Milanes.» Read at about 6x; the groom's forename is partly legible («Dube»), the second witness doubtful. A Šojat marrying a widow at Senj in 1786 — the Šojat surname of the Karlobag/Senj families this archive holds. The year is fixed by «1786 Janvar» at the head of image 130L|dube-sojat-of-senj|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1788-10-marko-salanic-antonia-prpic|senj-marriage-1788-10-marko-salanic-antonia-prpic-line.jpg||Senj, 9 October 1788 — Antonia Prpić daughter of Matte|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 136, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LWZ2|«9. Sakupich u S. Matrimonij ja Plovan Vikar General i Prepošt Juraj Milanes sina Lute Šalanicha Marka s hčierom Matte Perpich Antonion, koji bihu naprodani tri puta; svidoci bihu Gn Leutenant Osip Baldsar i Gn Anton Suppe.» Read at about 6x from a clear Croatian-language entry; the year 1788 is that of the run (the heading «1788 Januar» is on image 134R and «1789» is on 136R after the October entries). A Prpić [Perpich] bride at Senj, daughter of a Matte Prpić|antonia-prpic-daughter-of-matte|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1812-08-petrus-bozijan-widow-vincentia-blazevich|senj-marriage-1812-08-petrus-bozijan-widow-vincentia-blazevich-line.jpg||Senj, 18 August 1812 — Vincentia Blažević widow bride of 1812|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 194, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L7RQ|«18 Franciscus Succich Canon. Lector. conjunxit in Matrimonium dispensatos in denuntiationibus Viduum Petrum Bozijan et Viduam Vincentiam Blazevich, testibus Joane Berich et Fabiano Blazevich.» Read at about 8x from a crop; the year 1812 follows from the headings («Anno 1812» on image 193R, «Anno 1813» on 194R after the September entries). A Blažević widow marrying at Senj, and the Fabijan Blažević who is a witness at Senj marriages in 1802, 1803, 1804, 1805 and 1812|vincentia-blazevic-widow-bride-of-1812|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-witness-fabianus-blazevich-1802-1812|senj-witness-fabianus-blazevich-1802-1812-line.jpg||Senj, 1802–1812 — Fabianus Blažević witness at Senj 1802-1812|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 193, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LW7Q|«testibus … Fabiano Blazevich» — read in the margins of 166R (May 1802, with Antonius Boxich), 171R (July 1803), 173R (Nov 1804, «Blasevich»), 175R (June 1805, with Joseph Venzel at the marriage of Blasius Kurkovich and Felicitas Cilota) and 193R (14 June 1812, with Antonius Matticki, at the marriage of Franciscus Gjurgjevich and Elias Milenich) and 194L (18 Aug 1812). Each line was read at about 6x from the full-page view; none was cropped separately, so the snapshot shown is the 1812 marriage of the widow Vincentia Blažević, 194L, where he is the second witness.|fabianus-blazevic-witness-at-senj-1802-1812|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1850-06-gergo-blazevic-of-krmpote-terezia-cacic|senj-marriage-1850-06-gergo-blazevic-of-krmpote-terezia-cacic-line.jpg||Senj, 9 June 1850 — Georgius Blažević son of Ivan of Krmpote groom of 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 221, right-hand page, the Croatian entry below the 1844 tabular line|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L75Z|«Ja Anton Zdesky sv. Bogoslovja Doc. Professor združio sam u Stolnoj Crkvi u Senju na 9. Lipnja léta 1850 s dopuštjenjem preuzv. g. Kanonika i Plovana Senjskoga Franje Černogorčevića u sveti Matrimonij mladića Gergu Blažević sina Ivana, Anne Blažević iz planine Kermpotske godinah 21 s djevojkom planine Senjske Terezom Čačić kćerom Ivana i Magdalene Čačić rođenom u Prizni godinah 21 pred svjedoci: Valentin Vlačić, Jakov Merslich.» Read at about 6x from a Croatian entry on the right-hand page of image 221 (page 10 of the second sequence, in the loose Croatian-language run of 1849–50 that follows the 1844 and 1836 tabular entries). The year 1850 is in the text; an entry for the 4th of the month in 1850 follows it. A Georgius Blažević of Krmpote marrying at the Senj cathedral — the surname and the home village of this archive's Blažević side|georgius-blazevic-son-of-ivan-of-krmpote-groom-of-1850,tereza-cacic-of-senj-bride-of-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1832-xbris-fabianus-blazevich-widower-tailor-margaritha|senj-marriage-1832-xbris-fabianus-blazevich-widower-tailor-margaritha-line.jpg||Senj, 17 [?]bris 1832 — Fabianus Blažević widower tailor of Senj groom of 1832|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 222, right-hand page, third entry, right-hand page (page 11 of the tabular sequence)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L71Q|«17 [Xbris?] 1832. Fabianus Blaxevich Viduus et Viduam Margaritham M[…]ich, oriundi Parochiae Segniensis, aliquo [in] loco et domicilio …» — tabular entry no. 3 of the right-hand page 11 of the second sequence (age column «68» and «28», trade «Sartor»; witnesses Antonius Berovich sartor, Vito Pollas, Josephus Janusich). Read at about 6x; the month abbreviation is `[…]bris` (September–December) and the groom's age is read 68 and could be 58 or 63. **A Fabianus Blažević, a widower and a tailor, of the Senj parish — very probably the Fabianus Blažević who witnessed marriages at Senj in 1802–1812**|fabianus-blazevic-widower-tailor-of-senj-groom-of-1832|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1842-01-antonius-babich-maria-calanich|senj-marriage-1842-01-antonius-babich-maria-calanich-line.jpg||Senj, 23 January 1842 — Antonius Babić of Senj groom of 1842|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 226, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L716|«1842 Die 23 Januarii in Ecclesia Cathedrali Segniae copulati fuere. Antonius Babich caelebs, parochianus hujas, filius legitimus vita functi Patris Georgii Babich et Mariae Matre viventis natae Babich. Iniuit Matrimonium cum Puella Maria Calanich parochiana hujas et filia vero Jacobi et Magdalenae […]»; ages 28 / 20; witness Franc. Bonafaccia and Petrus Korrenich as chaplain. Read at about 3x; the groom's age is read 28; the bride's age 20; the bride's surname is read «Calanich» (Kalanj) from the first line and from the first line of the next entry's block|antonius-babic-of-senj-groom-of-1842,maria-kalanj-bride-of-babic-1842|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1842-02-laurentius-babich-anna-kuppar|senj-marriage-1842-02-laurentius-babich-anna-kuppar-line.jpg||Senj, 6 February 1842 — Laurentius Babić of Senj groom of 1842|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 226, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L716|«1842 Die 6 Februarii in Eccl. Cathed. Segniae copulati fuerunt. Laurentius Babich caelebs filius legitimus Francisci et Dorotheae natae Babich Parochianorum hujatum, cum puella Anna Kuppar filia legitima Matthiae et Vincentiae natae […]»; ages 25 / 21; witnesses Ant. Parenchiesich? and Gregorius Sefento? Read at about 3x; the bride's surname is read «Kuppar»|laurentius-babic-of-senj-groom-of-1842|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1847-franciscus-babich-maria-bajsich|senj-marriage-1847-franciscus-babich-maria-bajsich-line.jpg||Senj, 6 [?] 1847 — Franciscus Babić of Senj groom of 1847|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 228, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L7BM|«1847 die 6 [month not read] in Ecclesia Cathedrali copulati fuere. Franciscus Babich filius Francisci Babich et Dogmae [Dorotheae?] natae Babich, caelebs, Parochianus hujas, et Maria Bajsich [?] filia Martini Bajsich et Mariae natae […] Parochiana hujas, viduati?…»; ages 21 / 19; entry no. 41; witnesses Nicolo Bronzin, tailor? Read at about 3x; the month and the bride's surname are not firm. Brother or cousin of the Laurentius Babich of 1842 (whose parents are the same Franciscus and Dorothea née Babich)|franciscus-babic-of-senj-groom-of-1847,maria-bajsich-bride-of-babic-1847|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1848-03-stephanus-babich-catharina-ostoman|senj-marriage-1848-03-stephanus-babich-catharina-ostoman-line.jpg||Senj, 6 March 1848 — Stephanus Babić of Senj groom of 1848|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 229, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L72G|«1848 Die 6 Martii in Eccl. Cathed. Segniae copulati fuere. Stephanus Babich filius Georgii et Ursulae Babich, Parochianus hujas, et Catharina Ostoman[?] filia Matthiae et Mariae Ostoman Parochiana hujas»; ages 30 / 31; entry no. 43; witnesses Josephus Antich? and Antonius Belobarbich. Read at about 3x|stephanus-babic-of-senj-groom-of-1848,catharina-ostoman-bride-of-babic-1848|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1831-10-christophorus-gerzanich-antonia-babich-novigrad|senj-marriage-1831-10-christophorus-gerzanich-antonia-babich-novigrad-line.jpg||Senj, 23 October 1831 — Christophorus Gerzanich groom of 1831 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 255, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L7JK|«1831, 23 Octobris. Christophorus Gerzanich filius Joannis — Antonia Babich [second word not read] Novogradensis»; ages 22 / 21; condition column «Mercurius»? Read at about 4x. A Babić bride from Novigrad, marrying at Senj in the first sequence of the Cathedral register of 1831–1858 (sequence G). Whether this is the Novigrad (Lika-Senj) or another is not stated|christophorus-gerzanich-groom-of-1831-at-senj,antonia-babic-of-novigrad-bride-of-1831|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1849-12-vincentius-uroda-of-karlobag-maria-gerbacz|senj-marriage-1849-12-vincentius-uroda-of-karlobag-maria-gerbacz-line.jpg||Senj, 27 December 1849 — Vincentius Uroda of Karlobag groom of 1849 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 259, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L7X9|«[1849] Die 27 Decembris, Cathedrali Segniae … copulati sunt. Vincentius Filius Conjugum Joannis et Maria Uroda Carlobagensis annorum 24 et Maria Filia Rochi [?] et Anna Gerbacz Starigradensis annorum 22»; entry no. 31; witnesses Thomas Uzarkevich? [read «Thomas Garkevich»] and Joannes Kajzer?, the celebrant Carolus Zvanich?; marginal note on dispensation. Read at about 8x. The surname Uroda stands once, at the end of the parents' names, and is read as the groom's own; the day is read 27 and the month December; the year is 1849 because the next entry is of 13 October 1850. A man born about 1825 of a Karlobag household named Uroda — a third household at Karlobag is not yet separate from the others|vincentius-uroda-of-karlobag-groom-of-1849-at-senj,maria-gerbacz-bride-of-vincentius-uroda-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1857-02-antonius-gerbac-widower-catharina-widow-of-stephanus-babich|senj-marriage-1857-02-antonius-gerbac-widower-catharina-widow-of-stephanus-babich-line.jpg||Senj, 10 February 1857 — Antonius Gerbac widower of Starigrad groom of 1857|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 260, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L7LP|«Anno Domini 1857, die 10 Februarii … Vidua[s] Antonius Gerbac [fidelis] Starigradensis, nauta penes c.r. Segniensem Portus Inspectoratum … et Vidua Catharina denati Cajuli [?] Stephani Babich parochiana Segniensis»; ages 60 and 40; entry no. 34 [the number read]. Read at about 8x in two overlapping zooms. A Babić only as the dead first husband of the bride; the Gerbac of Starigrad is not the Karlobag Gerkacs|antonius-gerbac-widower-of-starigrad-groom-of-1857,catharina-widow-of-stephanus-babic-bride-of-1857|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1858-05-lucas-glavicsich-maria-tomlenovich-of-karlobag|senj-marriage-1858-05-lucas-glavicsich-maria-tomlenovich-of-karlobag-line.jpg||Senj, 30 May 1858 — Lucas Glavicsich of Senj groom of 1858|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 260, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L7LP|«Anno Domini 1858, die 30 Maji … Caelebs Lucas Glaviesich filius legitimus Joannis Glaviesich et ejus defuncti? uxoris Annae natae Babic, fidelis Segniensis, et puella Maria filia legitima Michaelis Tomlenovich et ejus uxoris Matthae natae Mandekich parochiana Carlobagensis, a Venerabili Officio parochiali dtd Carlobagi 19 …»; ages 25 and 22; entry no. 39. Read at about 6x. A Tomljanović bride of Karlobag; the groom's mother is née Babić|lucas-glavicsich-of-senj-groom-of-1858,maria-tomljenovic-of-karlobag-bride-of-1858|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1858-08-franciscus-vincentius-gerzic-martha-loncarich-widow|senj-marriage-1858-08-franciscus-vincentius-gerzic-martha-loncarich-widow-line.jpg||Senj, August 1858 — Franciscus Vincentius Gerzic of Senj groom of 1858|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 261, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L73N|«Caelebs Franciscus Vincentius Gerzic filius legitimus Joannis Gerzic et ejus uxoris Philippae natae Basić et Martha relicta Vidua denati Murarii Andreae Linić, nata vero Loncsarich, fideles Segnienses; ab Inclyto magistratu Segniensi dtd 31 Julii 1858 N. 1107 Matrimonium ineundi facultate muniti, servatis…»; ages 30 and 38; entry no. 40. Read at about 8x; the day of the month is not read|franciscus-vincentius-gerzic-of-senj-groom-of-1858,martha-loncaric-widow-of-linic-bride-of-1858|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1845-georgius-haas-francisca-loncarich|senj-marriage-1845-georgius-haas-francisca-loncarich-line.jpg||Senj, 1845 — Georgius Haas groom of 1845 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 264, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L7GZ|«1845 die 16 [?] … Georgius Hoff [?] filius … Segniensis, et puella Francisca Lonzarich filia … parochiana hujus; provisi licentia a parte loci politica, ac per inter Missarum solemnia denuntiati, quae in fasciculo parochiali sub L. N. 7 asservantur»; entry no. 7; witness Antonio Jarichich? and Petrus Stein [?]. Read at about 5x; the month, the groom's surname and the parents are not read|georgius-haas-groom-of-1845-at-senj,francisca-loncaric-bride-of-1845|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1853-02-josephus-herro-bride-babich-witness-zubranic|senj-marriage-1853-02-josephus-herro-bride-babich-witness-zubranic-line.jpg||Senj, 6 February 1853 — Georgius Zubranić witness at Senj marriage of 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 265, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L789|«1853 Die 6 Februarii in Ecclesia B.M.V. ad Aram copulati fuere. Josephus Herro [?] filius legitimus Joannis parochiani Segniensis et Vincentiae Dommer [?] filia legitima jugalium Caroli et Vincentiae natae Babić parochiana hujus, ambo caelibes»; ages 24 and 34; entry no. 15; witnesses Josephus Markovie, Georgius Zubranić (Segniae); celebrant Joannes Slaus?, Religionis Cooperator. Read at about 6x; the bride's own forename is not read. A bride whose mother is née Babić, and a witness named Zubranić — «Žubrinić» in the other spelling this register uses|georgius-zubranic-witness-at-senj-marriage-of-1853|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1832-11-martinus-lenack-anna-loncarich|senj-marriage-1832-11-martinus-lenack-anna-loncarich-line.jpg||Senj, 25 November 1832 — Martinus Lenack groom of 1832 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 269, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L7R3|«[25 Novembris] 1832 [in] Ecclesia filiali B.M. Virginis Annunciatae copulati [sunt]. Martinus Lenack filius legitimus denati patris Joannis Lenack et matris Helenae — Conjunctus fuit in matrimonium cum puella Anna filia legitima Georgii et Ursulae Lonczarich commorantium in Selce [? read «Seldze»] — tribus vicibus inter Missarum Solemnia denunciati»; ages 33 and 22; entry no. 3; witnesses Matheus Lenacz and Michael Lenacz, mariners [?]. Read at about 8x; the bride's own surname is her father's, Lončarić; her place is read «Selce» but not firm|martinus-lenack-groom-of-1832-at-senj,anna-loncaric-bride-of-lenack-1832|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1846-02-mathias-jurcic-laurentia-antic-of-lukovo|senj-marriage-1846-02-mathias-jurcic-laurentia-antic-of-lukovo-line.jpg||Senj, 16 February 1846 — Mathias Jurcić of Senj groom of 1846|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 272, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L7HT|«1846 die 16 Februarii in Ecclesia cathedrali Segniae copulati fuerunt. Mathias Jurcich … caelebs parochianus hujas cum puella Laurentia filia Mathei et Katharina Antich, parochiana Lukovensi, Regimenti Otocano? Centuria S. Georgensi. Dicti sponsi ea parte politica potestate licentia provisi …»; ages 30 and 26; entry no. 15; witnesses Josephus Gerbac and Blaz Dragicevich. Read at about 6x; an Antić bride of Lukovo (Senj-Otočac frontier regiment, the company of St George)|mathias-jurcic-of-senj-groom-of-1846,laurentia-antic-of-lukovo-bride-of-1846|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1850-11-croatian-entry-bride-ante-daughter-of-jure-babic|senj-marriage-1850-11-croatian-entry-bride-ante-daughter-of-jure-babic-line.jpg||Senj, 28 November 1850 — Ante Babić bride of 1850 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 273, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L76R|«Godine 1850. Dana 28 Studena [Novembra] u Malnoj Crkvi druzih u S. Renetbu [?] ja Filip [Hrisković] Kapelan Mladića [?] [Cristić?] godišt 32 Sina Frane [Tanković] za Divojku Antu godišt 24 ter pokojnoga Jure Babić, i ove tri puta objavljene po dopuštenju prevuišenoga prevtlogi? Biskupa Emerica Ozegovich? Barlabersonj? na prijdi. Nikola Bronzini, Jure Radetić [witnesses]». A one-line Croatian entry, written in a different hand, between two Latin ones. Read at about 6x; groom's and priest's names uncertain, the bride's father Jure Babić clear|ante-babic-bride-of-1850-at-senj|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1822-01-michael-krmpotich-widower-witness-franciscus-zubrinich|senj-marriage-1822-01-michael-krmpotich-widower-witness-franciscus-zubrinich-line.jpg||Senj, 23 January 1822 — Michael Krmpotić widower of Senj groom of 1822|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 276, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L7XY|«23 Januarii [1822]. Georgius Cajalich Coop. conjunxit in Matrimonium praemissis praevie 3 [tribus] Denuntiationibus ac dispensato in 3° et 4° plus consanguinitatis gradu impedimento Viduum Michaelem Krmpotich Segniensem Carolinarum? et Viduam Stanislavam Cragich Kvizijutensem, praesentibus testibus Francisco Zubrinich et Matthia Lonczarich» — one of the abbreviated one-paragraph entries of the 1820s; the clause «dispensato in 3° et 4° consanguinitatis gradu impedimento» says the couple were blood relations in the third and fourth degree. Read at about 5x; the bride's name and the place after «Carolinarum?» are not firm; the year is 1822 from the heading «1821 / 1822» above it|michael-krmpotic-widower-of-senj-groom-of-1822,stanislava-widow-bride-of-krmpotic-1822|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1830-05-michael-krmpotich-widower-54-antonia-tomlanovich-widow|senj-marriage-1830-05-michael-krmpotich-widower-54-antonia-tomlanovich-widow-line.jpg||Senj, 18 May 1830 — Michael Krmpotić widower of Senj groom of 1830|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 277, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L7HK|«18 Maji [1830]. Joannes Mikovich Coop. Saecularis et Sanctae conjunxit in Matrimonium Viduum Michaelem Krmpotich Parochianum Segniensem oriundum ex loco ad S. Salvatorem Domus N° 30, aetatis annorum 54, et Viduam Antoniam Tomlanovich [?] Kvizijutensem aetatis annorum 30, et quidem tribus praevie praemissis Denunciationibus ac habita pro parte ejusdem requisita licentia; praesent. testibus Georgio Nobich et Matthaeo Lonczarich». The only entry on the page, under the heading «1830». Read at about 6x; the bride's surname is read «Tomlanovich» but the second half is not firm. The same two names, a widower Michael Krmpotić with a Lončarić as witness, stand in the entry of 23 January 1822 on image 276R (his age is not given there) — whether it is the same man married a second time cannot be told from the two lines|michael-krmpotic-widower-of-senj-groom-of-1830,antonia-widow-bride-of-krmpotic-1830|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1832-franciscus-aloysius-kovacich-widower-witness-krmpotich|senj-marriage-1832-franciscus-aloysius-kovacich-widower-witness-krmpotich-line.jpg||Senj, 25 [?] 1832 — Franciscus Aloysius Kovačić widower groom of 1832 with Krmpotić witness|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 277, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L7HK|«1832 25 [8bris?]. Viduum Franciscum Aloysium Kovacich ad Caesar.-Regium Officium Ligaminis Agens … dtd Zagrabiae 13 Aprilis 1832 N° 4999 et Nepomucenam Lochmer Virginem, filiam Joannis et Vincentiae Lochmer, domicilii ambo Segniae — dispensati in denuntiationibus»; ages 38 and 28; entry no. 4; witness column: «Joannes Nepo Draganich de Drachenfeld Capitaneus Judex Civitatis & Krmpotich perceptionum tenens». A Krmpotić in the witness column. Read at about 6x|franciscus-aloysius-kovacic-widower-groom-of-1832-with-krmpotic-witness|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1849-05-croatian-entry-mihovil-kriskovic-maria-basic-witness-joso-antic|senj-marriage-1849-05-croatian-entry-mihovil-kriskovic-maria-basic-witness-joso-antic-line.jpg||Senj, 28 May 1849 — Joso Antić witness at Senj marriage of 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 281, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L7J3|«1849. Dana 28 Svibnja. Združih ja Philipp Kriskovich Kapelan u sv. Zenitbu Mihovila Kriskovića godišta 43 za divojku Mariu Basić godišta 40, na prid svjedokah Jure Bellobarbić [?], Joso Antić». A one-paragraph Croatian-language entry, no. 21, on the foot of the page. Read at about 6x; the groom's name is not firm; the witness Joso Antić is clear|joso-antic-witness-at-senj-marriage-of-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1850-10-philip-kruk-helena-loncarich-croatian-entry|senj-marriage-1850-10-philip-kruk-helena-loncarich-croatian-entry-line.jpg||Senj, 27 October 1850 — Philip Kruk groom of 1850 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 282, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L7LM|«1850. Dana 27 Listopada združih ja Toma Sladović kapelan u svetoj Zenidbu u stolnoj crkvi Philipa Kruk, star godin 22, sina Valentina i Lucie Kruk, s divojkom Hellenom godin 20, kćerom Mathe i Marthe Lončarich rodjene Turina, oba katolici i Senske [= of Senj], na prid svjedokah Franjo Aberlein? i Daniel Cribac?». Read at about 8x; the day is 27 and the month Listopad (October or November — Croatian Listopad = October); the witnesses' names are not firm|philip-kruk-groom-of-1850-at-senj,helena-loncaric-bride-of-kruk-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1858-05-martinus-kirn-witness-antonius-babich|senj-marriage-1858-05-martinus-kirn-witness-antonius-babich-line.jpg||Senj, 30 May 1858 — Antonius Babić witness at Senj marriage of 1858|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 283, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L7HM|«Anno Domini 1858 die 30 Maji in Cathedrali Ecclesia Segniensi copulati fuerunt. Caelebs Martinus Kirn filius legitimus Jacobi Kirn et ejus uxoris Mariae natae Stele…»; age 31; entry no. 41; witness column «Martinus Mutta [?] ferrarius et Antonius Babić vigilus parochiani Segnienses». Read at about 6x; the bride's name is not read; the page is the last of the 1855–58 sequence|antonius-babic-witness-at-senj-marriage-of-1858|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-286L|senj-seen-286L-line.jpg||Senj, 1833–36 — Lončarić and Antić entries|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 286, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L78N|Page-scale read of the whole page (sequence 1833–36). Entry 1, 18 November 1833: groom Martinus Lončarić [«Loncarich»] of Senj, bride of Vinodol, parents named Lončarić; entry 2, 26 October 1834: groom Josephus Lončarić, son of Matthias and Martha Lončarić, aged 22; entry 4, 24 January 1836: bride Matha, daughter of Joannes and Ursula Antić [«Antich»], aged 20, groom a mariner Georgius [?] aged 26. Names read at page scale only.||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-286R|senj-seen-286R-line.jpg||Senj, 1836–38 — Lončarić and Babić entries|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 286, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L78N|Page-scale read of the whole page (sequence 1836–38). Entry 6 (21 November 1836): the witness column names Antonius Babić [«Babich»], Bajzak?, living in the suburb; entry 8 (5 August 1838): groom Alexander Lončarić [«Lonczarich»], aged 35, son of the late Alexander and Helena Lončarić, marrying the widow Antonia Milutich [?], aged 37. Names read at page scale only.||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-287L|senj-seen-287L-line.jpg||Senj, 1838–41 — Lončarić entry|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 287, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L7LY|Page-scale read of the whole page (sequence 1838–41). Entry 9 (25 November 1838): groom Valentinus Lončarić [«Loncarich»], aged 21, bride Ursula Lenac [«Lenacz»], aged 20. Entries of 1840 (Stephanus Lukić? × Lucia, aged 24 in the Otočac regiment) and 1841 (Jacobus Lenac) bear on no family listed. Names read at page scale only.||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-288L|senj-seen-288L-line.jpg||Senj, 1843 — Lončarić and Babić entries|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 288, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L74D|Page-scale read of the whole page (sequence 1843). Entry 14 (12 November 1843): groom Stephanus Lončarić [«Loncsarich»], aged 23, son of Aloysius and Antonia Lončarić, bride Catharina Bašić [«Basich»], aged 20, daughter of Joannes and Maria Bašić; entry 15 (26 November 1843): groom Andreas Linić [«Linich»], aged 30, bride Martha Lončarić, aged 25, daughter of Matthias Lončarić and Martha née Turin; the witness column of entry 15 names Antonius Babić [«Babich»]. Names read at page scale only.||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-288R|senj-seen-288R-line.jpg||Senj, 1844–45 — Lončarić entry|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 288, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L74D|Page-scale read of the whole page (sequence 1844–45). Entry 17 (22 December 1844): groom Franciscus Lobel [?], aged 43, bride Maria Lončarić, aged 25, daughter of Aloysius and Margaretha Lončarić. Entries 16 and 18 (Josephus Lochmer × Maria Butković, 1845) bear on no family listed except Butković. Names read at page scale only.||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1849-05-valerian-lukatella-of-karlobag-ana-dragicevic|senj-marriage-1849-05-valerian-lukatella-of-karlobag-ana-dragicevic-line.jpg||Senj, 14 May 1849 — Valerian Lukatella of Karlobag groom of 1849 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 289, left-hand page, third entry on the page (entry 20-something, between the 16 April and 1850 entries)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L7FC|«1849 dne 14 Svib[nja] u kapeli B.D.M. od Arta združeni u Svetu Ženitbu: Valerian Lukatella, rodom iz Karlobaga, sin Mate, trgovca, i Marte rođene Smojver, katolik, mladić; i Ana Dragičević, kćer Nikole, Granitčara [?], i Ane Miškulin, rodom iz Jablanca, katolika, divojka»; ages 30 and 25; witnesses Anton [Žigmand?], Franz Vinsky [?] and Ivan Grubišić; the entry is in Croatian, one of the first Croatian-language entries of the volume (from April 1849). Read at about 6x in two zooms. Lukatelli is a listed surname; Smojver is a listed surname (the groom's mother). Karlobag is the home of the Smojver and Lukatelli households of this archive|valerian-lukatella-of-karlobag-groom-of-1849-at-senj,ana-dragicevic-bride-of-valerian-lukatella-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1853-08-jacobus-lenac-maria-butkovic-witnesses-babich-perpic|senj-marriage-1853-08-jacobus-lenac-maria-butkovic-witnesses-babich-perpic-line.jpg||Senj, 21 August 1853 — Jacobus Lenac groom of 1853 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 290, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ5D|«1853 die 21 augusti in Ecclesia Parochiali copulati fuerunt. Jacobus filius legitimus Christophori et Catharinae jugalium Lenac caelebs Segniensis, et Maria filia legitima Josephi et [Mariae] Margarethae Butkovic Parochiae Ledinicensis [?]»; ages 24 and 22; entry no. 29; witness column: «+ Franciscus Babić, + Joannes Perpić»; celebrant Gregorius Potočnjak, cooperator Segniensis. Read at about 6x in four zooms. Butković (the bride) is a listed surname, Babić and Perpić (Prpić) as witnesses|jacobus-lenac-groom-of-1853-at-senj,maria-butkovic-bride-of-lenac-1853|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1820-07-joannes-malik-soldier-customs-bride-francisca-spalj|senj-marriage-1820-07-joannes-malik-soldier-customs-bride-francisca-spalj-line.jpg||Senj, 2 July 1820 — Joannes Malik soldier groom of 1820 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 292, right-hand page, second entry on the page, under the heading «1820» (page number 76)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L77D|«2° Julij [1820]. Petrus Kovacich Cooperator conjunxit in Matrimonium praemissis praevie 3 Denuntiationibus Joannem Malik Militem ad C.R. Officium Telonii, et Franciscam Spalj, praesentibus testibus Josepho Jurcich, et Matthaeo Festas». One of the short one-paragraph entries of the 1820s (the celebrant is Petrus Kovačić, cooperator). Read at about 6x. The groom's surname is read «Malik»; the bride's «Spalj» is clear. Špalj is a listed surname; Jurčić (the witness) is a listed surname|joannes-malik-soldier-groom-of-1820-at-senj,francisca-spalj-bride-of-malik-1820|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1850-04-toma-pasquan-catharina-zubranic-of-baska|senj-marriage-1850-04-toma-pasquan-catharina-zubranic-of-baska-line.jpg||Senj, 28 April 1850 — Toma Pasquan groom of 1850 at Senj with a Žubrinić bride of Baška|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 320, right-hand page, first entry on the page, written across the top of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L7X3|«1850 dana 28 Travnja združi ja Toma Sladović kapelan u sveti Matrimon Tomu Pasquan godišt 23 plovanie Senske, sina pokojnoga Pave i pokojne Anne, s Divojkom Catharinom Zubranić godišt 21 Plovanie Baschanske, kćer Mathe Zubranića i Hellene rodjene Kruher [?]; uz dopuščenja svjetovnoga i crkvenoga, poklam trahu tri puta polak navode naviščeni, na prići svidokov: + Mathe Kremenić Tojak [?], + Stjepan Lončarić». A Croatian-language entry, no. 24 [read «25»], on the first line of the page. Read at about 6x in a single zoom; the surname Zubranić is clear (the same Žubrinić name spelled Zubrenich, Zubranich in other books)|toma-pasquan-groom-of-1850-at-senj-with-a-zubrinic-bride-of-baska,catharina-zubrinic-of-baska-bride-of-pasquan-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1845-12-joannes-perpich-francisca-lenac|senj-marriage-1845-12-joannes-perpich-francisca-lenac-line.jpg||Senj, 16 December 1845 — Joannes Perpich groom of 1845 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 319, right-hand page, first entry on the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ5F|«1845 Die 16 9bris in Ecclesia Cathedrali Segniae copulati fuere. Joannes Perpich Baja[…] filius Franciscae? et Barbarae?… parochianus hujas, et puella Francisca Lenaz filia Georgii et Matthae… parochiana hujas, provisi licentia a parte locali politica…»; ages 22 and 20; witnesses Valentin Lončarić and the cooperator Thomas Sladovich; entry no. 19 [read «20»]. Read at about 6x; the groom's surname is read «Perpich» and a word «Ba[g?]ilis» stands in the condition column; his parents' names are not read|joannes-perpich-groom-of-1845-at-senj,francisca-lenac-bride-of-perpich-1845|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1821-10-thomas-orichovich-maria-sbarich|senj-marriage-1821-10-thomas-orichovich-maria-sbarich-line.jpg||Senj, [?] October 1821 — Thomas Orichovich groom of 1821 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 309, right-hand page, second entry on the page, under the heading «1821»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQYB|«14? Octobris [1821]. Petrus Kovacich Coop. conjunxit in Matrimonium praemissis praevie 3bus Denuntiationibus Thomam Orichovich [?], et Mariam Sbaich [?], praesentibus testibus Elia Mahorovich? et Francisco Dumanich». One of the short one-paragraph entries of the 1820s, under the heading «1821». Read at about 6x; the groom's surname is read as «Orichovich» (a possible Orešković) and the bride's is not firm; no ages or parents given|thomas-orichovich-groom-of-1821-at-senj,maria-sbaich-bride-of-orichovich-1821|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1853-02-franciscus-perpic-anna-brozincevic|senj-marriage-1853-02-franciscus-perpic-anna-brozincevic-line.jpg||Senj, 6 February 1853 — Franciscus Prpić groom of 1853 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 321, right-hand page, first entry on the page, written across the top above the columns (page number 105)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L7MR|«1853. Die 6ta Februarii in Ecclesia Cathedrali, Ego Thomas Petrović Professor Reg. Superioris Gymnasii Segniensis, indulta Reverendissimi Domini Abbatis, Canonici Cathed. et Parochi, Franciscum Perpić caelibem ann. 22, filium legitimum jugalium Francisci et Antoniae natae Basić; et Annam Mariam Theresiam [?] Brozinčević puellam ann. 22, filiam legitimam jugalium Natalis et Theresiae natae Šučić [?], parochianos hujus, Dominicis diebus [tribus] inter Missae Parochialis solemnia, nullo[que] legitimo impedimento detecto, habita potestate [civili] … matrimonio conjunxi; praesentibus testibus Casimir Georgievich, Anton Perzanst [?]». Read at about 8x in two overlapping zooms. Entry heads page 105 of the 1852–58 sequence, written as a whole paragraph across the page above the printed columns. Prpić is a listed surname|franciscus-prpic-groom-of-1853-at-senj,anna-maria-theresia-brozincevic-bride-of-prpic-1853|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1844-09-aloysius-rubelli-justina-lukatelli|senj-marriage-1844-09-aloysius-rubelli-justina-lukatelli-line.jpg||Senj, 29 September 1844 — Aloysius Rubelli groom of 1844 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 328, left-hand page, entry no. 9 of the 1844 page, second entry on the left-hand page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L79F|«1844 Die 29 Septembris in domo privata copulati fuere. Aloysius Rubelli caelebs Parochianus Segniensis filius legitimus Ludovici et Mariae Rubelli, cum puella Justina Lukatelli filia legitima Joannis Evae [?] Lukatelli Parochiana hujatis»; ages 32 and 22; entry no. 9; witnesses Joseph Bach[…] and Maximilian Rubelli [?] «Wolfgangus Bilanić [?]»; the entry is followed by the dispensation clause «Praedicti sponsi habita ab Illustrissimo et Reverendissimo Domino Emerico Ossegovich de Barlabassevez … in privata etiam domo copulari possint …». Read at about 7x in two zooms. A Lukatelli of Senj parish — a daughter Justina, born about 1822 — whose father's forename is read «Joannis Evae» (Joannes Ivo?). Lukatelli is a listed surname|aloysius-rubelli-groom-of-1844-at-senj,justina-lukatelli-bride-of-rubelli-1844|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1850-12-luka-pukavina-catharina-cacic-mother-tomljanovic|senj-marriage-1850-12-luka-pukavina-catharina-cacic-mother-tomljanovic-line.jpg||Senj, 29 December 1850 — Luka Pukavina groom of 1850 at Senj with a Čačić bride|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 329, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQVH|«1850: dana 29 Prosinca združih ja Toma Sladović kapelan u sveti Matrimon Luku Pukavina godin 25, sina Jure Pukavina i Mathie rođene Tomljanović, Plovanie Dolnjega Pazarišća, s Divojkom Catharinom Čačić godin 20, kćerom pokojnoga Nikole Čačić, Plovanie Prtna [?], pri svidocih: + Toma Krmanović [?] šoštar, + Franc Matulas Scheidar [Schneider]. Uslied dopuščenja crkvenoga i svjetovnoga, poklam trahu tri puta polak navode naviščeni». A Croatian-language entry. Read at about 6x in two zooms. The groom's mother is née Tomljanović; the bride's surname Čačić is the surname of the Terezia Čačić who married Gergo Blažević of Krmpote at Senj on 9 June 1850 (image 221R) — the two may be sisters, daughters of the late Nikola Čačić, but this entry does not say so|luka-pukavina-groom-of-1850-at-senj-with-a-cacic-bride,catharina-cacic-bride-of-pukavina-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1849-02-josip-rubicic-widower-witness-jure-vukelic|senj-marriage-1849-02-josip-rubicic-widower-witness-jure-vukelic-line.jpg||Senj, 19 February 1849 — Jure Vukelić sailor witness at Senj marriage of 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 329, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQVH|«1849. dana 19 Veljače [Februara] združih ja Toma Sladović kapelan Senski u sv. Ženidbu udovca Josu Rubičića udovicom Marom Dierich godišt 36 Plovanie Senske, na prici svidoki + Jure Vukellich mornar». The first entry of a page of Croatian-language entries, the clerk's note «Alleg. …» in the next column. Read at about 5x; the groom's age is not read|jure-vukelic-sailor-witness-at-senj-marriage-of-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1852-04-blasius-rossi-mother-anna-nee-vukelic|senj-marriage-1852-04-blasius-rossi-mother-anna-nee-vukelic-line.jpg||Senj, 29 April 1852 — Blasius Rossi groom of 1852 at Senj whose mother was née Vukelić|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 331, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L737|«1852 Die 29 Aprilis ego Mathias Cop. Theologiae Professor habita prae manibus facultate [Inclytae] Directionis Financialis Fluminensis et Magistratus Segniensis … Domini Abbatis, in Matrimonium conjunxi Domi Blasium Rossi Catholicum Segniensem, filium legitimum Conjugum Nicolai et Annae natae Vukellić, conditione Officientem penes c.r. financialem Directionem Fluminis, aetatis annorum 26; et Johannam Aloysiam, filiam legitimam defuncti Andreae et viae Catharinae Conjugum Zurat? Segniensem, aetatis annorum 27, utroque Romano-Catholicae; praesentibus notis testibus». Read at about 6x in two zooms. The groom's mother is née Vukelić [Vukellić] — a Vukelić of Senj, not placed in a household of this archive|blasius-rossi-groom-of-1852-at-senj-whose-mother-was-nee-vukelic|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1832-05-valentinus-savretic-widow-maria-oreskovic|senj-marriage-1832-05-valentinus-savretic-widow-maria-oreskovic-line.jpg||Senj, 9 May 1832 — Valentinus Savretić groom of 1832 with an Orešković widow bride|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 336, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQT8|«9° Maji 1832 Joannes Radović Professor conjunxit in Matrimonium Viduam defuncti Mathiae Thian [?] nomine Mariam, natam Orešković 3tio praevie promisso denuntiationibus A Valentinum Savretić, praesentibus testibus Stepano et Blazio Lončarić». One of the abbreviated one-paragraph entries of 1829–32, the last on the page. Read at about 6x; the first husband's surname «Thian» is not firm; no ages given|valentinus-savretic-groom-of-1832-with-an-oreskovic-widow-bride,maria-oreskovic-widow-bride-of-savretic-1832|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1828-11-simon-samarsia-bride-mathia-krmpotich|senj-marriage-1828-11-simon-samarsia-bride-mathia-krmpotich-line.jpg||Senj, 28 November 1828 — Simon Samarsia groom of 1828 with a Krmpotić bride|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 335, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LQ18|«28° Novemb: Joannes Mikovich Presbyter Coop. et Sacrista [?] conjunxit in Matrimonium 3tia [?] praevie promissis Denunt., Simonem Samarsia Celibem [?] Sti Georgiensem [?] statu libero provisum et Virginem Mathiam Krampotich Celibem [?] Parochianam Segniensem oriundam Dom: d. Salvatorem, praesent. testibus Jacobo Munich et Matthae Savreti». The last entry of the page, under the heading «1828». Read at about 6x in four overlapping zooms; the groom's surname and the witnesses are not firm; the bride's surname is clear (Krmpotić, written Krampotich)|simon-samarsia-groom-of-1828-with-a-krmpotic-bride,mathia-krmpotic-bride-of-samarsia-1828|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1823-georgius-savretic-lucia-lonaric-witnesses-joannes-laurentius-boras|senj-marriage-1823-georgius-savretic-lucia-lonaric-witnesses-joannes-laurentius-boras-line.jpg||Senj, [?] 1823 — Georgius Savretić groom of 1823 with Boras witnesses|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 335, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LQ18|«… Vincentius Bastatich Cooperator conjunxit in Matrimonium … Georgium Savretich et Virginem Luciam Lonaric praemissis praevie 3tiis Denuntiationibus … praesentibus testibus Joanne Boraz et Laurentio Boraz». Two lines of an abbreviated one-paragraph entry of 1823 (the date is lost from the line cropped), read at about 6x. Two Boras (Boraš) men as witnesses at Senj in 1823|georgius-savretic-groom-of-1823-with-boras-witnesses,lucia-loncaric-bride-of-savretic-1823|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1823-05-bride-from-dalmatia-witness-josephus-boras|senj-marriage-1823-05-bride-from-dalmatia-witness-josephus-boras-line.jpg||Senj, 7 May 1823 — Josephus Boras witness at Senj marriage of 1823|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 335, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LQ18|«7 Maji [1823]. Petrus Rossich Cooperator conjunxit in Matrimonium tribus praevie praemissis Denuntiationibus, [N.N.] Dalmatam ex.. [?] statu liberum et Viduam M[…] … praesentibus testibus Antonio Pavlić [?] et Josepho Boras». Read at about 6x; the couple's names are not read, only the witness Josephus Boras|josephus-boras-witness-at-senj-marriage-of-1823|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1838-11-gregorius-smojver-of-jablanac-widow-maria-miskulin|senj-marriage-1838-11-gregorius-smojver-of-jablanac-widow-maria-miskulin-line.jpg||Senj, [?] November 1838 — Gregorius Smojver of Jablanac groom of 1838|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 340, left-hand page, first entry of the page (entry no. 23)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQ25|«1838 die [?] Novembris in Ecclesia Cathedrali copulati sunt Segniae. Gregorius Smojver Caelebs, Parochianus Jablanacensis, cum praevie productam a Centuria Licentiam Dti S. Georgii 4:° 8bris, ac [?] quam et secus productam libero suo statu a respectivo parocho originis suae Dti Jablanaz 26 Septembris a.c. — Conjunctus fuit in Matrimonium cum Vidua Maria Miskulin, Uxore Defuncti Vincentii Miskulin Nautae — praedicti Sponsi tribus diebus Dominicis inter missarum solemnia proclamati fuerunt et in quarto simplicis affinitatis gradu a sua Illustritate dispensati erant»; ages 25 and 32; condition «Bajulus» [porter]; entry no. 23; celebrant Laurentius Heský, cooperator. Read at about 8x. A Smojver of Jablanac, a labouring man, marrying a widow to whom he was related in the fourth degree of affinity|gregorius-smojver-of-jablanac-groom-of-1838,maria-miskulin-widow-bride-of-gregorius-smojver-1838|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1839-01-josephus-schwarz-maria-smojver-of-karlobag|senj-marriage-1839-01-josephus-schwarz-maria-smojver-of-karlobag-line.jpg||Senj, 30 January 1839 — Josephus Schwarz corporal groom of 1839 with a Smojver bride of Karlobag|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 340, right-hand page, third entry on the right-hand page (entry no. 25), whole entry in three zooms|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQ25|«1839 die 30 Januarii in Ecclesia Cathedrali copulati sunt Segniae. Josephus Schwarz Caelebs [natus in Magna Bukowin in Bohemia], religione Catholicus, filius legitimus Defunctorum Joannis et Veronicae Schwarz, fabristignarii [?]. Produxit Licentiam Inclytae Generalis Directionis dd. Wiennae 20 Octobris 1838 N° 4048 et Districtualis Superioritatis dd. Carlostadii 1 Novembris a.c. N° 1286, matrimonio jungendi cum Domicella Maria Smojver Parochiana Carlobagensi, filia legitima Defuncti Dni Nicolai Smojver Caes.-Reg. Cancellistae Sanitatis et ejus Conthoralis adhuc viventis Ursulae. Tribus diebus Dominicis inter missarum solemnia praedicti Sponsi proclamati fuerunt»; ages 39 and 22; condition «Corporalis fortificationis»; entry no. 25; witnesses Johann Wukelich [Vukelić!] and another (Lukinger? Lohringer? «Lehringer Lohraffer»); celebrant Laurentius Heský, cooperator. Read at about 8x in three zooms (groom, bride's line, bride's parents). A Smojver household at KARLOBAG in 1839: the father Nicolaus Smojver, a chancery officer of the sanitary service (the cordon), already dead, the mother Ursula living. The witness «Johann Wukelich» is a Vukelić|josephus-schwarz-corporal-groom-of-1839-with-a-smojver-bride-of-karlobag,maria-smojver-of-karlobag-bride-of-josephus-schwarz-1839|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1838-10-ambrosius-stokich-margaritha-witness-josephus-boras-merchant|senj-marriage-1838-10-ambrosius-stokich-margaritha-witness-josephus-boras-merchant-line.jpg||Senj, 1 October 1838 — Josephus Boras merchant witness at Senj marriage of 1838|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 339, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQR9|«1838 die 1ma Octobris in Ecclesia Cathedrali copulati sunt Segniae. Ambrosius Stokich Caelebs filius legitimus Matthaei et Helenae Stokich Bajulorum Parochianus hujus — iniit matrimonium cum Puella Margaritha Klissanin filia legitima Josephi et Catharinae jugalium denatorum Klissanin Bajulorum Parochiana hujus — praevie producta a potestate Civili Licentia dtd 12 Septembris a.c. N° 17 — et tribus diebus Dominicis inter missarum solemnia denuntiati fuerunt»; ages 24 and 29; condition «Bajulus»; entry no. 22; witness column «+ Josepe Boras Mercante» and «+ Matija Radetić Marinaro» with «Joseph Janušić» and «Joseph Kalijević [?]». Read at about 6x. A Boras (Boraš), by trade a merchant, as witness at Senj in 1838 — the same name as Joannes, Laurentius and Josephus Boras, witnesses of 1823|josephus-boras-merchant-witness-at-senj-marriage-of-1838|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1837-08-georgius-tomjanovich-vincentia-smojver-of-jablanac|senj-marriage-1837-08-georgius-tomjanovich-vincentia-smojver-of-jablanac-line.jpg||Senj, 27 August 1837 — Georgius Tomjanović groom of 1837 with a Smojver bride of Jablanac|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 349, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ82|«1837 die 27 Augusti in Ecclesia Cathedrali copulati sunt Segniae. Georgius Tomjanovich Parochianus hujas filius vero Doymi? iniit matrimonium cum Puella Vincentia Smoiver Parochiana Jablanacensi, filia vero Marci et Barbarae jugalium Smoiver Agricolarum, praemissis tamen tribus inter missarum solemnia denunciationibus et libero suo statu a potestate Civili Licentia provisi — prout in fasciculo Sub Litt. T. N° 6»; ages 40 and 30; condition «Campo» [farmer]; entry no. 6; witnesses «Gregorio Jesenko, Mercator» and «Giovanni Felici, Mercante»; celebrant Laurentius Heský, cooperator. Read at about 8x. A Smojver household of Jablanac in 1837: Marcus Smojver and Barbara, farmers, their daughter Vincentia (born about 1807); a Gregorius Smojver of Jablanac married at Senj in 1838 (image 340L) — whether he is her brother cannot be told from the two entries. Tomjanović is a name near the listed Tomljanović|georgius-tomjanovic-groom-of-1837-with-a-smojver-bride-of-jablanac,vincentia-smojver-of-jablanac-bride-of-georgius-tomjanovic-1837|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1826-02-franciscus-thian-maria-vukelich-of-st-georgen|senj-marriage-1826-02-franciscus-thian-maria-vukelich-of-st-georgen-line.jpg||Senj, 5 February 1826 — Franciscus Thian groom of 1826 with a Vukelić bride of Sveti Juraj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 347, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQ2B|«5 Februarii [1826]. Georgius Jandonati Cooperator conjunxit in Matrimonium 3tio praevie promissis denuntiationibus Franciscum Thian et Puellam Mariam Vukelich St. Georgensem, praesentibus testibus Vincentio Baraž et Francisco Mihalich». An abbreviated one-paragraph entry of the 1820s, under the heading «1826». Read at about 6x; the witness «Baraž» is the Boras / Baraz of the 1821–23 lines on image 346L, spelled differently|franciscus-thian-groom-of-1826-with-a-vukelic-bride-of-sveti-juraj,maria-vukelic-of-sveti-juraj-bride-of-franciscus-thian-1826|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1833-02-petrus-tomaich-soldier-helena-krmpotich-of-st-salvator|senj-marriage-1833-02-petrus-tomaich-soldier-helena-krmpotich-of-st-salvator-line.jpg||Senj, 4 February 1833 — Petrus Tomaić soldier groom of 1833 with a Krmpotić bride of St Salvator|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 348, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQFD|«4to Februarii 1833. Petrus Tomaijch Parochianus Lukovensis Centuriae St. Georgensis, Domus N° [?], Miles, filius Georgii et Evae Tomaich comorantium in Lukovo. Sponsa Helena Krempotich, filia Nicolai et Marthae Krempotich oriunda ad S. Salvatorem Centuriae St. Georgensis Domus sub 30 ex Hollaci [?] —»; ages 22 and 17; condition «Miles»; entry no. 3; witnesses Georgius Tomaich of Lukovo and Antonius Kalavina, both soldiers of the company of St Georgen; celebrant Hieronymus Francichi [?]. Read at about 8x in four zooms (the entry sits on the right-hand page of image 348; images 347R and 348R are the same page). A Krmpotić household at Sveti Spas (the St Salvator church above Senj, in the frontier company of St Juraj), 1833: Nicolaus and Martha Krmpotić of house 30, their daughter Helena aged 17 (born about 1816)|petrus-tomaic-soldier-groom-of-1833-with-a-krmpotic-bride-of-st-salvator,helena-krmpotic-of-st-salvator-bride-of-petrus-tomaic-1833|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1843-11-joannes-thian-maria-oreskovich|senj-marriage-1843-11-joannes-thian-maria-oreskovich-line.jpg||Senj, 26 November 1843 — Joannes Thian groom of 1843 with an Orešković bride|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 350, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQ2D|«1843 Die 26 Novembris in Ecclesia Cathedrali Segniae copulati sunt. Joannes Thian caelebs, defuncti Matthaei Thian, et defunctae Antoniae filius, cum puella Maria Oreskovich Leonosi [?] et Mariae Oreskovich filia, Parochiae Segniensis»; ages 23 and 20; condition «Bajulus»; entry no. 13; witnesses Georgius Thian and Franciscus Thian, both fishermen [«Piscator»]; celebrant Hippolytus Domazetovich?, cooperator. Read at about 6x; the bride's father's forename is not firm; both her parents are written Orešković|joannes-thian-groom-of-1843-with-an-oreskovic-bride,maria-oreskovic-bride-of-joannes-thian-1843|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1845-02-bartholomaeus-tomjanovich-lucia-smojver-of-jablanac|senj-marriage-1845-02-bartholomaeus-tomjanovich-lucia-smojver-of-jablanac-line.jpg||Senj, [?] February 1845 — Bartholomaeus Tomjanović groom of 1845 with a Smojver bride of Jablanac|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 350, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQ2D|«1845 Die 2da Februarii in Ecclesia Cathedrali Segniae copulati fuere. Bartholomaeus Tomjanovich Coelebs Parochianus Fluminensis?, filius Nicolai et Annae — et puella Lucia Smoj-ver Parochiana Jablanacensi, filia [quae] immediata [?]»; ages 27 and 33; condition «Bajulus»; entry no. 15; witnesses Natale Lohmer, a barber of Senj, and Georgius Tomljanović, a fisherman of Senj; celebrant Joannes Grubisich, canon. Read at about 7x in one zoom that cuts the bride's line at «Smoj-»; the name is read «Smojver»; her parents' names are not read|bartholomaeus-tomjanovic-groom-of-1845-with-a-smojver-bride-of-jablanac,lucia-smojver-of-jablanac-bride-of-bartholomaeus-tomjanovic-1845|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1849-09-mathe-thian-maria-oreskovich-croatian-entry|senj-marriage-1849-09-mathe-thian-maria-oreskovich-croatian-entry-line.jpg||Senj, 9 September 1849 — Mathe Thian groom of 1849 with an Orešković bride|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 351, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ55|«1849. dana 9. Setembra združih ja Toma Sladovich kapelan u sveti Matrimon Mathu Thian godišt 28 Plovanie Senske, sina pokojnoga Mathe Thiana, s Divojkom Mariom Oreskovich godišt 22 kćerom pokojnoga formosa [?] Oreskovich i Marie rodjene Tkovich [?], Plovanie Senske. na prici svidoci: + Anton Miskulin Tekaši [?] + Pavlo [?] Aichtar [?] Tojak». A Croatian-language entry. Read at about 7x; the bride's father's forename and her mother's maiden name are not firm|mathe-thian-groom-of-1849-with-an-oreskovic-bride,marija-oreskovic-bride-of-mathe-thian-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1853-04-ignatius-turkalj-maria-maglich-mother-oreskovich|senj-marriage-1853-04-ignatius-turkalj-maria-maglich-mother-oreskovich-line.jpg||Senj, 10 April 1853 — Ignatius Turkalj soldier groom of 1853 whose mother was a Borić|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 352, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQ5J|«1853 Aprilis 10 in Cathedrali Ecclesia Segniae. Ignatius Turkalj, in Inclyta Legione Sluniensi, Sluniensis filius legitimus Josephi Turkalj vigitarum Praefecti ejusque conthoralis Annae natae Borzich, caelebs catholicus; et Maria filia legitima Martini Maglich ejusque conjugis Mariae natae Oreskovich, Segniensis, caelebs catholica»; ages 31 and 19; condition «Armigerius» [soldier]; entry no. 29; witnesses Ivan Rontich [?] and Domenico Petich, merchants; celebrant Joannes Grubisich, canon-cantor. Read at about 8x. A Borić (the groom's mother) and an Orešković (the bride's mother) in one entry — both listed surnames, as maiden names|ignatius-turkalj-soldier-groom-of-1853-whose-mother-was-a-boric,maria-maglicic-bride-of-ignatius-turkalj-1853-whose-mother-was-an-oreskovic|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1856-07-casparus-paulus-babich-maria-of-bescanensis|senj-marriage-1856-07-casparus-paulus-babich-maria-of-bescanensis-line.jpg||Senj, 20 July 1856 — Casparus Paulus Babić mariner groom of 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 358, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L7QK|«Anno Domini 1856 die 20ma Julii in Cathedrali Ecclesia Segniensi copulati fuerunt. Caelebs Casparus Paulus, filius legitimus Bajuli Augustini Babich, et ejus consortis Mariae natae Farcsich, nautae Segniensis, et Maria, filia legitima Dominici Vukovich? et Catharinae natae Likarach?, parochiana Bescanensis [?], habita facultate a politica juris- dictione matrimonium ineundi dd. Segniae 5to Julii 1856 …»; ages 24 and 26; condition «Marinarius»; entry no. 20 [read «69» in the margin]; witnesses Joannes Bragonovich and Vincentius Cihotta?, both [Speculatores? «Specilantes»]; celebrant Antonius Lukonić, cooperator. Read at about 8x in two zooms; the bride's surname and her place are not firm|casparus-paulus-babic-mariner-groom-of-1856,maria-of-bescan-bride-of-casparus-paulus-babic-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1833-06-petrus-vukelich-widower-of-krasno-martha-krmpotich-widow|senj-marriage-1833-06-petrus-vukelich-widower-of-krasno-martha-krmpotich-widow-line.jpg||Senj, 24 June 1833 — Petrus Vukelić widower of Krasno groom of 1833 with a Krmpotić widow|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 360, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQKY|«Die 24 Junii 1833. Viduus Petrus Vukelich Parochiae Krasnensis fidelis — Vidua Martha Krempotich Parochiana Segniensis, ambo Jurisdictionis Inclytae Leg. Ottocensis, Centuriae vero S. Georgiensis Domiciliati in Krasno — qui inter Missarum solemnia denuntiati fuerunt»; ages 59 and 48; condition [blank / Confinarius?]; entry no. 3; witnesses «+ Ivan Vukelich, Confinarius Parochiae Krasnensis» and «+ Dionisius Zurko? … S. Georgii»; celebrant Laurentius Heský, cooperator. Read at about 7x in two zooms. A Vukelić widower of Krasno marrying a Krmpotić widow, two listed surnames in one entry; a witness Ivan Vukelić, probably a relation. This entry sits on page 141 of the register's second sequence (the 1831–34 tabular entries that follow the 1820s abbreviated lines)|petrus-vukelic-widower-of-krasno-groom-of-1833-with-a-krmpotic-widow,martha-krmpotic-widow-bride-of-petrus-vukelic-1833|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1828-04-paulus-vukelich-catharina-miskulin-witness-joseph-boras|senj-marriage-1828-04-paulus-vukelich-catharina-miskulin-witness-joseph-boras-line.jpg||Senj, 27 April 1828 — Joseph Boras witness at Senj marriage of 1828|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 360, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQKY|«27 Aprilis [1828]. Nicolaus Gorich Cooperator conjunxit in Matrimonium 3tio praevie praemissis Denuntiationibus Paulum Verkovich? et Virginem Catharinam Miskulin, praesent. testibus Josepho Boras et Nicolao Prinacitich». An abbreviated one-paragraph entry of 1828. Read at about 5x in one zoom; the groom's surname is read «Verkovich» (a possible Vuković) and the witness «Boraš» is clear|joseph-boras-witness-at-senj-marriage-of-1828|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1851-05-vitus-vukellich-antonia-dvoich|senj-marriage-1851-05-vitus-vukellich-antonia-dvoich-line.jpg||Senj, 25 May 1851 — Vitus Vukelić tailor groom of 1851 from Kosinj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 363, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ6G|«1851 Die 25 Maji in Cathedrali Ecclesia copulati fuere. Vitus Vukellić filius legitimus Lemmi [?] et Annae Vukellić Parochianus inferioris Kosinjensis, cum puella Antonia Dvoić filia legitima Defuncti Matthiae Dvoić et Justinae natae Filić [?] Parochiana Segniensis — Praedicti sponsi inter Missarum solemnia denuntiati fuerunt, et in fasciculo sub litt. V N° 19 asservantur»; ages 24 and 22; condition «Sartor»; witnesses Gergo Jesenko and L. Trescherich? [«Truschenich»]; celebrant Philippus Khuzmanić?, cooperator; entry no. 19. Read at about 8x. A Vukelić man of Kosinj with a Vukelić mother, marrying at Senj; the other Vukelić entries of this register (1833, 1839) are of Krasno, Senj and Sveti Juraj|vitus-vukelic-tailor-groom-of-1851-from-kosinj,antonia-dvoic-bride-of-vitus-vukelic-1851|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1851-07-vincentius-bride-lucia-butkovich-of-ledenice|senj-marriage-1851-07-vincentius-bride-lucia-butkovich-of-ledenice-line.jpg||Senj, [?] July 1851 — Vincentius mariner groom of 1851 with a Butković bride of Ledenice|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 363, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ6G|«1851 die [?] Julii in Cathedrali Ecclesia Segniae copulati fuere. Vincentius … filius legitimus … et … parochianus … cum puella Lucia Butkovic filia legitima Andreae et Ellentinae [Helenae] Butkovic Parochiae Ledenicensi — praedicti sponsi inter missarum solemnia denuntiati fuerunt, et licentia a respectiva auctoritate politica provisi fuere, quae in archivio parochiali sub littera V N° 20 in fasciculo asservantur»; ages 26 and 24; condition «Nauta» [mariner]; entry no. 20; witnesses Dasma? Bilan and Marcy Tranie?; celebrant Gregorius Potočnjak, cooperator senior. Read at about 8x; the groom's name and father are not read. A Butković bride of Ledenice, parents Andreas and Helena|vincentius-mariner-groom-of-1851-with-a-butkovic-bride-of-ledenice,lucia-butkovic-of-ledenice-bride-of-1851|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1851-08-joannes-vukelich-of-gospic-francisca-tomjanovich|senj-marriage-1851-08-joannes-vukelich-of-gospic-francisca-tomjanovich-line.jpg||Senj, 19 August 1851 — Joannes Vukelić of Gospić groom of 1851|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 363, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ6G|«1851 die 19 Augusti in Cathedrali Ecclesia Segniae copulati fuere. Joannes Vukelić filius legitimus Georgii et Magdalenae jugalium Vukelić ex Parochia Gospiciensi, parochianus Gospiciensis, cum puella Francisca Tomjanović filia legitima Gregorii et Franciscae Tomjanović jugalium, parochiana Corbaviensi [?]. Praedicti sponsi inter missarum solemnia denunciati, et licentia a respectiva auctoritate politica provisi fuere, quae in archivio parochiali sub littera V N° 21 in fasciculo asservantur»; ages 26 and 25; conditions «Bajulus» [porter, read] and «Serva»; witnesses Lukas? Jakomini? Zemar? Tomljanović; celebrant Gregorius Potočnjak, cooperator senior; page 144, entry no. 21. Read at about 8x in two zooms; the groom's father's and mother's names are Georgius and Magdalena Vukelić. A Vukelić of Gospić and a Tomjanović bride|joannes-vukelic-of-gospic-groom-of-1851,francisca-tomjanovic-bride-of-joannes-vukelic-1851|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1841-01-georgius-vukelich-widower-of-st-georgen-hellena|senj-marriage-1841-01-georgius-vukelich-widower-of-st-georgen-hellena-line.jpg||Senj, [2?] January 1841 — Georgius Vukelić widower mariner of St Georgen groom of 1841|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 362, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQFP|«1841 Die 2[?] Januarii … copulati fuere in domo privata … Georgius Wukelich Viduus Sanctae Georgiensis parochianus, filius Josephi? jugalium Defunctorum [Vukelich?] — cum Vidua Hellena [Mikorovich?] filia jugalium Thomae et Hellenae Gladzich Leguiensium — praedicti sponsi a respectiva auctoritate … inter Missarum solemnia manifestis denuntiationibus … matrimonio juncti sunt. Documenta in fasciculo sub litt. W N° 16 …»; ages 45 and 37; condition «Nauta» [mariner]; witnesses «+ Franciscus Thian Piscator, et + Elias Stofsich Piscator ambo Segnienses»; celebrant De Vicentii? Dottor? Antonius Lucich? cooperator; entry no. 16. Read at about 8x; the groom's parents and the bride's surname are not firm, the groom's own surname «Wukelich» is clear (Vukelić) and his home Sveti Juraj|georgius-vukelic-widower-mariner-of-st-georgen-groom-of-1841|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1853-06-franciscus-samarzia-widower-maria-krmpotich|senj-marriage-1853-06-franciscus-samarzia-widower-maria-krmpotich-line.jpg||Senj, 19 June 1853 — Franciscus Samarzia widower soldier groom of 1853 with a Krmpotić bride|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 366, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ6L|«1853 Die 19 Junii in Ecclesia Cathedrali Segniae copulati sunt. Viduus Franciscus Samarzia filius Petri sim[plex] miles Regimenti Otociani Parochianus Sancti Georgiensis ex pago Belgrane [?], Cum puella Maria filia Michaelis et Antoniae Krempotić Parochiana Segniensis. Sub[l]atis sponsi et… licentia provisi fuere»; ages 27 and 19; condition «Miles simplex»; entry no. 73; witnesses Georgius Samarzia and Elias Samarzia; celebrant Philippus Hreskovic, cooperator. Read at about 8x in two zooms; the entry runs below the zoomed lines and the bride's parents' names are read down to «Krempotić». A Krmpotić household of Senj parish in 1853: Michael and Antonia, their daughter Maria aged 19 (born about 1834)|franciscus-samarzia-widower-soldier-groom-of-1853-with-a-krmpotic-bride,maria-krmpotic-bride-of-franciscus-samarzia-1853|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1851-02-josephus-boras-widower-maria-sucic|senj-marriage-1851-02-josephus-boras-widower-maria-sucic-line.jpg||Senj, 1 February 1851 — Josephus Boras groom of 1851 at Senj|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 375, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQ65|«1851 Die 1° Februarii in Domo privata copulati fuere. Caelebs Josephus Boras filius Defunctorum Josephi et Annae Boras natae Butirach [?] cum Vidua Maria Sučić [?] Parochiana Segniensi. Praedicti sponsi respective potestate politica licentia provisi, ac ab Excellentissimo et Illustrissimo Domino Dioecesano Episcopo ad denuntiationes … dispensati fuere, quae omnia in fasciculo sub Litt. B.B. N° 52 asservantur»; ages 32 and 28; condition [«Nauta»?]; entry no. 52; witnesses Franciscus Abat? and Michael Spanić; celebrant Philippus Hreskovic, cooperator loci. Read at about 7x in four zooms (the date, the groom's line and the bride's line); the groom's mother's maiden name and the bride's surname are not firm. A JOSEPH BORAS OF SENJ, born about 1819, son of the late Josephus Boras and Anna — the Boras household whose men stand as witnesses at Senj from 1823 (images 335L, 339R, 360L)|josephus-boras-groom-of-1851-at-senj,maria-sucic-widow-bride-of-josephus-boras-1851|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1851-07-christophorus-babich-catharina-stillin-of-ledenice|senj-marriage-1851-07-christophorus-babich-catharina-stillin-of-ledenice-line.jpg||Senj, 13 July 1851 — Christophorus Babić mariner groom of 1851 with a bride of Ledenice|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 375, right-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQ65|«1851 Die 13. Julii in Ecclesia Cathedrali copulati sunt. Christophorus Babić Parochianus hujas cum Catharina filia Georgii et Annae Stillin Parochiana Ledenicensi. Praedicti sponsi ter inter missarum solemnia denuntiati fuerunt, et a potestate politica licentia provisi, quae in fasciculo sub litt. BB N° 54 asservantur»; ages 30 and 29; condition «Nauta»; entry no. 54; witnesses Franciscus Gregorović and Christophorus Janković; celebrant Philippus Hreskovic, cooperator loci. Read at about 8x|christophorus-babic-mariner-groom-of-1851-with-a-bride-of-ledenice,catharina-stillin-of-ledenice-bride-of-christophorus-babic-1851|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1856-04-jacobus-zerkovic-widower-of-st-georgen-josepha-widow-krmpotich|senj-marriage-1856-04-jacobus-zerkovic-widower-of-st-georgen-josepha-widow-krmpotich-line.jpg||Senj, [14?] April 1856 — Jacobus Žerković widower groom of 1856 with a Krmpotić widow bride|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 375, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQ65|«… 1856 die 14 … in Ecclesia … Segniae copulati fuere. Viduus Jacobus Žerkovic Sancti Georgii Parochiae fidelis, militis [?] Regiminis Otocani, Centuriae Sancti Georgiensis, et Vidua Josepha, defuncti Joannis Krempotić Centuriae Krempotićanis, nata vero [?] … a politica Jurisdictione dd. St. Georgii 26 martii 1856 …, idem Dni Sponsi dd. St. Georgii 14 Aprilis 1856 … Praedicti sponsi … matrimonium ineundi … denuntiationibus … dispensati»; ages 49? and 48?; entry no. 14; witnesses «+ Franciscus Babich Senior populi? parochii St Georgii» and «+ Gregorius Krempotich … parochii S.M.V. ad Nives»; celebrant Ignatius Pavlić? Read at about 7x in four zooms; the date and ages are not firm but the bride's father Joannes Krmpotić of the company of Krmpotić, and the witness Gregorius Krmpotić of S.M.V. ad Nives (the church of Our Lady of the Snows above Senj), are clear. A Krmpotić household at S. Maria ad Nives in 1856|jacobus-zerkovic-widower-groom-of-1856-with-a-krmpotic-widow-bride,josepha-krmpotic-widow-bride-of-jacobus-zerkovic-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1852-08-michael-belobarbic-francisca-petrinovic-of-novi|senj-marriage-1852-08-michael-belobarbic-francisca-petrinovic-of-novi-line.jpg||Senj, 31 August [1852] — Michael Belobarbić groom of 1852 with a bride of Novi in Vinodol|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 376, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQNZ|«[1852] Die 31° [Augusti] in Ecclesia Cathedrali copulati fuere. Michael Belobarbić Parochianus hujas, cum puella Francisca filia Joannis Petrinović et Ursulae natae Petrinović Parochiana Novensis in Vinodol. Praedicti sponsi respective potestate politica licentia provisi, ter inter Missarum solemnia denuntiati, et ab Excellentissimo ac Illustrissimo Domino Dioecesano Episcopo ut in Domo privata copulari possent, dispensati fuere, quae in fasciculo sub lit. B.B. N° 57 asservantur»; ages 28 and 27; condition «Bajulus»; entry no. 56 [read «57» in the bundle reference]; witnesses «Samuel? Draskovich? an[d] Georgius Sandrovich?»; celebrant Philippus Hreskovic, cooperator loci. Read at about 8x in three zooms; the year is not read (the next entry is of 21 November 1852). Belobarbić is a listed surname|michael-belobarbic-groom-of-1852-with-a-bride-of-novi-in-vinodol,francisca-petrinovic-of-novi-bride-of-michael-belobarbic-1852|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1852-11-joannes-babic-mother-maria-nee-jurcic-jacoba-fabris|senj-marriage-1852-11-joannes-babic-mother-maria-nee-jurcic-jacoba-fabris-line.jpg||Senj, 21 November 1852 — Joannes Babić mariner groom of 1852 whose mother was née Jurčić|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 376, left-hand page, see the entry quoted|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQNZ|«1852 Die 21 Novembris in Ecclesia Cathedrali copulati fuere. Joannes Babić filius Augustini Babić et Mariae natae Jurcić, cum puella Jacoba filia Defuncti Alexii Fabris et Vlgangae natae Tr[ovic?] Parochianis hujas. Praedicti sponsi potestate politica licentia provisi, ter inter Missarum solemnia denuntiati, et ex fasciculo sub lit. B.B. N° 59 asservantur»; ages 24 and 24; condition «Marinarius»; entry no. 59; witnesses «Christophorus Janković, Anton Babić»; celebrant Philippus Hreskovic, cooperator loci. Read at about 8x. A Babić, son of Augustinus Babić and a Jurčić [listed surname as the mother's maiden name]; Augustinus Babić is the labourer who is the father of the mariner Casparus Paulus Babić married in 1856 (image 358R) — the same man's household, probably|joannes-babic-mariner-groom-of-1852-whose-mother-was-nee-jurcic,jacoba-fabris-bride-of-joannes-babic-1852|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1830-01-margaritha-blazevich-aged-50|senj-death-1830-01-margaritha-blazevich-aged-50-line.jpg||Senj, 24 January 1830 — Margaritha Blažević died Senj January 1830|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 384, left-hand page, third line of the 1830 heading, page 4|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQJJ|«24 January [1830] obiit Margaritha Blazevich S. provisa, aetatis annorum circiter 50» — the death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), one line per death: date, «obiit», the name, whether she received the sacraments, the age; the right-hand column gives the age as 50. Read at about 3x on the page and in a zoom of the line (the surname «Blazevich» is clear). Her husband, father or children are not named (the register of this period gives neither parents nor husband for adults)|margaritha-blazevic-died-senj-january-1830|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1830-08-francisca-blazevich-aged-70|senj-death-1830-08-francisca-blazevich-aged-70-line.jpg||Senj, 7 August 1830 — Francisca Blažević died Senj August 1830|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 384, left-hand page, 1830 section, 7 August, page 4|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQJJ|«7° Augusti obiit Francisca Blazevich [Sacramentis provisa], aetatis annorum 70» — the death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), page 4, the 1830 section; the right-hand age is 70. Read in a zoom of the line (the surname «Blazevich» is clear)|francisca-blazevic-died-senj-august-1830|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1838-10-paulus-butkovich-vigil-of-krmpote-aged-26|senj-death-1838-10-paulus-butkovich-vigil-of-krmpote-aged-26-line.jpg||Senj, 15 October 1838 — Paulus Butković watchman of Krmpote died Senj 1838|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 389, left-hand page, entry 68 of the death register, page 6|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQZB|«1838 die 15° Octobris. Paulus Butkovich Vigil Tricesimae, Oriundus ex Krumpote [Krmpote], 26 [annorum], Phthisis, provisus, Ad S. Vitum [sepultus], [sepeliens: L. Heský, cooperator]; Nro protocolli 68». The death register of Senj, page 6 (1838), tabular: date, name and surname, age in years, disease, sacraments, place of burial, the priest, number. Read at about 8x. A Butković (a listed surname) from KRMPOTE (a listed place), a customs watchman at Senj, died young; the entry names no parents|paulus-butkovic-watchman-of-krmpote-died-senj-1838|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1839-06-josephus-boros-aged-50-with-josephus-gallas|senj-death-1839-06-josephus-boros-aged-50-with-josephus-gallas-line.jpg||Senj, [?] June 1839 — Josephus Boras died Senj 1839 aged 50|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 389, right-hand page, entry 79 of the death register, page 7, second line|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LQZB|«1839 die 23 [Junii] [Josephus Gallas, 67; second line:] Josephus Boros, 50» — the cause of death, written once for both, «Magistri Cyatho?, Laevorum [?] Inflammatio pulmonum», the sacraments «provisi», burial at S. Vitus; the priest Veronicus? Entry no. 79 [? read «79» or «74»]. Read at about 8x in three zooms; the first line's name is «Josephus Gallas» and the age beside it is 67, the second line is «Josephus Boros» and 50. The year is 1839; the surname is written «Boros» but is read as Boras — a Josephus Boras, born about 1789, whose men and namesakes are the Boras witnesses of the marriages of 1823–1838 and a Josephus Boras (born about 1819) who married at Senj in 1851 (images 375R)|josephus-boras-died-senj-1839-aged-50|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1840-09-margaritha-blazevich-aged-50|senj-death-1840-09-margaritha-blazevich-aged-50-line.jpg||Senj, 18 September 1840 — Margaritha Blažević died Senj September 1840|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 390, left-hand page, entry 86 of the death register, page 7|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ8Q|«1840 Die 18 Septembris Segniae obiit. Margaritha Blazewich, 50 [annorum], Gangraena intestinorum, provisa, Ad S. Vitum, [sepelivit] Petrus Dorrenich [Korrenich?] Cooperator; N° protocolli 86». The death register of Senj, page 7 (the 1840 section), tabular. Read at about 8x at page scale and in a zoom of the top of the row. The woman who died in 1830 aged 50 (images 384L) is another or the same Margaritha with a clerk's rounding of her age; no husband or parents named|margaritha-blazevic-died-senj-september-1840|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1841-09-anna-widow-boras-aged-51|senj-death-1841-09-anna-widow-boras-aged-51-line.jpg||Senj, 1 September 1841 — Anna Boras widow died Senj September 1841|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 390, right-hand page, entry 96 of the death register, page 8|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ8Q|«1841 Die 1ª Septembris Segniae obiit. Anna Vidua Boraſs [Boras], 51 [annorum], Phthisis pulmonalis, Omnibus morientium S. sacramentis provisa, Ad S. Vitum, [sepelivit] Petrus Dorrenich Cooperator; N° protocolli 96». The death register of Senj, page 8, tabular. Read at about 7x in a zoom of the row. A Boras widow, aged 51 [born about 1790] — two years after a Josephus Boras of 50 died (image 389R), perhaps her husband; and she is a «Vidua» of the Boras whose men are witnesses at Senj marriages of 1823–1838|anna-boras-widow-died-senj-september-1841|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1842-04-jacobus-blazevich-aged-10|senj-death-1842-04-jacobus-blazevich-aged-10-line.jpg||Senj, [?] April 1842 — Jacobus Blažević aged 10 died Senj April 1842|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 391, right-hand page, entry 107 of the death register, page 9, first line|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQ4X|«1842 Die [?] Aprilis Segniae expiravit. Jacobus Blazevich, 10 [annorum], Phthisis scrophulosa, —, Ad S. Vitum, [sepelivit] Petrus Dorrenich Cooperator; N° protocolli 107». The death register of Senj, page 9, tabular; the first entry of the page. Read at about 3x at page scale (the entry is large and the surname is clear); no parents named|jacobus-blazevic-aged-10-died-senj-april-1842|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1844-03-fabianus-blazevich-widower-aged-74|senj-death-1844-03-fabianus-blazevich-widower-aged-74-line.jpg||Senj, 27 March 1844 — Fabianus Blažević widower aged 74 died Senj March 1844|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 392, right-hand page, entry 130 of the death register, page 10|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LQF5|«1844 Die 27 Martii Segniae obiit. Viduus Fabianus Blazevich, 74 [annorum], Marasmus senilis, Moribundum S. Sacramentis provisus, Ad S. Vitum, [sepelivit] Petrus Dorrenich Cooperator; N° protocolli 130». The death register of Senj, page 10, tabular. Read at about 8x in one zoom of the row (the first word is «Viduus», the surname «Blazevich»). A man born about 1770; he is very probably the Fabianus Blažević who stood as witness at Senj marriages of 1802–1812 (images 154–206) and who married, as a widower tailor, the widow Margaritha M[…]ich on 17 [?]bris 1832 (image 222R, his age read there as 68, which would be a clerk's or a reader's error for about 62) — and the entry calls him a widower again, so Margaritha, who was about 28 in 1832, died before March 1844; the death register of 1832–44 would show her|fabianus-blazevic-widower-aged-74-died-senj-march-1844|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1824-09-marcus-son-of-marcus-and-francisca-krmpotich-aged-1|senj-death-1824-09-marcus-son-of-marcus-and-francisca-krmpotich-aged-1-line.jpg||Senj, 16 September [1824] — Marcus Krmpotić infant died Senj September 1824|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 439, left-hand page, K section, page 49-50 (image 439 left page), first entry under «Mense Septembri»|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LC7J|«[Mense Septembri] 16° Septembris obiit Marcus filius Marci et Franciscae Krampotich, Anni circiter unius». The abbreviated one-line death entries of the 1820s (the register of Senj, Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848, the K section): date, «obiit», the name, the age; the entry is the first under the month heading «Mense Septembri»; the year is 1824 by the heading «1825» that follows below it two entries later. Read at about 3x in a zoom of the line|marcus-krmpotic-infant-died-senj-september-1824|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1825-09-maria-daughter-of-michael-krmpotich-of-st-salvator|senj-death-1825-09-maria-daughter-of-michael-krmpotich-of-st-salvator-line.jpg||Senj, 2 September 1825 — Maria Krmpotić daughter of Michael of St Salvator died Senj 1825|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 439, left-hand page, K section, 1825, 2 September|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LC7J|«2° Septembris obiit Maria filia Michaelis Krampotich ad S. Salvatorem aetatis annorum [—]» — the death register of Senj, the K section, 1825; the right-hand age is not read at this crop. Read at about 3x in a zoom of the line. The father Michael Krmpotić of S. Salvator is very probably the Michael Krmpotić who married a widow in 1822 (image 276R) and again in 1830 (image 277L), if he is one man; the two marriage entries give him at Senj with a Lončarić as witness, the second 'oriundus ex loco ad S. Salvatorem domus N° 30', aged 54|maria-krmpotic-daughter-of-michael-of-st-salvator-died-senj-1825|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1834-02-anna-krmpotich-born-at-st-salvator-aged-30|senj-death-1834-02-anna-krmpotich-born-at-st-salvator-aged-30-line.jpg||Senj, 16 February 1834 — Anna Krmpotić born at St Salvator died Senj February 1834|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 439, left-hand page, K section, 1834, last entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LC7J|«1834 16 Februarii obiit Anna Krampotich nata ad S. Salvatorem, Parochiana vero Segniensis, S. provisa, aetatis annorum circiter 30». The death register of Senj, the K section (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848). Read at about 3x in a zoom of the two lines; a woman born at Sveti Spas about 1804, married or not is not said (the 1820s lines do not give a husband for a woman) — perhaps the Helena Krmpotić of Sveti Spas of 1833 [she was 17 in Feb 1833: born 1816] is a different person|anna-krmpotic-born-at-st-salvator-died-senj-february-1834|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1831-03-michael-krmpotich-aged-14-and-nicolaus-krmpotich-aged-48-of-st-salvator|senj-death-1831-03-michael-krmpotich-aged-14-and-nicolaus-krmpotich-aged-48-of-st-salvator-line.jpg||Senj, March 1831 — Nicolaus Krmpotić of St Salvator died Senj March 1831|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 440, right-hand page, K section, page 51, entries 1 and 2|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHBP|«1831 [?] Martii. Michael Krempotich filius Michaelis, Confiniari S. Georgensis Centuriae Regiminis Ottocensis, [aetatis] quatuordecim, [morbus:] debilitate, [sine sacramentis], ad S. Petrum [sepultus], [sepeliens:] Maxim. Gjorgolich Cooperator, N° 1.» and «1831 15 Martii. Nicolaus Krempotich Centuriae S. Georgensis, Regiminis Ottocensis Militaris Subditus, domicilitatus ad S. Salvatorem prope Segniam, 48, [Phthisis], provisus, ad S. Vitum, Hieron. Franich Cooperator, N° 2». The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the K section, page 51, the first two entries of the tabular series of 1831; the page also gives the place of burial (S. Petrus for the boy, S. Vitus for the man) and the number of the entry. Read at about 6x at the two rows. The same company, the same village, the same year as Helena, daughter of Nicolaus and Martha Krmpotić of S. Salvator (house 30), who married at Senj in February 1833 (image 348R), and the Martha Krmpotić, widow, of the 1833 marriage to the widower Petrus Vukelić (image 360R) — a household that lost its head and a son in the one month|nicolaus-krmpotic-of-st-salvator-died-senj-march-1831|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1835-02-helena-krmpotich-aged-90|senj-death-1835-02-helena-krmpotich-aged-90-line.jpg||Senj, 16 February 1835 — Helena Krmpotić aged 90 died Senj February 1835|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 443, left-hand page, K section, entry 31 (443L, second row)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHYX|«1835. die 16 Februarii. Hellena Kermpotich, 90, Senium, provisa, Ad S. Vitum, [sepelivit] Bichanich Cooperator, N° 31». The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the K section, tabular, page 52–53, the second entry of the page (the first is Matthaeus Kriskovich, 30, died 16 October 1834). Read at about 8x. A Krmpotić woman born about 1745; no husband or children named — the row says nothing more|helena-krmpotic-aged-90-died-senj-february-1835|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1836-09-lucia-widow-kraljikas-aged-106|senj-death-1836-09-lucia-widow-kraljikas-aged-106-line.jpg||Senj, 3 September 1836 — Lucia widow Kraljikas aged 106 died Senj September 1836|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 443, right-hand page, K section, entry 43 (443R, fourth row)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHYX|«1836 die 3° Septembris. Lucia Vid.ª Kraljikas, 106 [?], Senium, provisa, Ad S. Vitum, [sepelivit] Bichanich Cooperator, N° 43». The death register of Senj, the K section, tabular, page 53. Read at about 8x in a zoom of the row: the surname is written «Kraljikas» (the ending is not Kraljić), the age is a heavily over-written three-figure number [«106»] that no one in a register of this period would have counted in years with confidence. Recorded because Kraljić is on the family list as a surname; the spelling does not settle it|lucia-widow-kraljikas-aged-106-died-senj-september-1836|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1838-11-catharina-widow-kralj-aged-84|senj-death-1838-11-catharina-widow-kralj-aged-84-line.jpg||Senj, [5?] November 1838 — Catharina widow Kralj aged 84 died Senj November 1838|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 444, left-hand page, K section, entry 54 (444L, fifth row)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LH22|«1838. die [5°?] Novembris. Catharina Vidua Kralj, 84, Apoplexia, provisa, Ad S. Vitum, [sepelivit] Hesky Cooperator, N° 54». The death register of Senj, the K section, tabular, page 54 (the page's left half). Read at about 8x in a zoom of the row's lower part. A widow born about 1754 with a surname written «Kralj» — the stem of the listed surname Kraljić (Kralich) — which a clerk could have shortened; not placed in any Kraljić household|catharina-widow-kralj-aged-84-died-senj-november-1838|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1844-01-eva-lukatelli-widow-aged-54|senj-death-1844-01-eva-lukatelli-widow-aged-54-line.jpg||Senj, 6 January 1844 — Eva Lukatelli widow aged 54 died Senj January 1844|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 452, right-hand page, L section, page 62, entry 53, third row|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LHK8|«1844 Die 6° Januarii Segniae obiit. Eva Lukatelli Vidua, 54, Febris dispaescens [?], Sacramentis morientium provisa, S.tus Vitus, [sepelivit] Hippolytus Domazetovich? Cooperator, N° 53». The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the L section, tabular, page 62, the third entry of the page. Read at full page scale (about 1x, the row is legible whole) because the zoom crops missed the row; the surname «Lukatelli» is clear. A Lukatelli widow, born about 1790, at Senj; the Lukatelli of this archive are at Karlobag (a Valerian Lukatella of Karlobag married at Senj in 1849, image 289L, and a Justina Lukatelli of Senj parish in 1844, image 328L)|eva-lukatelli-widow-aged-54-died-senj-january-1844|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1844-12-joanna-krmpotich-aged-60|senj-death-1844-12-joanna-krmpotich-aged-60-line.jpg||Senj, 28 December 1844 — Joanna Krmpotić aged 60 died Senj December 1844|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 452, right-hand page, L section, page 62, entry 57|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LHK8|«1844 Die 28 Decembris Segniae obiit. Joanna Kerepatich [Krempotich], 60, Febris dispaescens, Sacramentis morientium provisa, S. Vitus, [sepelivit] Petrus Dorrenich Cooperator, N° 57». The death register of Senj, the L section, tabular, page 62, the ninth row (the K surname Krmpotić is filed here under L by the clerk; the first letters read «Ker-», the ending «-patich»). Read at full page scale (the row is legible whole); the reading «Kerepatich» for Krmpotić is not firm — the second syllable is lost in the clerk's hand; no husband or children named|joanna-krmpotic-aged-60-died-senj-december-1844|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1833-35-children-of-formosus-oreskovich-clara-juliana-carolina|senj-death-1833-35-children-of-formosus-oreskovich-clara-juliana-carolina-line.jpg||Senj, 1833–1834 — Clara Orešković child of Formosus died Senj May 1833|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 469, right-hand page, O section, page 78, entries 5-7|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHC9|«1833 8° Maji. Clara Oreskovich, filia Formosi Oreskovich, 7, Consumptio, [—], ad S. Vitum, Laurentius Hesky Coop., N° 5». «1834 die 29° Augusti. Juliana Oreskovich filia legitima Formosi, 3, Diarrhea, [—], Ad S. Vitum, Bichanich Coop., N° 6». «1834 die 6° Octobris. Carolina Oreskovich filia legitima Formosi, 15 dierum, Convulsiones, Ad S. Vitum, Hesky Coop., N° 7». The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the O section, tabular, page 78, rows 5, 6 and 7. Read at full page scale (about 1x, the three rows legible whole); the father Formosus [Fortunatus?] Orešković is not otherwise placed. Three small children dead within eighteen months in one household|clara-oreskovic-child-of-formosus-died-senj-may-1833|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1826-27-andreas-oreskovich-aged-68-and-georgius-oreskovich-drowned-aged-20|senj-death-1826-27-andreas-oreskovich-aged-68-and-georgius-oreskovich-drowned-aged-20-line.jpg||Senj, 1826–1827 — Georgius Orešković drowned at sea aged 20 died Senj June 1827|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 468, right-hand page, O section, page 77, two lines under 1826–1827|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHXV|«3° Februarii obiit Andreas Ora Konich [Oreskovich?] St. provisus aetatis annorum 68» and «22 Junii obiit Georgius Oreskovich, et quidem submersus per infortunium in mari, aetatis annorum 20». Two one-line entries of the abbreviated 1820s lines of the O section, page 77 (under the headings «1826» and «1827»). Read at full page scale only (about 1x): the surname of the first is written in a hand that can be read «Oreskovich» or «Ora Konich», the second is clear. Not placed in any Orešković household of this archive|georgius-oreskovic-drowned-at-sea-aged-20-died-senj-june-1827|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1833-04-franciscus-ab-oresnovich-vice-colonel-aged-58|senj-death-1833-04-franciscus-ab-oresnovich-vice-colonel-aged-58-line.jpg||Senj, 7 April 1833 — Franciscus ab Oresnovich vice-colonel died Senj April 1833|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 469, right-hand page, O section, page 78, entry 4|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHC9|«1833 7° Aprilis. Dominus Vice-Colonellus et commendans Militaris Franciscus ab Oresnovich, 58, Hydrops, provisus, [ad S. Trinitatem? ad Marianum], Hesky Coop., N° 4». The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the O section, tabular, page 78, the fourth row. Read at full page scale only (about 1x): the surname is written «Oresnovich» (not Oreskovich), the rank «Vice-Colonellus et commendans Militaris» — an officer commanding a frontier regiment; buried in a different church from the common dead. A man born about 1775. The surname may be a clerk's slip for Orešković but this is not shown by the page|franciscus-ab-oresnovich-vice-colonel-died-senj-april-1833|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1836-37-franciscus-maria-ludomilla-children-of-formosus-oreskovich|senj-death-1836-37-franciscus-maria-ludomilla-children-of-formosus-oreskovich-line.jpg||Senj, 1836–1837 — Franciscus Orešković child of Formosus died Senj August 1836|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 470, left-hand page, O section, page 79, rows 1, 2 and 5|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHCW|«1836 die 26° Augusti. Franciscus Oreskovich filius legitimus Formosi, 1½, Convulsiones, [—], Ad S. Vitum, Bichanich Coop.» — «1836 die 27° Augusti. Maria Oreskovich filia legitima Formosi, 1/12, Convulsiones, Ad S. Vitum, Hesky Coop.» — «1837 die 15° Novembris. Ludomilla Oreskovich filia legitima Formosi, 4/12, Convulsio, Ad S. Vitum, Bichanich Coop.». The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the O section, tabular, page 79, rows 1, 2 and 5. Read at full page scale (about 1x, the rows legible whole). The twins' pair of deaths a day apart (a boy of 18 months and a girl of a month) look like the one household's two youngest children|franciscus-oreskovic-child-of-formosus-died-senj-august-1836|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1848-01-mathia-oreskovich-aged-80|senj-death-1848-01-mathia-oreskovich-aged-80-line.jpg||Senj, 20 January 1848 — Mathia Orešković aged 80 died Senj January 1848|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 470, right-hand page, O section, page 79, entry 27|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHCW|«1848 die 20 Januarii Segniae obiit. Mathia Oreskovich, 80, Marasmus senilis, Sacramentis morientium provisa, S. Vitus, Thomas Sladovich cooperator, N° 27». The death register of Senj, the O section, tabular, page 79, the ninth row. Read at full page scale (the row is legible whole). A woman (not a man: the clerk writes «Mathia» for a woman's name) born about 1768 whose husband and children are not named|mathia-oreskovic-aged-80-died-senj-january-1848|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-473L|senj-seen-473L-line.jpg||Senj, 1824–1827 — Pilepich (Pilipić) deaths, one-line entries|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 473, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHPQ|Page-scale read of the whole page: the one-line death entries of 1824–27 of the P section (page 80-81 of the Senj death register, Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848) name a Pilepich [«Pilepich»/«Pilipich»] eleven times: Matthaeus, son of Joannes Pilepich [1824]; Natalia Pilepich, aged 39 [1825]; Bartholomaeus Pilepich [1826, August]; Stellana, daughter of Joannes Pilepich, aged 2 [1826, September]; Stanislaus, son of Antonius Pilepich, aged 3 [1826, 8 November]; Francisca, daughter of Joannes Pilepich, aged 7 [days; 1827, 5 June]; Joannes Petrinovich 1827 and others of Petrinović/Pulanich. A Joannes Pilepich who loses three children in three years. Names and figures read at page scale only (the line crops did not take at zoom); Pilipić is a listed surname — to be re-read in quarter-width windows.||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-473R|senj-seen-473R-line.jpg||Senj, 1827–1830 — Pilepich (Pilipić) death, Pulanich and Petrovich|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 473, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHPQ|Page-scale read of the whole page (page 81 of the Senj death register): Helena, daughter of Franciscus Pavat? [1827, 5 September]; Matthaeus Petrinovich, aged 56 [1827]; Maria Petrich, aged 50 [1827, 28 December]; Justina Angela, an illegitimate daughter of Maria Pulanich [1828]; Margaritha, daughter of Joannes and Juliana Pulanich [1828]; Vidua Antonia Petrovich, aged 75 [1828]; Anna, daughter of Joannes Pilepich, aged 1 [14 September 1830] — a fourth Pilepich child of the Joannes Pilepich of 473L. Names read at page scale only.||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-472R|senj-seen-472R-line.jpg||Senj, 1820–1824 — P section one-line deaths (Petrovich, Pulanich, Pilepich)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 472, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHQY|Page-scale read of the whole page (page 80, the first page of the P section of the Senj death register): Petrovich, Pulanich, Perat, Pilepich entries of 1820–24: «Franciscus Petrovich filius Antonii» 1820, «Philippa filia Mathiae Petrovich, 7 days», «Vidua Magdalena Pulanich, 90», «Vidua Maria Petrovich, 82», «Vidua Michael Pasquan 85», «Antonius Perat 21», … Names read at page scale; no Papa/Papić, Pavelić, Prpić, Perković or Pilipić is read on the page at that scale.||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1831-32-catharina-widow-pilipich-aged-86-and-franciscus-son-of-andreas-pilipich-aged-6|senj-death-1831-32-catharina-widow-pilipich-aged-86-and-franciscus-son-of-andreas-pilipich-aged-6-line.jpg||Senj, 16 June 1831 and 5 January 1832 — Catharina widow Pilipić aged 86 died Senj June 1831|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 474, right-hand page, P section, page 82, rows 3 and 4|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHKD|«1831 16° Junii. Vidua Catharina Pillipich, 86, Debilitate, provisa, ad S. Vitum, Franich Coop., N° 3.» and «1832 5° Januarii. Franciscus Pillipich filius Andreae et Carolinae, 6, Consumptio, [—], ad S. Petrum, Maxim. Gjorgolich Coop., N° 4.» The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the P section, tabular, page 82, rows 3 and 4. Read at full page scale (about 1x, both rows legible whole); Pilipić is a listed surname and the row-4 target is a Pilipić bride of 1856–57: a Pilipić household of Senj in 1831–32 — an Andreas and Carolina Pilipić, a son of six, and a widow of 86 — is the earliest Pilipić found at Senj in this volume|catharina-widow-pilipic-aged-86-died-senj-june-1831|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1833-anna-daughter-of-vitus-pilipich-and-antonia-daughter-of-joannes-pilipich|senj-death-1833-anna-daughter-of-vitus-pilipich-and-antonia-daughter-of-joannes-pilipich-line.jpg||Senj, 28 September and 7 December 1833 — Anna Pilipić daughter of Vitus died Senj September 1833|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 475, left-hand page, P section, page 82 cont. (image 475L), rows 4 and 7|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LH6Q|«1833 28° Septembris. Anna filia Viti Pilipich, 12, Consumptio, provisa, ad S. Vitum, Fr[anich?] Coop.» and «1833 7° Decembris. Antonia filia Joannis Pilipich, 2, Convulsiones, —, ad S. Vitum, Hesky Coop.». The death register of Senj, the P section, tabular, page 82–83 (image 475 left page), rows 4 and 7 of the page. Read at full page scale (about 1x); the page also holds Catharina and Franciscus Pasquan, Petrus Georgii Pulanich, Anna Pasquan, Catharina Vankovich and a Victoria Pespik. Two more Pilipić households of Senj, Vitus and Joannes, in the autumn of 1833|anna-pilipic-daughter-of-vitus-died-senj-september-1833|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-475R|senj-seen-475R-line.jpg||Senj, 1834–1835 — Perpick? (Prpić?) death among Pulanich and Pasquan|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 475, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LH6Q|Page-scale read of the whole page (page 83 of the Senj death register, P section, tabular): «1834 6° Octobris. Andreas Perpick [?], 70, Debilitas virium, provisus, Ad S. Vitum, Bichanich Coop., N° 27» — the surname is written «Perpick»/«Cerpick», a possible Perpić/Prpić; surrounding entries Planinach Paulus 40, Pulanich Paulus 60, Pavlovich Rosalia 43, Pulanich Margaritha 70, Petranovich Catharina 64, Persich Eduardus 1½, Pasquan Mathias 2½, Pomajevich Franciscus 4, Pesil? Maria 18 days, Cimper? Mathia vidua 70. Names read at page scale only.||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-474R|senj-seen-474R-line.jpg||Senj, 1831–1833 — P section rows (Pilipić rows recorded separately)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 474, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHKD|Page-scale read of the whole page (page 82 of the Senj death register): the page's Pilipić rows are recorded as their own snapshot; the other rows are Natalis, son of Antonius Persen (a magistrate's chancellor), Philippus, son of Antonius Pulanich, Michael Pe[k]ich 53, Georgius Pauss (a retired customs officer) 82, Aloysius Perma? 75, Rocatus? son of Joannes Petmajevich 7, Vidua Anna Pasquan 78, Marcus Pulanich 45, Vidua Barbara Pe[...]ich 53. Names read at page scale only.||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1836-09-maria-widow-perpich-aged-63|senj-death-1836-09-maria-widow-perpich-aged-63-line.jpg||Senj, 22 September 1836 — Maria Perpić widow aged 63 died Senj September 1836|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 476, right-hand page, P section, page 84, entry 44|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHVX|«1836 die 22° Septembris. Maria Vidua Perpich, 63, Profusio alvi, provisa, Ad S. Vitum, Hesky Coop., N° 44.» The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the P section, tabular, page 84, the first row. Read at full page scale (about 1x, the row legible whole). A Perpić [Prpić in the modern spelling; Perpich, Perpić, Prpić are on the family list] widow, born about 1773; no husband or children named|maria-perpic-widow-aged-63-died-senj-september-1836|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1837-03-apollonia-widow-perpich-aged-45-died-suddenly|senj-death-1837-03-apollonia-widow-perpich-aged-45-died-suddenly-line.jpg||Senj, 25 March 1837 — Apollonia Perpić widow aged 45 died suddenly Senj March 1837|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 476, right-hand page, P section, page 84, entry 46|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHVX|«1837 die 25° Martii. Apollonia Vidua Perpich inopinate mortua, 45, Apoplexia, [—], Ad S. Vitum, Hesky Coop., N° 46.» The death register of Senj, the P section, tabular, page 84, the third row. Read at full page scale (the row is legible whole); a second Perpić widow on one page, a young one (born about 1792), who died without the sacraments|apollonia-perpic-widow-aged-45-died-suddenly-senj-march-1837|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1839-04-franciscus-pilipovich-aged-50|senj-death-1839-04-franciscus-pilipovich-aged-50-line.jpg||Senj, 29 April 1839 — Franciscus Pilipović aged 50 died Senj April 1839|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 477, left-hand page, P section, page 85 (image 477L), seventh row|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHD8|«1839 die 29° Aprilis. Franciscus Pilipovich, 50, Apoplexia, Sacramentis provisus, Ad Cometerium S. Viti, Petrus Dorrenich Coop.» The death register of Senj, the P section, tabular, page 85 (image 477 left page), the seventh row. Read at full page scale (the row is legible whole); Pilipović, a name close to the listed Pilipić / Pilepich, born about 1789|franciscus-pilipovic-aged-50-died-senj-april-1839|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1840-03-franciscus-perpich-aged-48|senj-death-1840-03-franciscus-perpich-aged-48-line.jpg||Senj, 6 March 1840 — Franciscus Perpić aged 48 died Senj March 1840|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 477, right-hand page, P section, page 85, entry 70|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHD8|«1840 die 6° Martii obiit. Franciscus Perpich, 48, Inflammatio pulmonum, provisus, Ad S. Vitum, Petrus Dorrenich Coop., N° 70.» The death register of Senj, the P section, tabular, page 85, the eighth row. Read at full page scale (the row is legible whole). A man born about 1792 whose surname is written like the two Perpić widows of 1836 and 1837 on the page before; a Perpić household at Senj, 1836–40|franciscus-perpic-aged-48-died-senj-march-1840|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1841-04-maria-perpich-aged-48-and-1841-06-vitus-perpich-aged-2|senj-death-1841-04-maria-perpich-aged-48-and-1841-06-vitus-perpich-aged-2-line.jpg||Senj, 20 April and 8 June 1841 — Maria Perpić aged 48 died Senj April 1841|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 478, right-hand page, P section, page 86, entries 83 and 84|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LH49|«1841 Die 20 Aprilis Segniae obiit. Maria Perpich, 48, Hydrops sanguinosus?, Omnibus Sacramentis morientium provisa, [In] Ecclesia Cath. [?], Petrus Dorrenich Coop., N° 83» and «1841 Die 8 Junii Segniae obiit. Vitus Perpich filius legitimus Catholicus, 2, Febris infantum, —, ad S. Vitum, Petrus Dorrenich Coop., N° 84». The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the P section, tabular, page 86, the first two rows. Read at full page scale (about 1x, both rows legible whole). A woman of 48 (born about 1793) and a little boy of two: possibly mother and child, though no relationship is written; Perpich is the spelling of the widows of 1836–37 and Franciscus of 1840 on pages 84–85|maria-perpic-aged-48-died-senj-april-1841|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1842-07-josephus-perpich-aged-61-confiniarius|senj-death-1842-07-josephus-perpich-aged-61-confiniarius-line.jpg||Senj, 31 July 1842 — Josephus Perpić frontier soldier aged 61 died Senj July 1842|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 479, left-hand page, P section, image 479L, entry 93|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LHWB|«1842 Die 31 Julii Segniae obiit, [ex] Slocomio?. Josephus Perpich Confiniarius Centuriae Hergotalak? [Ergolatich?] Regim. Ogul. N° 3. Catholicus, 61, Febris hectica, Provisus, ad S. Vitum, Ant. Lucich Coop., N° 93». The death register of Senj, the P section, tabular, page 86 cont. (image 479 left page), the second row. Read at full page scale (the row is legible whole except the name of the company); a Perpich of a frontier-regiment company, born about 1781|josephus-perpic-frontier-soldier-aged-61-died-senj-july-1842|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1844-12-augustinus-perpic-aged-1|senj-death-1844-12-augustinus-perpic-aged-1-line.jpg||Senj, 5 December 1844 — Augustinus Perpić infant died Senj December 1844|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 479, right-hand page, P section, page 87, entry 109|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LHWB|«1844 Die 5° [Decembris] Segniae obiit. Augustinus Perpic, 1, Spasmus, —, Sanctus Vitus, Hippolytus Domazetovich? Coop., N° 109». The death register of Senj, the P section, tabular, page 87, the third row from the bottom. Read at full page scale (the row is legible whole); no parents named|augustinus-perpic-infant-died-senj-december-1844|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1847-01-maria-pilepich-aged-9-months-and-1847-02-antonia-perpich-aged-35|senj-death-1847-01-maria-pilepich-aged-9-months-and-1847-02-antonia-perpich-aged-35-line.jpg||Senj, 28 January and [February?] 1847 — Maria Pilipić infant died Senj January 1847|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 482, left-hand page, P section, image 482L, entries 135 and 136|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LH4V|«1847 die 28 Januarii Segniae obiit. Maria Pilepich, 9 [mensium], Spasmus, —, Sct. Vitus, Gladovich Coop., N° 135» and «1847 die [?] Februarii Segniae obiit. Antonia Perpich [Per-/-pich], 35, Phthisis pulmonalis, Sacramentis morientium provisa, Sct. Vitus, Gladovich Coop., N° 136». The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the P section, tabular, page 88–89 (image 482 left page), the fourth and fifth rows. Read at full page scale (about 1x); the spellings are «Pilepich» for the infant (the Pilipić of the 1820s–30s lines) and «Per-pich» with the hyphen of a line break for the woman. A Pilipić child and a Perpić woman on one page|maria-pilipic-infant-died-senj-january-1847,antonia-perpic-aged-35-died-senj-february-1847|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
