senj-death-1820-03-joannes-spal-aged-80|senj-death-1820-03-joannes-spal-aged-80-line.jpg||Senj, [?] 1820 — Joannes Špalj Spal aged 80 died Senj 1820|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 490, right-hand page, S section, page 95, second dated line of 1820|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LH43|«[?] Martii [1820] obiit Joannes Vidua? Spal. S. provisus annorum circiter — [80]». One of the abbreviated one-line death entries of 1820 (the first page of the S section, page 95 of the Senj death register, Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848): date, «obiit», the name, the sacraments, the age; the age in the right margin reads «80». Read at full page scale (about 1x); the first word after the name is not firm («Vidua» would make the name a woman's, but the register gives no surname to a widow in this period only in the form «Vidua» before the name). Špalj is a listed surname; the spelling here is «Spal»|joannes-spalj-spal-aged-80-died-senj-1820|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1828-11-joannes-spal|senj-death-1828-11-joannes-spal-line.jpg||Senj, 27 November 1828 — Joannes Špalj Spal died Senj November 1828|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 491, right-hand page, S section, page 96, a line near the foot (27 November 1828)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHKN|«27 Novembris [1828] obiit Joannes Spal, S. provisus, aetatis annorum circiter [—]». One of the abbreviated one-line death entries of the late 1820s (page 96 of the Senj death register, the S section), the age figure is lost to the right edge of the page. Read at full page scale only (about 1x); the same surname «Spal» as the Joannes Spal of 1820 on the previous page — the second Špalj of the S section|joannes-spalj-spal-died-senj-november-1828|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1830-12-antonia-sojat-aged-95|senj-death-1830-12-antonia-sojat-aged-95-line.jpg||Senj, 18 December 1830 — Antonia Šojat aged 95 died Senj December 1830|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 492, left-hand page, S section, page 96, last-but-one dated line of 1830|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LH8L|«18 Decembris [1830] obiit Antonia Sojat, S. provisa, annorum circiter 95». One of the abbreviated one-line death entries of 1830 (page 96–97, the S section of the Senj death register, Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848); the age figure in the right margin is «95». Read at full page scale (about 1x, the line legible whole). Šojat is a listed surname (the Šojat grooms of Senj of 1745 and 1786, images 9–206); a woman born about 1735, the generation of the 1745 and 1786 Šojat marriages' families — no husband or children named|antonia-sojat-aged-95-died-senj-december-1830|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1831-08-simon-smojver-aged-70|senj-death-1831-08-simon-smojver-aged-70-line.jpg||Senj, 1 August 1831 — Simon Smojver aged 70 died Senj August 1831|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 492, right-hand page, S section, page 97, entry 6|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LH8L|«1831 1ma Augusti. Simon Smojver, Catholicus, 70, Debilitas, provisus, ad S. Vitum, Hieron. Franich Coop., N° 6.» The death register of Senj (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848), the S section, tabular, page 97 (image 492 right page), the sixth row. Read at full page scale (about 1x, the row is legible whole; the surname is written «Smojver»). A Simon Smojver at Senj, born about 1761; the Smojver households of this archive are at Karlobag (Vitus Smojver, baptised 1780; the Smojver–Bacchi marriage of 1774) and Jablanac — see the Smojver brides of 1837–45 on images 349L and 350R|simon-smojver-aged-70-died-senj-august-1831|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1831-11-hellena-spalj-aged-79|senj-death-1831-11-hellena-spalj-aged-79-line.jpg||Senj, 23 November 1831 — Hellena Špalj aged 79 died Senj November 1831|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 492, right-hand page, S section, page 97, entry 8|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LH8L|«1831 23 Novembris. Hellena Spalj, 79, Debilitate, provisa, ad S. Vitum, Maxim. Gjorgolich Coop., N° 8.» The death register of Senj, the S section, tabular, page 97, the eighth row. Read at full page scale (about 1x, the row is legible whole). Špalj is a listed surname; a woman born about 1752; the Joannes Spal of 1820 and 1828 (images 490R, 491R) is probably her husband or son|hellena-spalj-aged-79-died-senj-november-1831|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1836-08-catharina-widow-spalj-aged-78|senj-death-1836-08-catharina-widow-spalj-aged-78-line.jpg||Senj, 2 August 1836 — Catharina Špalj widow aged 78 died Senj August 1836|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 495, right-hand page, page 100, entry 57|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LH8B|«1836 die 2da Augusti. Catharina Vidua Spalj, 78, Inventa est in universum (?) mortua [found dead], ad S. Vitum, Hesky Coop., N° 57.» The death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum 1833–), page 100 (image 495 right page), entry 57. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the surname «Spalj» and the age «78» legible; the cause column is hard to read and is given with a query). Špalj is a listed surname; a widow born about 1758, a generation after the Špalj bride of 1820 and the Spal deaths of 1820, 1828 and 1831|catharina-spalj-widow-aged-78-died-senj-august-1836|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1838-12-laurentius-widower-sojat-aged-80|senj-death-1838-12-laurentius-widower-sojat-aged-80-line.jpg||Senj, 6 December 1838 — Laurentius Šojat widower aged 80 died Senj December 1838|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 497, left-hand page, first entry of the left page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHCK|«1838 die 6ta Decembris. Laurentius Vidus Sojat, 80, Senium, Sacramentis provisus, Ad Cemeterium S. Viti, Laurentius Hesky 1 Cooperator.» The death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum 1833–), image 497 left page, first entry. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the surname «Sojat» and the age «80» legible, the «Vidus» abbreviation read as widower). Šojat is a listed surname (the Šojat grooms of 1745 and 1786); a man born about 1758, a generation after the 1745 marriage and contemporary with the 1786 one — no wife or children named|laurentius-sojat-widower-aged-80-died-senj-december-1838|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1841-02-gregorius-smojver-aged-26|senj-death-1841-02-gregorius-smojver-aged-26-line.jpg||Senj, 20 February 1841 — Gregorius Smojver aged 26 died Senj February 1841|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 498, right-hand page, page 103, entry 129|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHXW|«1841 Die 20 Februarii obiit Gregorius Smojver [«Smoiver»], 26, Phtysis pulmonalis, provisus, ad S. Vitum, Petrus Dorrenich [Korrenich] Cooperator, N° 129.» Death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum), page 103 (image 498 right page), entry 129; a note «uxoratus» (married) follows the name. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the surname written «Smoiver»/«Smojver», the age «26» and the cause legible; the note on his status, «uxoratus», is read with a query). A Smojver man born about 1815, married; the same register has Bartholomeus Smo[kvina?] 54 in January 1841 (not recorded) and the Smojver brides of 1837–45 (images 349L, 350R)|gregorius-smojver-aged-26-died-senj-february-1841|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1846-06-mikael-sojat-aged-51|senj-death-1846-06-mikael-sojat-aged-51-line.jpg||Senj, 15 June 1846 — Michael Šojat aged 51 died Senj June 1846|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 503, left-hand page, entry 171|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LH4Z|«1846 die 15 Junii Segniae obiit. Mikael Sojat, 51, Phtisis pulmonalis, Sacramentis morientium provisus, S. Vitus, Sladovich Coop. [Tomas Sladovich], N° 171.» Death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum), image 503 left page, entry 171. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the surname «Sojat», the age «51» and the cause legible). Šojat is a listed surname; a man born about 1795, no wife or children named|michael-sojat-aged-51-died-senj-june-1846|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-505R-tomljanovich|senj-seen-505R-tomljanovich-line.jpg||Death register 1832: Vidua Clara Tomljanovich (?) 31 March 1832|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 505, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHSQ|Page 109 (image 505 right), entry 3 of 1832: «Vidua Clara Tom[lj]anovich, coniux olim defuncti, Locumis: Thoma Tom[lj]anovich», age written «Arbo»?, died of consumption (consumatio), with the sacraments, buried ad S. Petrum. Read at page scale only (the «lj» is not certain; it may be «Tomsanovich» or «Tomjanovich») — recorded as a seen row, not a found person, until a re-read at higher zoom settles the spelling. Tomljanović is a listed surname (the Tomljanović grooms of 1853 and 1858). The T section here begins on image 504R with one-line entries 1820–30 for Tintor, Thian [Tijan], Trinaistich, Tomasich, Tomich — none Tomljanović. Also 505R top: «Gregorius filius Antonii Tom...novich et ejus legitimae conjugis ...», February 1831, unread beyond that||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1834-02-mattia-daughter-of-matthias-tomljanovich-one-day|senj-death-1834-02-mattia-daughter-of-matthias-tomljanovich-one-day-line.jpg||Senj, 25 February 1834 — Mattia Tomljanović infant died Senj February 1834|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 506, right-hand page, page 110, entry 23|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LH72|«1834 die 25 Februarii. Mattia Tomljanovich filia legitima Matthiae, unius diei, Debilitas virium, —, ad S. Vitum, Cherzgoller? Coop., N° 23.» Death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum), page 110 (image 506 right page), entry 23. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name and the «lj» in «Tomljanovich» legible). A daughter of a Matthias Tomljanović of Senj, born and died on the same day in February 1834; the same page has Maria, widow Tomljanović, aged 60, of April 1834 (entry 24); compare Lucas, son of Matthias Tomljanović, 1842 (image 507R)|mattia-tomljanovic-infant-died-senj-february-1834|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1834-04-maria-widow-tomljanovich-aged-60|senj-death-1834-04-maria-widow-tomljanovich-aged-60-line.jpg||Senj, 8 April 1834 — Maria Tomljanović widow aged 60 died Senj April 1834|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 506, right-hand page, page 110, entry 24|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LH72|«1834 die 8 Aprilis. Maria Vidua Tomljanovich, 60, Consumatio, provisa, ad S. Vitum, Heski Coop., N° 24.» Death register of Senj, page 110 (image 506 right page), entry 24, immediately below the one-day-old Mattia Tomljanović. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the surname written across the line break «Tom- / ljanovich»). A widow born about 1774; the grandmother or mother in the same house as Matthias Tomljanović, whose child died six weeks earlier, is a reading only|maria-tomljanovic-widow-aged-60-died-senj-april-1834|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1842-02-lucas-son-of-matthias-tomljanovich-aged-4-months|senj-death-1842-02-lucas-son-of-matthias-tomljanovich-aged-4-months-line.jpg||Senj, 22 February 1842 — Lucas Tomljanović infant died Senj February 1842|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 507, right-hand page, page 111, entry 48|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4Y6|«1842 Die 22 Februarii Segniae expiravit. Lucas filius Mathiae Tomljanovich, Mensium 4, Spasmus, ad S. Vitum, Petrus Dorrenich Cooperator, N° 48.» Death register of Senj, page 111 (image 507 right page), entry 48. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name legible). A son of Matthias Tomljanović, born about October 1841 — the same father as the infant Mattia (a daughter) of 1834 on image 506R is only a reading, the Christian name being common. Compare the Tomljanović grooms of Senj of 1853 and 1858|lucas-tomljanovic-infant-died-senj-february-1842|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1843-04-mathias-tomljanovich-aged-3|senj-death-1843-04-mathias-tomljanovich-aged-3-line.jpg||Senj, 19 April 1843 — Mathias Tomljanović infant died Senj April 1843|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 508, left-hand page, entry 56|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHFX|«1843 Die 19 Aprilis Segniae expiravit. Mathias Tomljanovich, 3, Tabes infantum, —, ad S. Vitum, Petrus Dorrenich Cooperator, N° 56.» Death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum), image 508 left page, entry 56. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name legible, the age unit not given — the cause «tabes infantum» says an infant). Possibly the brother of Lucas Tomljanović of February 1842 (image 507R) and a child of the same Matthias — a reading, not a statement of the page|mathias-tomljanovic-infant-died-senj-april-1843|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1846-12-margaritha-tomljanovich-aged-9|senj-death-1846-12-margaritha-tomljanovich-aged-9-line.jpg||Senj, 6 December 1846 — Margaritha Tomljanović aged 9 died Senj December 1846|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 509, left-hand page, third entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHW2|«1846 die 6 10bris Segniae obiit. Tomljanovich Margaritha, 9, Scrophulosis, —, S. Vitus, Sladovich Cooperator.» Death register of Senj, image 509 left page, third entry. Read at full page scale (about 1x; surname and age legible). The date's month is written «10bris» — read as December; it follows entries of 27 October (?) and 6 December of the same page, in order. A girl of nine, born about 1837|margaritha-tomljanovic-aged-9-died-senj-december-1846|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1847-12-virginia-tomljanovich-aged-4|senj-death-1847-12-virginia-tomljanovich-aged-4-line.jpg||Senj, 5 December 1847 — Virginia Tomljanović aged 4 died Senj December 1847|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 509, left-hand page, fifth entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHW2|«1847 die 5 Decembris Segniae obiit. Virginia Tomljanovich, 4, pneumonitis, S. Vitus, Thomas Sladovich Cooperator.» Death register of Senj, image 509 left page, fifth entry. Read at full page scale (about 1x; surname legible with the «lj»). A girl of four, born about 1843|virginia-tomljanovic-aged-4-died-senj-december-1847|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1848-maria-tomljanovich-aged-57|senj-death-1848-maria-tomljanovich-aged-57-line.jpg||Senj, 1848 (day 22; month abbreviated) — Maria Tomljanović aged 57 died Senj 1848|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 509, right-hand page, page 113, entry 85|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHW2|«1848 die 22 ?bris Segniae obiit. Maria Tomljanovich, 57, febris dejiciens, Sacramentis morientium provisa, Sanctus Vitus, Thomas Sladovich Cooperator, N° 85.» Death register of Senj (page 113), image 509 right page, last entry. Read at full page scale (about 1x). The month is an abbreviation ending «-bris» and is not read with certainty (7bris/8bris/9bris/10bris are all possible); it follows entries of May 1848, so it is September to December 1848. A woman born about 1791; compare Maria, widow Tomljanović, aged 60, 1834 (image 506R)|maria-tomljanovic-aged-57-died-senj-1848|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1824-05-widow-vukelich|senj-death-1824-05-widow-vukelich-line.jpg||Senj, 10 May 1824 — Widow Vukelić aged 70 died Senj May 1824|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 511, right-hand page, V section, page 115, last-but-one line (1824)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4RS|«10 Maji obiit Vidua Ursula? Vukelich, Sa. provisa, aetatis annorum circiter 70.» One of the abbreviated one-line death entries of the V section of the Senj death register (page 115, image 511 right page), the last-but-one line. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the surname «Vukelich» legible, the widow's Christian name and the age figure read with a query). A woman born about 1754|widow-vukelic-aged-70-died-senj-may-1824|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1824-08-joannes-son-of-petrus-vukelich|senj-death-1824-08-joannes-son-of-petrus-vukelich-line.jpg||Senj, 12 August 1824 — Joannes Vukelić son of Petrus died Senj August 1824|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 511, right-hand page, V section, page 115, last line (1824)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4RS|«12 Augusti obiit Joannes Vukelich filius Dni Petri Vukelich, Sa. provisus, qui peractus ad Ecclesiam St. Ambrosii sepultus est, aetatis annorum circiter 22.» The last line of the V section on page 115 (image 511 right page). Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the surname written twice, «Vukelich», and the age «22» legible). A young man born about 1802, son of Petrus Vukelić («Dominus» — a man of standing); the Vukelić grooms and brides of Senj 1826–52 are in the marriage register (images 9–350)|joannes-vukelic-son-of-petrus-died-senj-august-1824|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1825-06-dominus-petrus-vukelich-aged-70|senj-death-1825-06-dominus-petrus-vukelich-aged-70-line.jpg||Senj, 4 June 1825 — Petrus Vukelić aged 70 died Senj June 1825|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 512, left-hand page, V section, page 114, 1825|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LHMB|«4° Junii [1825] obiit Dnus Petrus Vukelich, Sa. provisus, aetatis annorum [circiter 70].» An abbreviated one-line death entry of the V section of the Senj death register (page 114, image 512 left page, the year 1825 heading above it). Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the title «Dnus» and the surname legible; the age 70 in the right margin). He is the «Dominus Petrus Vukelich» whose son Joannes, aged about 22, died on 12 August 1824 (image 511R); born about 1755|petrus-vukelic-aged-70-died-senj-june-1825|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1826-07-thomas-son-of-georgius-vukelich-aged-8-months|senj-death-1826-07-thomas-son-of-georgius-vukelich-aged-8-months-line.jpg||Senj, 26 July 1826 — Thomas Vukelić infant died Senj July 1826|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 512, left-hand page, V section, page 114, 1826|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LHMB|«26 Julii [1826] obiit Thomas filius Georgii Vukelich, aetatis Mensium Octo.» An abbreviated one-line death entry of the V section of the Senj death register (page 114, image 512 left page). Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the father's name and the age in months legible). A Georgius Vukelić at Senj with a daughter, aged 1½, who died on 10 September 1825 (the previous line group); so two children of one Georgius within a year, a reading|thomas-vukelic-infant-died-senj-july-1826|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1827-01-lucas-vukelich|senj-death-1827-01-lucas-vukelich-line.jpg||Senj, 10 January 1827 — Lucas Vukelić died Senj January 1827|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 512, left-hand page, V section, page 114, 1827|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LHMB|«10 Januarii [1827] obiit Lucas Vukelich, Sa. provisus, exportatus vero fuit idem praesepultus? ad S. Georgium [?].» An abbreviated one-line death entry of the V section of the Senj death register (page 114, image 512 left page). Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x): the name «Lucas Vukelich» is legible; the age is not read, and the note on the body being carried to a church is read with a query|lucas-vukelic-died-senj-january-1827|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1828-05-juliana-daughter-of-dr-stephanus-vukelich|senj-death-1828-05-juliana-daughter-of-dr-stephanus-vukelich-line.jpg||Senj, 19 May 1828 — Juliana Vukelić infant died Senj May 1828|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 512, left-hand page, V section, page 114, 1828|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LHMB|«19° Maji [1828] obiit Juliana filia Dni Stephani Vukeleti? [Vukelich] Medici civitatis, dierum 6.» An abbreviated one-line death entry of the V section of the Senj death register (page 114, image 512 left page). Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the surname written «Vukelich»/«Vukeleti» and the words «Medici civitatis» legible, the age «dierum 6» in the margin). A town physician Stephanus Vukelić at Senj in 1828|juliana-vukelic-infant-died-senj-may-1828|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1834-06-ursula-daughter-of-laurentius-vukelich-aged-12|senj-death-1834-06-ursula-daughter-of-laurentius-vukelich-aged-12-line.jpg||Senj, 22 June 1834 — Ursula Vukelić aged 12 died Senj June 1834|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 513, right-hand page, page 117, entry 11|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHH7|«1834 die 22 Junii. Ursula Vukelich filia legitima Laurentii, 12, Consumatio, provisa, Ad S. Vitum, Hesky Cooperator, N° 11.» Death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum), page 117, image 513 right page, entry 11. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the whole row clearly legible). A girl of twelve born about 1822, daughter of a Laurentius Vukelić|ursula-vukelic-aged-12-died-senj-june-1834|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1836-01-joannes-vukelich-aged-77|senj-death-1836-01-joannes-vukelich-aged-77-line.jpg||Senj, 9 January 1836 — Joannes Vukelić aged 77 died Senj January 1836|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 513, right-hand page, page 117, entry 19|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHH7|«1836 die 9 Januarii. Joannes Vukelich, 77, Retentio urinae, provisus, Ad S. Petrum, Hesky Cooperator, N° 19.» Death register of Senj, page 117, image 513 right page, entry 19. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the row clearly legible). A man born about 1759; the entry below it records Maria, widow Vukelić, aged 70, five days later|joannes-vukelic-aged-77-died-senj-january-1836|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1836-01-maria-widow-vukelich-aged-70|senj-death-1836-01-maria-widow-vukelich-aged-70-line.jpg||Senj, 14 January 1836 — Maria Vukelić widow aged 70 died Senj January 1836|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 513, right-hand page, page 117, entry 20|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHH7|«1836 die 14° Januarii. Maria Vidua Vukelich, 70, Phthisis, provisa, Ad S. Petrum, Bichanich Cooperator, N° 20.» Death register of Senj, page 117, image 513 right page, entry 20. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the row clearly legible). A widow born about 1766; whether she is the widow of the Joannes Vukelić who died five days earlier (entry 19, aged 77) is not stated|maria-vukelic-widow-aged-70-died-senj-january-1836|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1836-08-lucas-vukelich-of-st-georgius-aged-22|senj-death-1836-08-lucas-vukelich-of-st-georgius-aged-22-line.jpg||Senj, 9 August 1836 — Lucas Vukelić aged 22 died Senj August 1836|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 514, left-hand page, entry 23|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LH42|«1836 die 9° Augusti. Lucas Vukelich, Parochianus S. Georgii, 22, Phthisis, provisus, Ad S. Vitum, Hesky Cooperator, N° 23.» Death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum), image 514 left page (page 117 verso), entry 23. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the row clearly legible). A young man born about 1814, of the parish of St George (a church in the Senj area); see the infant Joannes, son of a Lucas and Cecilia Vukelić, who died seventeen days later (entry 25)|lucas-vukelic-aged-22-died-senj-august-1836|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1836-08-joannes-son-of-lucas-and-cecilia-vukelich-aged-5-days|senj-death-1836-08-joannes-son-of-lucas-and-cecilia-vukelich-aged-5-days-line.jpg||Senj, 26 August 1836 — Joannes Vukelić infant died Senj August 1836|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 514, left-hand page, entry 25|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LH42|«1836 die 26° Augusti. Joannes Vukelich filius legitimus Lucae [et] Ceciliae Vukelich, 5 Dierum, Convulsiones, Ad S. Vitum, Hesky Cooperator, N° 25.» Death register of Senj, image 514 left page, entry 25. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the parents' names are read as «Lucae et Ceciliae» with a query on the conjunction). A child of five days, born about 21 August 1836, a son of the Lucas Vukelić who died on 9 August 1836, seventeen days earlier (entry 23) — the father's name makes it likely, the register does not say it|joannes-vukelic-infant-died-senj-august-1836|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1844-01-josephus-gasparus-vukelich-aged-8-days|senj-death-1844-01-josephus-gasparus-vukelich-aged-8-days-line.jpg||Senj, 13 January 1844 — Josephus Gasparus Vukelić infant died Senj January 1844|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 515, right-hand page, page 119, entry 59|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4YC|«1844 Die 13° Januarii Segniae expiravit. Josephus Gasparus filius Dni? Vukelich, Dierum 8, Spasmus, Ad S. Vitum, Hippolytus Ivancich? Cooperator, N° 59.» Death register of Senj, page 119, image 515 right page, entry 59. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name and surname clear, the father's title and the curate's name less so). The next entry, 10 February 1844, is Anna Vukelić, aged 34 — she may be the infant's mother, a reading only|josephus-gasparus-vukelic-infant-died-senj-january-1844|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1844-02-anna-vukelich-aged-34|senj-death-1844-02-anna-vukelich-aged-34-line.jpg||Senj, 10 February 1844 — Anna Vukelić aged 34 died Senj February 1844|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 515, right-hand page, page 119, entry 60|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4YC|«1844 Die 10° Februarii Segniae obiit. Anna Vukelich, 34, Febris dejiciens, Sacramentis morientium provisa, Ad S. Vitum, Petrus Dorrenich Cooperator, N° 60.» Death register of Senj, page 119, image 515 right page, entry 60, the line below Josephus Gasparus Vukelić, 8 days old, of 13 January. Read at full page scale (about 1x). A woman born about 1810; whether she is the infant's mother is not stated|anna-vukelic-aged-34-died-senj-february-1844|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-514R-vukelich-catharina|senj-seen-514R-vukelich-catharina-line.jpg||Death register 1840: Catharina Vidua V[u]kelich? (70) 20 February 1840|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 514, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LH42|Page 118, image 514 right page, entry 42: «1840 Die 20 Februarii Segniae obiit. Catharina Vidua Vef?c-lich, Segniensis, Catholica, 70, Hydrops, Sacramentis Moriaturn non nunciatis improvisam mortem, ad S. Vitum, Antonius Suscich? Coop., N° 42.» The surname is written in a hand that may be Vukelich or Veselich or Vekelich and is not read with certainty at the zoom used (about 3x of the line) — a seen row, not a found person, to be re-read with the Vukelić of the 1830s. Entry 43, a day later and a few lines down: Franciscus, son of Philippus Veljačić?, 4, none core||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1847-06-joannes-vukellich-aged-67|senj-death-1847-06-joannes-vukellich-aged-67-line.jpg||Senj, 22 June 1847 — Joannes Vukelić aged 67 died Senj June 1847|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 516, right-hand page, page 120, entry 79|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHMQ|«1847 die 22 Junii Segniae obiit. Vukellich Joannes, 67, pneumonia, Sacramentis morientium provisus, S. Vitus, Tomas Sladovich Cooperator, N° 79.» Death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum), page 120, image 516 right page, entry 79. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the surname written «Vukellich», the age and the cause legible). A man born about 1780; the surname is written before the Christian name here, as in the next entry|joannes-vukelic-aged-67-died-senj-june-1847|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1847-10-rosalia-vukellich-aged-18|senj-death-1847-10-rosalia-vukellich-aged-18-line.jpg||Senj, 7 October 1847 — Rosalia Vukelić aged 18 died Senj October 1847|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 516, right-hand page, page 120, entry 80|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHMQ|«1847 die 7° Octobris Segniae obiit. Vukellich Rosalia, 18, Phthisis, Sacramentis morientium provisa, S. Vitus, Tomas Sladovich Cooperator, N° 80.» Death register of Senj, page 120, image 516 right page, entry 80, the line below Joannes Vukelić of 22 June. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the surname, the age 18 and the cause legible; the day «7» read with a query). A girl born about 1829|rosalia-vukelic-aged-18-died-senj-october-1847|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1848-05-matho-zuppan-aged-82|senj-death-1848-05-matho-zuppan-aged-82-line.jpg||Senj, 14 May 1848 — Mathias Župan aged 82 died Senj May 1848|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 519, left-hand page, Z section, fifth entry of the tabular page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LHMJ|«1848 die 14 Maji Segniae obiit. Matho Zuppan, 82, marasmus senilis, Sacramentis morientium provisus, S. Vitus, Tomas Sladovich Cooperator, N° 5.» Death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum), Z section, image 519 left page, fifth entry. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, the age 82 and the cause legible). «Zuppan» is the Italianate spelling of Župan, a listed surname; a man born about 1766, no wife or children named. The rest of the Z section (images 518R–519L: Zagar, Zarkovich, Zankovich, Zivkovich, Zettar) has no other core name|mathias-zupan-aged-82-died-senj-may-1848|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1835-05-joanna-zuppan-aged-4-days|senj-death-1835-05-joanna-zuppan-aged-4-days-line.jpg||Senj, 9 May 1835 — Joanna Župan infant died Senj May 1835|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 521, left-hand page, Z section, entry 8|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4TC|«1835 die 9° Maji. Joanna Zuppan [«Zupsan»?], 4 Dierum, Convulsiones, —, Ad S. Vitum, Bichanich Cooperator, N° 8.» Death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum), Z section, page 122 verso, image 521 left page, entry 8. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the surname's second letters are not entirely clear — «Zuppan» or «Zupsan» — and the reading rests on the next entries, which are clearly Zuppan). An infant of four days|joanna-zupan-infant-died-senj-may-1835|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1836-08-catharina-widow-zuppan-aged-70|senj-death-1836-08-catharina-widow-zuppan-aged-70-line.jpg||Senj, 21 August 1836 — Catharina Župan widow aged 70 died Senj August 1836|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 521, left-hand page, Z section, entry 10|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4TC|«1836 die 21° Augusti. Catharina Zuppan, Vidua, 70, Hydrops, provisa, Ad S. Vitum, Bichanich Cooperator, N° 10.» Death register of Senj, Z section, image 521 left page, last entry. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the whole row legible). A widow born about 1766; compare Matho (Mathias) Zuppan, aged 82, died 1848 (image 519L) — the register does not link them|catharina-zupan-widow-aged-70-died-senj-august-1836|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1848-02-zuppan-woman-aged-66|senj-death-1848-02-zuppan-woman-aged-66-line.jpg||Senj, 2 February 1848 (day faint) — Zuppan woman aged 66 died Senj February 1848|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 523, left-hand page, Z section, fourth entry of the tabular page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHM5|«1848 die 2? Februarii Segniae obiit. [Virginia?] Zuppan, 66, marasmus senilis, Sacramentis morientium provisa, [S. Vitus, Tomas Sladovich Cooperator], N° 43.» Death register of Senj (Matricula Defunctorum), Z section, image 523 left page, fourth entry. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x): the surname «Zuppan» and the age «66» are legible; the Christian name, the day of the month and the burial columns are faint (a fading line of the page) and are not read with certainty. A woman born about 1782; compare the Zuppan deaths of Catharina (1836) and Joanna (1835) on image 521L and Matho (1848) on 519L|zuppan-woman-aged-66-died-senj-february-1848|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1849-03-ignatz-pilepich-aged-5-months|senj-death-1849-03-ignatz-pilepich-aged-5-months-line.jpg||Senj, 26 March 1849 — Ignatz Pilipić infant died Senj March 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 531, left-hand page, 1849 March, third entry from the foot of 531L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4B5|«1849. dana 26 Ožujka preminu Ignatz Pilepich mjesec 5 — i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Vida na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 531 left page, third entry from the foot of the March group. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the first name «Ignatz» and the surname written «Pilepich», legible, with the age «mjesec 5» = 5 months). An infant, so born about October 1848; the parents are not named in this register. Pilepich is the spelling this archive uses for Pilipić (the Pilepich of image 473)|ignatz-pilipic-infant-died-senj-march-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1849-07-martin-perpsich-aged-34|senj-death-1849-07-martin-perpsich-aged-34-line.jpg||Senj, 1 July 1849 — Martin Perpić aged 34 died Senj July 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 532, right-hand page, 1849 July, first entry on 532R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LH32|«1849. dana 1 Serpnja preminu Martin Perpsich godišt 34 — providjen s. sacramenti, i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Vida na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 532 right page, first entry under the heading «Serpanj (Juli)». Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the whole line legible; the surname's middle letters, «Perpsich» or «Perpcich», are a looped hand). A man born about 1815; the surname is read as a spelling of Perpić/Prpić — compare the Perpich deaths of 1836–48 in the Latin register (images 489–490 and nearby), which are also «Perpich»|martin-perpic-aged-34-died-senj-july-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1849-07-johann-baraz-aged-73|senj-death-1849-07-johann-baraz-aged-73-line.jpg||Senj, 12 July 1849 — Johann Boras aged 73 died Senj July 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 533, left-hand page, 1849 July, entry on 533L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHQC|«1849. dana 12 Serpnja preminu Johann Baraz godišt 73 — providjen s. sacramenti, i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Vida na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 533 left page, fourth entry. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name and age legible). A man born about 1776; «Baraz» is read as a spelling of Boras — the same doubt as for the earlier «Boras/Baraz» deaths (the note on the Boras row stands: this archive does not treat Baraz as certainly Boras)|johann-boras-aged-73-died-senj-july-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1849-07-formoz-oriskovic-aged-54|senj-death-1849-07-formoz-oriskovic-aged-54-line.jpg||Senj, 27 July 1849 — Formoz Orešković aged 54 died Senj July 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 533, left-hand page, 1849 July, entry on 533L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHQC|«1849. Dana 27 Serpnja preminu Formoz Oriskovič godišt 54 — providjen s. sacramenti, i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Vida na prici mene Filippa Khreskovich kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 533 left page, the entry above the heading «Kolovoz (August)». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name and the age legible, the entry written in a different hand, the curate's name now Filippo Khreskovich). A man born about 1795; he may be the Formosus Orešković whose six children died 1833–37 (images 483–486) — if he was born about 1795 he would have been about 38–42 then, which fits; this is a reading, not a statement of the register|formoz-oreskovic-aged-54-died-senj-july-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1849-08-kathe-vukelic-aged-36|senj-death-1849-08-kathe-vukelic-aged-36-line.jpg||Senj, 2 August 1849 — Kathe Vukelić aged 36 died Senj August 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 533, left-hand page, 1849 August, first entry on 533L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHQC|«1849. Dana 2 Kolovoza preminu Kathe Vukelić godešta 36 — providjena s. sacramenti, i bi zakopana u cimiteru s. Vida na prici mene Filippa Khreskovich kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 533 left page, the first entry under the heading «Kolovoz (August)». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name and the age legible). A woman born about 1813 (Kathe = Catharina); the surname is spelled out as «Vukelić» with the accent|kathe-vukelic-aged-36-died-senj-august-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1849-08-mihovil-zubranic-aged-47|senj-death-1849-08-mihovil-zubranic-aged-47-line.jpg||Senj, 8 August 1849 — Mihovil Žubrinić aged 47 died Senj August 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 533, right-hand page, 1849 August, first entry on 533R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHQC|«1849. Dana 8 Kolovoza preminu Mihovil Zubranić godišta 47 — providjen s. Sacramenti, i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Vida na prici mene Filippa Khreskovich kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 533 right page, first entry. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name and the age legible; the surname is written «Zubranić» — the spelling of the Žubrinić bride of Baška, 1850, image 349). A man born about 1802; whether he is of the Senj or the Baška Žubrinić is not stated|mihovil-zubrinic-aged-47-died-senj-august-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-531L-jacob-butkovich|senj-seen-531L-jacob-butkovich-line.jpg||Death register 1849: Jacob But?ovich? (8 months) 29 March 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 531, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4B5|Image 531 left page, last entry of March 1849: «1849. dana 29 Ožujka preminu Jacob Bu[t]kovich mjesec 8 — i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Vida na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» An infant of eight months. The surname is read as Butković with a query (the middle of the word is a looped hand; «Buthovich» is as likely): a seen row, not a found person. The same register has Ignatz Pilepich, 5 months, three entries above it. (The neighbouring entry of 16 February, «Frane Rupcich, 2 years», first read as Prpić, is Rupčić — the Rupcich entries of May 1849 spell the name out.)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1849-10-lovre-vukellich-aged-77|senj-death-1849-10-lovre-vukellich-aged-77-line.jpg||Senj, 6 October 1849 — Lovre Vukelić aged 77 died Senj October 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 534, right-hand page, 1849 October, entry 88 on 534R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4TT|«1849. dana 6 Listopada preminu Lovre Vukellich godišt 77 — bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Vida na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 534 right page, entry 88 (the protocol number is written in the right margin). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, the age and the surname's spelling legible). A man born about 1772; the Lovre/Laurentius Vukelić of the Latin register is the father of Ursula (died 1834, image 513R), a Lucas died 1836 — a reading, not a statement of the register|lovre-vukelic-aged-77-died-senj-october-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1849-11-ivan-pilepich-aged-60|senj-death-1849-11-ivan-pilepich-aged-60-line.jpg||Senj, 19 November 1849 — Ivan Pilipić aged 60 died Senj November 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 535, left-hand page, 1849 November, entry 90 on 535L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4B2|«1849. dana 19 Studena preminu Ivan Pilepich godišt 60 — providjen s. Sacramenti, i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Vida na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 535 left page, entry 90. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, the age and the spelling «Pilepich» legible). A man born about 1789; the same year as the infant Ignatz Pilepich, 5 months, of March 1849 (image 531L) — a father and son would be an obvious reading, but the register does not say so. «Pilepich» is the spelling this archive uses for Pilipić|ivan-pilipic-aged-60-died-senj-november-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1849-12-petar-belobarbich-aged-68|senj-death-1849-12-petar-belobarbich-aged-68-line.jpg||Senj, 13 December 1849 — Petar Belobarbić aged 68 died Senj December 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 535, right-hand page, 1849 December, entry 96 on 535R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4B2|«1849. dana 13 Prosinca preminu Petar Belobarbich godišt 68 — providjen s. Sacramenti, i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Vida na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 535 right page, entry 96 (page 7 of the book). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the whole line, and the name written across a line break as «Be- / lobarbich», legible). A man born about 1781. Belobarbić is a listed surname; the Belobarbić marriage of 1852 is image 349|petar-belobarbic-aged-68-died-senj-december-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1850-02-maria-wukellich-aged-8|senj-death-1850-02-maria-wukellich-aged-8-line.jpg||Senj, 16 February 1850 — Maria Vukelić aged 8 died Senj February 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 536, right-hand page, 1850 February, entry 11 on 536R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4T7|«1850. dana 16 Veljače preminu Maria Wukellich, godišt 8., i bi zakopana u cimiteru s. Petra, na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 536 right page, entry 11 (the protocol number in the margin). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the first name, the surname written «Wukellich» and the age legible). A girl born about 1842; the burial has moved from S. Vid to the cemetery of S. Petar in 1850|maria-vukelic-aged-8-died-senj-february-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-536L-antich|senj-seen-536L-antich-line.jpg||Death register 1850: Francisca Antich, 16, 25 January 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 536, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4T7|Image 536 left page, last entry: «1850 dana 25 Sječnja preminu Francisca Antich, godišt 16 — providjena s. sacramenti, i bi zakopana u cimiteru s. Petra na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» A girl of sixteen, born about 1834. Antić is a very common Senj name; kept as a page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-539L-loncaric|senj-seen-539L-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1850: Paulina Loncaric?, 3 months, 26 April 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 539, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4TQ|Image 539 left page, entry 44: «1850. dana 26 Travnja preminu Paulina Lonchaŕić? [Lončarić] — stara mjeseci 3, i bi zakopana u cimiteru s. Petra na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» An infant of three months. The surname is broken across a line («Loncha-/ric»); Lončarić is a very common Senj name: a page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-539R-jurcic|senj-seen-539R-jurcic-line.jpg||Death register 1850: Vinzenza Jurcic, 1 year (28 April), and Ivan Jurcic, 1 year (29 April)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 539, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4TQ|Image 539 right page, first two entries: «1850. dana 28 Travnja preminu Vinzenza Jurčić, godine 1» and «dana 29 Travnja preminu Ivan Jurčić, godine 1», both buried at s. Petra (the book's entries 46 and 47). Two children of one year on consecutive days — possibly twins of one household, or two households of the very common name Jurčić; page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1850-05-petar-zuppan-aged-1|senj-death-1850-05-petar-zuppan-aged-1-line.jpg||Senj, 31 May 1850 — Petar Župan infant died Senj May 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 540, right-hand page, 1850 May, last entry of May on 540R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4JK|«1850. dana 31 Svibnja preminu Petar Zuppan jedne godine star, i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Petra, na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 540 right page, the entry above the heading «Lipanj». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name and the age clear). An infant born about 1849; the parents are not named|petar-zupan-infant-died-senj-may-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-541R-antich|senj-seen-541R-antich-line.jpg||Death register 1850: Frane Antich, 80, 20 June 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 541, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4RN|Image 541 right page, entry 72: «1850. dana 20 Lipnja preminu Frane Antich godin 80 — providjen ss. Sacramenti, i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Petra na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» A man of eighty, born about 1770. Antić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1850-07-maria-babic-aged-7|senj-death-1850-07-maria-babic-aged-7-line.jpg||Senj, 7 July 1850 — Maria Babić aged 7 died Senj July 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 542, left-hand page, 1850 July, entry 79 on 542L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4PL|«1850. dana 7 Serpnja preminu Maria Babić godin 7, i bi zakopana u cimiteru s. Petra, na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 542 left page, entry 79 (the number in the margin). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name with its accent and the age clear). A girl of seven, born about 1843; the Babić marriages of 1842–56 are in the marriage register (images 246–325), where the Babić brides and grooms are Babić of Senj|maria-babic-aged-7-died-senj-july-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-542R-loncaric|senj-seen-542R-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1850: Josip Loncaric, 4, 18 July 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 542, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4PL|Image 542 right page, entry 84: «1850. dana 18 Serpnja preminu Josip Lončarić godin 4, i bi zakopan u cimiteru s. Petra na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» A boy of four. Lončarić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1850-09-michael-son-of-volfgang-adamic-aged-1|senj-death-1850-09-michael-son-of-volfgang-adamic-aged-1-line.jpg||Senj, 19 September 1850 — Michael Adamić infant died Senj September 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 545, right-hand page, 1850 September, entry 118 on 545R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHQ8|«1850. dana 19 Rujna preminu Michael sin Volfganga Adamića, godine 1 star, i bi zakopan u cimiteru svetoga Petra, na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 545 right page, entry 118 (the margin figure). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father «Volfganga Adamića» in the genitive, and the age clear). Adamić is a listed surname; a child born about 1849 whose father, Wolfgang (Volfgang) Adamić, lived at Senj in 1850|michael-adamic-infant-died-senj-september-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1850-09-michael-babic-aged-7-days|senj-death-1850-09-michael-babic-aged-7-days-line.jpg||Senj, 29 September 1850 — Michael Babić infant died Senj September 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 545, right-hand page, 1850 September, entry 120 on 545R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHQ8|«1850. dana 29 Rujna preminu Michael Babić, 7 dana, i bi zakopan u cimiteru svetoga Petra, na prici mene Tome Sladovicha kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 545 right page, entry 120. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name with its accent and the age clear). An infant born about 22 September 1850; the Maria Babić, aged 7, who died on 7 July of the same year (image 542L, entry 79) may be a sibling — a reading, the register names no parents|michael-babic-infant-died-senj-september-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1850-11-anton-babic-aged-3|senj-death-1850-11-anton-babic-aged-3-line.jpg||Senj, 24 November 1850 — Anton Babić aged 3 died Senj November 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 547, left-hand page, 1850 November, entry 141 on 547L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHQK|«1850. Dana 24. Studena preminu Anton Babić, godišt 3. i bi zakopan u Cimiteru svetoga Petra na prici mene Philippa Khreskovich Kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 547 left page, entry 141 (the margin figure); the curate is now Philip Khreskovich. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name with its accent and the age clear). A boy born about 1847; with Maria Babić, 7 (July 1850) and Michael Babić, 7 days (September 1850) the third Babić child of the year in this register — whether they are siblings is not stated|anton-babic-aged-3-died-senj-november-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1850-12-magdalena-vukellic-aged-5-months|senj-death-1850-12-magdalena-vukellic-aged-5-months-line.jpg||Senj, 20 December 1850 — Magdalena Vukelić infant died Senj December 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 547, right-hand page, 1850 December, entry 148 on 547R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHQK|«1850. Dana 20. Prosinca preminu Magdalina Vukellić, miseca 5. stara i bi zakopana u Cimiteru svetoga Petra na prici mene Philippa Khreskovich Kapelana.» The Croatian-language death register of Senj for 1849–1858 (Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849, Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 547 right page, entry 148 (the margin figure). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name and the age in months clear). An infant born about July 1850; the parents are not named|magdalena-vukelic-infant-died-senj-december-1850|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-547L-antic|senj-seen-547L-antic-line.jpg||Death register 1850: Fabo Antic, 40, 7 November 1850|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 547, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHQK|Image 547 left page, first entry: «1850. Dana 7. Studena preminu Fabo Antić 40. godin star providjen svetim Sakramenti, i bi zakopan u Cimiteru svetoga Petra na prici mene Philippa Khreskovich Kapelana.» A man of forty, born about 1810 (Fabo = Fabian). Antić is a very common Senj name: a page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1851-03-johannes-babic-vigil-finantialis-aged-54|senj-death-1851-03-johannes-babic-vigil-finantialis-aged-54-line.jpg||Senj, 1 March 1851 — Johannes Babić customs watchman aged 54 died Senj March 1851|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 548, left-hand page, 1851 March, entry 18 on 548L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4G1|«Die 1. Martii Obiit Johannes Babić Vigil finantialis annorum aetatis 54 ex Phtisi Pulmonali, provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Petrum Comitante Cadaver Philippo Khreskovich Coop.» The Latin-language death register of Senj for 1851 (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118, which changes from Croatian to Latin at the end of December 1850; the new form is «Die [day] [month]. Obiit [name] annorum aetatis suae N ex [cause], provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Petrum Comitante Cadaver Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci»), image 548 left page, the first entry under the heading «Martius» (the book's entry 18). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name with its accent, the occupation, the age and the cause clear). A man born about 1797, a finance guard (Grenzwache/Finanzwache), no wife or children named; the Babić grooms and brides of Senj 1842–56 are in the marriage register (images 246–325)|johannes-babic-customs-watchman-aged-54-died-senj-march-1851|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1851-08-catharina-oreskovic-aged-26|senj-death-1851-08-catharina-oreskovic-aged-26-line.jpg||Senj, 15 August 1851 — Catharina Orešković aged 26 died Senj August 1851|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 549, right-hand page, 1851 August, 15th, on 549R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4PD|«15° Obiit Catharina Oreskovic ex Phtisi pulmonali aetatis suae 26 Annorum provisa Sacramentis morientium, et sepulta est in Coemeterio ad S. Petrum Comitante Cadaver Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci.» The Latin-language death register of Senj for 1851 (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118, which changes from Croatian to Latin at the end of December 1850; the new form is «Die [day] [month]. Obiit [name] annorum aetatis suae N ex [cause], provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Petrum Comitante Cadaver Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci»), image 549 right page, in the group headed «Mense Augusto» (the date is read as the 15th of August; the entries on either side are 11 and 15 August). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name and the age clear). A woman born about 1825 — the Orešković marriages of Senj 1821–53 are in the marriage register; no husband or parents are named|catharina-oreskovic-aged-26-died-senj-august-1851|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-548R-loncaric|senj-seen-548R-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1851: Ursula Loncaric 35 (2 April) and Josephus Loncaric 1 month (29 April)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 548, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4G1|Image 548 right page, April 1851: «Die 2do Aprilis Obiit Ursula Lončarić ex Hydrope aetatis suae 35 Annorum provisa Sacramentis morientium» and «Die 29 Aprilis Obiit Josephus Lončarić ex Spasmo aetatis suae 1 Mensis et 8 Dierum» — a woman of 35 and an infant of 38 days (possibly mother and child, the register does not say). Lončarić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-549L-barac|senj-seen-549L-barac-line.jpg||Death register 1851: Francisca Barac, 63 (7 June 1851)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 549, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4PD|Image 549 left page: «Die 7ma Obiit Francisca Barac ex Hydrope universali aetatis suae 63 Annorum provisa Sacramentis morientium, et sepulta est in Coemeterio ad S. Petrum» (June 1851). A woman of 63, born about 1788. «Barac» may be a spelling of Boras (compare the Baraz/Boras reading of Johann Baraz, 73, 1849, image 533L) — kept as a page-scale seen row because the spelling is not firm, no found person||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1851-10-stephanus-babic-aged-30|senj-death-1851-10-stephanus-babic-aged-30-line.jpg||Senj, 6 October 1851 — Stephanus Babić aged 30 died Senj October 1851|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 550, left-hand page, 1851 October, 6th, on 550L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4LK|«Die 6ta Obiit Stephanus Babić ex Febri nervosa aetatis suae 30 Annorum, provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Petrum Comitante Cadaver Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci.» The Latin-language 1851 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; form «Die [day]. Obiit [name] ex [cause] aetatis suae N Annorum, provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Petrum Comitante Cadaver Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci»), image 550 left page, in the group headed «Mense Octobris» (the entries before it are of 2 and 4 October, the one after it of 6 October, Maria Pir, aged 55). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name with its accent, the cause and the age clear). A man born about 1821; no wife or children named. The Babić grooms and brides of Senj 1842–56 are in the marriage register|stephanus-babic-aged-30-died-senj-october-1851|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1851-10-anna-vukellic-aged-1|senj-death-1851-10-anna-vukellic-aged-1-line.jpg||Senj, October 1851 (day not read) — Anna Vukelić infant died Senj October 1851|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 550, right-hand page, 1851 October, on 550R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4LK|«[?] Obiit Anna Vukellić ex Spasmo aetatis suae 1 Anni 9 Mensium et sepulta est in Coemeterio ad S. Petrum Comitante Cadaver Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci.» The Latin-language 1851 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; form «Die [day]. Obiit [name] ex [cause] aetatis suae N Annorum, provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Petrum Comitante Cadaver Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci»), image 550 right page, in the October group (the entry before it is of 13 October, Petrus Franciscus Kini; the one after it opens «Mense Novembri»). Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x): the Christian name «Anna», the age «1 Anni 9 Mensium» and the cause are clear; the surname is written in a looped hand «Vukellić»/«Vihellić» (read as Vukelić with a query, since the V and the two l's are as in the Vukellich of 1847–50); the day of the month is cut by the page edge. An infant born about January 1850|anna-vukelic-infant-died-senj-october-1851|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-551R-krmpotic|senj-seen-551R-krmpotic-line.jpg||Death register 1852: Lucia Krepotic? (7 months), 30 January 1852|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 551, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4P3|Image 551 right page, January 1852 (the book's entry on page 23): «3[1]º Obiit Lucia Krepotić? ex Spasmo aetatis suae 7 Mensium et sepulta est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum Comitante Cadaver Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci.» An infant of seven months. The surname is written «Kerepotić»/«Krepotić» in a looped hand: read as a spelling of Krmpotić only with a query (the middle letters are not those of Krmpotić as the Senj marriage register writes it) — kept as a seen row, not a found person; the burials move back from S. Petrus to S. Vitus in November 1851||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1852-05-maria-daughter-of-michael-belobarbic-one-day|senj-death-1852-05-maria-daughter-of-michael-belobarbic-one-day-line.jpg||Senj, 22 May 1852 — Maria Belobarbić newborn died Senj May 1852|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 553, right-hand page, 1852 May, second entry on 553R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LH7P|«Die 22. obiit Maria filia Michaelis Belobarbić aetatis diei unius, et sepulta est in Coemeterio ad D. Vitum.» The Latin-language 1852 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; from May 1852 in a different, smaller hand with the burials «ad D. Vitum» [at S. Vitus]), image 553 right page, the second entry from the top (the page continues the entries of May 1852 begun on 553L; the heading «Junius» follows lower on the page). Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's genitive «Michaelis Belobarbić» and «aetatis diei unius» legible; the first letters of the surname are a looped hand, read as «Belobarbić»; the day is read as the 22nd, the entry above it ending at the 21st). A newborn daughter of a Michael Belobarbić of Senj, May 1852. Belobarbić is a listed surname; Petar Belobarbić, 68, died 1849 (image 535R) and the Belobarbić marriage of 1852 is image 349|maria-belobarbic-newborn-died-senj-may-1852|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1852-06-joannes-wukelic-cleric-aged-26|senj-death-1852-06-joannes-wukelic-cleric-aged-26-line.jpg||Senj, 10 June 1852 — Joannes Vukelić theology student aged 26 died Senj June 1852|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 553, right-hand page, 1852 June, tenth day, on 553R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LH7P|«Die 10. obiit Dns Joannes Wukelić Clericus Quarti Anni Theologiae, Annorum aetatis 26, ex Phtisi pulmonali, Sacramentis morientium provisus, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad D. Vitum.» The Latin-language 1852 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; from May 1852 in a different, smaller hand with the burials «ad D. Vitum» [at S. Vitus]), image 553 right page, in the group headed «Junius». Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; «Joannes Wukelić», «Clericus quarti anni Theologiae» and the age 26 legible; the line is written in a small slanted hand). A man born about 1826 who had studied for the priesthood to the fourth year; no parents are named — compare the Joannes Vukelić, son of Dominus Petrus, who died in 1824 (image 511R); that is a different man (born about 1802)|joannes-vukelic-theology-student-aged-26-died-senj-june-1852|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1853-01-antonius-vukellic-vigil-finantialis-aged-32|senj-death-1853-01-antonius-vukellic-vigil-finantialis-aged-32-line.jpg||Senj, 16 January 1853 — Antonius Vukelić customs watchman aged 32 died Senj January 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 555, right-hand page, 1853 January, 16th, on 555R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4JY|«Die 16. Obiit Antonius Vukellić Vigil finantialis ex Phtisi pulmonali aetatis suae 32 Annorum provisus Sacramentis morientium et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum Comitante Cadavere Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci.» The Latin-language 1853 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; heading «1853: Mensis Januarius», page 27), image 555 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, the occupation, the cause and the age clear). A man born about 1820, a finance watchman like the Johannes Babić of March 1851 (image 548L); no wife or children named|antonius-vukelic-customs-watchman-aged-32-died-senj-january-1853|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-554R-krepotic|senj-seen-554R-krepotic-line.jpg||Death register 1852: Thomas Krepotic? aged 26 (September 1852)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 554, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4LV|Image 554 right page, in the September 1852 group: «24. Obiit Thomas Kerepatić? aetatis suae 26 Annorum provisus Sacramentis morientium et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum Comitante Cadavere Philippo Khreskovich.» A man of 26, born about 1826. The surname is written «Kerepatić»/«Krepotić» in a small slanted hand — the same spelling as the infant Lucia of January 1852 (image 551R): read as Krmpotić only with a query, so a seen row, not a found person; if the 1850s clerks write Krmpotić this way, both entries belong with the Krmpotić of the marriage register||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-554L-antic|senj-seen-554L-antic-line.jpg||Death register 1852: Maria daughter of Mathias Antic, 8 days (3 August 1852)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 554, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4LV|Image 554 left page, August 1852: «Die 3tia Obiit Maria filia Mathaei Antić ex Spasmo aetatis suae 8 Dierum et sepulta est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum.» A newborn daughter of a Mathias Antić. Antić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1853-03-alexander-son-of-georgius-krmpotic-aged-9-days|senj-death-1853-03-alexander-son-of-georgius-krmpotic-aged-9-days-line.jpg||Senj, 6 March 1853 — Alexander Krmpotić newborn died Senj March 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 556, left-hand page, 1853 March, sixth day, on 556L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4LF|«Die 6ta Obiit Alexander filius Georgii Krmpotić ex Spasmo aetatis suae 9 Dierum et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum comitante Cadavere Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci.» The Latin-language 1853 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. Obiit [name] ex [cause] aetatis suae N, provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum Comitante Cadavere Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci»), image 556 left page, in the group headed «Martius» (entries of 4 March above and 8 March below). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the whole line legible; the surname is written with the small «e» of the clerk's hand, «Krmpotić»). A newborn son of a Georgius Krmpotić of Senj, born about 25 February 1853|alexander-krmpotic-newborn-died-senj-march-1853|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1853-05-vincentius-babic-aged-41|senj-death-1853-05-vincentius-babic-aged-41-line.jpg||Senj, 5 May 1853 — Vincentius Babić aged 41 died Senj May 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 556, right-hand page, 1853 May, fifth day, on 556R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4LF|«5ta Obiit Vincentius Babić ex Pneumonia aetatis suae 41 Annorum improvisus et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum Comitante Cadavere Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci.» The Latin-language 1853 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. Obiit [name] ex [cause] aetatis suae N, provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum Comitante Cadavere Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci»), image 556 right page (page 28), in the group headed «Mense Majo». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name with its accent, the cause and the age clear; «improvisus» is read as dying without the last sacraments). A man born about 1812; no wife or children named|vincentius-babic-aged-41-died-senj-may-1853|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1853-05-adolphus-son-of-antonius-vukellic-aged-1|senj-death-1853-05-adolphus-son-of-antonius-vukellic-aged-1-line.jpg||Senj, 30 May 1853 — Adolphus Vukelić infant died Senj May 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 557, left-hand page, 1853 May, thirtieth day, on 557L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4YF|«Die 30° Obiit Adolfus filius Antonii Vukellić ex Febri depascenti aetatis suae 1 Anni et se[...] et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum Comitante Cadavere Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci.» The Latin-language 1853 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. Obiit [name] ex [cause] aetatis suae N, provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum Comitante Cadavere Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci»), image 557 left page, the last entry before the heading «Junius». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's genitive «Antonii Vukellić» and the cause legible; the end of the age, the months, is cut by the line below). A child of about 14–18 months, born about 1851–52, a son of an Antonius Vukelić — very probably the Antonius Vukelić, a customs watchman, who died of phthisis on 16 January 1853 (image 555R), but the register does not say so; the father's name is the same and the dates are four months apart|adolphus-vukelic-infant-died-senj-may-1853|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-556L-antic|senj-seen-556L-antic-line.jpg||Death register 1853: Antonius Antic Sag? Vigil finantialis, 36, 1 February 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 556, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4LF|Image 556 left page, February 1853: «Die 1ma Obiit Antonius Antić Sag? Vigil Fin[antialis] ex Phtisi pulmonali aetatis suae 36 Annorum provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum.» A customs watchman of 36, born about 1816. Antić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-556R-loncaric|senj-seen-556R-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1853: Ursula Loncaric, 36, 1 May 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 556, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4LF|Image 556 right page, May 1853: «1ma Obiit Ursula Lončarić ex Phtisi pulmonali aetatis suae 36 Annorum provisa Sacramentis morientium, et sepulta est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum.» A woman of 36. Lončarić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-557L-loncaric|senj-seen-557L-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1853: Paulina daughter of Valentin Loncaric, 1 year, 19 June 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 557, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4YF|Image 557 left page, June 1853: «Die 19. Obiit Paulina filia Valentini Lončarić ex Spasmo aetatis suae 1 Anni, et sepulta est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum.» The page also has Maria, daughter of Stephanus Lončarić, aged 5 (11 July 1853), unrecorded. Lončarić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-557R-loncaric|senj-seen-557R-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1853: Joannes son of Josephus Loncaric, 16 (July 1853)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 557, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4YF|Image 557 right page, July 1853 (the first entry): «16. Obiit Joannes filius Josephi Lončarić ex Pneumonia aetatis suae 16 Annorum provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum.» Lončarić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1853-10-antonius-krmpotic-aged-70|senj-death-1853-10-antonius-krmpotic-aged-70-line.jpg||Senj, 6 October 1853 — Antonius Krmpotić aged 70 died Senj October 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 558, left-hand page, 1853 October, sixth day, on 558L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4VQ|«Die 6to Obiit Antonius Krmpotić aetatis suae 70 Annorum provisus Sacramentis morientium et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum comitante Cadavere Philippo Khreskovich Cooperatore loci.» The Latin-language 1853–54 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 558 left page (page 33 of the 1853 sequence), in the group headed «Mense Octobri» (entries of 1 and 3 October above it). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, with the surname written «Krmpotić», and the age 70 clear). A man born about 1783 — the Krmpotić grooms and widowers of Senj 1822–56 are in the marriage register; no wife or children named|antonius-krmpotic-aged-70-died-senj-october-1853|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-01-theresia-widow-vukellic-aged-72|senj-death-1854-01-theresia-widow-vukellic-aged-72-line.jpg||Senj, 4 January 1854 — Theresia Vukelić widow aged 72 died Senj January 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 559, left-hand page, 1854 January, fourth day, on 559L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHMN|«Die 4. obiit domina Theresia Vukellić vidua e marasmo senili annorum 72, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante cadavere Antonio Lukovich cooperatore.» The Latin-language 1853–54 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), image 559 left page, under the heading «1854 — Mense Januario» (a new hand writes the entries, the cooperator now Antonius Lukovich). Read at full page scale (about 1x; «domina Theresia Vukellić vidua» and «annorum 72» clear). A widow born about 1782, called «domina» (a woman of standing); no husband or children named|theresia-vukelic-widow-aged-72-died-senj-january-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-558L-loncaric|senj-seen-558L-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1853: Joannes Loncaric, 72, 1 October 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 558, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4VQ|Image 558 left page, October 1853: «Die 1. Obiit Joannes Lončarić ex Asthma aetatis suae 72 Annorum provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum.» A man of 72, born about 1781. Lončarić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-558R-loncaric|senj-seen-558R-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1853: Georgius Loncaric, 31, 2 November 1853|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 558, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4VQ|Image 558 right page, November 1853: «2. Obiit Georgius Lončarić ex Febri depascenti aetatis suae 31 Annorum provisus Sacramentis morientium, et sepultus est in Coemeterio ad S. Vitum.» A man of 31. Lončarić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-02-son-of-belobarbic-baptised-joannes-in-need|senj-death-1854-02-son-of-belobarbic-baptised-joannes-in-need-line.jpg||Senj, 8 February 1854 — Joannes Belobarbić newborn died Senj February 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 560, left-hand page, 1854 February, eighth day, first entry on 560L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L41H|«Die 8. Februarii obiit filius Belobarbić, in tempore difficilis partus in baptismo necessitatis Joannis nomen impositum, tempore nascentiae, sepultusque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. obiit [name] e [cause] annorum N, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore»), image 560 left page, the first entry (the heading «Februarius» is on the page before). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the surname «Belobarbić» and the words on the emergency baptism legible). A newborn son of a Belobarbić (the father's name is not given), named Joannes in an emergency baptism and buried on the day of birth; Belobarbić is a listed surname, and this is the second Belobarbić baby of 1854 (the daughter Ana, four months, of 2 March on 560R)|joannes-belobarbic-newborn-died-senj-february-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-02-franciscus-boras-aged-22|senj-death-1854-02-franciscus-boras-aged-22-line.jpg||Senj, 23 February 1854 — Franciscus Boras aged 22 died Senj February 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 560, left-hand page, 1854 February, twenty-third day, on 560L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L41H|«Die 23. obiit Franciscus Boras e phtysi pulmonali annos aetatis suae 22 provisus sacramentis morientium sepultusque est in coemeterio ad S. Vitum comitante Antonio Lukovich.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. obiit [name] e [cause] annorum N, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore»), image 560 left page, the last entry but two. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name written plainly «Boras» and the age 22 clear). A young man born about 1831; the surname is spelled Boras (not Baraz or Barac), the spelling this archive follows; no parents named|franciscus-boras-aged-22-died-senj-february-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-03-ana-daughter-of-antonius-belobarbic-aged-4-months|senj-death-1854-03-ana-daughter-of-antonius-belobarbic-aged-4-months-line.jpg||Senj, 2 March 1854 — Ana Belobarbić infant died Senj March 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 560, right-hand page, 1854 March, second day, first entry on 560R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L41H|«Die 2. obiit Ana filia Antonii Belobarbić e spasmo aetatis mens. 4, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. obiit [name] e [cause] annorum N, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore»), image 560 right page (page 32), the first entry under the heading «Mense Martio». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's genitive «Antonii Belobarbić» and the age legible). An infant born about November 1853, a daughter of an Antonius Belobarbić of Senj|ana-belobarbic-infant-died-senj-march-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-04-catharina-daughter-of-joannes-vukellic-aged-1|senj-death-1854-04-catharina-daughter-of-joannes-vukellic-aged-1-line.jpg||Senj, 5 April 1854 — Catharina Vukelić infant died Senj April 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 561, left-hand page, 1854 April, fifth day, on 561L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4J2|«Die 5. obiit Catharina filia Joannis Vukellić e morbillis anni 1 men[sium] 9, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich coop.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. obiit [name] e [cause] annorum N, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore»), image 561 left page (page 53), in the group headed «Mense Aprili». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's genitive «Joannis Vukellić», the cause «morbillis» and the age legible). A girl born about July 1852, a daughter of a Joannes Vukelić of Senj; the epidemic of measles is the cause of several infant deaths on this page|catharina-vukelic-infant-died-senj-april-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-04-margaritha-widow-pilepic-aged-56|senj-death-1854-04-margaritha-widow-pilepic-aged-56-line.jpg||Senj, 12 April 1854 — Margaritha Pilipić widow aged 56 died Senj April 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 561, right-hand page, 1854 April, twelfth day, first entry on 561R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4J2|«Die 12. obiit vidua Margaritha Pilepić e febri nervosa annorum 56, e S. Georgio in regimine Ottocano oriunda, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich coop.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. obiit [name] e [cause] annorum N, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore»), image 561 right page (page 33), the first entry. Read at full page scale (about 1x; «vidua Margaritha Pilepić», the age 56 and «S. Georgio in regimine Ottocano oriunda» — native of St George in the Otočac regiment — legible). A widow born about 1798, not a native of Senj: the parish of S. Georgius in the Otočac (Ottocan) regiment, which is Sv. Juraj in the Senj hinterland. Compare Elisabeta, daughter of Victor Pilepić, aged 4, who died on 26 April of the same year, a page below (the register does not link them)|margaritha-pilipic-widow-aged-56-died-senj-april-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-04-vincentius-son-of-martha-babic-aged-12-months|senj-death-1854-04-vincentius-son-of-martha-babic-aged-12-months-line.jpg||Senj, 16 April 1854 — Vincentius Babić infant died Senj April 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 561, right-hand page, 1854 April, sixteenth day, on 561R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4J2|«Die 16. obiit Vincentius filius Marthae Babić e morbillis mensium 12, sepultusque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich coop.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. obiit [name] e [cause] annorum N, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore»), image 561 right page (page 33). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the mother's genitive «Marthae Babić» and the age 12 months legible). An infant born about April 1853 whose mother is Martha Babić — only the mother is named, so he may be illegitimate (the register would have written «illegitimus» had it said so; it did not); the Vincentius Babić, aged 41, who died on 5 May 1853 (image 556R), is a possible father only as a reading|vincentius-babic-infant-died-senj-april-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-04-elisabeta-daughter-of-victor-pilepic-aged-4|senj-death-1854-04-elisabeta-daughter-of-victor-pilepic-aged-4-line.jpg||Senj, 26 April 1854 — Elisabeta Pilipić aged 4 died Senj April 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 561, right-hand page, 1854 April, twenty-sixth day, on 561R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4J2|«Die 26. obiit Elisabeta filia Victoris Pilepić e febri depascente annorum 4, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich coop.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. obiit [name] e [cause] annorum N, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore»), image 561 right page (page 33). Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's genitive «Victoris Pilepić» and the age 4 legible). A girl born about 1850, a daughter of a Victor Pilipić of Senj; the same page has the widow Margaritha Pilepić, aged 56, of 12 April|elisabeta-pilipic-aged-4-died-senj-april-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-05-ursula-widow-vukellic-aged-75|senj-death-1854-05-ursula-widow-vukellic-aged-75-line.jpg||Senj, 27 May 1854 — Ursula Vukelić widow aged 75 died Senj May 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 561, right-hand page, 1854 May, twenty-seventh day, last entry on 561R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4J2|«Die 27. obiit vidua Ursula Vukellić e marasmo senili annorum 75, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich coop.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the form «Die [day]. obiit [name] e [cause] annorum N, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore»), image 561 right page (page 33), the last entry, in the group headed «Mense Majo». Read at full page scale (about 1x; «vidua Ursula Vukellić» and «annorum 75» clear). A widow born about 1779; compare Theresia, domina and vidua Vukelić, aged 72, who died on 4 January 1854 (image 559L); no husband or children named|ursula-vukelic-widow-aged-75-died-senj-may-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-561R-antic|senj-seen-561R-antic-line.jpg||Death register 1854: Alexius Antic, 50, 16 April 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 561, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4J2|Image 561 right page, April 1854: «Die 16. obiit Alexius Antić e phtysi pulmonali annorum 50, provisus sacramentis morientium, sepultusque est in coemeterio S. Viti.» A man of 50, born about 1804. Antić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-06-theresia-daughter-of-franciscus-perpic-aged-10-months|senj-death-1854-06-theresia-daughter-of-franciscus-perpic-aged-10-months-line.jpg||Senj, 27 June 1854 — Theresia Perpić infant died Senj June 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 562, right-hand page, 1854 June, twenty-seventh day, on 562R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4RR|«Die 27 obiit Theresia filia Francisci Perpić e spasmo mensium nata 10, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; cooperators Antonius Lukovich and Laurentius Verhovac), image 562 right page (page 34), the entry above the one of 31 May and the heading «Mense Julio» on the page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's genitive «Francisci Perpić» and the age «mensium nata 10» legible; the surname's middle letters are a looped hand, «Perpić»/«Perpii», read as Perpić with a query). An infant born about August 1853; Perpić is the spelling this archive reads as Prpić, with the doubt noted on the Perpich rows of 1836–49|theresia-perpic-infant-died-senj-june-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-07-anna-smojver-aged-16|senj-death-1854-07-anna-smojver-aged-16-line.jpg||Senj, 26 July 1854 — Anna Smojver aged 16 died Senj July 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 562, right-hand page, 1854 July, twenty-sixth day, on 562R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4RR|«26 obiit Anna Smojver e scrophulosis annorum 16, provisa sacramentis morientium, sepultaque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Laurentio Verhovac cooperatore.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; cooperators Antonius Lukovich and Laurentius Verhovac), image 562 right page (page 34), the second entry from the foot, in the group headed «Mense Julio». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name «Anna», the cause «scrophulosis» and the age 16 legible; the surname is written in a looped hand, «Smojver» or «Smoljser», read as Smojver with a query). A girl born about 1838; Smojver is a listed surname — the Smojver brides of Jablanac 1837–45 (images 349L, 350R) and the Gregorius Smojver, 26, who died in 1841 (image 498R)|anna-smojver-aged-16-died-senj-july-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-09-franciscus-vukelic-aged-19|senj-death-1854-09-franciscus-vukelic-aged-19-line.jpg||Senj, 18 September 1854 — Franciscus Vukelić aged 19 died Senj September 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 563, left-hand page, 1854 September, eighteenth day, on 563L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L424|«Die 18. obiit Franciscus Vukelić 19 annorum e phtisi pulmonali, provisus sacramentis morientium, sepultusque est in coemeterio S. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore.» The Latin-language 1854 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; cooperators Antonius Lukovich and Laurentius Verhovac), image 563 left page (page 36), in the group headed «Mense Septembri». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name and the age 19 clear). A youth born about 1835; no parents named|franciscus-vukelic-aged-19-died-senj-september-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1854-12-josephus-son-of-georgius-belobarbic-aged-1y6m|senj-death-1854-12-josephus-son-of-georgius-belobarbic-aged-1y6m-line.jpg||Senj, 6 December 1854 — Josephus Belobarbić infant died Senj December 1854|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 564, left-hand page, 1854 December, sixth day, on 564L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHMV|«Die 6. obiit Josephus fil. Georg. Belobarbić 1 et ½ ann. e rachitide, sepultusque est in coemeterio s. Viti comitante Laurentio Verhovac cooperatore.» The Latin-language 1854–55 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; cooperators Antonius Lukovich and Laurentius Verhovac), image 564 left page, in the group headed «Mense Decembri». Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «Georg. Belobarbić» and the age «1 et ½ ann.» legible). A boy born about June 1853, a son of a Georgius Belobarbić of Senj. Belobarbić is a listed surname; compare the Belobarbić babies of February–March 1854 on image 560 (a son of a Belobarbić, and Ana, daughter of Antonius)|josephus-belobarbic-infant-died-senj-december-1854|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-01-georgius-babic-aged-78|senj-death-1855-01-georgius-babic-aged-78-line.jpg||Senj, 31 January 1855 — Georgius Babić veteran aged 78 died Senj January 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 564, left-hand page, 1855 January, thirty-first day, last entry on 564L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHMV|«Die 31. Februarii [Januarii above] obiit Georgius Babić [«Terezianis»? — a soldier's rank or status] aetatis in Regimento N° 2 Comp. N° 12 veteranus, e marasmo senili annorum 78, sepultusque est in coemeterio s. Viti comitante Antonio Lukovich cooperatore.» The Latin-language 1854–55 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; cooperators Antonius Lukovich and Laurentius Verhovac), image 564 left page, the last entry of the page (heading «Anno Domini 1855», the entry numbered 4). Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; «Georgius Babić», «marasmo senili annorum 78» and «Antonio Lukovich» legible; the words between the name and the regiment are a looped hand and are not read with certainty, and the month has a correction above it). A man born about 1777; if he served as a veteran of a border regiment (Grenzer regiment No. 2 was the Otočac or Lika regiment) the register records it, the age is the one fact that is certain|georgius-babic-veteran-aged-78-died-senj-january-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-564L-antic|senj-seen-564L-antic-line.jpg||Death register 1854: Katharina daughter of Josephus Antic (21 December 1854)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 564, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHMV|Image 564 left page, December 1854: «Die 21. obiit Katharina fil. Josephi Antić [aged] 1 anni? e spasmo sepultaque est in coemeterio s. Viti comitante Lukovich Antonio cooperatore.» A child of a Josephus Antić. Antić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-565R-antic|senj-seen-565R-antic-line.jpg||Death register 1855: Josephus son of Stephanus Antic, 13 days (15 March 1855)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 565, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L469|Image 565 right page, March 1855 (entry 34 of the book's year): «Anno Domini 1855 die 15ta Martii obdormivit in Domino: Josephus filius legitimus Stephani Antić, 13 dierum, e spasmo, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci.» The register now writes the full formula «obdormivit in Domino» with the «filius legitimus» of each child. Antić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-06-hellena-zubranic-aged-60-of-baska|senj-death-1855-06-hellena-zubranic-aged-60-of-baska-line.jpg||Senj, 27 June 1855 — Hellena Žubrinić of Baška aged 60 died Senj June 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 567, left-hand page, 1855 June, twenty-seventh day, first entry on 567L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4NJ|«Anno Domini 1855 die 27° Junii Segniae obiit in Domino: Hellena Zubranić, 60 Annorum, Catholica, e Baška oriunda, e morbo Dysenteria, omnibus moribundorum Sacramentis provisa, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore» (the entry number (66) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; from February 1855 each entry is written out in full: «Anno Domini 1855 die N [month] Segniae obiit in Domino: [name], [age], e [cause], omnibus moribundorum Sacramentis provisa, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich [or Laurentio Verhovac] Cooperatore loci»), image 567 left page, the first entry. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the name, the age, «Catholica, e Baška oriunda» and the cause legible; the surname is written «Zubranić» as in the Zubranić of 1849 and the Žubrinić bride of Baška of 1850, image 349). A woman born about 1795 who came to Senj from Baška on the island of Krk and died there of dysentery in the cholera summer of 1855; the Žubrinić of Baška are a family this archive follows, and the register says in so many words that she was «oriunda» (native) of Baška|hellena-zubrinic-of-baska-aged-60-died-senj-june-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-07-joannes-babic-bajulus|senj-death-1855-07-joannes-babic-bajulus-line.jpg||Senj, 20 July 1855 — Joannes Babić porter died Senj July 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 567, right-hand page, 1855 July, twentieth day, entry 88 on 567R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4NJ|«Anno Domini 1855 die 20ma Julii Segniae obiit in Domino: Joannes Babić bajulus, [age not read; the figure is a looped «18»?], e Dysenteria [Cholera added above], omnibus moribundorum Sacramentis provisus, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore» (the entry number (88) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; from February 1855 each entry is written out in full: «Anno Domini 1855 die N [month] Segniae obiit in Domino: [name], [age], e [cause], omnibus moribundorum Sacramentis provisa, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich [or Laurentio Verhovac] Cooperatore loci»), image 567 right page. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; «Joannes Babić bajulus» legible, the age figure is not read with certainty and the day «20» is read with a query). A porter of Senj who died in the cholera epidemic of July 1855|joannes-babic-porter-died-senj-july-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-04-maria-daughter-of-blasius-caric-aged-22|senj-death-1855-04-maria-daughter-of-blasius-caric-aged-22-line.jpg||Senj, 26 April 1855 — Maria Karić aged 22 died Senj April 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 566, left-hand page, 1855 April, twenty-sixth day, entry 48 on 566L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4GF|«Anno Domini 1855 die 26° Aprilis obiit in Domino: Maria, filia legitima Domini Blasii Carić, 22 Annorum, e phtisi pulmonali, omnibus moribundorum Sacramentis provisa, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry (48) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; from February 1855 each entry is written out in full: «Anno Domini 1855 die N [month] Segniae obiit in Domino: [name], [age], e [cause], omnibus moribundorum Sacramentis provisa, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich [or Laurentio Verhovac] Cooperatore loci»), image 566 left page. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the name, the father's title and name «Domini Blasii Carić», and the age 22 legible). A young woman born about 1833, a daughter of Blasius Carić («Dominus» — a man of standing). The surname is written with C; Karić is a listed surname and Carić is read as a spelling of it only with a query|maria-karic-aged-22-died-senj-april-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-07-jacobus-son-of-georgius-babic-aged-4|senj-death-1855-07-jacobus-son-of-georgius-babic-aged-4-line.jpg||Senj, 31 July 1855 — Jacobus Babić aged 4 died Senj July 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 569, left-hand page, 1855 July, thirty-first day, entry 131 on 569L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L46T|«Anno Domini 1855 die 31° Julii Segniae obiit in Domino: Jacobus filius hortulani Georgii Babić, 4 Annorum, e spasmo, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Laurentio Verhovac Cooperatore loci» (entry number (131) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera summer of 1855, when the entries run at five or six a day, image 569 left page. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's occupation and name «hortulani Georgii Babić» and the age legible). A boy born about 1851; his father Georgius Babić is a gardener of Senj — a different man from the veteran Georgius Babić, aged 78, of January 1855 (image 564L), though the register does not say so, and it may be the father of the Antonius Babić, aged 2, who died the next day (entry 138, image 569R; there the father is called bajulus, a porter)|jacobus-babic-aged-4-died-senj-july-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-08-antonius-son-of-georgius-babic-aged-2|senj-death-1855-08-antonius-son-of-georgius-babic-aged-2-line.jpg||Senj, 1 August 1855 — Antonius Babić aged 2 died Senj August 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 569, right-hand page, 1855 August, first day, first entry on 569R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L46T|«Anno Domini 1855 die 1ma Augusti Segniae obiit in Domino: Antonius filius bajuli Georgii Babić, 2 Annorum, e spasmo, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Laurentio Verhovac Cooperatore loci» (entry number (138) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera summer of 1855, when the entries run at five or six a day, image 569 right page, the first entry. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the name, the father's «bajuli Georgii Babić» and the age legible). A boy born about 1853, a son of a Georgius Babić who is called a porter (bajulus) here and a gardener (hortulanus) in the entry for Jacobus, aged 4, of the day before (entry 131) — the two may be brothers, the register does not say|antonius-babic-aged-2-died-senj-august-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-08-margarita-daughter-of-antonius-zuppan-aged-18|senj-death-1855-08-margarita-daughter-of-antonius-zuppan-aged-18-line.jpg||Senj, 3 August 1855 — Margarita Župan aged 18 died Senj August 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 569, right-hand page, 1855 August, third day, entry 139 on 569R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L46T|«Anno Domini 1855 die 3tia Augusti Segniae obiit in Domino: Margarita filia bajuli Antonii Zuppan, 18 Annorum, e cholera, moriantium Sacramentis provisa, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (139) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera summer of 1855, when the entries run at five or six a day, image 569 right page, the second entry. Read at a band of the half-page cropped to the lines, at page scale (about 1x; the name, the father's name «Antonii Zuppan» — the surname begun on the line above, finished below — and the age 18 legible). A girl born about 1837, a daughter of a Senj porter Antonius Župan; Župan is a listed surname (the Zuppan deaths of 1835, 1836, 1848 and 1850 on images 519L, 521L and 540R)|margarita-zupan-aged-18-died-senj-august-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-568L-loncaric|senj-seen-568L-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1855 (cholera): Lucas Loncaric, stonemason, 48, 24 July 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 568, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L48Y|Image 568 left page, entry 105: «Anno Domini 1855 die 24° Julii Segniae obiit in Domino: Lucas Lončarić lapidarius, uxoratus, 48 Annorum, e cholera, moriantium Sacramentis provisus, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Laurentio Verhovac Cooperatore loci.» A stonemason of 48, married. Lončarić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-569L-loncaric|senj-seen-569L-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1855 (cholera): Aloysius Loncaric, mason, 63, 30 July 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 569, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L46T|Image 569 left page, entry 126: «Anno Domini 1855 die 30° Julii Segniae obiit in Domino: Aloysius Lončarić muratorius, uxoratus, 63 Annorum, e cholera, moriantium Sacramentis provisus, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci.» A mason of 63, married. Lončarić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-08-antonius-son-of-antonius-belobarbic-aged-14|senj-death-1855-08-antonius-son-of-antonius-belobarbic-aged-14-line.jpg||Senj, 14 August 1855 — Antonius Belobarbić aged 14 died Senj August 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 570, left-hand page, 1855 August, fourteenth day, entry 157 on 570L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4KL|«Anno Domini 1855 die 14ta Augusti Segniae obiit in Domino: Antonius filius bajuli Antonii Belobarbić, 14 Annorum, e Cholera, moriantium Sacramentis provisa [sic], et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (157) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera epidemic of August–September 1855, when each page holds some thirty entries, image 570 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Antonii Belobarbić», the age «14 Annorum» — the figure may be «1½» — and the cause legible). A boy of fourteen (or an infant), born about 1841, a son of a porter Antonius Belobarbić of Senj; the Antonius Belobarbić who was the father of the infant Ana (died March 1854, image 560R) may be this man, the register does not say. Belobarbić is a listed surname|antonius-belobarbic-aged-14-died-senj-august-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-08-josepha-daughter-of-laurentius-babic-aged-10|senj-death-1855-08-josepha-daughter-of-laurentius-babic-aged-10-line.jpg||Senj, 23 August 1855 — Josepha Babić aged 10 died Senj August 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 570, left-hand page, 1855 August, entry 169 on 570R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4KL|«Anno Domini 1855 die 23° [22°?] Augusti Segniae obiit in Domino: Josepha filia bajuli Laurentii Babić, 10 Annorum, e cholera, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (169) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera epidemic of August–September 1855, when each page holds some thirty entries, image 570 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Laurentii Babić», the age and the cause legible). A girl born about 1845, a daughter of a porter Laurentius Babić|josepha-babic-aged-10-died-senj-august-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-08-ursula-daughter-of-franciscus-babic-aged-3|senj-death-1855-08-ursula-daughter-of-franciscus-babic-aged-3-line.jpg||Senj, 27 August 1855 — Ursula Babić aged 3 died Senj August 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 570, right-hand page, 1855 August, twenty-seventh day, entry 177 on 570R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4KL|«Anno Domini 1855 die 27ma Augusti Segniae obiit in Domino: Ursula filia bajuli Francisci Babić, 3 Annorum, e cholera, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio Sancti Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (177) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera epidemic of August–September 1855, when each page holds some thirty entries, image 570 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Francisci Babić», the age and the cause legible). A girl born about 1852; the next entry, Maria, daughter of the same Franciscus Babić, aged 6, died the same day, and two more daughters of a porter Franciscus Babić died on 28 and 29 August (image 571L) — four children of one household within three days, if the register's father is one man (it does not say)|ursula-babic-aged-3-died-senj-august-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-08-maria-daughter-of-franciscus-babic-aged-6|senj-death-1855-08-maria-daughter-of-franciscus-babic-aged-6-line.jpg||Senj, 27 August 1855 — Maria Babić aged 6 died Senj August 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 570, right-hand page, 1855 August, twenty-seventh day, entry 178 on 570R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4KL|«Anno Domini 1855 die 27ma Augusti Segniae obiit in Domino: Maria filia bajuli Francisci Babić, 6 Annorum, e cholera, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Laurentio Verhovac Cooperatore loci» (entry number (178) in the margin), the last entry of the page. The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera epidemic of August–September 1855, when each page holds some thirty entries, image 570 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Francisci Babić», the age and the cause legible). A girl born about 1849; Ursula, aged 3, daughter of the same Franciscus Babić, died the same day (entry 177)|maria-babic-aged-6-died-senj-august-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-08-francisca-romana-daughter-of-franciscus-babic-aged-4|senj-death-1855-08-francisca-romana-daughter-of-franciscus-babic-aged-4-line.jpg||Senj, 28 August 1855 — Francisca Romana Babić aged 4 died Senj August 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 571, left-hand page, 1855 August, twenty-eighth day, entry 183 on 571L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4L5|«Anno Domini 1855 die 28 Augusti Segniae obiit in Domino: Francisca Romana filia bajuli Francisci Babić, 4 Annorum, e cholera, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (183) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera epidemic of August–September 1855, when each page holds some thirty entries, image 571 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Francisci Babić», the age and the cause legible). A girl born about 1851, the third of the daughters of a porter Franciscus Babić to die in this epidemic (Ursula, 3, and Maria, 6, on 27 August, entries 177–178, image 570R; the fourth, Maria, 2½, on 29 August, entry 184)|francisca-romana-babic-aged-4-died-senj-august-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-08-maria-daughter-of-franciscus-babic-aged-2|senj-death-1855-08-maria-daughter-of-franciscus-babic-aged-2-line.jpg||Senj, 29 August 1855 — Maria Babić aged 2 died Senj August 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 571, left-hand page, 1855 August, twenty-ninth day, entry 184 on 571L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4L5|«Anno Domini 1855 die 29° Augusti Segniae obiit in Domino: Maria filia bajuli Francisci Babić, 2 Annorum [et] 5? mensium, e cholera, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (184) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera epidemic of August–September 1855, when each page holds some thirty entries, image 571 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Francisci Babić» and the cause legible; the months after «2 Annorum» are read with a query). A girl born about early 1853. There is another Maria, daughter of a bajulus Franciscus Babić, aged 6, who died two days before (entry 178, image 570R) — the register's two Marias of one father are read as two sisters (a first Maria would not usually share the name), but a clerk's mistake or two fathers of the same name are possible|maria-babic-aged-2-died-senj-august-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-09-vincentia-daughter-of-andreas-zuppan-aged-1y2m|senj-death-1855-09-vincentia-daughter-of-andreas-zuppan-aged-1y2m-line.jpg||Senj, 7 September 1855 — Vincentia Župan infant died Senj September 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 571, right-hand page, 1855 September, seventh day, entry 193 on 571R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4L5|«Anno Domini 1855 die 7ma Septembris Segniae obiit in Domino: Vincentia filia bajuli Andreae Zuppan, 1 Anni 2 mensium, e febri depascente, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (193) in the margin), the first entry of the page. The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera epidemic of August–September 1855, when each page holds some thirty entries, image 571 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Andreae Zuppan», the age and the cause legible). An infant born about July 1854, a daughter of a Senj porter Andreas Župan; Župan is a listed surname — compare Margarita, daughter of the porter Antonius Župan, who died of cholera on 3 August (image 569R)|vincentia-zupan-infant-died-senj-september-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-09-anna-butkovic-servant-aged-16|senj-death-1855-09-anna-butkovic-servant-aged-16-line.jpg||Senj, 11 September 1855 — Anna Butković maidservant aged 16 died Senj September 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 571, right-hand page, 1855 September, eleventh day, entry 205 on 571R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4L5|«Anno Domini 1855 die 11ma Septembris Segniae in civili Nosocomio obiit in Domino: puella Anna Butkovich, serva, e Lićnica [?], Centuria Kerpatencai [?], Regimine Ogulinensi oriunda, 16 Annorum, e cholera, moriantium Sacramentis provisa, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (205) in the margin), the last entry of the page. The Latin-language 1855 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118), in the cholera epidemic of August–September 1855, when each page holds some thirty entries, image 571 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, «serva», «Regimine Ogulinensi oriunda», the age 16 and the cause legible; the place-names «e Lićnica» and «Centuria Kerpatencai» are read with a query). A girl born about 1839 from a village in the Ogulin border regiment who died in the hospital of Senj; Butković is a listed surname (the Butković marriage of 1851, image 349)|anna-butkovic-maidservant-aged-16-died-senj-september-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-09-georgius-tomljanovic-confiniarius-of-krmpote-aged-57|senj-death-1855-09-georgius-tomljanovic-confiniarius-of-krmpote-aged-57-line.jpg||Senj, 17 September 1855 — Georgius Tomljanović of Krmpote aged 57 died Senj September 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 572, left-hand page, 1855 September, seventeenth day, entry 210 on 572L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L429|«Anno Domini 1855 die 17ma Septembris Segniae in civili nosocomio obiit in Domino: Georgius Tomljanović Confiniarius, e Kermpote, Regimine Ogulinensi oriundus, uxoratus, 57 Annorum, e Cholera, moriantium Sacramentis provisus, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (210) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855–56 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the cholera epidemic of September–November 1855 and the opening of 1856), image 572 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, «Confiniarius, e Kermpote, Regimine Ogulinensi oriundus», the age 57 and the cause legible). A married man born about 1798 from Krmpote — the village of that name in the Senj hinterland, on the coast (where the Krmpotić family comes from) — who died in the hospital at Senj; Tomljanović is a listed surname (the Tomljanović grooms of 1853 and 1858) and Krmpote is the home village of the Krmpotić|georgius-tomljanovic-of-krmpote-aged-57-died-senj-september-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-09-margarita-krmpotic-mendicant-of-krmpote|senj-death-1855-09-margarita-krmpotic-mendicant-of-krmpote-line.jpg||Senj, 20 September 1855 — Margarita Krmpotić mendicant of Krmpote died Senj September 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 572, left-hand page, 1855 September, twentieth day, entry 213 on 572L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L429|«Anno Domini 1855 die 20ma Septembris Segniae in civili nosocomio obiit in Domino: Margarita Kermpotić, mendicans, 6? Annorum [60?], e Hydropisia, Kermpote in Regimine Ogulinensi oriunda, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Laurentio Verhovac Cooperatore loci» (entry number (213) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855–56 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the cholera epidemic of September–November 1855 and the opening of 1856), image 572 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name «Margarita Kermpotić», «mendicans», «e Hydropisia» and «Kermpote in Regimine Ogulinensi oriunda» legible; the age is a single figure followed by a flourish and is read with a query as 60). A woman beggar of about sixty from Krmpote who died in the hospital; the surname is the village's, and she is a Krmpotić of Krmpote|margarita-krmpotic-mendicant-of-krmpote-died-senj-september-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1855-11-joannes-son-of-philippus-tomljanovic-aged-2y6m|senj-death-1855-11-joannes-son-of-philippus-tomljanovic-aged-2y6m-line.jpg||Senj, 15 November 1855 — Joannes Tomljanović aged 2 died Senj November 1855|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 572, right-hand page, 1855 November, fifteenth day, entry 230 on 572R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L429|«Anno Domini 1855 die 15ta Novembris Segniae obiit in Domino: Joannes filius legitimus Philippi Tomljanović, 2½ Annorum, e Rachitide, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (230) in the margin). The Latin-language 1855–56 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the cholera epidemic of September–November 1855 and the opening of 1856), image 572 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «Philippi Tomljanović» and the age legible). A boy born about May 1853, a son of a Philippus Tomljanović of Senj; the Tomljanović grooms of Senj of 1853 and 1858 are in the marriage register (images 246–325)|joannes-tomljanovic-aged-2-died-senj-november-1855|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1856-01-wolfgangus-son-of-georgius-belobarbic-aged-1y|senj-death-1856-01-wolfgangus-son-of-georgius-belobarbic-aged-1y-line.jpg||Senj, 3 January 1856 — Wolfgangus Belobarbić infant died Senj January 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 573, right-hand page, 1856 January, third day, first entry of 1856 on 573R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4VQ|«Anno Domini 1856 die 3tia Januarii Segniae obiit in Domino: Wolfgangus filius legitimus bajuli Georgii Belobarbić, 1½? anni, e tussi spasmodica, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number 1 of the year 1856, after the heading «Anno Domini 1856 — Januarius»). The Latin-language 1855–56 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; the cholera epidemic of September–November 1855 and the opening of 1856), image 573 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Georgii Belobarbić» and the cause legible; the age figure is read with a query). A boy born about 1854–55; the Georgius Belobarbić whose son Josephus (1½) died on 6 December 1854 (image 564L) is a porter of the same name — a second child of one household within thirteen months, if it is the same father (the register does not say it is)|wolfgangus-belobarbic-infant-died-senj-january-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1856-02-vincentia-wife-of-georgius-belobarbic-aged-28|senj-death-1856-02-vincentia-wife-of-georgius-belobarbic-aged-28-line.jpg||Senj, 22 February 1856 — Vincentia Belobarbić wife of Georgius aged 28 died Senj February 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 574, left-hand page, 1856 February, twenty-second day, entry 18 on 574L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L423|«Anno Domini 1856 die 22 Februarii Segniae in nosocomio civili obiit in Domino: Vincentia uxor Georgii Belloberbich, bajuli, 28 Annorum, e febri depascente, moriensium Sacramentis provisa, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Laurentio Verhovac Cooperatore loci» (entry number (18) in the margin). The Latin-language 1856 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full with the legitimacy and the father's occupation), image 574 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, «uxor Georgii Belloberbich, bajuli», the age 28 and the cause legible). A woman born about 1828, the wife of a porter Georgius Belobarbić, who is very probably the father of the infants Josephus (1½, died 6 December 1854, image 564L) and Wolfgangus (died 3 January 1856, image 573R) — the register names the father and mother in separate entries and does not join them. She died seven weeks after Wolfgangus, probably the mother of both|vincentia-belobarbic-wife-of-georgius-aged-28-died-senj-february-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1856-02-petrus-son-of-bartholomeus-tomljanovic-aged-2|senj-death-1856-02-petrus-son-of-bartholomeus-tomljanovic-aged-2-line.jpg||Senj, 24 February 1856 — Petrus Tomljanović aged 2 died Senj February 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 574, left-hand page, 1856 February, twenty-fourth day, entry 20 on 574L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L423|«Anno Domini 1856 die 24 Februarii Segniae obiit in Domino: Petrus filius legitimus Canonis? [the father's occupation is read with a query] Bartholomei Tomljanovich, 2 Annorum, e Scrophulis, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Laurentio Verhovac Cooperatore loci» (entry number (20) in the margin). The Latin-language 1856 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full with the legitimacy and the father's occupation), image 574 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «Bartholomei Tomljanovich», the cause and the age legible; the word before the father's name is not read). A boy born about 1854, a son of a Bartholomeus Tomljanović of Senj; Tomljanović is a listed surname|petrus-tomljanovic-aged-2-died-senj-february-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1856-04-carolus-son-of-centurion-petrus-vukelic-aged-1y6m|senj-death-1856-04-carolus-son-of-centurion-petrus-vukelic-aged-1y6m-line.jpg||Senj, 10 April 1856 — Carolus Vukelić aged 1 died Senj April 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 575, left-hand page, 1856 April, tenth day, first entry on 575L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L48Q|«Anno Domini 1856 die 10ma Aprilis Segniae obiit in Domino: Carolus filius legitimus pensionati Centurionis Domini Petri Vukelich, 1½ Annorum, e Scrophulis, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante Laurentio Verhovac Cooperatore loci» (entry number (37) in the margin), the first entry on the page. The Latin-language 1856 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full with the legitimacy and the father's occupation), image 575 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's rank and name «pensionati Centurionis Domini Petri Vukelich» and the age legible). A boy born about October 1854, a son of a pensioned centurion Petrus Vukelić of Senj — a man of standing (a retired officer of the border regiment), who lost a second child, Leopoldina, aged 2, five weeks later (entry 49, 16 May)|carolus-vukelic-aged-1-died-senj-april-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1856-05-leopoldina-daughter-of-centurion-petrus-vukelic-aged-2|senj-death-1856-05-leopoldina-daughter-of-centurion-petrus-vukelic-aged-2-line.jpg||Senj, 16 May 1856 — Leopoldina Vukelić aged 2 died Senj May 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 575, left-hand page, 1856 May, sixteenth day, entry 49 on 575L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L48Q|«Anno Domini 1856 die 16ta Maji Segniae obiit in Domino: Leopoldina filia legitima pensionati Centurionis Domini Petri Wukelich, 2 Annorum, e febri depascente, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Laurentio Verhovac Cooperatore loci» (entry number (49) in the margin). The Latin-language 1856 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full with the legitimacy and the father's occupation), image 575 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's rank and name «pensionati Centurionis Domini Petri Wukelich», the age 2 and the cause legible). A girl born about 1854; the sister, probably, of Carolus (aged 1½, entry 37, 10 April) — the register names the same father, a pensioned centurion Petrus Vukelić; two children of one household lost within five weeks|leopoldina-vukelic-aged-2-died-senj-may-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1856-06-francisca-babic-servant|senj-death-1856-06-francisca-babic-servant-line.jpg||Senj, 29 June 1856 — Francisca Babić servant died Senj June 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 575, right-hand page, 1856 June, twenty-ninth day, on 575R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L48Q|«Anno Domini 1856 die 29 Junii Segniae in nosocomio civili omnibus moriantium Sacramentis provisa obiit in Domino: Caelebs Francisca Babich, serva, [..] Annorum, e hydropisi, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (the margin figure is read as (60)). The Latin-language 1856 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full with the legitimacy and the father's occupation), image 575 right page, the entry above the heading «Julius». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, «Caelebs», «serva» and the cause legible; the figure before «Annorum» is cut by the line above and the page edge)|francisca-babic-servant-died-senj-june-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1856-08-maria-daughter-of-gregorius-babic-aged-2y6m|senj-death-1856-08-maria-daughter-of-gregorius-babic-aged-2y6m-line.jpg||Senj, 14 August 1856 — Maria Babić aged 2 died Senj August 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 576, right-hand page, 1856 August, fourteenth day, entry 78 on 576R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4XT|«Anno Domini 1856 die 14ta Augusti Segniae obiit: Maria filia legitima bajuli Gregorii Babich, 2½ Annorum, e dysenteria, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (78) in the margin). The Latin-language 1856 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full), image 576 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Gregorii Babich», the age and the cause legible). A girl born about February 1854, a daughter of a porter Gregorius Babić of Senj — a name not met before in the Babić rows; compare the porter Georgius (Gregorius) Babić of 1855, whose children died in the cholera (images 569–571) — Georgius and Gregorius are different names, and the register does not join them|maria-babic-aged-2-died-senj-august-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1856-08-thomas-vukelic-confiniarius-of-krmpote-aged-26|senj-death-1856-08-thomas-vukelic-confiniarius-of-krmpote-aged-26-line.jpg||Senj, 25 August 1856 — Thomas Vukelić Grenzer of Krmpote aged 26 died Senj August 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 576, right-hand page, 1856 August, twenty-fifth day, entry 82 on 576R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4XT|«Anno Domini 1856 die 25ta Augusti Segniae omnibus moriantium Sacramentis provisus obiit: Thomas Vukelich [?] Confiniarius Inclyti Regiminis Ogulinensis, Centuria Kermpotensis, uxoratus, 26 Annorum aetatis, e inflamatione intestinorum, et sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (82) in the margin). The Latin-language 1856 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full), image 576 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x), and again as a band of the page at the same scale (the first letter and the middle of the surname are a looped hand: «Vukelich», read with a query; the title «Confiniarius Inclyti Regiminis Ogulinensis, Centuria Kermpotensis» and the age 26 are legible). A married man born about 1830 from the border company of Krmpote, a soldier of the Ogulin regiment — the same regiment as the Krmpote people of the cholera pages of September 1855 (Georgius Tomljanović and Margarita Krmpotić, images 572L); the Vukelić of Senj town are a different stock (the Dominus Petrus Vukelić of 1824, the pensioned centurion Petrus Vukelić of 1856, images 511R and 575L)|thomas-vukelic-grenzer-of-krmpote-aged-26-died-senj-august-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1856-10-joanna-smojver-servant-aged-57|senj-death-1856-10-joanna-smojver-servant-aged-57-line.jpg||Senj, 25 October 1856 — Joanna Smojver aged 57 died Senj October 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 577, left-hand page, 1856 October, twenty-fifth day, entry 97 on 577L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4FG|«Anno Domini 1856 die 25ta Octobris Segniae morientium Sacramentis provisa in nosocomio civico obiit: Joanna Smojver uxorata, serva conditione, 57 Annorum, e febri depascente, et sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore loci» (entry number (97) in the margin). The Latin-language 1856 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full), image 577 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, «uxorata, serva conditione», the age 57 and the cause legible). A married woman born about 1799 who was in service and died in the hospital at Senj; Smojver is a listed surname — the Smojver brides of Jablanac 1837–45 (images 349L, 350R), the Smojver deaths of 1831 and 1841 (images 492R, 498R) and a Smojver girl of 1854 (image 562R)|joanna-smojver-aged-57-died-senj-october-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1856-12-theresia-daughter-of-augustinus-babic-aged-14|senj-death-1856-12-theresia-daughter-of-augustinus-babic-aged-14-line.jpg||Senj, 20 December 1856 — Theresia Babić aged 14 died Senj December 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 577, right-hand page, 1856 December, twentieth day, entry 109 on 577R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4FG|«Anno Domini 1856 die 20ma Decembris Segniae moriantium Sacramentis provisa obiit: Theresia filia legitima murarii Augustini Babich, 14 Annorum, e febri depascente, et servato praescripto termino in communi Coemeterio St. Viti sepulta est, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore» (entry number (109) in the margin). The Latin-language 1856 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full), image 577 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the name, the father's occupation and name «murarii Augustini Babich», the age and the cause legible). A girl born about 1842, a daughter of a mason Augustinus Babić of Senj|theresia-babic-aged-14-died-senj-december-1856|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-577R-loncaric|senj-seen-577R-loncaric-line.jpg||Death register 1856: Ursula Loncaric, servant, 19, 28 October 1856|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 577, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4FG|Image 577 right page, entry 100: «Anno Domini 1856 die 28° Octobris Segniae moriantium Sacramentis provisa obiit: Ursula Loncarich puella serviens, 19 Annorum, e Typho, et praescripto termino in communi Coemeterio St. Viti sepulta est, comitante Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore.» A servant girl of 19. Lončarić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1857-01-joanna-daughter-of-joannes-vukelic-aged-2y6m|senj-death-1857-01-joanna-daughter-of-joannes-vukelic-aged-2y6m-line.jpg||Senj, 15 January 1857 — Joanna Vukelić aged 2 died Senj January 1857|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 578, left-hand page, 1857 January, fifteenth day, entry 5 on 578L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4G7|«Anno Domini 1857 die 15ta Januarii Segniae obiit: Joanna filia legitima bajuli Joannis Vukelich, 2½ Annorum, e Scrophulis, et observato praescripto termino sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore» (entry number (5) in the margin). The Latin-language 1857 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full: «Anno Domini 1857 die N [month] Segniae obiit: [name], filia/filius legitima/us [father's occupation and name], [age], e [cause], et observato praescripto termino sepulta/us est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore»), image 578 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Joannis Vukelich» and the age legible). A girl born about July 1854, a daughter of a porter Joannes Vukelić of Senj — a child of the same age and name-pair as Catharina, 1 year 9 months, daughter of a Joannes Vukelić, who died of measles on 5 April 1854 (image 561L); the register does not say they are sisters, and Joannes is a common name|joanna-vukelic-aged-2-died-senj-january-1857|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1857-03-vincentia-daughter-of-antonius-belobarbic-aged-2-months|senj-death-1857-03-vincentia-daughter-of-antonius-belobarbic-aged-2-months-line.jpg||Senj, 22 March 1857 — Vincentia Belobarbić infant died Senj March 1857|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 579, left-hand page, 1857 March, twenty-second day, entry 25 on 579L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4GX|«Anno Domini 1857 die 22 Martii Segniae e spasmo obiit: Vincentia filia legitima bajuli Antonii Belobarbich, 2 mensium, et observato praescripto termino sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore» (entry number (25) in the margin). The Latin-language 1857 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full: «Anno Domini 1857 die N [month] Segniae obiit: [name], filia/filius legitima/us [father's occupation and name], [age], e [cause], et observato praescripto termino sepulta/us est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore»), image 579 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Antonii Belobarbich» and the age legible). An infant born about January 1857, a daughter of a porter Antonius Belobarbić of Senj — the Antonius Belobarbić, porter, whose son Antonius (14) died of cholera in 1855 (image 570L) and whose daughter Ana (4 months) died in March 1854 (image 560R) is the same man if the register's father is one — three children lost over four years, a reading|vincentia-belobarbic-infant-died-senj-march-1857|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1857-03-maria-daughter-of-laurentius-babic-aged-5y6m|senj-death-1857-03-maria-daughter-of-laurentius-babic-aged-5y6m-line.jpg||Senj, 26 March 1857 — Maria Babić aged 5 died Senj March 1857|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 579, left-hand page, 1857 March, twenty-sixth day, entry 26 on 579L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4GX|«Anno Domini 1857 die 26ta Martii Segniae obiit in Domino: Maria filia legitima bajuli Laurentii Babich, 5½ Annorum, e febri depascente, et servato praescripto termino sepulta est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore» (entry number (26) in the margin). The Latin-language 1857 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full: «Anno Domini 1857 die N [month] Segniae obiit: [name], filia/filius legitima/us [father's occupation and name], [age], e [cause], et observato praescripto termino sepulta/us est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore»), image 579 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Laurentii Babich», the age and the cause legible). A girl born about September 1851, a daughter of a porter Laurentius Babić — very probably the father of Josepha (10), who died of cholera on 23 August 1855 (image 570R), but the register does not say it|maria-babic-aged-5-died-senj-march-1857|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1857-04-franciscus-son-of-matthaeus-vukelic-aged-2|senj-death-1857-04-franciscus-son-of-matthaeus-vukelic-aged-2-line.jpg||Senj, 13 April 1857 — Franciscus Vukelić aged 2 died Senj April 1857|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 579, left-hand page, 1857 April, thirteenth day, last entry (30) on 579L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4GX|«Anno Domini 1857 die 13tia Aprilis Segniae obiit e spasmo: Franciscus filius legitimus bajutis Policiae Vigilis Matthaei Wukelich, 2 Annorum, et servato praescripto termino sepultus est in communi Coemeterio Sancti Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore» (entry number (30) in the margin), the last entry of the page. The Latin-language 1857 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full: «Anno Domini 1857 die N [month] Segniae obiit: [name], filia/filius legitima/us [father's occupation and name], [age], e [cause], et observato praescripto termino sepulta/us est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore»), image 579 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's rank and name «Policiae Vigilis Matthaei Wukelich» — the words before «Vigilis» are read with a query — and the age legible). A boy born about 1855, a son of a watchman Matthaeus Vukelić of Senj|franciscus-vukelic-aged-2-died-senj-april-1857|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1857-05-matthaeus-son-of-georgius-belobarbic-aged-7|senj-death-1857-05-matthaeus-son-of-georgius-belobarbic-aged-7-line.jpg||Senj, 9 May 1857 — Matthaeus Belobarbić aged 7 died Senj May 1857|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 579, right-hand page, 1857 May, ninth day, entry 35 on 579R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4GX|«Anno Domini 1857 die 9na Maji Segniae e febri depascente obiit: Matthaeus filius legitimus bajuli Georgii Belobarbich, 7 Annorum, et servato praescripto termino sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore» (entry number (35) in the margin). The Latin-language 1857 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full: «Anno Domini 1857 die N [month] Segniae obiit: [name], filia/filius legitima/us [father's occupation and name], [age], e [cause], et observato praescripto termino sepulta/us est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore»), image 579 right page, the first entry under the heading «Majus». Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «bajuli Georgii Belobarbich», the age and the cause legible). A boy born about 1850, a son of a porter Georgius Belobarbić of Senj — the third child of that porter in the death register (Josephus, 1½, 1854, image 564L; Wolfgangus, 1856, image 573R) and the mother's death (Vincentia, 28, 22 February 1856, image 574L) would make this a family stripped over thirty months, if the register's father is one man — the register's evidence is the repeated name «Georgius Belobarbić, bajulus»|matthaeus-belobarbic-aged-7-died-senj-may-1857|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1857-06-fridericus-son-of-centurion-petrus-vukelic-aged-5|senj-death-1857-06-fridericus-son-of-centurion-petrus-vukelic-aged-5-line.jpg||Senj, 22 June 1857 — Fridericus Vukelić aged 5 died Senj June 1857|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 581, left-hand page, 1857 June, twenty-second day, first entry (43) on 581L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4RV|«Anno Domini 1857 die 22da Junii Segniae e Scrophulis obiit: Fridericus filius legitimus pensionati Centurionis Domini Petri Vukelich, 5 Annorum, et observato praescripto termino sepultus est in communi Coemeterio Sancti Viti, comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore» (entry number (43) in the margin), the first entry of the page. The Latin-language 1857 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full), image 581 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's rank and name «pensionati Centurionis Domini Petri Vukelich» and the age 5 legible). A boy born about 1852, the third child of the pensioned centurion Petrus Vukelić to die in fourteen months (Carolus, 1½, on 10 April 1856, image 575L, and Leopoldina, 2, on 16 May 1856, image 575L, before him)|fridericus-vukelic-aged-5-died-senj-june-1857|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1857-08-maria-daughter-of-georgius-butkovic-aged-5y6m|senj-death-1857-08-maria-daughter-of-georgius-butkovic-aged-5y6m-line.jpg||Senj, 18 August 1857 — Maria Butković aged 5 died Senj August 1857|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 581, right-hand page, 1857 August, eighteenth day, entry 58 on 581R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4RV|«Anno Domini 1857 die 18va Augusti Segniae e febri depascente obiit: Maria filia legitima Servi Georgii Buthkovich, 5½ Annorum, et praestis [praescripto termino?] favendis sepulta est in Coemeterio St. Viti comitante: Antonio Lukovich Cooperatore» (entry number (58) in the margin). The Latin-language 1857 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; entries written out in full), image 581 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; the child's name, the father's «Servi Georgii Buthkovich» — servus here a servant, a house-servant — the age and the cause legible; the burial formula is abbreviated). A girl born about February 1852, a daughter of a Georgius Butković of Senj. Butković is a listed surname (the Butković marriage of 1851, image 349; a Jacob Butković, 8 months, seen on 531L); the Anna Butković, a maidservant of the Ogulin regiment, died in the hospital in September 1855 (image 571R)|maria-butkovic-aged-5-died-senj-august-1857|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1858-01-gregorius-krmpotic-confiniarius-aged-75|senj-death-1858-01-gregorius-krmpotic-confiniarius-aged-75-line.jpg||Senj, 8 January 1858 — Gregorius Krmpotić Grenzer aged 75 died Senj January 1858|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 582, right-hand page, 1858 January, eighth day, entry 4 on 582R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4N2|«Anno Domini 1858 die 8 Januarii in filiali hujus Parochiae ad Sanctum Salvatorem inaprimate [?], e marasmo senili, physica aetatis 75 annorum obiit: Confiniarius Gregorius Kermpotić a No. Domus 30, et observato praescripto termino sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Joanne Bušić Cooperatore loci» (entry number (4) in the margin). The Latin-language 1857–58 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; from October 1857 the entries are in a new hand, with the cooperators Joannes Bušić and Eduardus Biankini), image 582 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x), and again as a band of the page at the same scale (the name «Gregorius Kermpotić», «Confiniarius», the age «75 annorum» and «a No. Domus 30» legible; the words after «Sanctum Salvatorem» are read with a query). A man born about 1783 of the border-soldier class from the Krmpotić house No. 30 of Sv. Spas — the village «St. Salvator», where the Krmpotić of Senj hold land (Maria, daughter of Michael Krmpotić of S. Salvator, 1825, image 481; Michael 14 and Nicolaus 48 of S. Salvator, 1831, image 491). A Krmpotić grandfather of the generation of the Antonius Krmpotić, 70, of 1853 (image 558L)|gregorius-krmpotic-grenzer-aged-75-died-senj-january-1858|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1857-11-jacobus-boric-finance-watchman-of-udbina-aged-19|senj-death-1857-11-jacobus-boric-finance-watchman-of-udbina-aged-19-line.jpg||Senj, 19 November 1857 — Jacobus Borić finance watchman aged 19 died Senj November 1857|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 582, left-hand page, 1857 November, nineteenth day, entry 77 on 582L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4N2|«Anno Domini 1857 die 19no Novembris in militari nosocomio Segniensi, moriens [? with the sacraments provisus], physica aetatis 19 annorum obiit: Caelebs Jacobus Boric ex financia Vigil, ex Udbinae oriundus, et observato praescripto termino sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Joanne Bušić Cooperatore loci» (entry number (77) in the margin), the last entry of the page; a note «ex inflamatione» below it. The Latin-language 1857–58 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; from October 1857 the entries are in a new hand, with the cooperators Joannes Bušić and Eduardus Biankini), image 582 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x), and again as a band of the page at the same scale (the name, «caelebs», «financia Vigil», «ex Udbinae oriundus» and the age 19 legible). A young man of nineteen born about 1838 at Udbina, in the Lika, in the finance-guard; Borić is a listed surname|jacobus-boric-finance-watchman-aged-19-died-senj-november-1857|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1858-06-matthaeus-tomljanovic-provisionatus-vigil-aged-54|senj-death-1858-06-matthaeus-tomljanovic-provisionatus-vigil-aged-54-line.jpg||Senj, 2 June 1858 — Matthaeus Tomljanović retired watchman aged 54 died Senj June 1858|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 585, right-hand page, 1858 June, second day, entry 66 on 585R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4Z2|«Anno Domini 1858 die 2da Junii Segniae sub Hao domali 377, e febri nervosa, physica aetatis 54 annorum, omnibus moriendum [moriendi?] Sacramentis provisus obiit: Matthaeus Tomljanović, uxoratus, provisionatus Vigil, et observato praescripto legis termino sepultus est in Coemeterio communi St. Viti, comitante: Joanne Bušić Cooperatore loci» (entry number (66) in the margin). The Latin-language 1858 pages of the Senj death register (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; from February 1858 each entry also names the house number: «sub Hao domali [N]»). Read at full page scale (about 1x), and again as a band of the page at the same scale (the name, «uxoratus, provisionatus Vigil», the age 54 and the cause legible; the house number is read as 377). A married man born about 1804, a retired watchman of the finance guard; Tomljanović is a listed surname (the Tomljanović deaths of 1834–56 on images 506R–574L, and the grooms of 1853 and 1858 in the marriage register)|matthaeus-tomljanovic-retired-watchman-aged-54-died-senj-june-1858|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-585R-antic|senj-seen-585R-antic-line.jpg||Death register 1858: Josephus Antic, 48, of Selca in the Vinodol (19 May 1858)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 585, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4Z2|Image 585 right page, entry 60: «Anno Domini 1858 die 19no Maji Segniae sub Hao domali 177, e phtysi, physica aetatis 48 annorum, moriendum [moriendi] Sacramentis provisus, e Selca in Vinodol oriundus obiit: Josephus Antić, uxoratus, et observato legis termino sepultus est in Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Joanne Bušić Cooperatore loci.» A married man of 48 from Selce in the Vinodol. Antić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-585R-jurcic|senj-seen-585R-jurcic-line.jpg||Death register 1858: Vincentia, wife of the mason Michael Jurcic, 26 (8 May 1858)|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 585, right-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4Z2|Image 585 right page, entry 58: «Anno Domini 1858 die 8va Maji Segniae sub Hao domali 427, e corrosionibus Spasmi, physica aetatis 26 annorum, moriendum Sacramentis provisa obiit: Vincentia uxor muratori Michaëlis Jurcic, et sepulta est observato legis termino in Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Joanne Bušić Cooperatore loci.» A woman of 26, wife of a mason Michael Jurčić. Jurčić is a very common Senj name: page-scale seen row (no found person)||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1858-11-anna-widow-smojver-aged-90|senj-death-1858-11-anna-widow-smojver-aged-90-line.jpg||Senj, 10 November 1858 — Anna Smojver widow aged 90 died Senj November 1858|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 588, left-hand page, 1858 November, tenth day, entry 116 on 588L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4FG|«Anno Domini 1858 die 10ma Novembris Segniae e marasmo senili, physica aetatis 90 annorum, moriendum [moriendi] Sacramentis provisa obiit: Vidua Anna Smojver, et sepulta est observato termino in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Eduardo Biankini Coop. loci» (entry number (116) in the margin). The last pages of the Latin-language death register of Senj 1849–1858 (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; every entry here gives the house number and the cooperator Eduardus Biankini or Joannes Bušić), image 588 left page. Read at full page scale (about 1x; «Vidua Anna Smojver» and «aetatis 90 annorum» legible). A widow born about 1768 — the oldest Smojver in the register, of the generation of the Simon Smojver, 70, who died in 1831 (image 492R) and of the Karlobag Smojver of the 1770s–80s; the register does not say whom she married|anna-smojver-widow-aged-90-died-senj-november-1858|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1858-11-andreas-son-of-michael-belobarbic-newborn|senj-death-1858-11-andreas-son-of-michael-belobarbic-newborn-line.jpg||Senj, 25 November 1858 — Andreas Belobarbić newborn died Senj November 1858|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 588, left-hand page, 1858 November, twenty-fifth day, last entry of 588L|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4FG|«Anno Domini 1858 die 25to Novembris ob difficilem partum sicstatim post susceptum baptismum necessitatis obiit: Andreas filius legitimus bajuli Michaëlis Bellobarbick, et servato praescripto termino sepultus est in Coemeterio Sancti Viti, comitante: Eduardo Biankini Coop. loci» (the entry has no margin number; it follows entry 121 of 22 November and the next entry, number 123, is of 28 November). The last pages of the Latin-language death register of Senj 1849–1858 (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; every entry here gives the house number and the cooperator Eduardus Biankini or Joannes Bušić), image 588 left page, the last entry of the page. Read at full page scale (about 1x), and again as a band of the page at the same scale (the child's name, the father's «bajuli Michaëlis Bellobarbick» and the cause legible). A son of a porter Michael Belobarbić of Senj, who was already the father of the infant Maria Belobarbić, one day old, died 22 May 1852 (image 553R, «filia Michaelis Belobarbić»)|andreas-belobarbic-newborn-died-senj-november-1858|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1858-12-simeon-son-of-georgius-butkovic-aged-1y6m|senj-death-1858-12-simeon-son-of-georgius-butkovic-aged-1y6m-line.jpg||Senj, 23 December 1858 — Simeon Butković aged 1 died Senj December 1858|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 588, right-hand page, 1858 December, twenty-third day, entry 126 on 588R|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4FG|«Anno Domini 1858 die 23tia Decembris Segniae e Rachitide, physica aetatis 1½ anni obiit: Simeon filius legitimus bajuli Georgii Butkovic, et observato praescripto legis termino sepultus est in communi Coemeterio St. Viti, comitante: Eduardo Biankini Coop. loci» (entry number (126) in the margin). The last pages of the Latin-language death register of Senj 1849–1858 (the book «Knjiga Mertvih od God. 1849», Državni arhiv Zagreb, Zbirka matičnih knjiga Br. 1118; every entry here gives the house number and the cooperator Eduardus Biankini or Joannes Bušić), image 588 right page. Read at full page scale (about 1x), and again as a band of the page at the same scale (the child's name, the father's «bajuli Georgii Butkovic», the age and the cause legible). A boy born about June 1857, a son of a porter Georgius Butković — very probably the Georgius Butković whose daughter Maria, 5½, died of a wasting fever on 18 August 1857 (image 581R, there called «Servi Georgii Buthkovich»), a reading|simeon-butkovic-aged-1-died-senj-december-1858|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1735-10-stipe-bukvic-katarina-daughter-of-mikula-butkovic-of-ledenice|senj-marriage-1735-10-stipe-bukvic-katarina-daughter-of-mikula-butkovic-of-ledenice-line.jpg||Senj, 18 October 1735 («8bra») — Katarina Butković of Ledenice bride 1735|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 10, right-hand page, image 10R, entry of 18 October|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L46V|«Na 18 8bra Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Stipu Bukvicha skherom Mikule Butkovicha iz Ledenic imenom Katarina, Kim bi ja svido-ka Miko Kraljich i …» — «8bra» is October. The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian-language entries of the parish priest «Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy …»; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 10 right page, the sixth entry from the foot. Read in the STRIP PASS at a window that includes the page's left and right edges (the first pass of image 10 used a window that missed the right edge, where the bride's father and the witnesses are written); the year 1735 is not on this page and is taken from the sequence (the page before has May–August, image 11R carries the heading 1736). Butković is a listed surname and Ledenice a place of the Butković marriages of 1851 and 1853 (image 349); the witness «Miko Kraljich» is a Kraljić, another listed surname|katarina-butkovic-of-ledenice-bride-1735|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1736-02-franjo-butkovic-of-karlobag-mara|senj-marriage-1736-02-franjo-butkovic-of-karlobag-mara-line.jpg||Senj, 13 February 1736 — Franjo Butković of Karlobag groom 1736|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 12, left-hand page, image 12L, last entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4XR|«Na 13 Februara [..] zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Franciscka Butkovicka od Karlobaga skherom Francilia Pot: [..]kovicha imenom Mara, Kim bi ja svidoka Rade Maurovi[c] i Gve Granich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian-language entries of the parish priest «Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy …»; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 12 left page, the last entry of the page. Read in the STRIP PASS (the first pass window missed the right edge of the left page, where the end of each line stands); the bride's father's surname is cut by the page edge and the first words of the line are blurred. A Butković groom of Karlobag in February 1736 — the earliest Butković of this archive's Karlobag side|franjo-butkovic-of-karlobag-groom-1736|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1737-05-pangracij-onufric-katarina-witness-boze-sojat|senj-marriage-1737-05-pangracij-onufric-katarina-witness-boze-sojat-line.jpg||Senj, 1 May 1737 (day read «2»?) — Božo Šojat witness 1737|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 15, right-hand page, image 15R, first entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L48W|«Na [1/2] Maya Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Pangracia Onuphicha is Plovania Lorke skherom Pivice Shovicha imenom Katarinu, Kim bi ja svidoka Boze Soyat i Anton Maleta.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 15 right page, the first entry (page 10 of the book), under the year 1737 begun on 15L. Read in the STRIP PASS (the first pass window missed the right edge of this page). Šojat is a listed surname: «Boze Soyat» is the earliest Šojat in this volume, a witness eight years before the Šojat groom of 1745 (image 37L); the register gives him no relationship to the couple|bozo-sojat-witness-1737|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1738-02-antonio-speranci-klara-daughter-of-vule-tomjanovic|senj-marriage-1738-02-antonio-speranci-klara-daughter-of-vule-tomjanovic-line.jpg||Senj, 18 February 1738 — Klara Tomljanović bride 1738|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 18, left-hand page, image 18L, first entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4PS|«Na 18 Februara Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Antonia Speranci od Rilke skherom K: Vule Tomjanovicha imenom Klara, Kim bi ja svidoka K. Pave Tomjanovich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 18 left page, the first entry (the year 1738, begun on 17L). Read in the STRIP PASS; the end of the second line («imenom Klara, Kim») is at the edge of the page and the neighbouring tile of the image had not loaded, so the end of the line is read with a query. Tomljanović is a listed surname: a Tomljanović bride and a Tomljanović witness at Senj in 1738, a century before the Tomljanović deaths of 1834–58 on images 506–585 and the groom of 1853; the register names no link NOTE added at 23R: «K.» before a Tomjanović name is probably «Kanonik» (a canon): on image 23R (2 Oct 1739) a «Kanonik Titular Pop Pave Tomjenovich» is the celebrant, so this Tomljanović family of 1738–39 is a family of Senj priests or nobles, not a town household of the later registers.|klara-tomljanovic-bride-1738|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1738-12-pera-stabar-klara-witness-pave-tomjanovic|senj-marriage-1738-12-pera-stabar-klara-witness-pave-tomjanovic-line.jpg||Senj, 23 October 1738 («gbra» read as 8bra/October) — Pave Tomljanović witness 1738|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 20, right-hand page, image 20R, third entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L48Q|«Na 23 [8]bra Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Peru Stabara skherom Pok: Jure Hrehanovicha Gdinom Klarom, Kim bi ja svidoka Gn: Dane Hrehanovich i K. Pave Tommynovich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 20 right page (page 14 of the book), the third entry. Read in the STRIP PASS (the first pass window missed the right edge of the right page, where the second witness's name finishes: «K. Pave Tommy-/novich»). The month abbreviation is «gbra»/«obra» and is read as October (the entries before it are of 13 and 25 October and those after of 29 and 31 December, so «23 Xbra» is possible: it is the Pave Tomljanović of 18 February 1738 either way). Pave Tomjanović is the witness of the Tomljanović bride of image 18L, in the same year; the register gives no relationship NOTE added at 23R: «K.» before a Tomjanović name is probably «Kanonik» (a canon): on image 23R (2 Oct 1739) a «Kanonik Titular Pop Pave Tomjenovich» is the celebrant, so this Tomljanović family of 1738–39 is a family of Senj priests or nobles, not a town household of the later registers.|pave-tomljanovic-witness-1738|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1739-05-francisca-bexilva-antonia-daughter-of-jule-tomjanovic|senj-marriage-1739-05-francisca-bexilva-antonia-daughter-of-jule-tomjanovic-line.jpg||Senj, 14 May 1739 — Antonia Tomljanović bride 1739|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 22, right-hand page, image 22R, third entry (faded)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4DX|«Na 14 Maya Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Franciska Bexilva? skherom K: Jule Tom-yanovicha imenom Antoniu a to po zapovidi Gna Vikara d'Cholich, Kim bi ja svidoka Ive Borkovich, Jure Melarovich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 22 right page (page 16 of the book), the third entry. Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale; the line is FADED (the whole entry is lighter than its neighbours and the groom's name is not read with certainty), and the bride's father's surname, broken across two lines, is read as «Tomjanovicha» with a query. If so, a second Tomljanović bride of 1738–39, the daughter of a Jule (Julije?) Tomjanović, after Klara daughter of Vule Tomjanović in February 1738 (image 18L); the two fathers may be one man NOTE added at 23R: «K.» before a Tomjanović name is probably «Kanonik» (a canon): on image 23R (2 Oct 1739) a «Kanonik Titular Pop Pave Tomjenovich» is the celebrant, so this Tomljanović family of 1738–39 is a family of Senj priests or nobles, not a town household of the later registers.|antonia-tomljanovic-bride-1739|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1739-10-franu-parskovic-klara-celebrant-pop-pave-tomjanovic-canon|senj-marriage-1739-10-franu-parskovic-klara-celebrant-pop-pave-tomjanovic-canon-line.jpg||Senj, 2 October 1739 («gbra») — Pave Tomljanović canon officiating priest 1739|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 23, right-hand page, image 23R, third entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L4CZ|«Na 2 [gbra]: Po prispuschenju Plovanskomu Kanonik Titular Pop Pave Tomjenovich zakupi u sti Matrimoniy Franu Parskovicha, Judovom Pok: Mike Bukovca imenom Klaru, Kim bi ja svidoka David Hrehanovich i Anton Baftanci.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 23 right page (page 17 of the book), the third entry. Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale. «Po prispuschenju Plovanskomu» is «with the permission of the parish priest»: the celebrant is a canon, Pop Pave Tomljanović — and so the «K. Pave Tomjanovich» who is the witness of the marriages of 18L (Feb 1738) and 20R (1738) is very probably the same canon («K.» = Kanonik), and the «K. Vule Tomjanovicha» of 18L (the bride Klara's father) is perhaps a canon too, a Tomjanović priest or a noble («K.» standing before his name). The surname is read as Tomjenovich; the first name Pave is read with a query (the line shows «Pop Jure/Pave»)|pave-tomljanovic-canon-officiating-priest-1739|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1741-01-boric-of-hrizina-barbara-daughter-of-loncan-of-bakar|senj-marriage-1741-01-boric-of-hrizina-barbara-daughter-of-loncan-of-bakar-line.jpg||Senj, January 1741 (day read «15») — Borić groom 1741|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 26, left-hand page, image 26L, first entry of 1741|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LW1R|«Na 15 Jenvara Ja Pop Luka Kuhacevich Plovan zakupih u sti Matrimoniy [..] Boricha od hrizina skherom Loncan od Bakra imenom Barbarom, Kim bi [ja svidoka …].» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 26 left page, the first entry under the year 1741 (the priest is now Pop Luka Kuhacevich). Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale; the first words of the line are lost in the gutter of the book (the groom's Christian name is not seen), and the place after «od» is read as «hrizina» with a query. Borić is a listed surname|boric-groom-1741|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1742-01-pero-tomjanovic-margarita-celebrated-by-his-brother-pop-marko-tomjanovic|senj-marriage-1742-01-pero-tomjanovic-margarita-celebrated-by-his-brother-pop-marko-tomjanovic-line.jpg||Senj, 18 January 1742 — Pero Tomljanović groom 1742|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 28, right-hand page, image 28R, second entry of 1742|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L44W|«Na 18 Genvara Pop Marko Tomjanovich dopuschenjam Plovanskim zakupi u sti Matrimoniy svoga brata Pera Tomjanovicha skherom Pok: Tome Dopenovicha imenom Margarita, Kim bi ja svidoka Gdicich Felica d'Vukasovich i Gdicich Perica d'Vukasovich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 28 right page (page 22 of the book), the second entry from the top, under the year 1742. Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale (the whole line is legible, in a faded page). A priest, Pop Marko Tomljanović, marries «his brother Pero Tomljanović» with the permission of the parish priest — the Tomljanović of Senj of 1738–42 are a family of priests: Pave (a titular canon, 1739), Perica (a canon, 1741), Marko (1742) and their brother Pero. The first Tomljanović marriage of a layman in the volume; compare the Tomljanović deaths of 1834–58 (images 506–585) of a later, town household — the register joins none of them|pero-tomljanovic-groom-1742|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1741-11-franu-roxanic-widow-celebrated-by-canon-perica-tomjanovic|senj-marriage-1741-11-franu-roxanic-widow-celebrated-by-canon-perica-tomjanovic-line.jpg||Senj, November 1741 («..stra», read as «18 8bra»?) — Perica Tomljanović canon celebrant 1741|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 27, right-hand page, image 27R, entry after 9 October 1741|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4Z8|«Na 18 8bra: Kan: Pop Perica Tomjanovich zakupi u sti Matrimoniy Franu Roxanicha, judovom Pokoy: Elize Celovicha imenom Mandu, Kimbi ja svidoka Bogmestar Gn: Pave Hrehanovich, Gn: Bogmestar Jos Dimeli.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 27 right page (page 21 of the book), the entry after the one of 9 October. Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale; the day and month are read with a query, and the bride's name after «imenom» is «Mandu» (Magdalena). The celebrant, «Kan: Pop Perica Tomjanovich», is a canon and priest of the Tomljanović of Senj of this decade (Pave in 1739, image 23R; Marko and his brother Pero in 1742, image 28R); the register does not say that the three priests are brothers, but names Marko's brother Pero|perica-tomljanovic-canon-celebrant-1741|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1746-01-antona-papic-jelena-of-grobnik|senj-marriage-1746-01-antona-papic-jelena-of-grobnik-line.jpg||Senj, 30 January 1746 — Antona Papić groom 1746|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 38, left-hand page, image 38L, fourth entry of 1746|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LW1R|«Na 30 Genvara Zakupih Ja Plovan Kuhacevich Matrimoniy Antona Papicha skherom Fra[..]voticha iz Grobnika imenom Jelenu, Kim bi ja svidoka Marko Marusich i Ivan Simac.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 38 left page, the fourth entry under the year 1746 (the year heading «1746» stands above the entry of 16 January). Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale: the end of every line of the left page is cut by the edge of the window and the bride's father's Christian name and surname are only in part visible. A PAPIĆ groom — Papić is a listed surname, and the Papić bride of 1747 (image 43R) is the next such entry; the second entry of the same page, three lines below, has a Lovro Papić as witness at the marriage of Martin Gurfinić of 3 February 1746 (the lines are cut at the edge)|antona-papic-groom-1746|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1746-06-mate-butkovic-of-brinje|senj-marriage-1746-06-mate-butkovic-of-brinje-line.jpg||Senj, 12 June 1746 — Mate Butković groom of Brinje 1746|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 39, left-hand page, image 39L, last entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4MG|«Na 12 Junja Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Mate Butkovicha skherom [..], obadva iz Briny imenom [..], Kim bi ja svidoka Marko Tomyanovich i Marko Butorac po uvdinu Gna: Vice Vikara i Arki[popa] …sticha.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 39 left page, the last entry. Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale: the bride's name is cut by the page's right edge and the neighbouring tile had not loaded; «obadva iz Briny» is read with a query as «both of Brinje». Butković is a listed surname: the earliest Butković groom of the Senj marriage volume after the Butković bride of 1735 and the groom of Karlobag of 1736 (images 10R, 12L); the witness Marko Tomjanović is a Tomljanović (the Tomljanović of Senj of this decade include three priests: images 23R, 27R, 28R)|mate-butkovic-groom-of-brinje-1746|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1747-05-matia-spalj-lieutenant-of-krmpote-barbara-simanic|senj-marriage-1747-05-matia-spalj-lieutenant-of-krmpote-barbara-simanic-line.jpg||Senj, 28 May 1747 — Matia Špalj lieutenant of Krmpote groom 1747|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 42, right-hand page, image 42R, fourth entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4XW|«Na 28 Maya Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy G: Matia Spalyj Lajtmanta od Kermpot skherom K. Jure Simanicha imenom Barbaru, Kim bi ja svidoka Oberstar otoske Einiftayne i Cap Jve Aichelburg.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 42 right page (page 36 of the book), the fourth entry. Read in the STRIP PASS and cropped at page scale (the whole line is legible). A ŠPALJ groom, and a Krmpote man: Lieutenant Matia Špalj of the Krmpote company, with the colonel of the Otočac regiment (and Captain Aichelburg) as witnesses — so an officer of the border regiment at Krmpote in 1747. Špalj and Krmpote are both listed; the only Špalj of the volume before this is the bride of 1820 (image 209–213) and the Spal deaths of 1820–1836 (images 490R–495R)|matia-spalj-lieutenant-of-krmpote-groom-1747|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1748-04-jou-rokovic-of-lovran-katarina-daughter-of-matiya-babic|senj-marriage-1748-04-jou-rokovic-of-lovran-katarina-daughter-of-matiya-babic-line.jpg||Senj, 29 April 1748 — Katarina Babić of Sv Juraj bride 1748|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 45, left-hand page, image 45L, fifth entry of 1748|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4W8|«Na 29 Aprila Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Jou Rokovicha od Lovrana skherom Matiya Babicha od Sv: Jurya imenom Katarinu [..], Kim bi ja svidoka Anton Jaxich i Osin Bontich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 45 left page, the fifth entry (the year 1748, begun on 44L). Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale; the end of every line is cut at the edge of the window and the bride's mother is not named. A BABIĆ father, Matiya Babić of Sv. Juraj (St George; a village of the Senj coast, the parish of the Otočac regiment of the 1854 widow Margaritha Pilipić of «S. Georgio in regimine Ottocano», image 561R) — the earliest Babić of the Senj marriage volume|katarina-babic-of-sv-juraj-bride-1748|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1750-08-frano-kulbiric-maria-daughter-of-mike-butkovic-of-savil|senj-marriage-1750-08-frano-kulbiric-maria-daughter-of-mike-butkovic-of-savil-line.jpg||Senj, 3 August 1750 — Matiya Butković of Savil bride 1750|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 50, left-hand page, image 50L, entry of 3 August|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LWTG|«Na 3 Agusta Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Frana Kolbinicha skherom Mik[e] Butkovicha if Savil imenom Matiya, Kim bi ja svidoka Martin Biltan i Marko Dubravichia.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 50 left page, the second entry from the foot of the third group of the page (the entries are of 14 and 31 July, and 3, 7 and 28 August 1750). Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale; the end of the lines is cut at the edge of the window, and the bride's Christian name is read with a query (the line ends «imenom Matiya»). A BUTKOVIĆ father, Mike (Mihovil) Butković of Savil — the third Butković household in the Senj marriage volume (the bride's father Mikula Butković of Ledenice, 1735; Franjo Butković of Karlobag, 1736; Mate Butković of Brinje, 1746)|matiya-butkovic-of-savil-bride-1750|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1751-10-jure-tommyanovic-widower-mandalena|senj-marriage-1751-10-jure-tommyanovic-widower-mandalena-line.jpg||Senj, 13 October 1751 («gbra») — Jure Tomljanović groom 1751|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 51, left-hand page, image 51L, second entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4C3|«Na 13 8bra Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Jura Tommyanovicha judovom Pok: Antona Fabianicha imenom Mandalenu, Kim bi ja svidoka K. Jure Malagrudichia i Ive Rucich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 51 left page, the second entry from the top, under the year 1751 (the entry above is of 1 October). Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale; «judovom Pok: Antona Fabianicha» is the widow of the late Anton Fabianić, so the BRIDE is the widow and Jure Tomljanović the groom, and the line is read with a query on who is the widow. The «K.» before the witness's name is a title (Kanonik or Kapitan). A Tomljanović LAYMAN of the Senj marriage volume — the family that supplied three priests in 1739–42 (images 23R, 27R, 28R), and the Pero Tomljanović who married in 1742|jure-tomljanovic-groom-1751|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1752-10-jakov-boric-urshula-daughter-of-matia-ugrin-of-bribir|senj-marriage-1752-10-jakov-boric-urshula-daughter-of-matia-ugrin-of-bribir-line.jpg||Senj, 30 October 1752 («gbra») — Jakov Borić groom 1752|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 56, right-hand page, image 56R, last entry of 1752|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L47N|«Na 30 gbra. Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Jakova Boreicha shherom Matia Ugrina ig Bribira imenom Urshula, Kim bi ja svi[doka …].» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries of the parish priest Kuhacevich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 56 right page (page 50 of the book), the entry before the year heading «1753». Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale (the line is legible; the witnesses fall on the next line and are not read). A BORIĆ groom: Borić is a listed surname; the month is abbreviated «gbra» and read as October because the previous entries on the page are of 19 and 26 October and the following one of 30 October|jakov-boric-groom-1752|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1762-04-canon-petar-tomljanovic-celebrant|senj-marriage-1762-04-canon-petar-tomljanovic-celebrant-line.jpg||Senj, 24 April 1762 — Petar Tomljanović canon celebrant 1762|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 69, left-hand page, image 69L, last entry of April 1762|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LWT1|«Na 24. Eň. Canonik T. Petar Tomlyanovich zdruxi u S. Matrimony Gna Maria [?] Osipa Vrinyanin za Udovu Klaru Pasquich. Kon… Svidoki bihu F. Vice Preses Juray Homolich, i Eň: Canciler Juray Danicich.» (Eň = Erdodni? the abbreviation is of «Ervoredni»: Reverend). The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 69 left page (page 59 of the book), the last entry of April 1762 — the first entry under the heading «Aprilis» is of 19 April; the book from 1761 is a Latin-script Croatian register of the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich. Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale: the end of the first line is cut by the edge of the window («Gna …aria Osipa Vrinyanin»: the groom is a Josip Vrinjanin and the bride the widow Klara Pasquich). Pave (1739), Perica (1741) and Marko (1742) Tomljanović were priests of Senj; Petar Tomljanović is a canon in 1762, twenty years later|petar-tomljanovic-canon-celebrant-1762|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1763-12-mate-kohe-margarita-witness-jura-butkovic|senj-marriage-1763-12-mate-kohe-margarita-witness-jura-butkovic-line.jpg||Senj, December 1763 («Decembar») — Jura Butković witness 1763|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 71, right-hand page, image 71R, entry under Decembar|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L47V|«Ĺn kanonik Luka de Vranyanin zdruxi u S. Matrimony Mate Koh[e]cicha za kchier Pok. Mache Pasquana imenom Margarita, kim svidoki bihu Ive Baschian i Jura Butkovich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries in Latin script of the canons and the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich, 1761–; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 71 right page (page 65 of the book), the first entry under the heading «Decembar». Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale (the whole line is legible; the groom's surname is divided across a line break and is read with a query). The celebrant is the canon Luka de Vranyanin. A BUTKOVIĆ witness, Jura (Juraj) Butković, at Senj in 1763 — the third mention of a Butković in the volume (1735, 1736, 1746, 1750)|jura-butkovic-witness-1763|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1764-01-andrea-deskovic-ursula-witness-tome-vukelic|senj-marriage-1764-01-andrea-deskovic-ursula-witness-tome-vukelic-line.jpg||Senj, 7 January 1764 — Tome Vukelić witness 1764|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 71, right-hand page, image 71R, first entry of 1764|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L47V|«Na 7. Ĺn. Kanonik Luka de Vranyanin zdruxi u S. Matrimoniy Andreu Deskovichia za kchier Jakova Mihlystichia imenom Ursulu, kim svidoki bihu Tome Vukelyich, i Ivan Velich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries in Latin script of the canons and the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich, 1761–; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 71 right page, the first entry under the year heading «1764». Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale (the whole line is legible; the groom's and the bride's father's names are read with a query). A VUKELIĆ witness, Tome Vukelić, at Senj in January 1764 — the earliest Vukelić of the volume|tome-vukelic-witness-1764|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1764-09-canon-petar-tomljanovic-celebrates|senj-marriage-1764-09-canon-petar-tomljanovic-celebrates-line.jpg||Senj, September 1764 — Petar Tomljanović canon celebrant 1764|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 72, right-hand page, image 72R, entry under Septembar|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4S6|«Ĺn Kanonik T: Petar Tomlyanovich zdruxi u S. Matrimony K. Antona Pasquich za Gna Matta Udovu Lakovich. Kim Svidoki bihu Gn Capitan Wolfango Homolich, i Gn Canciler Juray de Danicich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries in Latin script of the canons and the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 72 right page (page 64 of the book), the entry under the heading «Septembar». Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale (the whole line is legible). The second entry in the volume to name Canon Petar Tomljanović as celebrant (24 April 1762, image 69L); a Tomljanović priest of Senj in 1762–64|petar-tomljanovic-canon-celebrant-1764|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1764-11-juraj-verbanic-widow-of-anton-butkovic-matija|senj-marriage-1764-11-juraj-verbanic-widow-of-anton-butkovic-matija-line.jpg||Senj, 24 November 1764 — Matija widow of Anton Butković bride 1764|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 73, left-hand page, image 73L, third entry under November|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L44Z|«Na 24: Ĺn Pop Vicko Marinich zdruxi u S. Matrimonij Udovca Jurja Verbanich za udovu P. Antona Butkovich imenom Mattia. [Kim…] ovitse pozakonise prez svakoga navovidanya, kim svidoki bihu Primus Fabian i Mattiy Sray.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries in Latin script of the canons and the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 73 left page (page 65 of the book), the third entry under the heading «November» (the entries before are of 12 and 24 November). Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale (the whole line is legible; the bride's Christian name is read with a query, the line has a deleted «kim» and a note «B. ovitse pozakonise prez svakoga navovidanya» — «married lawfully without banns»). A BUTKOVIĆ: the widow of the late Anton Butković, so an Anton Butković had lived and died at Senj before 1764 — the fifth Butković of the Senj marriage volume|matija-widow-of-anton-butkovic-bride-1764|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1765-12-mihovil-vukelic-bride-widow-of-mikula-tomjenovic-magdalena|senj-marriage-1765-12-mihovil-vukelic-bride-widow-of-mikula-tomjenovic-magdalena-line.jpg||Senj, 17 December 1765 (the entry is the last of the page; the 1765 headings are above) — Mihovil Vukelić groom 1765|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 74, left-hand page, image 74L, last entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L4MT|«Na 17: Ĺn Pri: Aki=pop, i Plovan, i Vikar Kapitular zdruxi u S. Matrimony polak pisma Vikarskoga quamvis mihi non constet de libertate … u Soebi A Mihovila Vukelich albi Biordichia za Udovu Mikule Tomjenovichia imenom Mandalenu. Kim svidoki bihu Jure Babich, i Jerko Biordich. NB: Supra nominatus Brijt [Brid?] Scribit mihi se habere attestationes libertatis supra nominatorum, ab aliorum respective Parochis absque ulla denunciatione.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries in Latin script of the canons and the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 74 left page, the last entry of the page. Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale (the two main lines are legible; the preceding line and the clause on the freedom from banns are partly abbreviated). A VUKELIĆ groom (Mihovil Vukelić, also known as Biordić), the widow of a Mikula TOMLJANOVIĆ as bride, and a BABIĆ witness (Jure Babić) in the same line — three listed surnames at once, in December 1765|mihovil-vukelic-groom-1765|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1766-02-matu-babic-katarina-daughter-of-jure-sablic|senj-marriage-1766-02-matu-babic-katarina-daughter-of-jure-sablic-line.jpg||Senj, early February 1766 (heading «Februarius», the 2nd?) — Mate Babić groom 1766|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 75, right-hand page, image 75R, second entry of February 1766|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4HH|«Na [2?]: Ĺn Pop Martin Pasquan zdruxi u S. Matrimony Matu Babich za kchier Jure Sablichia imenom katarinu, kim svidoki bihu Matea Bakich, i Elia Malinarich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries in Latin script of the canons and the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 75 right page (page 67 of the book), the second entry under the heading «Februarius» (the day is read with a query). Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale (the whole line is legible). A BABIĆ groom, Mate Babić — the second Babić of the volume after the father Matiya Babić of Sv. Juraj (1748, image 45L), and the next generation of the Babić who appear as witnesses in 1765 (Jure Babić, image 74L)|mate-babic-groom-1766|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1766-06-jurja-sayfon-maru-witness-tome-vukelic|senj-marriage-1766-06-jurja-sayfon-maru-witness-tome-vukelic-line.jpg||Senj, 18 June 1766 — Tome Vukelić witness 1766|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 76, left-hand page, image 76L, entry of 18 June 1766|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4H2|«Na 18: Ĺn Pop Tome Jankovich zdruxi u S. Matrimony Jurja Zayfon za kchier Mike Paganeto imenom Maru, kim svidoki bihu Tome Vukelich, i Anton Jetich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries in Latin script of the canons and the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 76 left page, the first entry under the year 1766 (the entry above is the end of a May entry). Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale. A VUKELIĆ witness, Tome Vukelić — the same name as the Tome Vukelić of 7 January 1764 (image 71R), two and a half years later; the register does not say they are the same man|tome-vukelic-witness-1766|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1766-11-iliya-vukelic-of-sv-jurja-widow-vicenca|senj-marriage-1766-11-iliya-vukelic-of-sv-jurja-widow-vicenca-line.jpg||Senj, 15 November 1766 («Na 15», under «Novembar») — Ilija Vukelić of Sv Juraj groom 1766|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 77, left-hand page, image 77L, second entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4SJ|«Na 15: Ĺn Pop Osip Kucanich zdruxi u Matrimoniy Iliyu Vukelichia od Sv: Jurya za udovu P. Felica Flako…ynei? imenom Vicenca. Kim svidoki bihu [Anton …]sich, i [Anton] …vich, Ive Barchich, i Ive Smolcich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries in Latin script of the canons and the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 77 left page (page 69 of the book), the second entry of the page. Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale (the first two lines are legible; the end of each line is cut by the right edge and by the black margin of the film). A VUKELIĆ groom of Sv. Juraj (St George, a village of the Senj coast and a parish of the Otočac regiment) — Ilija Vukelić; with Tome (1764, 1766) and Mihovil (1765) the fourth Vukelić of the volume within three years|ilija-vukelic-of-sv-juraj-groom-1766|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1767-02-bernardo-frakasa-antonija-pop-fabre-vuklic|senj-marriage-1767-02-bernardo-frakasa-antonija-pop-fabre-vuklic-line.jpg||Senj, 7 February 1767 — Pop Fabre Vuklić celebrant 1767|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 78, left-hand page, image 78L, under Februarius 1767|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4QQ|«Na 7. Ĺn Pop Fabre Vuklich zdruxi u Matrimony Bernarda Frakassa za kchier P. Marka Tomkuch? imenom Antoniyu. Svidoki bihu Ivan Dubravcich, i Anton Dubravcich. NB Frakassa ni imal svoga slobochine, nego po Sv Vikara vogli bi paraloynan.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries in Latin script of the canons and the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 78 left page, under the heading «Februarius» (the entry stands under the 1767 heading of 77R). Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale: the celebrant's surname «Vuklich» and the bride's father's surname «Tomkuch» are both read with a query — «Vuklich» may be a spelling of Vukelić (a priest of the name), «Tom…» may be Tomljanović. NOT recorded as a certain reading of either surname; kept as a possible Vukelić and Tomljanović|pop-fabre-vuklic-celebrant-1767|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1767-03-toma-carofiglio-margarita-witness-ivan-butkovic|senj-marriage-1767-03-toma-carofiglio-margarita-witness-ivan-butkovic-line.jpg||Senj, early March 1767 (the entry is the third of the page headed «Martius») — Ivan Butković witness 1767|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 79, left-hand page, image 79L, third entry under Martius|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L4MT|«Na 2: Ĺn Pop Sima Debya zdruxi u Matrimoniy Toma Carofiglio od [Pri…] za kchier P. Jure … imenom Margarita Mattrovic …, kim svidoci bihu Ivan Butkovich i Anto[n Kovacich].» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Croatian entries in Latin script of the canons and the Vicar General Carlo de Wkassovich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 79 left page, the third entry under the heading «Martius». Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale: the end of every line is lost to the cut at the right edge of the left page, so the groom's origin, the bride's father and the second witness are not read. A BUTKOVIĆ witness, Ivan Butković, in March 1767; with Jura Butković (December 1763, image 71R) and the widow of Anton Butković (1764, image 73L) the Butković of Senj in the 1760s|ivan-butkovic-witness-1767|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1754-10-martin-eikovic-anna-daughter-of-mihe-sojat|senj-marriage-1754-10-martin-eikovic-anna-daughter-of-mihe-sojat-line.jpg||Senj, 5 October 1754 («8bra») — Anna Šojat bride 1754|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 62, right-hand page, image 62R, October 1754 entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LW5Y|«[Na] 5: 8bra: zakupi u sti Matrimony Plovan Juraj Homolich Martina Eikovicha shke[rom] rom Annom Mihe Sojata, kumi Marko Coshran, i Anzak Danicic …» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the cramped Latin-script hand of the priest Juraj Homolić, 1753–60; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 62 right page (page 56 of the book), in the group under the year 1754, after the entry of 8 May. Read in the STRIP PASS at page scale: the hand is very cramped and several words are guessed (the groom's surname begins with a letter that may be E, S or T; the bride's father is read as «Mihe Sojata»; the witnesses are partly illegible). A ŠOJAT father, Mihe (Mihovil) Šojat, in 1754 — between the witness Božo Šojat (1737, image 15R) and the Šojat groom Mihu Sojata of 10 October 1745 (image 37L): probably the same man as the groom of 1745, who would then have a daughter of marriageable age nine years later, which the register does not say|anna-sojat-bride-1754|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1754-01-anton-tomljanovic-named-in-entry-58r-top|senj-marriage-1754-01-anton-tomljanovic-named-in-entry-58r-top-line.jpg||Senj, early January 1754 (under the heading «Leta 1754 na 6 Jenvara») — Anton Tomljanović named in an entry of 1754|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 58, right-hand page, image 58R, first entry|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L47L|«[Leta 1754 na 6: Jenvara] … zakupi u sti Matrimony Primancer Juraj Homolich [..]marinaricha Anton Tomlyenovichkom, bi svidok [..]ick, Fraron Subatom.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the cramped hand of the priest Juraj Homolić, 1753–60; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 58 right page (page 52 of the book), the first entry. Read in the SECOND PASS, at about 2x of the page (a quarter of a page wide per view: the first pass at page scale had not made it out). The role of Anton Tomljanović is not established: the surname is clear and the Christian name «Anton», but the line is the end of an entry that starts on the foot of the left page, and the groom's and bride's names fall in the gutter; he may be the bride's father or a witness. The Tomljanović of Senj are the family of priests of 1739–42 (images 23R, 27R, 28R) and the canon Petar (1762–64, images 69L, 72R)|anton-tomljanovic-named-in-an-entry-of-1754|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1754-02-josip-kosovic-anna-daughter-of-the-late-ivan-blazevic|senj-marriage-1754-02-josip-kosovic-anna-daughter-of-the-late-ivan-blazevic-line.jpg||Senj, 14 February 1754 — Anna Blažević bride of Josip Kosović 1754|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 59, left-hand page, image 59L, entry of 14 February 1754|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LW5F|«Na 14: Gn Pop Anton Vratkovich zakupi u sti Matrimony dopustkom Plovanskim Josipa Kosovicha, [shkerom] pokoynoga Ivana Blaxevicha imenom Annom, bi svidok Gn Vicko Homolich, … Juron Kognica?» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the cramped hand of the priest Juraj Homolić and his curates, 1753–60; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 59 left page (page 53 of the book), the entry of 14 February 1754 under the heading «1754». Read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x of the page (the first pass at page scale, which only made out «Kosovicha» and «Blaxevicha» as unclear words). The page enlarged on this entry shows «pokoynoga Ivana Blaxevicha»: a BLAŽEVIĆ at Senj in 1754 — the bride's father, already dead; the groom's surname is read as Kosović and the word before «dopustkom» is the celebrating priest. A Blažević daughter's marriage at Senj in 1754 is a new piece of evidence for the Blažević of this archive, a few years before the Blažević widow Anna of March 1768 and the Blažević grooms of 1769 and 1779 (see the Blažević list in the note); the register does not say where the Blažević family lived|anna-blazevic-bride-of-josip-kosovic-1754|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1790-08-georgius-tomljan-otocac-soldier-martha-filipovic-of-krmpote|senj-marriage-1790-08-georgius-tomljan-otocac-soldier-martha-filipovic-of-krmpote-line.jpg||Senj, end of August 1790 (banns of 15, 22 and 29 August; entry under the heading «Mense Augusti») — Georgius Tomljan soldier of the Otočac regiment groom 1790|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 141, right-hand page, image 141R, first entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LW5G|«Josephus Cithkovich Cooperator Parochiae Segniensis conjunxit in Matrimonium Georgium Tomljan ex Pos[sessione?] [..] Sablanicenii Legionis Ottochensis militem gregarium, et Marthan Philipowich origine Krmpotersem [= Kermpotensem?] praemissis tribus Denuntiationibus 15, 22 [et 29] Aug., Testibus Michaele Jomanich Leg. Ottochensis [..], et Domino Segot.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819, the Latin numbered entries of 1790 («Copulati in Civitate Segniae de anno 1790», entries by the cooperators Georgius Milanes, Paulus Markovich and Josephus Cithkovich; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 141 right page (page 143 of the book), the first entry of the right page, before the entry numbered 343. Read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x of the page (the first pass had read this page at 0.75 and had not made the surname out). A TOMLJAN — Tomljanović in its short form, read with a query — a soldier of the Otočac regiment marrying a bride of KRMPOTE origin, in 1790. Krmpote is the home village of the Krmpotić and the place where the 1855 Grenzer Georgius Tomljanović (image 572L) and the Špalj lieutenant of 1747 (image 42R) lived: a Tomljanović of Krmpote line, at Senj, 65 years before|georgius-tomljan-soldier-of-the-otocac-regiment-groom-1790,martha-filipovic-of-krmpote-bride-1790|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1793-04-thomas-pavelic-magdalena|senj-marriage-1793-04-thomas-pavelic-magdalena-line.jpg||Senj, April 1793 (banns of 31 March and 7 April; entry 167, under the heading «Mense Aprilis», page 138 of the book) — Thomas Pavelić groom 1793|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 149, right-hand page, image 149R, first entry of April 1793|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LW98|«167. Philippus de Vukasovich C.E. legt. [= legis?] Canus Cath. conjunxit in Matrimonium Thomam Pavelich [..] in bina partibus ab infantia coruntum [?], et Magdalenam [Burelich?], denuntiatos 31 Martii et 7 Aprilis, Testibus Georgio Svetich et Vincentio [..].» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819, the Latin numbered entries of 1793 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 149 right page (page 138 of the book), the first entry under «Mense Aprilis». Read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x of a third of the page (the first pass at 0.75 had not made the surname out). PAVELIĆ is a listed surname: a Pavelić groom at Senj in April 1793; the phrase after the name, in the right margin, is cut by the edge of the window and the film's black margin, so the bride's surname and the second witness are not read. The registers of this archive at Senj name no earlier Pavelić|thomas-pavelic-groom-1793|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1814-01-thomas-starich-maria-spalj|senj-marriage-1814-01-thomas-starich-maria-spalj-line.jpg||Senj, 23 January 1814 (the entry number 23 of the year, under the heading «Anno 1814 — Mense Januario») — Maria Špalj bride 1814|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 195, left-hand page, image 195L, entry 23 of January 1814|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LWM5|«23. Carolus Vranich Coop. loci conjunxit in Matrimonium [praemissis tribus] denuntiationibus Thomam Ofarich [Starich?] et Mariam Spalj, testibus Blasio Ofarich et Carolo Helpho[..].» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Latin numbered entries of the cooperator Carolus Vranich, 1813–14; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 195 left page, the last-but-one entry of the page. Read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x of the lower part of the left page (the first pass at 0.75 had not made the surname out). A Maria ŠPALJ, a bride at Senj in January 1814 — the Špalj entries of the volume were the Lieutenant Matia Špalj of Krmpote (1747, image 42R), this bride (1814), the Špalj bride of 1820 and the Spal/Spalj deaths of 1820–36. Whether the second name is Starić or Čarić (or another) is not read with certainty; the Špalj bride is|maria-spalj-bride-1814|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1814-autumn-georgius-babic-citizen-of-sv-juraj-mathia-butkovic|senj-marriage-1814-autumn-georgius-babic-citizen-of-sv-juraj-mathia-butkovic-line.jpg||Senj, autumn 1814 (under the heading «Mense Octobris»?; the day is not read) — Georgius Babić groom 1814|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 196, right-hand page, image 196R, fifth entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-L7TT|«Idem conjunxit in Matrimonium [praemissis tribus] denuntiationibus Georgium Babich Civem [S.] Georgii et Mathiam Buthkovich Civem Principi[..]: fidelis [..] respectivi ex utraque parte… testes fuerunt Georgius Rampotich et Dominicus Padavich [?].» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Latin numbered entries of the cooperator Carolus Vranich, 1813–15; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 196 right page (page 181 of the book), the fifth entry of the page. Read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x of a third of the right page (the first pass at 0.75 had made out neither name). The same spread was photographed twice (images 196 and 197). A BABIĆ groom and a BUTKOVIĆ bride (surname read with a query: the second letter pair is «th» or «rk»), with a witness whose surname is read as a spelling of Krmpotić («Rampotich»/«Kumpotich», with a query): three of the families of this archive in one entry. Babić and Butković are both listed surnames|georgius-babic-groom-1814|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1815-06-franciscus-jurcic-joanna-babic|senj-marriage-1815-06-franciscus-jurcic-joanna-babic-line.jpg||Senj, June 1815 (entry 11, under the heading «Mense Junio», page 182 of the book) — Joanna Babić bride 1815|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 198, right-hand page, image 198R, entry 11 of June 1815|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L7LB|«11. Carolus Vranich Coop. loci conjunxit in Matrimonium praemissis tribus denuntiationibus Franciscum Jurcich et Joannam Babich, testes fuerunt Michael Lenaz et Matthaeus Stepanich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Latin numbered entries of the cooperator Carolus Vranich, 1813–16; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 198 right page, entry 11, just under the heading «Mense Junio». Read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x (the first pass at 0.75 had not made the surname out); the second name is clear. A BABIĆ BRIDE, Joanna, at Senj in June 1815 (the groom is a Jurčić, one of the very common Senj names kept as seen rows)|joanna-babic-bride-1815|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1815-autumn-franciscus-babic-of-novigrad-doima-babic|senj-marriage-1815-autumn-franciscus-babic-of-novigrad-doima-babic-line.jpg||Senj, autumn 1815 (second entry of the page, under the heading «Mense Octobri»; the day is not read) — Franciscus Babić of Novigrad groom 1815|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 199, left-hand page, image 199L, second entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-L751|«Idem conjunxit in Matrimonium praemissis tribus denuntiationibus Franciscum Babich Civem Novigradensem, ergo licentiam respectivi Parochi, et Doimam Babich, praesentibus testibus Rocho Sattin, et Philippo Babich Novigradensi.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Latin numbered entries of the cooperator Carolus Vranich, 1813–16; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 199 left page, the second entry of the page (the heading «Mense Octobri & Decembri vacat» follows below). Read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x. A BABIĆ groom of Novigrad (the Novigrad on the Adriatic coast near Senj), a BABIĆ bride Doima, and a BABIĆ witness, Philippus, in one entry — three Babić in an entry of 1815 — a household of Babić of Novigrad with Senj as the place of the wedding by licence of their parish priest|franciscus-babic-of-novigrad-groom-1815|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1816-05-josephus-hanich-maria-borach|senj-marriage-1816-05-josephus-hanich-maria-borach-line.jpg||Senj, May 1816 (entry 6, under the heading «Mense Majo»; the day is not read) — Maria Borach Boras query bride 1816|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 200, left-hand page, image 200L, entry 6 of May 1816|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LW7Z|«6. Carolus Vranich Coop. loci conjunxit in Matrimonium praevijs tribus denuntiationibus Josephum Hanich et Mariam Borach, testes fuerunt Georgius Paulacich et Vincentius Bichianich.» The Senj marriage register 1734–1819 (the Latin numbered entries of the cooperator Carolus Vranich, 1813–16; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 200 left page, the entry under the heading «Mense Majo» after «Martius & Aprilis vacat». Read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x. The bride's surname is «Borach» (the middle letter is an r in a looped hand, so «Boxach»/«Borach»): BORAS is a listed surname and its earlier Senj spellings were «Boras» and «Baraz» (images 349L and 533L); «Borach» is read as a possible Boras only with a query. If it is, this is the earliest Boras bride of the Senj marriage volume|maria-borach-boras-query-bride-1816|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1849-11-ivan-belobarbic-vincenca-gregoric|senj-marriage-1849-11-ivan-belobarbic-vincenca-gregoric-line.jpg||Senj, 18 November 1849 («dana 18 Studena»; the entry number 55 in the margin) — Ivan Belobarbić groom 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 345, right-hand page, image 345R, entry 55 of 1849|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L7WV|«1849. dana 18 Studena izdružih ja Toma Petrović? [Radović], Profesor c.k. Gimnazije Senske [..], u svetu Matrimoni mladića Ivu Belobarbić Flovanis? godišt. 22, sina Petra i Mare? … plovanie Senske, s Dvojkom Vincenom Gregorić godišt 20, … Vjerom Stjepana i pokojne ..» The Croatian-language marriage entries of Senj for 1849–51 (the tabular book of the parish; one long Croatian line per marriage, with the age of each spouse and the parents; the celebrant Toma Radovich, cooperator at Senj; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 345 right page, entry 55, after the entry of 21 October. Read in the SECOND PASS in quarter-page windows (about 2x of a half page; the first pass at page scale had caught only the name «Belobarbic» among the names). A BELOBARBIĆ GROOM: Ivan, aged 22 (born about 1827), son of a Petar Belobarbić — and a PETAR BELOBARBIĆ aged 68 died at Senj on 13 December 1849, four weeks later (image 535R, entry 96); the register does not say that the two are father and son, but the names agree. The first marriage of a Belobarbić in the volume; compare the Belobarbić marriage of 1852 noted on image 349|ivan-belobarbic-groom-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-marriage-1849-10-josip-pavetic|senj-marriage-1849-10-josip-pavetic-line.jpg||Senj, 21 October 1849 («dana 21 Listopada»; entry 52–53 on the page) — Josip Pavetić groom 1849|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 345, right-hand page, image 345R, entry of 21 October 1849|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-L7WV|«1849. dana 21 Listopada izdružih ja Toma Radović, kapelan, u svetu Matrimoni mladića Josipa Pavetich, godišt 24, sina pokojnoga Jure i pokojne Luce Pavetich, plovanie Senske, s Dvojkom Ozrom Luicich, godišt 20 … [Berbelić? Baški] na prvie svidokov: Pime Pavetich, Fejak? [and] Frane Šković, Postolar.» The Croatian-language marriage entries of Senj for 1849–51 (the tabular book of the parish; one long Croatian line per marriage, with the age of each spouse and the parents; the celebrant Toma Radovich, cooperator at Senj; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 345 right page, the entry above entry 55. Read in the SECOND PASS in quarter-page windows. PAVELIĆ is a listed surname and «Pavetich» is read with a query as a spelling of it (the third letter of the name in this hand is a «t» or a looped «l», and the same name is written twice in the entry): a Pavelić (or Pavetić) groom of the Senj parish in October 1849, with the witness Pime (Pere?) Pavetić|josip-pavetic-groom-1849|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1824-07-matthaeus-son-of-joannes-pilipic|senj-death-1824-07-matthaeus-son-of-joannes-pilipic-line.jpg||Senj, 11 July [1824] — Matthaeus Pilipić child died Senj July 1824|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 473, left-hand page, page 128, first entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHPQ|«11 Julii obiit Matthaeum filium Joannis Pilipich aetatis annorum circiter —.» One of the abbreviated one-line death entries of 1820–30 of the Senj death register (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848, the P section, page 128; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 473 left page, read in the SECOND PASS in bands of about a fifth of the page (about 2x; the first pass at page scale had kept the whole page as a seen row). The year is read from the centred headings of the page (1825, 1826, 1827), which stand at the head of each year's entries|matthaeus-pilipic-child-died-senj-july-1824|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1826-09-stephana-daughter-of-joannes-pilipic|senj-death-1826-09-stephana-daughter-of-joannes-pilipic-line.jpg||Senj, 28 September 1826 — Stephana Pilipić daughter of Joannes died Senj September 1826|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 473, left-hand page, page 128, entry of 28 September 1826|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHPQ|«28 Septembris obiit Stephana filia Joannis Pilipich aetatis annorum — [52?].» One of the abbreviated one-line death entries of 1820–30 of the Senj death register (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848, the P section, page 128; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 473 left page, read in the SECOND PASS in bands of about a fifth of the page (about 2x; the first pass at page scale had kept the whole page as a seen row). The year is read from the centred headings of the page (1825, 1826, 1827), which stand at the head of each year's entries|stephana-pilipic-daughter-of-joannes-died-senj-september-1826|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1826-11-nicolaus-son-of-antonius-pilipic-aged-3|senj-death-1826-11-nicolaus-son-of-antonius-pilipic-aged-3-line.jpg||Senj, 8 November 1826 — Nicolaus Pilipić aged 3 died Senj November 1826|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 473, left-hand page, page 128, entry of 8 November 1826|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHPQ|«8 Novemb. obiit Nicolaus filius Antonii Pilipich aetatis annorum — 3.» One of the abbreviated one-line death entries of 1820–30 of the Senj death register (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848, the P section, page 128; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 473 left page, read in the SECOND PASS in bands of about a fifth of the page (about 2x; the first pass at page scale had kept the whole page as a seen row). The year is read from the centred headings of the page (1825, 1826, 1827), which stand at the head of each year's entries|nicolaus-pilipic-aged-3-died-senj-november-1826|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1827-06-francisca-daughter-of-franciscus-pilipic|senj-death-1827-06-francisca-daughter-of-franciscus-pilipic-line.jpg||Senj, 5 June 1827 — Francisca Pilipić daughter of Franciscus died Senj June 1827|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 473, left-hand page, page 128, last entry of the page|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHPQ|«5 Junii obiit Francisca filia Francisci Pilipich aetatis annorum —.» One of the abbreviated one-line death entries of 1820–30 of the Senj death register (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848, the P section, page 128; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 473 left page, read in the SECOND PASS in bands of about a fifth of the page (about 2x; the first pass at page scale had kept the whole page as a seen row). The year is read from the centred headings of the page (1825, 1826, 1827), which stand at the head of each year's entries|francisca-pilipic-daughter-of-franciscus-died-senj-june-1827|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1830-anna-daughter-of-joannes-pilipic-aged-1|senj-death-1830-anna-daughter-of-joannes-pilipic-aged-1-line.jpg||Senj, 1830 (day not read: «1[4]» September?) — Anna Pilipić aged 1 died Senj 1830|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 473, right-hand page, page 129, last entry (1830)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99C-LHPQ|«1[4] Sept. obiit Anna filia Joannis Pilipich anni 1.» One of the abbreviated one-line death entries of 1820–30 of the Senj death register (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848, the P section; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 473 right page, the last entry of the page, under the centred heading «1830». Read in the SECOND PASS in bands of about a fifth of the page (about 2x; the first pass at page scale had kept the page as a seen row). A child of a Joannes Pilipić — the same name as the father of Matthaeus (1824) and Stephana (1826) on image 473L|anna-pilipic-aged-1-died-senj-1830|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1831-02-gregorius-son-of-antonius-tomljanovic|senj-death-1831-02-gregorius-son-of-antonius-tomljanovic-line.jpg||Senj, February 1831 (the day is not read; the row is the first of the tabular page, «Anno 1831») — Gregorius Tomljanović son of Antonius died Senj February 1831|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 505, right-hand page, image 505R, first row|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHSQ|«Dies Februarii Anno 1831: Gregorius filius Antonii Tom-janovich et ejus legit. matris conjugis [..] natus ibidem Familiae Parochiae.» The tabular pages of the Senj death register (Matricula Defunctorum 1820–1848, the T section; columns Dies Mortis, Nomen et cognomen Defuncti, Aetas annorum, Morbus, Sacramenta, Locus sepulturae, Sepeliens, N°; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 505 right page (page 109), read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x of a fifth of the page, the first row under the column headings of the page, at the foot of the heading «Matricula Defunctorum». The row has no entries in the age, disease, sacrament and place columns; it names the child only by his father and mother, so he is an infant or was baptised and died at once. A son of an Antonius Tomljanović of Senj, born and died in the winter of 1830–31|gregorius-tomljanovic-son-of-antonius-died-senj-february-1831|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1832-03-clara-widow-tomljanovic-aged-60|senj-death-1832-03-clara-widow-tomljanovic-aged-60-line.jpg||Senj, 31 March 1832 («31 Martii» in the margin; the year «1832») — Clara Tomljanović widow aged 60 died Senj March 1832|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 505, right-hand page, image 505R, third row of 1832|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHSQ|«1832 31. Martii: Vidua Clara Tomjanovich conjux fuit defuncti Locumis [?] Thoma Tomjanovich, Anno 60, Consumptio, provisa, ad S. Petrum, [Maximilian? Sergalo?] Coop., N° 6.» The tabular pages of the Senj death register (Matricula Defunctorum 1820–1848, the T section; columns Dies Mortis, Nomen et cognomen Defuncti, Aetas annorum, Morbus, Sacramenta, Locus sepulturae, Sepeliens, N°; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 505 right page (page 109), read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x of a fifth of the page, the third row of 1832 (the previous rows are of 27 February «Matthaeus filius Joannis Thian» and 8 March «Laurentius Domini catholicus filius Thomae Thian»). The kinship words are read with a query: «Vidua Clara Tomjanovich, conjux fuit defuncti [Laurentii?] Thomae Tomjanovich» — a widow of 60 (born about 1772) whose husband, deceased, is named in the genitive, and a Thomas Tomljanović after him (a father-in-law or the husband's father or a second name of the husband). The first pass at page scale had kept this row as a seen row, with the spelling of the surname unsettled; the surname is now read: «Tomjanovich»|clara-tomljanovic-widow-aged-60-died-senj-march-1832|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1820-02-joannes-son-of-franciscus-perpic-after-emergency-baptism|senj-death-1820-02-joannes-son-of-franciscus-perpic-after-emergency-baptism-line.jpg||Senj, 29 February 1820 (the first entry under the centred heading 1820) — Joannes Perpić newborn died Senj February 1820|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 472, right-hand page, page 127, first line (1820)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LHQY|«29 Februarii obiit mox suscepto Sacro Baptismo Joannes filius Francisci Perpich —.» One of the abbreviated one-line death entries of 1820–30 of the Senj death register (Protocollum mortuorum 1820–1848, the P section, the first line of image 472 right page, directly under the heading «1820»; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P). Read in the SECOND PASS in bands of about a fifth of the page (about 2x; the first pass at page scale had kept the page as a seen row). A PERPIĆ — Perpić is the spelling this archive reads as Prpić — of Senj in 1820, the earliest entry of the name in the death register, sixteen years before the Perpich deaths of 1836–49 (images 489–490)|joannes-perpic-newborn-died-senj-february-1820|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-death-1834-10-andreas-perpic-aged-70|senj-death-1834-10-andreas-perpic-aged-70-line.jpg||Senj, 6 October 1834 (entry 27) — Andreas Perpić aged 70 died Senj October 1834|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 475, right-hand page, image 475R, entry 27|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99C-LH6Q|«1834 die 6 Octobris: Andreas Perpick, 70, Debilitas Virium, provisus, Ad S. Vitum, Biancini? Coop., N° 27.» One of the tabular rows of the Senj death register (Matricula Defunctorum 1820–1848, the P section; FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P), image 475 right page, entry 27. Read in the SECOND PASS at about 2x of a third of the page (the first pass at page scale had flagged this entry as a possible Prpić). A man born about 1764; the surname's second half is written «-pick»/«-pich» in a looped hand, so Perpić is a reading with a query|andreas-perpic-aged-70-died-senj-october-1834|14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-seen-26L-cubranic|senj-seen-26L-cubranic-line.jpg||Marriage 1741: Stipu Cubranicha (Zubranić?) x [..] Strapecha, early February 1741|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) 1734–1819, 1820–1858 and deaths 1820–1858 (FamilySearch waypoint 9RK1-W3P, 592 images)|image 26, left-hand page (whole page, read at page scale)|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-899C-LW1R|Image 26 left page, the last entry: «Na 2 Febraja Ja Plovan Kuhacevich zakupih u sti Matrimoniy Stipu Cubranicha skherom Pok: [..] Strapecha imenom [..], Kim bi ja svidoka [..] Stighich i Bastul Carich.» The groom's surname is written «Cubranicha» (a C, or a looped Z): read as Čubranić, and a possible early spelling of Žubrinić («Zubranich» of the 1849 Senj deaths and the Baška bride of 1850) only with a query — a seen row, not a found person, until the Žubrinić question of Senj is settled||14 October 2026|notes/senj-marriage-volume-walk.md
senj-birth-1886-milka-lucia-papic|senj-birth-1886-milka-lucia-papic-entry.jpg||Senj births, str. 122, entry 96 — Milka Lucia Papić, born 9 and baptised 17 October 1886|Senj births (Rođeni) 1878–1894 (FamilySearch waypoint 9R2D-JWL, 269 images)|image 140 of 269, left-hand page: entries 94–97, the date and name columns above and the parents' column of the right-hand page below|https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99X-1QDP|Entry 96: «1886 listopada 9. / 17.» — Milka Lucia — zakonita; parents (right-hand page): «Josip Papić, trhonoša, i Tonka rođ. Prpić», rim. kat. The month is written once, «listopada» (October), across both columns, so she was born 9 and baptised 17 October 1886. Entry 97 beneath it: «1886 listopada 27. / 31.» — Kate — parents «Jaso Špalj, težak, i Ana rođ. Prpić». The FamilySearch index of this volume gives Milka's dates as 9 and 17 NOVEMBER and Kate's as 27 November: it has read «listopada» as November (listopad is October; studeni is November). The tree's baptism date of 19 October is a slip for 17. Re-read 16 October 2026 from the image at full resolution; first read 10 September 2026.|milka-lucia-papic,josip-anton-papic,kate-spalj-spalj,josip-spalj-spalj|16 October 2026|notes/reading-2026-09-10.md
